{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T02:40:02.290Z","ordinal":485630,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18587-58f2-7892-8994-e5f40936b49b","call_id":"call_2e53e4d4dd714f15bd7123a3b5cf7096","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 6.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"entire_help:\nSearch checkpoints, commits, and sessions using hybrid search (semantic + keyword),\npowered by the Entire search service.\n\nRequires authentication via 'entire login' (GitHub device flow).\n\nBy default, results are scoped to the current repository. Use --all-repos to\nsearch across all accessible repos.\n\nRun without arguments to open an interactive search. Results are\ndisplayed in an interactive table. Use --json for machine-readable output,\nand add --compact for a trimmed per-result shape suited to agents (implies\n--json): id, type, repo, branch, author, date, files touched, score, match\nsnippet, and a truncated title instead of the full prompt (repo hits add\ndescription and checkpoint count). Fetch full detail\nfor a single result with 'entire checkpoint explain <id>', or add --full to\nthat command to pull the checkpoint's entire session transcript. For a\ncheckpoint or commit hit from another repo, add --repo gh/<owner>/<repo> for\na GitHub mirror or --repo et/<project>/<repo> for an Entire-native repo. The\nforge prefix is required, and the hit's id must be a full checkpoint ID (12-char hex or 26-char ULID) or a full commit SHA\n(a SHA is resolved to its checkpoint by that repo's Entire API). Prefixes\ncannot be resolved in another repo. This is unrelated to this command's\n--repo filter below.\n\nCLI queries also support inline filters like author:<name>, date:<week|month>,\nbranch:<name>, repo:<owner/name>, and repo:* to search all accessible repos.\n\nUsage:\n  entire search [query] [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entire search \"retry backoff\" --json\n  entire search \"retry backoff\" --json --compact\n  entire search \"auth timeout author:alice date:week\"\n  entire search --code \"parseToken\"\n\nFlags:\n      --all-repos        Search all accessible repos instead of just the current one\n      --author string    Filter by author name\n      --branch string    Filter by branch name\n      --case-sensitive   Case-sensitive code search (only with --code)\n      --code             Search code content across repositories\n      --compact          Trimmed JSON output for agents: id, repo, files touched, score, match snippet, and a truncated title instead of the full prompt (implies --json)\n      --date string      Filter by time period (week or month)\n  -h, --help             help for search\n      --json             Output as JSON\n      --limit int        Maximum number of results (per page for checkpoint search, total for --code) (default 10)\n      --page int         Page number (1-based) (default 1)\n      --repo strings     Filter by repository (gh/owner/repo, et/proj/repo, owner/repo, ULID, or *); repeatable and comma-separated for multiple repos\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\nOperations on checkpoints — the persistent records of agent work tied to commits.\n\nCommands:\n  list     List checkpoints on the current branch\n  explain  Explain a checkpoint, commit, or session\n  tokens   Show token usage and optimization recommendations\n  search   Search checkpoints (semantic + keyword)\n  delete   Delete a checkpoint locally and from checkpoint remotes\n\nExamples:\n  entire checkpoint list\n  entire checkpoint explain <id|sha>\n  entire checkpoint tokens <id>\n  entire checkpoint search \"fix login\"\n  entire checkpoint delete <id> --dry-run\n\nUsage:\n  entire checkpoint [command]\n\nAliases:\n  checkpoint, cp, checkpoints\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  delete      Delete a checkpoint locally and from checkpoint remotes\n  explain     Explain a session, commit, or checkpoint\n  list        List checkpoints on the current branch\n  search      Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using semantic and keyword matching\n  tokens      Show token usage and optimization recommendations for a checkpoint\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for checkpoint\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire checkpoint [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"gh_checks:\nEntire Gates\tfail\t44m14s\thttps://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/26/changes/nexus-code/26\t\nCodeQL\tpass\t2s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/123216208343\t\nCodeRabbit\tpass\t0\t\tReview skipped\njavascript-typescript\tpass\t1m29s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40803164136/job/123215785333\t\nlinux-x86_64\tpass\t24m9s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40803164040/job/123222122058\t\ntest-matrix (22)\tpass\t19m55s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40803164040/job/123215785135\t\ntest-matrix (24)\tpass\t18m55s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40803164040/job/123215784655\t\n{\"completed_at\":\"2026-10-29T02:38:10Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"details_url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40803164040/job/123222122058\",\"id\":123222122058,\"name\":\"linux-x86_64\",\"started_at\":\"2026-10-29T02:14:01Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"}\n{\"completed_at\":\"2026-10-29T01:55:25Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"details_url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/123216208343\",\"id\":123216208343,\"name\":\"CodeQL\",\"started_at\":\"2026-10-29T01:55:23Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"}\n{\"completed_at\":\"2026-10-29T01:55:33Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"details_url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40803164136/job/123215785333\",\"id\":123215785333,\"name\":\"javascript-typescript\",\"started_at\":\"2026-10-29T01:54:04Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"}\n{\"completed_at\":\"2026-10-29T02:13:59Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"details_url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40803164040/job/123215785135\",\"id\":123215785135,\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"started_at\":\"2026-10-29T01:54:04Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"}\n{\"completed_at\":\"2026-10-29T02:12:59Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"details_url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40803164040/job/123215784655\",\"id\":123215784655,\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"started_at\":\"2026-10-29T01:54:04Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"}\n{\"completed_at\":\"2026-10-29T02:38:13Z\",\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"details_url\":\"https://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/26/changes/nexus-code/26\",\"id\":123215769507,\"name\":\"Entire Gates\",\"started_at\":\"2026-10-29T01:53:59Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"claims_index:\n126\n.git/nexus-claims/V1_QUALIFY_ALL_ACCEPTED_V9_REVIEW_20261028/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/SUITE/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/V1_CHECKPOINT_TRAIL23_REMEDIATION_20261028/owner.json\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"suite_progress:\n    PID STAT     ELAPSED %CPU WCHAN\n3922403 Sl         03:53  0.0 ep_poll\n260:\u001b[1m\u001b[92m     Running\u001b[0m unittests src/main.rs (core/target/debug/deps/harness_core-5566b07e625326be)\n305:test result: ok. 41 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 12.72s\n307:\u001b[1m\u001b[92m     Running\u001b[0m unittests src/bin/nexus_tui.rs (core/target/debug/deps/nexus_tui-497e8000c84141df)\n341:test live_state::tests::a_failed_sidecar_offers_restart_and_quit_only ... ok\n360:test live_state::tests::a_tool_without_a_record_says_so_and_failed_requests_stay_in_the_p