{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T02:41:58.452Z","ordinal":485724,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18576-ae93-7cb0-a977-576664719de6","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-15acc215-54e2-4214-9ab9-b4a56cc6b5a7","process_id":"52496","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","entire session --help; entire activity --json; entire trail --help; git worktree remove /var/tmp/nexus-requirements-b10a85"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire session --help; entire activity --json; entire trail --help; git worktree remove /var/tmp/nexus-requirements-b10a85"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"View and manage agent sessions tracked by Entire.\n\nCommands:\n  list     List all sessions across all worktrees\n  info     Show detailed information for a specific session\n  tokens   Show token usage and optimization recommendations\n  stop     Stop one or more active sessions\n  current  Show the active session for the current worktree\n  attach   Attach an existing agent session\n  adopt    Adopt an active session from another worktree\n  resume   Switch to a branch and resume its session\n\nExamples:\n  entire session list                      List all sessions\n  entire session info <session-id>         Show session details\n  entire session info <session-id> --json  Output as JSON\n  entire session tokens <session-id>       Show token usage\n  entire session stop                      Interactive stop\n  entire session current                   Active session for cwd\n  entire session attach <session-id>       Attach an external session\n  entire session adopt <session-id> --from ../repo  Adopt a moved session\n  entire session resume <branch>           Resume from a branch\n\nUsage:\n  entire session [command]\n\nAliases:\n  session, sessions\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  adopt       Adopt an active session from another worktree\n  attach      Attach an existing agent session\n  current     Show the session running this command, or the most recent one here\n  info        Show detailed session information\n  list        List all sessions\n  resume      Resume a stopped session (interactive picker, or by branch)\n  stop        Stop one or more active sessions\n  tokens      Show token usage and optimization recommendations for a session\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for session\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire session [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\nUsage:\n  entire [flags]\n  entire [command]\n\nEntire Setup:\n  agent                      Manage agent integrations (add, remove, list)\n  clean                      Clean up Entire session data\n  configure                  Update Entire settings in the current repository\n  disable                    Disable Entire in current repository\n  doctor                     Diagnose and fix session issues\n  enable                     Enable Entire in current repository\n  plugin                     Manage Entire plugins (install, list, upgrade, search, remove)\n  status                     Show Entire status\n\nSessions & Checkpoints:\n  activity                   Show your activity overview\n  checkpoint                 Inspect and search checkpoints\n  dispatch                   Generate a dispatch summarizing recent agent work\n  recap                      Summarize recent checkpoint activity\n  search                     Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using semantic and keyword matching\n  session                    Manage agent sessions tracked by Entire\n\nTrails:\n  trail                      Manage trails across repositories and branches\n\nAccount:\n  auth                       Manage authentication\n  login                      Log in to Entire\n  logout                     Log out of Entire\n\nControl Plane:\n  api                        Make an authenticated request to an Entire API and print the response\n  cluster                    Show the Entire clusters you can place projects and repos on\n  org                        Manage Entire organizations\n  project                    Manage Entire projects\n  repo                       Manage Entire repositories\n\nAdditional Commands:\n  agent-help                 Machine-readable usage for coding agents (always matches the installed CLI)\n  help                       Help about any command\n  labs                       Explore experimental Entire workflows\n  version                    Show build information\n\nFlags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n\nError: Invalid usage: unknown flag: --json\nA trail captures project intent across repositories and branches. Manage intent and discussions on the whole trail; use --repo and --branch to select context for checkout, sessions, findings, and approvals.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail [flags]\n  entire trail [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  approvals       List approval decisions on a trail\n  approve         Approve a trail\n  checkout        Check out a trail's branch\n  comment         Discuss the whole trail across repositories\n  create          Create a trail and publish its branch\n  finding         Manage a trail's agent findings\n  link            Link a repository branch to a trail\n  list            List trails in a project\n  merge           Merge one of a trail's changes into its base\n  resume          Resume a trail's agent session\n  show            Show trail intent and its repositories and branches\n  unlink          Unlink a repository branch without deleting its work\n  update          Update project intent and lifecycle\n  watch           Tail events for a trail's selected repository branch\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for trail\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire trail [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":375278180}},"started_at_ms":1793241718076,"completed_at_ms":1793241718452}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T02:41:59.754Z","ordinal":485725,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18589-23ca-7422-a5cf-5b880f6628d4","call_id":"call_1e645a7e1fdc4f57a7158bdc5e9eb850","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"View and manage agent sessions tracked by Entire.\n\nCommands:\n  list     List all sessions across all worktrees\n  info     Show detailed information for a specific session\n  tokens   Show token usage and optimization recommendations\n  stop     Stop one or more active sessions\n  current  Show the active session for the current worktree\n  attach   Attach an existing agent session\n  adopt    Adopt an active session from another worktree\n  resume   Switch to a branch and resume its session\n\nExamples:\n  entire session list                      List all sessions\n  entire session info <session-id>         Show session details\n  entire session info <session-id> --json  Output as JSON\n  entire session tokens <session-id>       Show token usage\n  entire session stop                      Interactive stop\n  entire session current                   Active session for cwd\n  entire session attach <session-id>       Attach an external session\n  entire session adopt <session-id> --from ../repo  Adopt a moved session\n  entire session resume <branch>           Resume from a branch\n\nUsage:\n  entire session [command]\n\nAliases:\n  session, sessions\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  adopt       Adopt an active session from another worktree\n  attach      Attach an existing agent session\n  current     Show the session running this command, or the most recent one here\n  info        Show detailed session information\n  list        List all sessions\n  resume      Resume a stopped session (interactive picker, or by branch)\n  stop        Stop one or more active sessions\n  tokens      Show token usage and optimization recommendations for a session\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for session\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire session [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\nUsage:\n  entire [flags]\n  entire [command]\n\nEntire Setup:\n  agent                      Manage agent integrations (add, remove, list)\n  clean                      Clean up Entire session data\n  configure                  Update Entire settings in the current repository\n  disable                    Disable Entire in current repository\n  doctor                     Diagnose and fix session issues\n  enable                     Enable Entire in current repository\n  plugin                     Manage Entire plugins (install, list, upgrade, search, remove)\n  status                     Show Entire status\n\nSessions & Checkpoints:\n  activity                   Show your activity overview\n  checkpoint                 Inspect and search checkpoints\n  dispatch                   Generate a dispatch summarizing recent agent work\n  recap                      Summarize recent checkpoint activity\n  search                     Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using semantic and keyword matching\n  session                    Manage agent sessions tracked by Entire\n\nTrails:\n  trail                      Manage trails across repositories and branches\n\nAccount:\n  auth                       Manage authentication\n  login                      Log in to Entire\n  logout                     Log out of Entire\n\nControl Plane:\n  api                        Make an authenticated request to an Entire API and print the response\n  cluster                    Show the Entire clusters you can place projects and repos on\n  org                        Manage Entire organizations\n  project                    Manage Entire projects\n  repo                       Manage Entire repositories\n\nAdditional Commands:\n  agent-help                 Machine-readable usage for coding agents (always matches the installed CLI)\n  help                       Help about any command\n  labs                       Explore experimental Entire workflows\n  version                    Show build information\n\nFlags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n\nError: Invalid usage: unknown flag: --json\nA trail captures project intent across repositories and branches. Manage intent and discussions on the whole trail; use --repo and --branch to select context for checkout, sessions, findings, and approvals.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail [flags]\n  entire trail [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  approvals       List approval decisions on a trail\n  approve         Approve a trail\n  checkout        Check out a trail's branch\n  comment         Discuss the whole trail across repositories\n  create          Create a trail and publish its branch\n  finding         Manage a trail's agent findings\n  link            Link a repository branch to a trail\n  list            List trails in a project\n  merge           Merge one of a trail's changes into its base\n  resume          Resume a trail's agent session\n  show            Show trail intent and its repositories and branches\n  unlink          Unlink a repository branch without deleting its work\n  update          Update project intent and lifecycle\n  watch           Tail events for a trail's selected repository branch\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for trail\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire trail [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18576-ae93-7cb0-a977-576664719de6","create_time":1793241719.7543914}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
