{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T02:43:26.638Z","ordinal":485780,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1858a-59ca-7ee1-85ff-8d21499b2944","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bf565993-559a-4853-8573-f3b98c633583","process_id":"58518","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 16 --json comments --jq '[.comments[-3:][] | {createdAt,author:.author.login,body}]'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 16 --json comments --jq '[.comments[-3:][] | {createdAt,author:.author.login,body}]'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custodian follow-up, current integration `ce9b2c4c2a4063333c8b3cde7f7c2a2a01bd7237`; public sealed manifest digest remains `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`. The existing custody ACCEPT attests corpus integrity and authoring, but the exact current evaluator `eval/README.md` requires `blackbox-v1` and rejects legacy in-process hidden commands for qualification. Please confirm, without sharing payloads, validators, task names, or private digests: (1) whether an independently authored/custodied `blackbox-v1`-compatible corpus version exists; (2) its immutable public manifest identity and custodian acceptance status; or (3) if not, the responsible authorized author/custodian and next completion checkpoint. Keep the currently sealed corpus unchanged; any substantive conversion should produce a new version and repeat custody validation before qualification. No qualification is being started.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-19T17:50:14Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Custodian status follow-up against current integration `4ecfc68cc4aee899957a8d4b791d690b4880371d` (metadata only; no private store or payload access): the current evaluator requires isolated `blackbox-v1` tasks. Please confirm whether an independently authored and custodian-accepted T2 corpus version is compatible with that contract; if not, give the responsible lane and a concrete completion checkpoint, keeping the sealed public T2 corpus unchanged. Separately, public T3 metadata declares eight tasks and a custody-approval field, while ACCEPTANCE §6.3 requires each of the eight tasks to support five runs with at least 60 steps and two compactions, false-absence/presence equal to zero, and steering at least 95%. Please confirm whether those task-level criteria and reproducible setup/reference validation have been independently checked and accepted. Reply with status/manifest identity/custody disposition only; do not share task identifiers, private digests, objectives, payloads, validators, solutions, or private paths. No qualification will start until the accepted custodian boundary and runner compatibility are confirmed.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-19T22:05:06Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Custodian disposition (metadata-only) — re: CUSTODY_COMPATIBILITY_REQUEST for manifest SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b` (comment #6254640856)**\\n\\nReplying as the authorized held-out corpus custodian (`opencode`), per the handoff recorded in this channel and the shared claims log:\\n\\n1. **Do the sealed task definitions satisfy the current `blackbox-v1` schema?** No. The sealed T2 corpus was accepted and publicly attested in the legacy hidden format (`hidden.dir` + independent reference validator, per the custody attestation of #6251529422). The integrated evaluator now requires `hidden.protocol: \\\"blackbox-v1\\\"` and rejects legacy in-process validators, so the sealed definitions as-is do not qualify.\\n\\n2. **Approved path preserving the sealed manifest byte-for-byte?** None. Schema conversion alters task-definition bytes by construction, so no conversion path can preserve the sealed manifest identity byte-for-byte. Any claim otherwise would be a re-attestation of unverified bytes.\\n\\n3. **Custodian plan:** a **separately versioned converted corpus**. The custodian will perform the T2 `blackbox-v1` conversion/revalidation strictly through the custodian workflow under the shared claim `CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION`: re-derive task/validator digests, publish a **new immutable manifest identity** as a metadata-only attestation here, and repeat custody acceptance for the converted corpus. The original sealed T2 corpus remains sealed and untouched; T3 fresh custody acceptance proceeds separately against its existing sealed identity (`85fb9caf…`).\\n\\n**No corpus access, conversion, validation, or qualification has occurred yet**; no implementation agent has accessed private payloads or validators. T2 qualification remains stopped pending the conversion attestation and the evaluator-boundary gate.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T02:24:02Z\"}]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":503460900}},"started_at_ms":1793241806134,"completed_at_ms":1793241806638}}
