{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T02:45:49.959Z","ordinal":485944,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1858a-59ca-7ee1-85ff-8d21499b2944","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ccfcc19c-5274-4aad-9164-39805445d115","process_id":"5758","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","for f in docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md; do echo \"--- $f\"; git show origin/main:\"$f\" 2>/dev/null | rg -n -C 2 'ACC-TUI-MANUAL|terminal matrix|terminal behavior|DEC-19|REQ-QUAL-108|exception|waiv' | head -90; done; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -type f -name owner.json -print | rg 'ACCEPTANCE|READINESS|PLAN-10|DECISIONS|REQUIREMENTS|FILE_docs_v1.0.0'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"for f in docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md; do echo \"--- $f\"; git show origin/main:\"$f\" 2>/dev/null | rg -n -C 2 'ACC-TUI-MANUAL|terminal matrix|terminal behavior|DEC-19|REQ-QUAL-108|exception|waiv' | head -90; done; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -type f -name owner.json -print | rg 'ACCEPTANCE|READINESS|PLAN-10|DECISIONS|REQUIREMENTS|FILE_docs_v1.0.0'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"--- docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n28-5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n29-\n30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n31-\n32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n33-\n34-The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n--\n49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n50-| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n52-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n53-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n54-\n55-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n56:### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n57-\n58-| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n--\n63-\n64-1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n66-3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n67-4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n--\n119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | **Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** No per-cell verdicts are recorded; this is not a PASS. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 remain required. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n--\n157-| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n158-\n159:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n160-\n161-### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n--\n188-| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n189-\n190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n191-\n192:**Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** The procedure below is retained for a successor release; it is not required for v1.0.0 and no cell verdict is recorded. The automated suites in §5.1 and §5.2 remain mandatory.\n193-\n194-Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n--\n204-7. NO_COLOR.\n205-\n206:Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); this does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\n207-\n208-**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n--\n334-- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n335-- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n336:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI and scripted gates PASS; the manual real-terminal matrix is waived for v1.0.0 per DEC-19.\n337-- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n338-- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n--\n341-- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\n342-  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\n343:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n344-- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\n345-- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\n--- docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n169-- **Historical freeze (ended):** while judging was open, the submitted material (contest docs, `experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/`, `demo/`, contest CI job) was not changed because post-deadline edits could have been read as amending the entry. The audit findings CON-001 to CON-014 were recorded during that period.\n170-- After judging concluded, PLAN-C1 proceeded as **post-contest hardening**. Its first task is the CON-001 correction, with a dated \"post-submission correction\" note in CONTEST.md.\n171:- During that historical freeze, one exception was considered: if contest rules permitted errata, an erratum could state that the documented deploy builds the legacy Experiment-1 Worker and reproduction is operator-host only. That restriction ended with judging; it does not limit current maintenance.\n172-- Client work that touched `demo/lib/real-agent-runner.mjs` (PLAN-01 task 8, `--yes`) was deferred while judging was open. That deferral has ended; update the demo alongside the client where needed. The runner may continue to pass `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` when required by the current CLI contract.\n173-\n--\n239-**Affected:** REQ-AGT-118; SPEC-11 §2.7 and ACC-VER-07; REQUIREMENTS ledger row REQ-AGT-118; `cli/test/fixtures/token_calibration.json` and `cli/test/tokens.test.ts`. No change to `cli/src/tokens.ts` behaviour.\n240-\n241:## DEC-18: v1.0.0 terminal screenshot-artifact waiver\n242-\n243:**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\n244-\n245:**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\n246-\n247:**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\n248-\n249:## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n250-\n251:**Context.** [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waived screenshot artifacts only; the fifteen manual matrix cells (five terminals × three sizes, ACCEPTANCE §5.3) remained mandatory. On 2026-10-29 the release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0.\n252-\n253:**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-29).** The manual E3 matrix, its per-cell PASS/FAIL verdicts and its evidence records are not required for v1.0.0. ACC-TUI-MANUAL is **waived**, not PASS: no cell verdict is recorded and none may be inferred. The automated CI PTY suites and the scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2) remain mandatory and are the only terminal evidence for this release. This waiver changes no other acceptance criterion, safety gate, or verification rule, and it does not change any requirements-ledger status: REQ-QUAL-108 remains `partial` unless the ledger owner records a different disposition.\n254-\n255:**Disclosure.** The v1.0.0 release notes must state that the manual real-terminal matrix was waived by owner decision and that terminal evidence is automated (PTY/CI) only.\n256-\n257:**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS.\n258-\n259-## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\n--- docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n3-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 22:00 UTC; custodian update 2026-10-29)\n4-\n5:**Custodian update (2026-10-29).** The release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0 ([DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)). The gate is **waived, not passed**: no cell verdicts were recorded, the automated CI PTY suites and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios remain required and passing, and the release notes must disclose the waiver. The terminal-matrix item is no longer an outstanding qualification gate; every other gate in this checkpoint is unchanged.\n6-\n7-**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496`, the PR #308 merge commit. Exact-main CI run [40770466028](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770466028) completed successfully at 2026-10-28 21:58:49 UTC on this SHA. Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices passed; Linux x86_64 passed Rust and CLI tests, requirements and security gates, reproducible package builds with matching output hashes, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. CodeQL run [40770465935](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770465935) completed successfully. On a clean detached worktree at this exact SHA, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n--\n9-**Integrated changes:** PR #309 merged as `b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af` at 20:36 UTC with checksummed RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider evidence. PR #300 merged as `79cba842e86d64f895e1a269636776cdf1e7e6da` at 21:07:46 UTC after Node 22/24, Linux packaging/tests, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. PR #308 merged as `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496` at 21:15:37 UTC; exact PR head `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` passed Node 22/24 and Linux, with JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; its GitHub Entire Gates check was neutral. A post-merge source reviewer found no blocking defect in the reviewed restore path and reported a separate Entire trail 23 signal: approvals failed and one high-severity finding was unresolved. A later authenticated, read-only Entire query on `ubuntu-desktop` (2026-10-28 21:48 UTC) found trail 23 open but its Nexus Code change marked merged; the finding and approvals commands reported no open change, so the historical finding text and its disposition could not be retrieved. The earlier high-severity signal therefore remains unresolved/unverified and must be reconciled before successor-RC qualification; the later query does not establish that it was resolved. The current-main source CI passed as recorded above; this does not qualify an installed release candidate.\n10-\n11:**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. Per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver), screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n12-\n13-**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n--\n19-**Integrated ch