der-connect tests 33/33, TUI Rust tests 6/6, TypeScript build, and `git diff --check` pass; no local full suite was run. Run exact PR checks after updating the public branch before integration.\n279-\n280:**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN; its latest metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Independent private custody, evaluator-compatible corpus sealing, and held-out acceptance remain unestablished; no held-out payload was accessed or run. Current-candidate provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The human terminal matrix remains **0/15**. RC8 is a prior prerelease, not a qualified candidate for this source; stable v1.0.0 is unpublished. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authority remains granted but gated.\n281-\n282-The 15:02 checkpoint immediately below is retained as historical evidence; this update supersedes its main CI and PR #256 review status.\n--\n289-**PR #256 local-provider change:** Public PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) remains at head `c3bb2235286a154280f8578458a4dc8570ae542a`, based on `b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421`; its exact-head CI run [40338957629](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957629) failed the same PTY model-picker test on Node 22 and 24 because the fixture navigated past the newly added Appliance row incorrectly. The owner’s local candidate `0490db3e9b85edd919fe7a05a4baf7b0b08ecdfa` was normally updated with current `main` by merge commit `9d898eb`; it is not pushed. Its focused build/test results (105/105) were reported by the implementer on the pre-merge head. Independent review of `0490db3` returned CHANGES_REQUIRED with four findings: pending Escape must cancel the matching setup, malformed credential-origin metadata must not rebind legacy keys, provisional-key UI copy is inaccurate, and invalid connected-provider URLs must not fail the entire catalog. The owner reacquired the relevant claims and is implementing regressions; no fixes are yet accepted on the refreshed branch.\n290-\n--- docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n34-| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (9×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\n35-| 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\n36:| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Run the full checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3 and record all per-cell outcomes and evidence. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). | ACCEPTANCE §5.3; DEC-18 | RC build |\n37-\n38-## PR slices\n--\n66-## Definition of done\n67-\n68:- REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-108 evidence is archived.\n69-- The DEC-05 thresholds were evaluated with the scorer verdict table, signed off before the run and reported after it.\n70-- REQ-QUAL-109/110 are met.\n--- docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\n99-| EXT-004 (middleware before/after audit) | PARTIALLY_DEMONSTRATED_BLOCKING | Open (HIST-01) | DEC-04: **implement** → REQ-SEC-116 (B) |\n100-| PERS-002 legacy identity-sensitive files | accepted limitation | Unchanged | Retained limitation. Permissions mitigate it (REQ-PER-101). |\n101:| CRED-003 crash/exception display | bounded envelope | Unqualified | RR re-qualify under REQ-P