{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T02:45:52.288Z","ordinal":485945,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1858c-b020-7b92-bc51-4fc9efa8206e","call_id":"call_8b7b2ce19d6d4dfc92965591bdf8fe57","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 13271)\nTotal output lines: 231\n\n--- docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n28-5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n29-\n30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n31-\n32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n33-\n34-The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n--\n49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n50-| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n52-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n53-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n54-\n55-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n56:### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n57-\n58-| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n--\n63-\n64-1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n66-3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n67-4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n--\n119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | **Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** No per-cell verdicts are recorded; this is not a PASS. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 remain required. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n--\n157-| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n158-\n159:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n160-\n161-### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n--\n188-| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n189-\n190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n191-\n192:**Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** The procedure below is retained for a successor release; it is not required for v1.0.0 and no cell verdict is recorded. The automated suites in §5.1 and §5.2 remain mandatory.\n193-\n194-Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n--\n204-7. NO_COLOR.\n205-\n206:Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); this does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\n207-\n208-**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n--\n334-- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n335-- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n336:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI and scripted gates PASS; the manual real-terminal matrix is waived for v1.0.0 per DEC-19.\n337-- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n338-- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n--\n341-- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\n342-  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\n343:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n344-- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\n345-- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\n--- docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n169-- **Historical freeze (ended):** while judging was open, the submitted material (contest docs, `experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/`, `demo/`, contest CI job)…8271 tokens truncated…ior prerelease, not a qualified candidate for this source; stable v1.0.0 is unpublished. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authority remains granted but gated.\n281-\n282-The 15:02 checkpoint immediately below is retained as historical evidence; this update supersedes its main CI and PR #256 review status.\n--\n289-**PR #256 local-provider change:** Public PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) remains at head `c3bb2235286a154280f8578458a4dc8570ae542a`, based on `b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421`; its exact-head CI run [40338957629](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957629) failed the same PTY model-picker test on Node 22 and 24 because the fixture navigated past the newly added Appliance row incorrectly. The owner’s local candidate `0490db3e9b85edd919fe7a05a4baf7b0b08ecdfa` was normally updated with current `main` by merge commit `9d898eb`; it is not pushed. Its focused build/test results (105/105) were reported by the implementer on the pre-merge head. Independent review of `0490db3` returned CHANGES_REQUIRED with four findings: pending Escape must cancel the matching setup, malformed credential-origin metadata must not rebind legacy keys, provisional-key UI copy is inaccurate, and invalid connected-provider URLs must not fail the entire catalog. The owner reacquired the relevant claims and is implementing regressions; no fixes are yet accepted on the refreshed branch.\n290-\n--- docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v