{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T02:47:14.298Z","ordinal":486001,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1858a-59ca-7ee1-85ff-8d21499b2944","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-db97cefe-3519-4d27-a12e-adb168fdc671","process_id":"40803","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git grep -n -C 4 'ACC-TUI-STEER\\|ACC-TUI-A11Y\\|ACC-TUI-MANUAL\\|DEC-19\\|Qualification applicability' origin/main -- docs/v1.0.0 scripts/check_requirements.mjs | head -260; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | sed -n '200,245p'; git show origin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs | rg -n -C 6 'Qualification applicability|qualificationExceptions|exceptions|NOT REQUIRED|qualificationNotApplicable' | head -200; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md | sed -n '235,246p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git grep -n -C 4 'ACC-TUI-STEER\\|ACC-TUI-A11Y\\|ACC-TUI-MANUAL\\|DEC-19\\|Qualification applicability' origin/main -- docs/v1.0.0 scripts/check_requirements.mjs | head -260; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | sed -n '200,245p'; git show origin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs | rg -n -C 6 'Qualification applicability|qualificationExceptions|exceptions|NOT REQUIRED|qualificationNotApplicable' | head -200; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md | sed -n '235,246p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-28-5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-29-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-30-The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-31-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-33-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-34-The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-35-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-36-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-47-| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-48-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-50-| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-52-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-53-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-54-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-55-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-106-These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-107-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-108-| ID | Check | Pass condition |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-109-|---|---|---|\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:110:| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:111:| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-113-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-114-| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-117-| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | **Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** No per-cell verdicts are recorded; this is not a PASS. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 remain required. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-122-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-124-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-125-### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-188-| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-189-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-190-### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-191-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:192:**Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** The procedure below is retained for a successor release; it is not required for v1.0.0 and no cell verdict is recorded. The automated suites in §5.1 and §5.2 remain mandatory.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-193-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-194-Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-195-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-196-For each terminal × size, check:\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-332-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-333-- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-334-- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-335-- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:336:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI and scripted gates PASS; the manual real-terminal matrix is waived for v1.0.0 per DEC-19.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-337-- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-338-- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-339-- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-340-- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-243-**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-244-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-245-**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-246-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:247:**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-248-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:249:## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-250-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-251-**Context.** [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waived screenshot artifacts only; the fifteen manual matrix cells (five terminals × three sizes, ACCEPTANCE §5.3) remained mandatory. On 2026-10-29 the release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-252-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:253:**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-29).** The manual E3 matrix, its per-cell PASS/FAIL verdicts and its evidence records are not required for v1.0.0. ACC-TUI-MANUAL is **waived**, not PASS: no cell verdict is recorded and none may be inferred. The automated CI PTY suites and the scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2) remain mandatory and are the only terminal evidence for this release. This waiver changes no other acceptance criterion, safety gate, or verification rule, and it does not change any requirements-ledger status: REQ-QUAL-108 remains `partial` unless the ledger owner records a different disposition.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-254-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-255-**Disclosure.** The v1.0.0 release notes must state that the manual real-terminal matrix was waived by owner decision and that terminal evidence is automated (PTY/CI) only.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-256-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:257:**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-258-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-259-## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-260-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-261-| # | Action | Why | When |\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-1-# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-2-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-3-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 22:00 UTC; custodian update 2026-10-29)\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-4-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:5:**Custodian update (2026-10-29).** The release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0 ([DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)). The gate is **waived, not passed**: no cell verdicts were recorded, the automated CI PTY suites and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios remain required and passing, and the release notes must disclose the waiver. The terminal-matrix item is no longer an outstanding qualification gate; every other gate in this checkpoint is unchanged.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-6-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-7-**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496`, the PR #308 merge commit. Exact-main CI run [40770466028](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770466028) completed successfully at 2026-10-28 21:58:49 UTC on this SHA. Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices passed; Linux x86_64 passed Rust and CLI tests, requirements and security gates, reproducible package builds with matching output hashes, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. CodeQL run [40770465935](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770465935) completed successfully. On a clean detached worktree at this exact SHA, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-8-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-9-**Integrated changes:** PR #309 merged as `b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af` at 20:36 UTC with checksummed RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider evidence. PR #300 merged as `79cba842e86d64f895e1a269636776cdf1e7e6da` at 21:07:46 UTC after Node 22/24, Linux packaging/tests, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. PR #308 merged as `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496` at 21:15:37 UTC; exact PR head `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` passed Node 22/24 and Linux, with JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; its GitHub Entire Gates check was neutral. A post-merge source reviewer found no blocking defect in the reviewed restore path and reported a separate Entire trail 23 signal: approvals failed and one high-severity finding was unresolved. A later authenticated, read-only Entire query on `ubuntu-desktop` (2026-10-28 21:48 UTC) found trail 23 open but its Nexus Code change marked merged; the finding and approvals commands reported no open change, so the historical finding text and its disposition could not be retrieved. The earlier high-severity signal therefore remains unresolved/unverified and must be reconciled before successor-RC qualification; the later query does not establish that it was resolved. The current-main source CI passed as recorded above; this does not qualify an installed release candidate.\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-180-The 12:42 checkpoint immediately below is retained as historical evidence and superseded for current branch, CI, and test status by this checkpoint.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-181-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-182-## Historical terminal cancellation checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 02:11 UTC)\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-183-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:184:Five targeted synthetic installed-RC10 cancellation rechecks at `TERM=dumb`, 100×30 completed with Esc delays from 0 to 1 second; idle return measured 0.405–0.507 seconds. The two earlier full-matrix timeouts remained valid and unresolved; this targeted recheck did not promote ACC-TUI-A11Y or E3. Evidence and raw PTY streams are preserved in [the cancellation timing recheck](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/cancel-timing-recheck-20261027/README.md). Human terminal acceptance remained 0/15. This historical record is retained from the PR #264 merge history.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-185-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-186-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 12:42 UTC)\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-187-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-188-**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `1d9357ee63b1066a891584a898842814de614fbf`, which integrates PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264). PR #264 merged at 12:38:40 UTC after exact-head CI [40499840211](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40499840211) passed its Node 22, Node 24, and Linux package/reproducibility jobs, and CodeQL [40499839711](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40499839711) passed. New post-merge main CI [40505388775](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40505388775) and CodeQL [40505388849](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40505388849) are still running on exact commit `1d9357e`; their results are not yet established. PR #264 is merged, not open.\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-477-**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-478-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-479-## Historical integration checkpoint (observed 2026-10-23 02:13 UTC at `fa16045`; superseded by the current status above)\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-480-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:481:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` was `fa16045a6351ce61763bc3fcc93b562c50849285`, the merge of PR #152. PR #152 carried the readiness checkpoint refresh and terminal worksheet wording separating the §5.3 disposition gate from `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`; its exact head `deaf56fdb074df3f5cd3b62d50f811a2f14ca101` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 package/repro/install-smoke CI in run `39881805268`; CodeQL `39881805274` passed. The independent reviewer accepted that exact head. Post-merge CI run `39885102002` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/smoke/install; post-merge CodeQL `39885101945` passed. These checks are bound to exact main `fa16045`. Retained post-merge check summary: [CI and CodeQL result](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/post-merge-ci-main-fa16045.txt).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-482-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-483-**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-484-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-485-**Source requirements gate:** At exact main `fa16045`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed in a clean detached Git worktree with isolated HOME/XDG. Retained stdout is in the [exact-main enforcement record](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/requirements-enforce-main-fa16045.txt). It reported 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, and 7 open; 12 rows are explicitly mapped to exact-RC qualification. This is the pre-RC source gate only. It does not qualify an installed RC or change any requirement's acceptance threshold.\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-55-| REQ-AGT-001 | COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY §A; operator directive | No default cumulative step or time ceiling. Turns end on completion, cancel, demonstrated stagnation, actionable failure or an operator-set budget. Resource-safety valves (provider iterations, 10k scheduler transitions, 5 compaction attempts) are allowed and labelled. | `types.ts:127-133`; `agent.ts:4379-4445` | TEST + SRC (A §5) | tested | N | — | ACC-CONT-04, ACC-QUAL-T3 | K | SPEC-04 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-56-| REQ-AGT-002 | quickstart; TOP_TIER B3; EXEC-005 | Truthful outcome taxonomy. VERIFIED requires a passing, deliverable-bound verifier run, plus fail-before/pass-after independence for discovered verifiers. UNVERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE, BLOCKED and LIMIT_REACHED are distinct, with exit codes 0/2/1/130. | `agent.ts:5726-5764`; `tester.ts:371-430,541-627`; `turn.ts:318-351` | TEST at db1ca55; candidate suite at `6151a23` passes ACC-VER-03/04/09 regression tests. Historical VER-04/05 findings and tuned-set/live evidence remain in [A2_verification.md](evidence/A2_verification.md) and the dated evidence files. | partial | N | M5 false-VERIFIED threshold remains unqualified pending held-out T2/T3/T4 evidence; historical VER-04/05 implementation defects have regression coverage at the candidate. | ACC-VER-03/04/09, ACC-QUAL-T2 | B | SPEC-11 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-57-| REQ-AGT-003 | COMPACTION §B | State-aware repetition and stagnation (action/outcome/state identity; polls vs loops; compaction re-acquisition is not repetition). | `execution_tracking.ts` | TEST (ACC-CONT-09; test:cli/test/execution_tracking.test.ts) | tested | N | — | ACC-CONT-09 | K | SPEC-04 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-58-| REQ-AGT-004 | COMPACTION §C | Durable compaction commit order archive → task → session (fsync). Failure stops the turn with PERSISTENCE_FAILED. Queued `/compact`. | `agent.ts:3070-3153` | TEST (`test:cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts::\"ACC-CONT-03: pressure compaction of a work unit survives SIGKILL and restores archived markers\"`, `compaction_continuity.test.ts:533`); HIST 1 live run | tested | Y (source/CI incl. M1/M3/L5 in PR #25; see `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/dispositions.md`) | Live long-task ACC-CONT-10 pending M5 installed-RC qualification | ACC-CONT-03, ACC-CONT-10 | B (work units) / K (depth 0) | SPEC-04 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:59:| REQ-AGT-005 | TOP_TIER; USER_MANUAL | Steering is queued, applied once at a step boundary, never silently dropped, and survives restore. | `agent.ts:1935-1973` | TEST + RT (PTY s4a/s6) | tested | N | — | ACC-TUI-STEER | K | — |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-60-| REQ-AGT-006 | EXEC-001; USER_MANUAL | Cancel during inference gives a truthful INTERRUPTED outcome naming the phase, within 5 s. | `agent.ts:4179-4190,4359-4372` | RT (PTY s5/s6: 0.2–2.4 s) | tested | N | TUI-11: one 11 s observation (UNV) | ACC-PROC-07 | K | SPEC-02 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-61-| REQ-AGT-007 | release notes alpha.2 | Output-truncated reply: nothing from it runs; one in-turn retry; a second consecutive truncation ends the turn. | `agent.ts:4671-4683`; `client.ts:1459-1468` | TEST (6/6, scripted) | tested | **N (pending)** | Never observed live | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-QUAL-T4 | K | SPEC-04 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-62-| REQ-AGT-008 | provider recovery design | Bounded provider recovery: 20 min deadline, jittered backoff, Retry-After honoured, probe before an UNKNOWN replay, ≤ 2 replays. | `provider_recovery.ts` | TEST 23/23 + 15/15 | tested | N | A never-reachable endpoint waits too long (TUI-06) | ACC-INF-07 | K | SPEC-05 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-63-| REQ-AGT-009 | EXEC-001..004, CAND-001..004 | One task lifecycle. Effects bound to a verified root. Validation bound to an immutable candidate. Merge requires receipt and identity equality. | `core/spine.ts`, `core/candidate.ts`, `worktree.ts:278-310` | TEST; HIST spot-check holds (F §4 #8) | tested | P (WP01/WP04 reviews) | — | existing suites | K | — |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-64-| REQ-AGT-010 | CTX-001 (Issue #12 blocker) | Injected context carries provenance and classification metadata. | `agent.ts:3301,3789` | SRC; TEST (v1 subset: `cli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts` ACC-TRUST-04, 5/5 at 2c70d39, source unchanged through 19dedc6) | partial | Y (v1 subset only: ACC-TRUST-04 skills/knowledge source annotations independently accepted 2026-10-18; not the full provenance graph) | DEC-04: v1 scope = skills, knowledge and other injected items carry source path and trust state (REQ-SEC-113); full provenance graph post-v1. Not an installed-RC acceptance. | ACC-TRUST-04 | RR (partial), P (rest) | SPEC-03 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-65-| REQ-TUI-001 | TOP_TIER B7, TUI surface F1–F3 | An approval is never decided by stray typing, bursts, pastes or resize. \"Approve all\" is deliberate. | `live.rs:317-481`; `live_state.rs:1249-1395` | RT (PTY s2/s3, this audit); TEST `tui_approval_input_e2e`; HIST round 5 | tested | **Y** | TUI-09 arrow keys resolved per button layout; hints complete at 40 cols (TUI-10) | ACC-SAFE-08 | K | SPEC-01 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:66:| REQ-TUI-002 | USER_MANUAL | NO_COLOR is honoured. States are distinguishable without colour. | `theme.rs:19-47` | RT (0 colour SGR in 867) | tested | N | — | ACC-TUI-A11Y | K | — |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-67-| REQ-TUI-003 | USER_MANUAL | Session resume in the TUI (`-r`, `/sessions`). | sidecar, `slash/session_commands.ts` | RT (PTY s7b) | tested | N | PER-05 corrupt-session messaging | ACC-PER-04 | K | SPEC-08 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-68-| REQ-SEC-001 | RES-001..004; DEC-01 ADR | File tools are confined to the workspace (lexical, symlink, parent-symlink, `/proc/self/fd` recheck). | `file_ops.rs:59-87,731-791` | RT (C §4 R1) | tested | P | TOCTOU swap race is untested; macOS branch is a no-op | ACC-SEC-JAIL (+ race test, P) | K | — |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-69-| REQ-SEC-002 | EXT-002, TOP_TIER B2 | Workspace MCP configs and plugins load only after `nexus trust`, and never in `--read-only`. | `workspace_trust.ts`; `mcp.ts:509-531`; `plugins.ts:47-76` | TEST + SRC | tested | N | Skills and knowledge are not gated (→ REQ-SEC-113) | ACC-TRUST-04 | K | SPEC-03 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-70-| REQ-SEC-003 | CRED-001..002; EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE §7 | Credentials are scoped to their origin. A project `.env` never re-homes credentials. credentials.json is 0600. | `client.ts:77-133`; `credentials.ts:68-75` | TEST | tested | Y (CRED003 bounded) | `.env` can still disable TLS (→ REQ-SEC-110) | ACC-TRUST-01 | K | SPEC-03 |\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-1-# Manual real-terminal acceptance worksheet\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-2-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:3:For `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-4-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:5:> **Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** This worksheet is retained for a successor release. It contains no results, no cell verdict is recorded for v1.0.0, and it does not qualify an RC.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-6-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-7-## Installed candidate identity\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-8-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-9-Fill these fields from the installed candidate before the first cell. Do not copy identity from a source branch or local build.\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-79-failure on another check has a written disposition. Mark it FAIL if any safety\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-80-check (2, 5, or 6) failed. Mark it INCOMPLETE when required evidence is missing\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-81-or a non-safety failure has no written disposition.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-82-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:83:ACC-TUI-MANUAL: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-84-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:85:Mark ACC-TUI-MANUAL PASS only when all 15 cell verdicts are PASS and the\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-86-per-cell outcomes and evidence records are complete. Screenshots are waived per DEC-18. Mark it FAIL if any\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-87-cell is FAIL. Mark it INCOMPLETE when evidence is missing and no cell has\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-88-failed. A documented known limitation for a non-safety failure may satisfy the\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:89:§5.3 disposition requirement, but the cell remains FAIL and ACC-TUI-MANUAL\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-90-remains unmet until every cell passes.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-91-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-92-Operator summary / evidence index: ______________________________________________\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-93-\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-79-   - Hidden tests are not readable by the agent uid.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-80-   - The scorer logs every replacement.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-81-   - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-82-7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:83:8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts) are mandatory. A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. **The manual matrix is waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)**; no per-cell verdicts are recorded and this is not a PASS. Screenshot artifacts were waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). Automated terminal evidence is the only terminal evidence for this release.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-84-9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0, false-presence = 0 (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-18), and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-85-10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-86-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-87-## 3. Design\n--\norigin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs-271-        if (row.blocking && rcQualificationOnly.has(id) && evidence.status !== \"product-qualified\") throw new Error(`${id}: exact-RC qualification requires product-qualified status`);\norigin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs-272-        if (row.blocking && evidence.status !== \"product-qualified\") {\norigin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs-273-          const decision = evidence.qualificationNotApplicable?.decision;\norigin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs-274-          const approvedDecision = rcQualificationExceptions.get(id);\norigin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs:275:          const decisionExists = new RegExp(`^\\\\s*[-*]\\\\s*Qualification applicability:\\\\s*${id}\\\\s*=\\\\s*NOT REQUIRED\\\\b`, \"m\").test(decisionSection(decision));\norigin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs-276-          if (evidence.status !== \"tested\" || typeof evidence.qualificationNotApplicable?.reason !== \"string\" || !evidence.qualificationNotApplicable.reason.trim() || decision !== approvedDecision || !decisionExists) throw new Error(`${id}: blocker must be product-qualified or tested with an explicitly approved decision and qualification-not-applicable reason`);\norigin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs-277-        }\norigin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs-278-        if (!Array.isArray(evidence.evidence) || evidence.evidence.length === 0) throw new Error(`${id}: qualification evidence references are required`);\norigin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs-279-        const requiredAccs = rcQualificationOnly.get(id) ?? row.acceptanceIds;\n**Option C, part 1: live gateway-stripped runs (REQ-PRV-106 part a).**\n- Nexus runs in a clean HOME with no homelab configuration: no `config.env` gateway entries, no gateway token file, no `X-Task-Class`.\n- It talks to `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` on `127.0.0.1`. The proxy forwards to the gateway with the gateway token injected on the proxy side. It strips every gateway extension: `/v1/models` is reduced to `{id, object, owned_by}`, `/v1/tokenize` returns 404, and `X-AIHost-*` response headers and admission headers are removed.\n- In a second profile, the proxy rewrites the `/models` and overflow-error shapes into the documented formats of llama.cpp `server`, vLLM and Ollama. That exercises each server kind's discovery and capacity-error path against real model output.\n- The standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 tasks) and the T4 subset run in both profiles.\n- The proxy only **removes** information. The gateway itself is unchanged, and all workload still flows through it, as the owner requires.\n\n**Option C, part 2: server-kind conformance (REQ-PRV-106 part b).**\n- Response-shape fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama are written from each project's published API documentation, with source references and versions recorded. They cover `/models`, `/props`, `/api/v0/models`, `/api/show`, SSE tool-call deltas, think tags and overflow bodies.\n- The fixtures run in CI.\n- Optionally, a CPU-only llama.cpp `server` built without AVX (this dev box is a Xeon X5650) with a ≤ 1.5B model is used for a protocol smoke test: one streamed reply, one tool call, one overflow. That is real server code, but task quality is out of scope.\n\n**Release statement:**\n- Release notes say: \"Live-qualified against llama.cpp-served models through a plain OpenAI-compatible interface (gateway extensions removed). vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama: protocol-conformance tested, not live-qualified.\"\n- LM Studio stays \"compatible, not live-qualified\" unless a user-run report is added.\n\n**Tradeoff:** live evidence for server kinds other than llama.cpp is limited to emulated shapes. This is stated plainly rather than over-claimed.\n\n**Affected:** REQ-PRV-106, REQ-QUAL-107; SPEC-05; SPEC-10; PLAN-05 task 7; PLAN-10; ACCEPTANCE §4.2. Owner action X3 (separate host) is withdrawn.\n\n## DEC-17: Token-estimator floor versus the calibration band\n\n**Question.** REQ-AGT-118 (SPEC-11 §2.7) requires the token estimator to be conservative for non-Latin scripts: **≥ 1 token per CJK, Hangul or kana character**. ACC-VER-07 requires the estimator to be **within 1.5× of a pinned tokenizer's count** for the CJK, digit, base64, emoji and prose corpora. For a tokenizer that merges common characters into multi-character tokens these two are mutually unsatisfiable.\n\n**Evidence (pinned worker `b0-live-llama-worker1`, limits_version `a3c2fcbc2f2b977c`; fixture `cli/test/fixtures/token_calibration.json`).**\n\n| Corpus | Characters | Estimator (floor) | Tokenizer reference | Ratio |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CJK common-word sentences × 50 | 400 | 400 | 200 | **2.00×** |\n| Hangul syllables × 200 | 200 | 200 | 120 | **1.67×** |\n\nThe floor forces 400 and 200 tokens; the band caps at 1.5 × 200 = 300 and 1.5 × 120 = 180. No estimator can satisfy both. This is a genuine, arithmetic inconsistency, not a measurement defect: the reference counts were re-measured on the pinned worker and the estimator was reproduced exactly.\n\n**Decision (chosen).** REQ-AGT-118's `≥ 1 token/char` floor is an **admission-safety** requirement, not an accuracy requirement: it guarantees the estimator never *under-admits* tokens for a non-Latin context, because an under-estimate silently overflows the context window (the failure class REQ-AGT-118 exists to prevent). ACC-VER-07's `≤ 1.5×` band is an **accuracy** target. The two are distinct properties, and where a merging tokenizer makes them collide the admission-safety floor takes precedence. ACC-VER-07 is therefore scoped to the corpora the floor does not dominate; for a merging tokenizer the floor-driven over-estimate is admitted as a **bounded admission-safety bias**. The `≤ 1.5×` accuracy threshold itself is **unchanged**.\n\nThis amendment is **narrow by design**. It applies only to corpora where the measured estimator is floor-bound — currently exactly the two in the table above — and it **does not silently exempt any other corpus**: any corpus whose estimator lands between the floor and the band must be examined and recorded (`tokens.test.ts` pins the floor-bound set to these two names and the full 14-corpus set, so neither an added exemption nor a silent corpus deletion can pass the test). The original accuracy failures are **preserved** — in the table above, in the fixture's `floorBound` entries, and in the base ledger wording (git history at `e1759ca`; the live row now records the amendment and stays `partial` until the changed tests pass and the amendment is independently accepted) — as recorded, failed accuracy evidence. They are not deleted or rewritten into passes.\n\n**Rejected alternatives.** (A) Lower the floor to satisfy the band — rejected: reintroduces under-estimation and the context-overflow class REQ-AGT-118 exists to prevent. (B) Drop the CJK/Hangul corpora from the fixture — rejected: removes the evidence. (C) Change the pinned tokenizer — out of scope; the fixture pins the qualification worker.\n\n**Affected:** REQ-AGT-118; SPEC-11 §2.7 and ACC-VER-07; REQUIREMENTS ledger row REQ-AGT-118; `cli/test/fixtures/token_calibration.json` and `cli/test/tokens.test.ts`. No change to `cli/src/tokens.ts` behaviour.\n\n## DEC-18: v1.0.0 terminal screenshot-artifact waiver\n\n**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\n\n**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\n132-  }\n133-  return result;\n134-}\n135-\n136-const rcQualificationOnly = qualificationOnlyRequirements();\n137-\n138:function qualificationExceptions() {\n139-  if (ledgerArg >= 0) return new Map();\n140-  const match = /<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->([\\s\\S]*?)<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->/.exec(acceptance);\n141-  const result = new Map();\n142-  if (!match) {\n143-    problems.push(\"ACCEPTANCE.md is missing the approved exact-RC qualification exception map\");\n144-    return result;\n--\n161-    }\n162-    result.set(id, decision);\n163-  }\n164-  return result;\n165-}\n166-\n167:const rcQualificationExceptions = qualificationExceptions();\n168-\n169-const sha256 = (file) => {\n170-  // Keep hashing synchronous with the checker's other filesystem validation.\n171-  return createHash(\"sha256\").update(fs.readFileSync(file)).digest(\"hex\");\n172-};\n173-function hasSymlinkComponent(absolutePath) {\n--\n267-      for (const [id, row] of requiredRows) {\n268-        const evidence = qualifiedRequirements[id];\n269-        if (!evidence) throw new Error(`missing qualification evidence for ${id}`);\n270-        if (!Object.hasOwn(RANK, evidence.status) || RANK[evidence.status] < RANK.tested) throw new Error(`${id}: qualification status is below tested`);\n271-        if (row.blocking && rcQualificationOnly.has(id) && evidence.status !== \"product-qualified\") throw new Error(`${id}: exact-RC qualification requires product-qualified status`);\n272-        if (row.blocking && evidence.status !== \"product-qualified\") {\n273:          const decision = evidence.qualificationNotApplicable?.decision;\n274-          const approvedDecision = rcQualificationExceptions.get(id);\n275:          const decisionExists = new RegExp(`^\\\\s*[-*]\\\\s*Qualification applicability:\\\\s*${id}\\\\s*=\\\\s*NOT REQUIRED\\\\b`, \"m\").test(decisionSection(decision));\n276:          if (evidence.status !== \"tested\" || typeof evidence.qualificationNotApplicable?.reason !== \"string\" || !evidence.qualificationNotApplicable.reason.trim() || decision !== approvedDecision || !decisionExists) throw new Error(`${id}: blocker must be product-qualified or tested with an explicitly approved decision and qualification-not-applicable reason`);\n277-        }\n278-        if (!Array.isArray(evidence.evidence) || evidence.evidence.length === 0) throw new Error(`${id}: qualification evidence references are required`);\n279-        const requiredAccs = rcQualificationOnly.get(id) ?? row.acceptanceIds;\n280-        const evidenceAccs = evidence.evidence.map((ref) => ref?.id);\n281-        if (requiredAccs.length === 0 || requiredAccs.some((accId) => !evidenceAccs.includes(accId)) || evidenceAccs.some((accId) => !requiredAccs.includes(accId))) throw new Error(`${id}: qualification evidence must cover every acceptance criterion specified for the requirement`);\n282-        for (const ref of evidence.evidence) {\n| REQ-QUAL-102 | DEC-05 | Matched conditions with a model fingerprint. | validity | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/validate.mjs` | TEST (EVL-004; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"a qualification run is refused without a model fingerprint\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EV