real-terminal matrix. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | TEST (PTY suites in CI); UNV (real terminals) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §5 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n| REQ-QUAL-109 | eval/README T3 | T3 long tasks: 8 × 5. | long-task workflow | `eval/` | — | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.3 | RR | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n| REQ-QUAL-110 | Audit | T1 self-test and a T4 smoke run in `make test`. | regression | `eval_harness.test.ts` | TEST (test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke: an overloaded endpoint is waited out\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | RR | — | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n\n## 4. Contest requirements (separate product; not client gates)\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27466}},"started_at_ms":1793242034297,"completed_at_ms":1793242034298}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T02:47:15.715Z","ordinal":486002,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1858d-f603-7d23-9c20-2cbdafbc56c8","call_id":"call_4854a4750b19403ca588fa61782151a5","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 11748)\nTotal output lines: 275\n\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-28-5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-29-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-30-The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-31-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-33-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-34-The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-35-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-36-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-47-| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-48-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-50-| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-52-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-53-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-54-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-55-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-106-These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-107-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-108-| ID | Check | Pass condition |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-109-|---|---|---|\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:110:| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:111:| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-113-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-114-| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-117-| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | **Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** No per-cell verdicts are recorded; this is not a PASS. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 remain required. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-122-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-123-## 4. Stan