CCEPTANCE.md-339-- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-340-- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\n--\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-243-**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-244-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-245-**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-246-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:247:**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-248-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:249:## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-250-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-251-**Context.** [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waived screenshot artifacts only; the fifteen manual matrix cells (five terminals × three sizes, ACCEPTANCE §5.3) remained mandatory. On 2026-10-29 the release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-252-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:253:**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-29).** The manual E3 matrix, its per-cell PASS/FAIL verdicts and its evidence records are not required for v1.0.0. ACC-TUI-MANUAL is **waived**, not PASS: no cell verdict is recorded and none may be inferred. The automated CI PTY suites and the scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2) remain mandatory and are the only terminal evidence for this release. This waiver changes no other acceptance criterion, safety gate, or verification rule, and it does not change any requirements-ledger status: REQ-QUAL-108 remains `partial` unless the ledger owner records a different disposition.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-254-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-255-**Disclosure.** The v1.0.0 release notes must state that the manual real-terminal matrix was waived by owner decision and that terminal evidence is automated (PTY/CI) only.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-256-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:257:**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-258-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-259-## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-260-\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-261-| # | Action | Why | When |\n--\norigin/main:docs/…5248 tokens truncated…\\b`, \"m\").test(decisionSection(decision));\norigin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs-276-          if (evidence.status !== \"tested\" || typeof evidence.qualificationNotApplicable?.reason !== \"string\" || !evidence.qualificationNotApplicable.reason.trim() || decision !== approvedDecision || !decisionExists) throw new Error(`${id}: blocker must be product-qualified or tested with an explicitly approved decision and qualification-not-applicable reason`);\norigin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs-277-        }\norigin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs-278-        if (!Array.isArray(evidence.evidence) || evidence.evidence.length === 0) throw new Error(`${id}: qualification evidence references are required`);\norigin/main:scripts/check_requirements.mjs-279-        const requiredAccs = rcQualificationOnly.get(id) ?? row.acceptanceIds;\n**Option C, part 1: live gateway-stripped runs (REQ-PRV-106 part a).**\n- Nexus runs in a clean HOME with no homelab configuration: no `config.env` gateway entries, no gateway token file, no `X-Task-Class`.\n- It talks to `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` on `127.0.0.1`. The proxy forwards to the gateway with the gateway token injected on the proxy side. It strips every gateway extension: `/v1/models` is reduced to `{id, object, owned_by}`, `/v1/tokenize` returns 404, and `X-AIHost-*` response headers and admission headers are removed.\n- In a second profile, the proxy rewrites the `/models` and overflow-error shapes into the documented formats of llama.cpp `server`, vLLM and Ollama. That exercises each server kind's discovery and capacity-error path against real model output.\n- The standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 tasks) and the T4 subset run in both profiles.\n- The proxy only **removes** information. The gateway itself is unchanged, and all workload still flows through it, as the owner requires.\n\n**Option C, part 2: server-kind conformance (REQ-PRV-106 part b).**\n- Response-shape fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama are written from each project's published API documentation, with source references and versions recorded. They cover `/models`, `/props`, `/api/v0/models`, `/api/show`, SSE tool-call deltas, think tags and overflow bodies.\n- The fixtures run in CI.\n- Optionally, a CPU-only llama.cpp `server` built without AVX (this dev box is a Xeon X5650) with a ≤ 1.5B model is used for a protocol smoke test: one streamed reply, one tool call, one overflow. That is real server code, but task quality is out of scope.\n\n**Release statement:**\n- Release notes say: \"Live-qualified against llama.cpp-served models through a plain OpenAI-compatible interface (gateway extensions removed). vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama: protocol-conformance tested, not live-qualified.\"\n- LM Studio stays \"compatible, not live-qualified\" unless a user-run report is added.\n\n**Tradeoff:** live evidence for server kinds other than llama.cpp is limited to emulated shapes. This is stated plainly rather than over-claimed.\n\n**Affected:** REQ-PRV-106, REQ-QUAL-107; SPEC-05; SPEC-10; PLAN-05 task 7; PLAN-10; ACCEPTANCE §4.2. Owner action X3 (separate host) is withdrawn.\n\n## DEC-17: Token-estimator floor versus the calibration band\n\n**Question.** REQ-AGT-118 (SPEC-11 §2.7) requires the token estimator to be conservative for non-Latin scripts: **≥ 1 token per CJK, Hangul or kana character**. ACC-VER-07 requires the estimator to be **within 1.5× of a pinned tokenizer's count** for the CJK, digit, base64, emoji and prose corpora. For a tokenizer that merges common characters into multi-character tokens these two are mutually unsatisfiable.\n\n**Evidence (pinned worker `b0-live-llama-worker1`, limits_version `a3c2fcbc2f2b977c`; fixture `cli/test/fixtures/token_calibration.json`).**\n\n| Corpus | Characters | Estimator (floor) | Tokenizer reference | Ratio |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CJK common-word sentences × 50 | 400 | 400 | 200 | **2.00×** |\n| Hangul syllables × 200 | 200 | 200 | 120 | **1.67×** |\n\nThe floor forces 400 and 200 tokens; the band caps at 1.5 × 200 = 300 and 1.5 × 120 = 180. No estimator can satisfy both. This is a genuine, arithmetic inconsistency, not a measurement defect: the reference counts were re-measured on the pinned worker and the estimator was reproduced exactly.\n\n**Decision (chosen).** REQ-AGT-118's `≥ 1 token/char` floor is an **admission-safety** requirement, not an accuracy requirement: it guarantees the estimator never *under-admits* tokens for a non-Latin context, because an under-estimate silently overflows the context window (the failure class REQ-AGT-118 exists to prevent). ACC-VER-07's `≤ 1.5×` band is an **accuracy** target. The two are distinct properties, and where a merging tokenizer makes them collide the admission-safety floor takes precedence. ACC-VER-07 is therefore scoped to the corpora the floor does not dominate; for a merging tokenizer the floor-driven over-estimate is admitted as a **bounded admission-safety bias**. The `≤ 1.5×` accuracy threshold itself is **unchanged**.\n\nThis amendment is **narrow by design**. It applies only to corpora where the measured estimator is floor-bound — currently exactly the two in the table above — and it **does not silently exempt any other corpus**: any corpus whose estimator lands between the floor and the band must be examined and recorded (`tokens.test.ts` pins the floor-bound set to these two names and the full 14-corpus set, so neither an added exemption nor a silent corpus deletion can pass the test). The original accuracy failures are **preserved** — in the table above, in the fixture's `floorBound` entries, and in the base ledger wording (git history at `e1759ca`; the live row now records the amendment and stays `partial` until the changed tests pass and the amendment is independently accepted) — as recorded, failed accuracy evidence. They are not deleted or rewritten into passes.\n\n**Rejected alternatives.** (A) Lower the floor to satisfy the band — rejected: reintroduces under-estimation and the context-overflow class REQ-AGT-118 exists to prevent. (B) Drop the CJK/Hangul corpora from the fixture — rejected: removes the evidence. (C) Change the pinned tokenizer — out of scope; the fixture pins the qualification worker.\n\n**Affected:** REQ-AGT-118; SPEC-11 §2.7 and ACC-VER-07; REQUIREMENTS ledger row REQ-AGT-118; `cli/test/fixtures/token_calibration.json` and `cli/test/tokens.test.ts`. No change to `cli/src/tokens.ts` behaviour.\n\n## DEC-18: v1.0.0 terminal screenshot-artifact waiver\n\n**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\n\n**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\n132-  }\n133-  return result;\n134-}\n135-\n136-const rcQualificationOnly = qualificationOnlyRequirements();\n137-\n138:function qualificationExceptions() {\n139-  if (ledgerArg >= 0) return new Map();\n140-  const match = /<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->([\\s\\S]*?)<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->/.exec(acceptance);\n141-  const result = new Map();\n142-  if (!match) {\n143-    problems.push(\"ACCEPTANCE.md is missing the approved exact-RC qualification exception map\");\n144-    return result;\n--\n161-    }\n162-    result.set(id, decision);\n163-  }\n164-  return result;\n165-}\n166-\n167:const rcQualificationExceptions = qualificationExceptions();\n168-\n169-const sha256 = (file) => {\n170-  // Keep hashing synchronous with the checker's other filesystem validation.\n171-  return createHash(\"sha256\").update(fs.readFileSync(file)).digest(\"hex\");\n172-};\n173-function hasSymlinkComponent(absolutePath) {\n--\n267-      for (const [id, row] of requiredRows) {\n268-        const evidence = qualifiedRequirements[id];\n269-        if (!evidence) throw new Error(`missing qualification evidence for ${id}`);\n270-        if (!Object.hasOwn(RANK, evidence.status) || RANK[evidence.status] < RANK.tested) throw new Error(`${id}: qualification status is below tested`);\n271-        if (row.blocking && rcQualificationOnly.has(id) && evidence.status !== \"product-qualified\") throw new Error(`${id}: exact-RC qualification requires product-qualified status`);\n272-        if (row.blocking && evidence.status !== \"product-qualified\") {\n273:          const decision = evidence.qualificationNotApplicable?.decision;\n274-          const approvedDecision = rcQualificationExceptions.get(id);\n275:          const decisionExists = new RegExp(`^\\\\s*[-*]\\\\s*Qualification applicability:\\\\s*${id}\\\\s*=\\\\s*NOT REQUIRED\\\\b`, \"m\").test(decisionSection(decision));\n276:          if (evidence.status !== \"tested\" || typeof evidence.qualificationNotApplicable?.reason !== \"string\" || !evidence.qualificationNotApplicable.reason.trim() || decision !== approvedDecision || !decisionExists) throw new Error(`${id}: blocker must be product-qualified or tested with an explicitly approved decision and qualification-not-applicable reason`);\n277-        }\n278-        if (!Array.isArray(evidence.evidence) || evidence.evidence.length === 0) throw new Error(`${id}: qualification evidence references are required`);\n279-        const requiredAccs = rcQualificationOnly.get(id) ?? row.acceptanceIds;\n280-        const evidenceAccs = evidence.evidence.map((ref) => ref?.id);\n281-        if (requiredAccs.length === 0 || requiredAccs.some((accId) => !evidenceAccs.includes(accId)) || evidenceAccs.some((accId) => !requiredAccs.includes(accId))) throw new Error(`${id}: qualification evidence must cover every acceptance criterion specified for the requirement`);\n282-        for (const ref of evidence.evidence) {\n| REQ-QUAL-102 | DEC-05 | Matched conditions with a model fingerprint. | validity | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/validate.mjs` | TEST (EVL-004; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"a qualification run is refused without a model fingerprint\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-004 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n| REQ-QUAL-103 | DEC-05 | 5 runs per task and configuration; Goose and OpenCode as peers. | statistics | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (`eval_harness.test.ts`: peer version/budget forwarding, installed RC/version/package pin, Nexus/provider-limit parity, paired fingerprint/limit/sampling/budget/version and 5-run checks; commits `ef2d040`, `b27ae04`; [validation record](../reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_PR-10d/validation.md)); UNV (live M5 runs) | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n| REQ-QUAL-104 | DEC-05 | Separately reported metrics, including false VERIFIED = 0. | honesty | `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (EVL-005; test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts, test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts) | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-005 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n| REQ-QUAL-105 | TOP_TIER Q6; DEC-05 | T4 fault injection: 9 classes × 5 runs (DEC-05 amendment 2026-10-17: union of the nine distinct scenarios retained), 100% truthful outcomes. | failure / recovery | `eval/model_proxy.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (EVL-001; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"the model proxy injects each scheduled fault\", test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T4 (ACCEPTANCE §6.2) | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n| REQ-QUAL-106 | Audit | Scoring integrity (symmetric infra handling, contamination, hidden tests). | validity | `eval/infra.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs` | TEST (EVL-002, EVL-003; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"contaminated runs leave the pass rate\", test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"infrastructure reruns use one rule\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-002, EVL-003, VER-07 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n| REQ-QUAL-107 | Standalone; DEC-06 | Standalone and provider live matrix. | standalone | — | HIST | open | ACCEPTANCE §4.2, §4.3 | **B** | HIST-08 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | PTY CI plus a manual real-terminal matrix. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | TEST (PTY suites in CI); UNV (real terminals) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §5 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n| REQ-QUAL-109 | eval/README T3 | T3 long tasks: 8 × 5. | long-task workflow | `eval/` | — | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.3 | RR | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n| REQ-QUAL-110 | Audit | T1 self-test and a T4 smoke run in `make test`. | regression | `eval_harness.test.ts` | TEST (test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke: an overloaded endpoint is waited out\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | RR | — | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n\n## 4. Contest requirements (separate product; not client gates)\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1858a-59ca-7ee1-85ff-8d21499b2944","create_time":1793242035.715741}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
