{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T02:49:08.620Z","ordinal":486070,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0db389702a7164cc016ae2b41fc8e4819fa6a44cff8af3eb68","status":"completed","call_id":"call_65df34445c9e40a3823fcf9d750def84","name":"exec","input":"const patch=\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/dec19-terminal-waiver-reconcile/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\\n@@\\n-| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\\n+| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | CI PTY checks and installed-RC scripted PTY scenarios (§5.1–§5.2); the manual matrix is waived by DEC-19 |\\n@@\\n-Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); this does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\\n+For successor-release qualification, record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts were waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); that screenshot waiver did not waive checks for a release where the matrix applied. The v1.0.0 manual matrix itself is waived by DEC-19 above.\\n@@\\n-**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\\n+**Successor-release gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/dec19-terminal-waiver-reconcile/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\\n@@\\n-| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Run the full checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3 and record all per-cell outcomes and evidence. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). | ACCEPTANCE §5.3; DEC-18 | RC build |\\n+| 12 | Manual terminal matrix: waived for v1.0.0 by [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver), not passed; no manual cells or evidence are required. Retain the five-environment × three-size procedure in ACCEPTANCE §5.3 for a successor release. CI PTY and installed-RC scripted PTY scenarios in ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2 remain required for v1.0.0. | ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.3; DEC-19 | v1.0.0 automated PTY gates; manual matrix for a successor release |\\n@@\\n-- REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-108 evidence is archived.\\n+- Applicable evidence for REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-108 is archived. For REQ-QUAL-108, record ACC-TUI-MANUAL as waived, not passed, under DEC-19; the CI and installed-RC scripted PTY criteria remain required.\\n*** End Patch\";\nconst r=await tools.apply_patch(patch);\ntext(r);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1858a-59ca-7ee1-85ff-8d21499b2944","create_time":1793242143.786286}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T02:49:08.660Z","ordinal":486071,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1858a-59ca-7ee1-85ff-8d21499b2944","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-1cc2ea45-f5fe-4ea0-b2d3-ccc345e0834f","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/dec19-terminal-waiver-reconcile/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -35,3 +35,3 @@\n | 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\n-| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Run the full checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3 and record all per-cell outcomes and evidence. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). | ACCEPTANCE §5.3; DEC-18 | RC build |\n+| 12 | Manual terminal matrix: waived for v1.0.0 by [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver), not passed; no manual cells or evidence are required. Retain the five-environment × three-size procedure in ACCEPTANCE §5.3 for a successor release. CI PTY and installed-RC scripted PTY scenarios in ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2 remain required for v1.0.0. | ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.3; DEC-19 | v1.0.0 automated PTY gates; manual matrix for a successor release |\n \n@@ -67,3 +67,3 @@\n \n-- REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-108 evidence is archived.\n+- Applicable evidence for REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-108 is archived. For REQ-QUAL-108, record ACC-TUI-MANUAL as waived, not passed, under DEC-19; the CI and installed-RC scripted PTY criteria remain required.\n - The DEC-05 thresholds were evaluated with the scorer verdict table, signed off before the run and reported after it.\n","move_path":null},"/home/mike/nexus-wt/dec19-terminal-waiver-reconcile/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -50,3 +50,3 @@\n | REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n-| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n+| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | CI PTY checks and installed-RC scripted PTY scenarios (§5.1–§5.2); the manual matrix is waived by DEC-19 |\n | REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n@@ -205,5 +205,5 @@\n \n-Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); this does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\n+For successor-release qualification, record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts were waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); that screenshot waiver did not waive checks for a release where the matrix applied. The v1.0.0 manual matrix itself is waived by DEC-19 above.\n \n-**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n+**Successor-release gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/dec19-terminal-waiver-reconcile/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/dec19-terminal-waiver-reconcile/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793242148656,"completed_at_ms":1793242148660}}
