{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T02:49:31.157Z","ordinal":486087,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1858a-59ca-7ee1-85ff-8d21499b2944","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ebaa8990-396d-4887-b1c0-0548da9764b8","process_id":"3505","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","for p in .git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_specs_SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md .git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md; do echo \"--- $p\"; test -f \"$p/owner.json\" && cat \"$p/owner.json\" || echo absent; done; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md | rg -n -C 3 'REQ-QUAL-108|manual real-terminal|terminal matrix|ACC-TUI'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md | sed -n '1,70p'; rg -n 'FILE_docs_v1.0.0_(specs_SPEC-10|TERMINAL-MATRIX)' .git/nexus-claims.log | tail -n 15"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"for p in .git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_specs_SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md .git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md; do echo \"--- $p\"; test -f \"$p/owner.json\" && cat \"$p/owner.json\" || echo absent; done; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md | rg -n -C 3 'REQ-QUAL-108|manual real-terminal|terminal matrix|ACC-TUI'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md | sed -n '1,70p'; rg -n 'FILE_docs_v1.0.0_(specs_SPEC-10|TERMINAL-MATRIX)' .git/nexus-claims.log | tail -n 15"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"--- .git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_specs_SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\nabsent\n--- .git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\nabsent\n3-| | |\n4-|---|---|\n5-| Status | Ready. Protocol and thresholds fixed by [DEC-05](../DECISIONS.md#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds); task authorship needs owner action X2. |\n6:| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\n7:| Requirements | REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-102, REQ-QUAL-103, REQ-QUAL-104, REQ-QUAL-105, REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 |\n8-| Findings | EVL-001, EVL-002, EVL-003, EVL-004, EVL-005, HIST-08, PRV G1/G2, TUI gaps (kitty/real terminals), VER-07 |\n9-| Plan | [PLAN-10](../plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) |\n10-| Acceptance | ACCEPTANCE.md §4–§7 |\n--\n80-   - The scorer logs every replacement.\n81-   - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\n82-7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n83:8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts) are mandatory. A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. **The manual matrix is waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)**; no per-cell verdicts are recorded and this is not a PASS. Screenshot artifacts were waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). Automated terminal evidence is the only terminal evidence for this release.\n84-9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0, false-presence = 0 (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-18), and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\n85-10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\n86-\n# Manual real-terminal acceptance worksheet\n\nFor `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3).\n\n> **Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** This worksheet is retained for a successor release. It contains no results, no cell verdict is recorded for v1.0.0, and it does not qualify an RC.\n\n## Installed candidate identity\n\nFill these fields from the installed candidate before the first cell. Do not copy identity from a source branch or local build.\n\n- RC tag: ______________________________________________\n- Full RC source commit: ________________________________\n- Installed package/archive name and location: ____________\n- Installed artifact SHA256: ____________________________\n- Installation procedure/run reference: __________________\n- `nexus --version` output reference: ____________________\n- Operator and UTC date/time: ____________________________\n- Host OS and version: __________________________________\n- Per-cell evidence record directory or reference: ________\n\nRecord the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\n\n| Environment | Version / protocol details |\n|---|---|\n| xterm | |\n| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | |\n| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux: ; GNOME Terminal: |\n| VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code: ; integrated terminal profile: |\n| GNOME Terminal | |\n\n## Procedure to perform in every matrix cell\n\nRun each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by that row. Record the observations and evidence references for the cell.\n\n1. Launch `nexus`; confirm the TUI appears.\n2. At the approval panel, type continuously across it, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Exercise multiline input with Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Press Esc during `sleep 30`; confirm no child processes survive.\n6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm clean terminal restoration (echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\n\nScreenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). This does not waive any live manual interaction, check, observation, per-cell verdict, or evidence record. Automated PTY runs do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\n\n## Terminal × size results\n\nSelect exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Record observed outcomes for every check and a per-cell evidence reference bound to the installed RC identity, terminal environment, and size. Record failures in the disposition/notes field.\n\n| # | Terminal environment | Size | Verdict (select one) | Per-cell evidence / result reference | Failure disposition / notes |\n|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|\n| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n\n## Acceptance gate\n\n- Safety checks 2, 5, and 6: **zero failures across all 15 cells**. Any failure here blocks this gate.\n- Any failure on another check requires a written disposition: fix, or a documented known limitation.\n594:2026-10-18T11:01:56Z CLAIM PLAN-10_T3_SEAL_DEC05 + FILE_eval_heldout-t3-manifest.json + FILE_docs_v1.0.0_DECISIONS.md + FILE_docs_v1.0.0_specs_SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md branch=v1/t3-seal-and-dec05 by=opencode (custodian)\n697:2026-10-18T12:26:35Z CLAIM PLAN-10_SPEC10_BOUNDARY_RECONCILIATION + FILE_docs_v1.0.0_specs_SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md branch=v1/plan-10-spec10-boundary-reconciliation scope=correct SPEC-10 stale evaluator isolation statement only; no scope expansion by=codex-lead\n2872:2026-10-23T00:06:42Z CLAIM FILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md agent=/root/acceptance_stage_clarification branch=v1/qual108-terminal-worksheet base=1da67c3622f7290944a496a58965606961a5afc0 scope=worksheet_15_terminal_size_cells\n2874:2026-10-23T00:08:45Z RELEASE CLAIM=FILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md owner=/root/acceptance_stage_clarification branch=v1/qual108-terminal-worksheet head=33732a3c244b163b307f472752be4a4e92cc2c18 independent_review=ACCEPT result=handoff_to_root_no_push_no_PR_branch_preserved\n3015:2026-10-23T09:14:48Z\tCLAIM\tFILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\t/root\tRC3-bound human terminal procedure preparation; no result claims\n3024:2026-10-23T09:30:00Z\tREVIEW\tFILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\t/root\tplan05_readonly_review ACCEPT for 986eed0; candidate identity and all 15 manual cells verified; blank results, no qualification claim\n3909:2026-10-25T05:47:00Z /root: FILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md candidate 2b55c031 independently ACCEPTed by current_main_rc_path