ivate\\n' \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" >> \"$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log\"; LOG=/var/tmp/nexus-custody-t2-conversion-20261029.log; opencode run --session ses_e7a8b8dedffeHBmmoNyBTmvt7l --format json 'Proceed with the accepted custodian workflow under CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION. Perform the T2 conversion to blackbox-v1 and complete the required setup/reference/oracle revalidation, preserving the original sealed store byte-for-byte and using a separately versioned successor store and new immutable manifest identity. Re-derive private digests and repeat custody checks. Then perform fresh T3 custody acceptance against the existing sealed identity. Follow all repository concurrency rules: isolated HOME/XDG for tests/probes, acquire SUITE before any test and do not run tests while another owner holds it, and never run qualification. Do not weaken the blackbox-v1 security boundary or enable legacy validators. Do not post payloads, objectives, validators, answers, patches, credentials, private digests, or protected content publicly. Publish only pass/fail counts, new immutable manifest identity, custody disposition, and next checkpoint through the approved metadata-only channel. Work autonomously through conversion/revalidation and T3 acceptance, then stop for independent review.' > \"$LOG\" 2>&1; status=$?; printf 'custodian_session_exit=%s raw_log_mode=%s raw_log_path=%s\\n' \"$status\" \"$(stat -c %a \"$LOG\")\" \"$LOG\"; exit \"$status\"\n3922403 3922402 S       18:13 node scripts/run_tests.mjs\n  ✔ a directory replaced by a link between diagnosis and repair is left alone (231.968401ms)\n  ✔ a cloud provider is diagnosed with that provider's protocol and credential (244.363069ms)\n✔ repair safety and provider-specific requests (677.884991ms)\n▶ repairs cannot be redirected by links anywhere in the path\n  ✔ a linked parent (~/.nexus -> elsewhere) gets no repair, and --fix changes nothing outside (126.991426ms)\n  ✔ ~/.nexus swapped for a link after the diagnosis: repairs, lock and backups stand down (434.312447ms)\n  ✔ a linked credentials parent (~/.config -> elsewhere) gets no repair (266.766851ms)\n  ✔ a planted lock link is never followed or written through (118.63542ms)\n  ✔ the change is bound to the verified object: a final or parent swap after diagnosis is detected (16.175232ms)\n  ✔ failed exclusive creation never unlinks a pathname that may have been replaced (18.057562ms)\n  ✔ failed directory creation never removes a pathname that may have been replaced (13.32725ms)\n✔ repairs cannot be redirected by links anywhere in the path (996.180822ms)\n▶ entry points share one engine\n  ✔ `nexus doctor --json` through the packaged launcher: isolated home, mock endpoint, exit code (5280.182053ms)\n  ✔ an invalid option is a doctor execution error (exit 3) with machine-readable JSON (488.613956ms)\n  ✔ help documents flags, exit codes and the repair scope (454.856466ms)\n  ✔ the session context diagnoses the session's own configuration (108.680994ms)\n✔ entry points share one engine (6333.263286ms)\n▶ SPEC-06 PR-6d requirements (ACC-PKG-06..09, REQ-DX-101..104)\n  ✔ ACC-PKG-06 (REQ-DX-101): doctor stderr is empty on a healthy run (no MaxListenersExceededWarning) (954.749719ms)\n  ✔ ACC-PKG-07 (REQ-DX-101): packaged doctor remedies contain no make or harness.sh (701.792351ms)\n  ✔ ACC-PKG-08 (REQ-DX-102): config.env at 0644 gives a warning and repair; --fix --yes sets 0600 (339.06894ms)\n  ✔ ACC-PKG-09 (REQ-DX-103): workspace path with a UUID segment appears unredacted in doctor output (95.402222ms)\n  ✔ REQ-DX-104: tui.launch verifies launchability via nexus-tui --live --check (96.148593ms)\n✔ SPEC-06 PR-6d requirements (ACC-PKG-06..09, REQ-DX-101..104) (2188.188135ms)\n✔ all source AutonomousAgent construction sites declare durability explicitly (20.768595ms)\n- Nexus is considering the next step\n✔ Nexus is considering the next step\n- Working: task_completed\n✔ Working: task_completed\n✔ AgentWorkUnitExecutor default construction persists a durable depth-1 implementer with its unit identity (3905.230589ms)\n✔ AgentWorkUnitExecutor applies durable identity when a custom factory omits constructor options (3524.395816ms)\n✔ ACC-CONT-03: pressure compaction of a work unit survives SIGKILL and restores archived markers (6802.534344ms)\n▶ V2: unverified changes survive retries, step limits, restarts and resumes\n  ✔ retry after UNVERIFIED: the resumed attempt changes nothing, the unit stays unverified and its dependent never runs (6878.975917ms)\n2026-10-29 02:54:09.257463067 +0000 400603 /var/tmp/nexus-trail23-suite-final2.log\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"2026-10-29T02:54:17Z\n706c3b6c docs(release): align terminal waiver qualification gates\n docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md                                    |  6 +++---\n docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md                     | 12 ++++++------\n docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md |  4 ++--\n docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md |  2 +-\n 4 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1858a-59ca-7ee1-85ff-8d21499b2944","create_time":1793242462.9091344}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
