{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T02:56:35.075Z","ordinal":486403,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18596-7f03-7810-89dd-b3222321b48a","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** for PR #315’s documentation diff. Reviewed base `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` → head `706c3b6cda2577f1ee3ae3665c42859045a9dfa2`. Cumulative diff SHA-256: `7fe68b53f754a5a33b6edbac53d63562957e71e82eb5a1746321f90430628b44`.\n\nThe changed acceptance map, worksheet, PLAN-10, and SPEC-10 consistently treat DEC-19 as a v1.0.0 manual-matrix waiver, not a pass; they retain the CI and scripted PTY gates and the successor-release matrix procedure. DEC-18 remains the separate screenshot-artifact waiver. REQUIREMENTS.md is unchanged.\n\nREADINESS.md is outside this diff and remains separately owned; its current checkpoint still needs reconciliation of manual-matrix status. This PR’s body explicitly calls out that separate work.\n\nI could not record the disposition on **Entire trail 30**: the only configured Entire context reports “Not logged in,” and trail access failed because `org.freedesktop.secrets` has no service on this host. I did not use the repository owner’s GitHub identity. At review time, Node 22/24 and Entire Gates were still running. No tests were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18596-7e75-7860-a296-7929a9fdc208","create_time":1793242595.0752907,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":22925}}
