{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:00:23.208Z","ordinal":486572,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18599-fa27-7611-a30e-d864e35b1c52","call_id":"call_09222b9f93594e7a95c434e0e48f8033","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"PR #311 is open at head `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954`. Current `main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`; GitHub reports the PR branch is **2 commits behind** and 32 ahead.\\n\\nThe ruleset requires `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64`. All three pass at the exact PR head. `Entire Gates` is not required. Its diagnostic reports two failures: no reviewer has approved the Entire trail, and the branch is two commits behind. Its Checks and Findings gates passed.\\n\\nNext owner action: update the PR branch with current `main`, push, and let required checks rerun. Then arrange an eligible reviewer’s approval in the Entire trail if that gate still needs clearing. No branch changes or test runs were made.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — PR #315’s exact head `706c3b6` against base `b10a85a` preserves DEC-19’s boundaries: exact-RC evidence retains CI and installed-RC scripted PTY gates; the manual matrix is **WAIVED, not PASS**, with the 5×3 procedure retained for successor releases. `REQUIREMENTS.md` is unchanged.\\n\\nI could not submit an independent PR or Entire disposition. GitHub authentication is for `mikeholownych`, the PR owner, and Entire could not load its active login token because the host’s `org.freedesktop.secrets` service is unavailable. An independent reviewer must authenticate through a working keyring, inspect the trail linked to PR #315 and confirm its exact head before submitting the branch approval. No approval was submitted.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for PR #315’s documentation diff. Reviewed base `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` → head `706c3b6cda2577f1ee3ae3665c42859045a9dfa2`. Cumulative diff SHA-256: `7fe68b53f754a5a33b6edbac53d63562957e71e82eb5a1746321f90430628b44`.\\n\\nThe changed acceptance map, worksheet, PLAN-10, and SPEC-10 consistently treat DEC-19 as a v1.0.0 manual-matrix waiver, not a pass; they retain the CI and scripted PTY gates and the successor-release matrix procedure. DEC-18 remains the separate screenshot-artifact waiver. REQUIREMENTS.md is unchanged.\\n\\nREADINESS.md is outside this diff and remains separately owned; its current checkpoint still needs reconciliation of manual-matrix status. This PR’s body explicitly calls out that separate work.\\n\\nI could not record the disposition on **Entire trail 30**: the only configured Entire context reports “Not logged in,” and trail access failed because `org.freedesktop.secrets` has no service on this host. I did not use the repository owner’s GitHub identity. At review time, Node 22/24 and Entire Gates were still running. No tests were run.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18597-d111-7772-bdaa-82d57dc21887","create_time":1793242823.2078378}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
