{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:01:21.474Z","ordinal":486597,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18597-d111-7772-bdaa-82d57dc21887","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18597-d111-7772-bdaa-82d57dc21887","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae2b6fadda4819fb926455512caeaad","usage":{"input_tokens":147887,"cached_input_tokens":146816,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":782,"reasoning_output_tokens":695,"total_tokens":148669},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2170197,"cached_input_tokens":2135808,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":10909,"reasoning_output_tokens":8240,"total_tokens":2181106},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9081280803,"cached_input_tokens":8984511616,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":26066661,"reasoning_output_tokens":15197974,"total_tokens":9107347464}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:01:22.719Z","ordinal":486598,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18597-d111-7772-bdaa-82d57dc21887","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bf21df5f-153f-47a9-a5b4-18192bafe87d","process_id":"76238","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -C 3 'stale|handoff|transfer|release|24 hours|owner' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -C 3 'stale|handoff|transfer|release|24 hours|owner' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md","query":"stale|handoff|transfer|release|24 hours|owner","path":"CONCURRENCY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"25-SLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\n26-if mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n27-  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n28:    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\n29-else\n30:  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\n31-fi\n32-```\n33-\n34:- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n35-- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n36:- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n37-- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n38-\n39-## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n40-\n41-| Resource | Rule |\n42-|---|---|\n43:| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n44-| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n45-| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n46-| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n--\n52-\n53-## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n54-\n55:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n56-\n57-| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\n58-|---|---|---|\n--\n84-2. Commits are scoped to the slice. Do not reformat or clean up files outside the boundary.\n85-3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n86-4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n87:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n88-6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n89-\n90-## 6. Coordination records\n--\n92-| Record | Where | Purpose |\n93-|---|---|---|\n94-| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n95:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n96-| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n97-| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n98-\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27632}},"started_at_ms":1793242882719,"completed_at_ms":1793242882719}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:01:23.991Z","ordinal":486599,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1859a-e797-7203-a88c-968ecc664cd6","call_id":"call_ff93cb5848504708874c1a3d5b1e55e3","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"25-SLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\n26-if mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n27-  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n28:    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\n29-else\n30:  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\n31-fi\n32-```\n33-\n34:- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n35-- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n36:- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n37-- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n38-\n39-## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n40-\n41-| Resource | Rule |\n42-|---|---|\n43:| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n44-| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n45-| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n46-| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n--\n52-\n53-## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n54-\n55:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n56-\n57-| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\n58-|---|---|---|\n--\n84-2. Commits are scoped to the slice. Do not reformat or clean up files outside the boundary.\n85-3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n86-4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n87:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n88-6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n89-\n90-## 6. Coordination records\n--\n92-| Record | Where | Purpose |\n93-|---|---|---|\n94-| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n95:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n96-| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n97-| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n98-\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18597-d111-7772-bdaa-82d57dc21887","create_time":1793242883.9914958}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
