ithub.fetch"},{"first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"fetch_topic"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15e3e-2987-7e62-9699-29ab11a9d023","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_issues"},{"first_turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"observation_search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a17ded-e7ae-7300-8479-0fca92a43367","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_user_login"},{"first_turn_id":"01a18105-4b30-7810-8340-21a990975e0a","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"get_observations"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_search"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_field_report"},{"first_turn_id":"01a18508-75af-7cb3-abdc-d10cbdc7b2fb","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"summarize_recent"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a18597-d111-7772-bdaa-82d57dc21887","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a18597-d111-7772-bdaa-82d57dc21887","turn_id":"01a18597-d111-7772-bdaa-82d57dc21887","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2b548355c819fa2e954772b9ff094","order":22918,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18594-251f-74f2-9fd6-e019b085e25f","text":"PR #315 is open on the intended branch and its exact-head checks are still running. The Entire Brain knows this worktree but has no synced branch facts; checkpoint search is blocked by the host keyring service. I’ve asked the prior independent reviewer to review this exact PR head while I check the active suite and custody lanes without touching their worktrees.","turn_id":"01a1858a-59ca-7ee1-85ff-8d21499b2944"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2b5c2f8fc819fafd572fd08602d64","order":22924,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a18596-08bd-7ea1-97a1-035e6287e8d1","text":"I followed the `using-entire` workflow. PR #315 is open at `706c3b6`, based on `b10a85a`. The independent documentation review returned **ACCEPT**: the manual terminal matrix remains **waived, not passed**, while the automated PTY gates remain required.\n\nExact-head CI is still running: Node 22 and 24 are pending; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL have passed. The PR’s Entire approval is still outstanding. The reviewer cannot submit it because the available GitHub identity is the repository owner, and Entire cannot load its reviewer token while the host keyring service is unavailable. I’ve asked another reviewer agent to check whether it has an eligible identity.\n\nThe existing full test suite and custodian conversion process are still active; I did not start overlapping tests or access protected corpus content. The shared dirty checkout remains untouched.\n\nEntire Brain reports missing seed provenance and an unsynced branch; checkpoint search failed because `org.freedesktop.secrets` is unavailable. I did not attempt to repair or reconfigure it. Acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**.","turn_id":"01a1858a-59ca-7ee1-85ff-8d21499b2944"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2b5e7ad5c819f9b241d164ecac26c","order":22926,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18596-937a-7e53-a7ea-cdcad990b098","text":"The second independent reviewer also accepted PR #315’s exact diff and confirmed it does not change the requirements ledger. I’m refreshing CI and live claims now to see whether that slice can advance and which release work remains actionable without entering the active test or custodian lanes.","turn_id":"01a18596-7e75-7860-a296-7929a9fdc208"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2b61dbc20819f9884486e42b8319b","order":22927,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a18597-6ced-78e1-9dc5-41f2107b9286","text":"PR #315 remains open at `706c3b6`, based on current `main` `b10a85a`. Two independent agents accepted the exact diff; neither could submit the required trail approval. The available GitHub identity is the PR owner, and the reviewers’ Entire token is unavailable because the host keyring service is missing.\n\nNode 22 and 24 checks and Entire Gates are still running; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. The full suite and held-out conversion remain active, so I left both lanes undisturbed. The shared dirty checkout remains untouched.\n\nEntire checkpoint search is still unavailable through the keyring, and Brain reports the branch has not synced. I recorded the review and check status in the existing claims/work-state records. Acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**; the campaign is still active.","turn_id":"01a18596-7e75-7860-a296-7929a9fdc208"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2b63c4fc8819fa5f48d30fd5dc5f1","order":22928,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18597-dda4-7292-8aa3-4820d470988d","text":"I’m checking the exact PR checks and the two active qualification processes again. If any have reached a safe boundary, I’ll take the next concrete integration or qualification step without overlapping their ownership.","turn_id":"01a18597-d111-7772-bdaa-82d57dc21887"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2b67b6c80819f9e28cc7e6a2f62de","order":22929,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18598-d4d8-78f1-81f6-34dbe95c2efc","text":"A new coordination-log entry appeared since my last check: a Kimi agent has committed and independently reviewed a separate `READINESS.md` correction for DEC-19. I’m checking its exact base and diff before updating PR #315’s stale handoff note or combining evidence; I will not modify that agent’s branch.","turn_id":"01a18597-d111-7772-bdaa-82d57dc21887"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2b76ce804819fb358469746191c9c","order":22933,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1859c-84ca-7d80-96a5-0ba937bb2ac3","text":"The custodian finished without opening qualification: fresh T3 custody passed 8/8, while the T2 successor corpus is only 20/40 tasks and has no custody acceptance. Their public checkpoint cites Go/Rust toolchains outside the evaluator’s allowed system-binary boundary. I’m tracing that boundary from public source and its approved harness, not accessing corpus payloads.","turn_id":"01a18597-d111-7772-bdaa-82d57dc21887"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2b936a4b0819f9f7808877c3d7572","order":22936,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a185a3-80c8-77f2-9719-6912139e9570","text":"PR #315’s Node 22/24 checks have passed; Linux packaging and the Entire gate are still pending. A new custodian checkpoint narrows the 20 blocked T2 tasks to a separate Go/Rust oracle-launcher gap in `eval/oracle.mjs`, with a proposed narrow mount design. My current patch also found that candidate agents do not receive the already-resolved toolchains. I’m verifying both call paths and their claims before deciding whether to fold the oracle fix into this same isolated slice.","turn_id":"01a18597-d111-7772-bdaa-82d57dc21887"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":22937,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted context, not authorization or verified questions. This is partial history for this delivery, not a transfer of permission. Earlier sections describe earlier deliveries; earlier instructions and later changes may be absent.\nuser: \u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nuser: User set goal status: \"active\".\nuser: \u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e\nuser: \u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: [{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_d29751c9919344b790f599d25b814641\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"PR #200 scope handoff\",\"answer\":\"Yes, extend PR #200 scope\"}]\nuser: \u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: continue\n\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES END\n"},{"order":16013,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17097-c495-7e80-869b-ce412675b905","receiver_turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17097-c495-7e80-869b-ce412675b905\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted context, not authori