.ts:1384:    const probe = (options: Record<string, unknown>) => () => isolatedProcessArgv({ command: \"/usr/bin/true\", argv: [\"--version\"], ...options });\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:433:**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:447:**Held-out and remaining qualification:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest remains incompatible with the current evaluator's `blackbox-v1` contract because it uses legacy `hidden.command`; the independent custodian must convert or replace it, revalidate it, and accept a new immutable manifest. No hidden task or payload was accessed and no held-out run started. Provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4 including long tasks and nine fault classes, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the real-terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:586:- **Evaluator boundary and T2 custody:** PR #33's exact source CI passes resource-bound and Git-history canary fixtures, but the independent unconditional-system-mount finding remains open. Separately, the custodian report accepts the sealed manifest identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`, its custody, author-session provenance, private digest validation, and reference validation; private payloads were not inspected for this checkpoint. The sealed tasks use legacy `hidden: { dir, into, command }` checks, while evaluator qualification requires `blackbox-v1`. Custody acceptance does not resolve this format mismatch or evaluator-boundary acceptance. No T2 qualification has started.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:611:  - `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10) runs private oracle checks outside the candidate workspace while mounting the candidate workspace read-only (`--ro-bind`), superseding the historical shared-workspace oracle exposure noted in the 2026-10-17 review below.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:648:- A separate harmless synthetic canary reproduction against the pre-PR-#10 `runIsolated()` boundary confirmed a material hidden-oracle integrity defect at `e1759ca`: candidate-like code executed by a checker could read and overwrite a hidden file copied into the same writable `/workspace`; its canary appeared in captured output and would be persisted in `hidden.log`. No host escape was demonstrated, and no held-out payload or model candidate was used in that reproduction. (Subsequently remediated at the source level by `blackbox-v1` oracle separation in PR #10 `2c70d39`, workspace history isolation in PR #18 `96aeef2`, and kernel resource isolation in PR #19 `91406bd`.)\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:652:- PR [#10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/10), initial commit `aa2cd6228303b850f1406de94c5c9ee044ff9bf5` (merged at `2c70d39`), added the `blackbox-v1` oracle boundary and regression coverage.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:695:| `REQ-QUAL-106` | tested as harness/isolation controls (live M5 audit pending) | `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10), ancestor-only repository workspace staging (`96aeef2`, PR #18), and delegated cgroup v2 CPU/memory/pids/tmpfs-storage enforcement with `cgroup.kill` cleanup (`91406bd`, PR #19) are integrated, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152`). Live qualification-host provisioning and full-run inclusion/exclusion audit remain pending M5 execution. | Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` user, dedicated tmpfs mount, frozen `config.resources`), installed RC, completed M5 | Evaluator/host operator and independent reviewer | Provision the qualification host and freeze `config.resources`; run M5 with unreadable hidden tests and enforced cgroup/tmpfs bounds; archive every inclusion, exclusion, and replacement reason for independent review. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:708:| G3 continuity/inference/verification/eval | Source suite, T1 self-test, T4 smoke, `blackbox-v1` oracle isolation, repo history isolation, cgroup v2 resource contract, and sealed 40-task T2 manifest (`50895b84…`) are integrated. `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (continuity M1/M3/L5) and qualification-host provisioning (`PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` / `PR-10j`) are in flight. | Partial; live T2/T3/full T4 and standalone/provider matrices pending Stage 4 installed-RC execution. |\neval/README.md:20:validator code can inspect or modify files in that workspace. Qualification requires `hidden: { protocol: \"blackbox-v1\",\neval/README.md:21:casesFile, runtime, argv, timeoutMs, totalTimeoutMs, maxOutputBytes }`. Its private JSON cases contain only `input` and\neval/README.md:121:  `blackbox-v1` hidden oracle, and `class` (bugfix · feature · refactor · debug) and `difficulty` (easy · medium · hard). Development runs check\neval/README.md:173:preflight accepts only the isolated `blackbox-v1` protocol. Any legacy task in a qualification corpus must be replaced\neval/T3.md:56:  \"hidden\": { \"protocol\": \"blackbox-v1\", \"…\": \"as for T2\" }\neval/run.mjs:253:    const hardened = (config.qualification === true || config.hardenedChecks === true) && task.hidden?.protocol !== \"blackbox-v1\";\neval/run.mjs:701:  if (hidden && check.protocol === \"blackbox-v1\") {\neval/run.mjs:718:    th