{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:14:29.223Z","ordinal":487154,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18597-d111-7772-bdaa-82d57dc21887","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2ba1456d0819fb6277b336bf30ac6","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I found the concrete gap: Python black-box oracles use `isolatedProcessArgv`, which currently mounts only system binaries, unlike the other validator sandbox. The isolated oracle already has `/tmp` tmpfs and network isolation. I’m extending only that Python-oracle path with the two pinned, read-only public toolchain roots, corpus-overlap refusal, offline cache locations, and preflight failure if the roots are not valid."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793243668361,"completed_at_ms":1793243669222}}
