{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:18:26.198Z","ordinal":487354,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a185aa-8096-7290-8f3b-e35cfa75dc70","author":"/root/pr311_draft_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr311_draft_review\nPayload:\nCHANGES_REQUIRED: `oracleToolchainsProblem()` at [eval/isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:77) rejects world-writable modes, but not group-writable ones. Its `W_OK` check at lines 84–85 tests only the current evaluator’s access, so another group member could still modify the tree. The success result is cached at line 72, and ancestor directories are not checked; a writable parent could allow the pinned root to be replaced after preflight.\n\nRequire group and world write bits to be clear throughout the trees, verify the root paths cannot be replaced through writable ancestors, and avoid retaining a successful preflight result if those paths can change.\n\nThe read-only mounts, corpus overlap checks, offline temporary caches, and synthetic fixture otherwise look sound. I did not run tests or inspect held-out or private material."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18597-d111-7772-bdaa-82d57dc21887","create_time":1793243906.19826,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":22946}}
