{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:25:39.484Z","ordinal":487705,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a185af-1d54-7c83-a43c-125f3d7c8f4c","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2bcb28464819f9c4a7cd6cb67ef34","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The qualification runner validates all task records before starting agents, and Python `blackbox-v1` validation invokes the pinned-toolchain preflight. I found candidate sandbox discovery still preferred `go env` or `rustc --print sysroot`, which could select user-home toolchains. I’ve removed those fallbacks and updated the mount-source fixture to assert only `/usr/local/go` and `/opt/nexus-qual/rust` are eligible."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793244338563,"completed_at_ms":1793244339484}}
