{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:27:05.038Z","ordinal":487791,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a185af-1d54-7c83-a43c-125f3d7c8f4c","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2bd062454819fa2a0de69f17096f7","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I advanced the evaluator work rather than waiting on the test lane. Candidate and oracle sandboxes now use only `/usr/local/go` and `/opt/nexus-qual/rust`; toolchains discovered through `go env` or `rustc --print sysroot` are no longer eligible. The Python-oracle preflight requires both pinned roots, verifies their integrity and corpus separation, and keeps builds offline in temporary storage. The fixture checks offline Go/Cargo builds and that the candidate workspace stays unchanged. See [isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:32), [oracle.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/oracle.mjs:69), and [eval_integrity.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:479).\n\nThe independent reviewer accepted the current diff. Syntax checks, diff checks, the pinned-root probe, and requirements enforcement on a clean `b10a85a` worktree passed. The evaluator tests remain unrun because the protected full-suite claim is still active. Its log now shows a failed pending-restore test and inference transport errors; the cause is not established, and I did not start overlapping tests.\n\n`origin/main` remains `b10a85a`; `origin/v1/integration` remains `7d6673f`. PR #315’s Linux and Entire checks are still running. RC10 remains the latest RC; no stable v1.0.0 tag or release exists.\n\n**Campaign: `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`. Acceptance: `IN_PROGRESS`.** Once the suite owner releases the claim, the next action is to run the focused evaluator tests, then proceed through review and integration."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793244422202,"completed_at_ms":1793244425038}}
