{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:30:06.052Z","ordinal":487937,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a185b5-2e64-7232-b28b-d8761ab6b90a","call_id":"call_bb3aa4dcacb84e10b81efe6842707533","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"ACCEPT. Toolchain discovery now uses only the two fixed roots, and the host-mount fixture expects those same roots. The Python oracle separately requires and validates both before mounting them. Corpus overlap checks still cover the selected roots.\\n\\nNo tests were run, and no held-out or private material was accessed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — PR #315’s exact head `706c3b6` against base `b10a85a` preserves DEC-19’s boundaries: exact-RC evidence retains CI and installed-RC scripted PTY gates; the manual matrix is **WAIVED, not PASS**, with the 5×3 procedure retained for successor releases. `REQUIREMENTS.md` is unchanged.\\n\\nI could not submit an independent PR or Entire disposition. GitHub authentication is for `mikeholownych`, the PR owner, and Entire could not load its active login token because the host’s `org.freedesktop.secrets` service is unavailable. An independent reviewer must authenticate through a working keyring, inspect the trail linked to PR #315 and confirm its exact head before submitting the branch approval. No approval was submitted.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for PR #315’s documentation diff. Reviewed base `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` → head `706c3b6cda2577f1ee3ae3665c42859045a9dfa2`. Cumulative diff SHA-256: `7fe68b53f754a5a33b6edbac53d63562957e71e82eb5a1746321f90430628b44`.\\n\\nThe changed acceptance map, worksheet, PLAN-10, and SPEC-10 consistently treat DEC-19 as a v1.0.0 manual-matrix waiver, not a pass; they retain the CI and scripted PTY gates and the successor-release matrix procedure. DEC-18 remains the separate screenshot-artifact waiver. REQUIREMENTS.md is unchanged.\\n\\nREADINESS.md is outside this diff and remains separately owned; its current checkpoint still needs reconciliation of manual-matrix status. This PR’s body explicitly calls out that separate work.\\n\\nI could not record the disposition on **Entire trail 30**: the only configured Entire context reports “Not logged in,” and trail access failed because `org.freedesktop.secrets` has no service on this host. I did not use the repository owner’s GitHub identity. At review time, Node 22/24 and Entire Gates were still running. No tests were run.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a185b3-b029-7902-8b23-e177e3cfc4d8","create_time":1793244606.0523424}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
