{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:34:54.454Z","ordinal":488133,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a185b9-4677-7fa0-b830-2d9649c1019d","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a185b9-4677-7fa0-b830-2d9649c1019d","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae2bedab088819fa7132af0b303bce7","usage":{"input_tokens":128108,"cached_input_tokens":124416,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":408,"reasoning_output_tokens":264,"total_tokens":128516},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":252603,"cached_input_tokens":246272,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1029,"reasoning_output_tokens":466,"total_tokens":253632},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9110585862,"cached_input_tokens":9013457152,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":26194651,"reasoning_output_tokens":15284885,"total_tokens":9136780513}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:34:56.763Z","ordinal":488134,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a185b9-4677-7fa0-b830-2d9649c1019d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-183bfdcd-fcc6-4a96-a8a1-87b0432df65f","process_id":"2469","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","export ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file; entire trail --help; entire checkpoint explain --help; gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commits/742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954/check-runs --jq '.check_runs[] | select(.name==\"Entire Gates\") | {id,name,status,conclusion,details_url,output,external_id}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"export ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file; entire trail --help; entire checkpoint explain --help; gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commits/742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954/check-runs --jq '.check_runs[] | select(.name==\"Entire Gates\") | {id,name,status,conclusion,details_url,output,external_id}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"A trail captures project intent across repositories and branches. Manage intent and discussions on the whole trail; use --repo and --branch to select context for checkout, sessions, findings, and approvals.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail [flags]\n  entire trail [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  approvals       List approval decisions on a trail\n  approve         Approve a trail\n  checkout        Check out a trail's branch\n  comment         Discuss the whole trail across repositories\n  create          Create a trail and publish its branch\n  finding         Manage a trail's agent findings\n  link            Link a repository branch to a trail\n  list            List trails in a project\n  merge           Merge one of a trail's changes into its base\n  resume          Resume a trail's agent session\n  show            Show trail intent and its repositories and branches\n  unlink          Unlink a repository branch without deleting its work\n  update          Update project intent and lifecycle\n  watch           Tail events for a trail's selected repository branch\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for trail\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire trail [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\nExplain provides human-readable context about sessions, commits, and checkpoints.\n\nUse this command to understand what happened during agent-driven development,\neither for self-review or to understand a teammate's work.\n\nBy default, shows checkpoints on the current branch. Pass a checkpoint ID or\ncommit SHA as a positional argument to explain a specific item, or use flags.\n\nViewing specific items:\n  entire checkpoint explain <id-or-sha>           Auto-detects checkpoint ID or commit SHA\n  entire checkpoint explain --checkpoint <id>     Force interpretation as checkpoint ID\n  entire checkpoint explain --commit <ref>        Force interpretation as commit ref\n\nCheckpoints in another repo:\n  entire checkpoint explain <id-or-sha> --repo gh/owner/name\n  entire checkpoint explain <id-or-sha> --repo et/project/repo\n                 Explain a checkpoint owned by another repository — the\n                 drill-down for a cross-repo 'entire search' hit. Reads it from\n                 that repo's Entire API; nothing is written to this repo.\n                 Needs a full checkpoint ID (12-char hex or 26-char ULID) or a full commit SHA\n                 (positional, --checkpoint, or --commit) and a checkpoint that\n                 has been pushed. A commit SHA is resolved to its checkpoint\n                 by that repo's Entire API, so prefixes cannot be used here.\n\nFiltering the list view:\n  --session      Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n\nOutput verbosity levels (when explaining a specific item):\n  Default:         Detailed view with scoped prompts (ID, session, tokens, intent, prompts, files)\n  --short          Summary only (ID, session, timestamp, tokens, intent)\n  --full           Parsed full transcript (all prompts/responses from entire session)\n  --raw-transcript Raw transcript file (JSONL format)\n\nMachine-readable export modes (additive surface for external consumers):\n  --json           Metadata-only JSON. Lists checkpoints when no target is given;\n                   emits a single checkpoint envelope when a target is supplied,\n                   including its subagent task records under \"tasks\".\n                   Transcript bytes are NEVER embedded in the JSON envelope.\n  --transcript     Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes (JSONL) to stdout\n                   for the selected session. Same bytes as --raw-transcript\n                   while checkpoints v1 is the checkpoint store.\n  --session-index  Pick a session within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based).\n                   Defaults to the latest session. Only meaningful with\n                   --transcript or --raw-transcript.\n  --task           With --transcript, stream a subagent's stored transcript\n                   instead, selected by tool_use_id or agent_id (as listed\n                   under \"tasks\" in --json).\n  --limit          Cap the number of checkpoints returned by the list view.\n                   Defaults to 100. When the cap is hit, a stderr note\n                   says how many were skipped. Only meaningful with --json.\n\nSummary generation:\n  --generate    Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint. This is the only\n                part of this command that writes: it stores the summary on the\n                checkpoint and spends tokens with the configured summary\n                provider. Every other mode only reads.\n  --force       Regenerate even if a summary already exists (requires --generate)\n\nPerformance options:\n  --search-all  Remove branch/depth limits when searching for commits (may be slow)\n\nCheckpoint detail view shows:\n  - Author of the checkpoint\n  - Associated git commits that reference the checkpoint\n  - Prompts and responses from the session\n\nNote: --session filters the list view; the positional arg, --commit, and --checkpoint are mutually exclusive.\n\nUsage:\n  entire checkpoint explain [checkpoint-id | commit-sha] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -c, --checkpoint string             Explain a specific checkpoint (ID or prefix)\n      --commit string                 Explain a specific commit (SHA or ref, \"commit-ish\")\n      --force                         Regenerate summary even if one already exists (requires --generate)\n      --full                          Show full parsed transcript (all prompts/responses)\n      --generate                      Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint\n  -h, --help                          help for explain\n      --insecure-http-auth            Allow plain-HTTP auth for --repo (local dev only)\n      --json                          Output metadata as JSON (no transcript bytes)\n      --limit int                     Cap the list view at N checkpoints (default: 100). Only meaningful with --json.\n      --no-pager                      Disable pager output\n      --raw-transcript                Show raw transcript file (JSONL format)\n      --repo string                   Explain a checkpoint owned by another repo (gh/owner/name, et/project/repo, entire://<host>/gh/<owner>/<repo>, or entire://<host>/et/<project>/<repo>), read from that repo's Entire API\n      --search-all                    Search all commits (no branch/depth limit, may be slow)\n      --session string                Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n      --session-index int             Session index within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based, defaults to latest) (default -1)\n  -s, --short                         Show summary only (omit prompts and files)\n      --summary-timeout-seconds int   Hard deadline in seconds for --generate summary generation; overrides summary_timeout_seconds setting. 0 = use setting; if setting is also unset or 0, no automatic deadline applies.\n      --task string                   Subagent task (tool_use_id or agent_id) whose stored transcript --transcript streams\n      --transcript                    Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes to stdout (a session's, or a subagent's with --task)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"details_url\":\"https://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/26/changes/nexus-code/26\",\"external_id\":\"entire-gates:742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954\",\"id\":123215769507,\"name\":\"Entire Gates\",\"output\":{\"annotations_count\":0,\"annotations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/check-runs/123215769507/annotations\",\"summary\":\"- ❌ **Approvals**: failed — No reviewers have approved this trail\\n- ✅ **Checks**: passed — CI checks have passed\\n- ✅ **Findings**: passed — Agent review found no blocking issues\\n- ❌ **Up to date**: failed — 2 commits behind\\n\\n[Trail #26 on Entire](https://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/26/changes/nexus-code/26)\",\"text\":null,\"title\":\"2 blocking gates not passing\"},\"status\":\"completed\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":644023804}},"started_at_ms":1793244896118,"completed_at_ms":1793244896762}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:34:58.497Z","ordinal":488135,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a185b9-a4c1-7423-a354-83ab427c0a7e","call_id":"call_28ad8237fdce400fbf68182195253c44","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"A trail captures project intent across repositories and branches. Manage intent and discussions on the whole trail; use --repo and --branch to select context for checkout, sessions, findings, and approvals.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail [flags]\n  entire trail [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  approvals       List approval decisions on a trail\n  approve         Approve a trail\n  checkout        Check out a trail's branch\n  comment         Discuss the whole trail across repositories\n  create          Create a trail and publish its branch\n  finding         Manage a trail's agent findings\n  link            Link a repository branch to a trail\n  list            List trails in a project\n  merge           Merge one of a trail's changes into its base\n  resume          Resume a trail's agent session\n  show            Show trail intent and its repositories and branches\n  unlink          Unlink a repository branch without deleting its work\n  update          Update project intent and lifecycle\n  watch           Tail events for a trail's selected repository branch\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for trail\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire trail [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\nExplain provides human-readable context about sessions, commits, and checkpoints.\n\nUse this command to understand what happened during agent-driven development,\neither for self-review or to understand a teammate's work.\n\nBy default, shows checkpoints on the current branch. Pass a checkpoint ID or\ncommit SHA as a positional argument to explain a specific item, or use flags.\n\nViewing specific items:\n  entire checkpoint explain <id-or-sha>           Auto-detects checkpoint ID or commit SHA\n  entire checkpoint explain --checkpoint <id>     Force interpretation as checkpoint ID\n  entire checkpoint explain --commit <ref>        Force interpretation as commit ref\n\nCheckpoints in another repo:\n  entire checkpoint explain <id-or-sha> --repo gh/owner/name\n  entire checkpoint explain <id-or-sha> --repo et/project/repo\n                 Explain a checkpoint owned by another repository — the\n                 drill-down for a cross-repo 'entire search' hit. Reads it from\n                 that repo's Entire API; nothing is written to this repo.\n                 Needs a full checkpoint ID (12-char hex or 26-char ULID) or a full commit SHA\n                 (positional, --checkpoint, or --commit) and a checkpoint that\n                 has been pushed. A commit SHA is resolved to its checkpoint\n                 by that repo's Entire API, so prefixes cannot be used here.\n\nFiltering the list view:\n  --session      Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n\nOutput verbosity levels (when explaining a specific item):\n  Default:         Detailed view with scoped prompts (ID, session, tokens, intent, prompts, files)\n  --short          Summary only (ID, session, timestamp, tokens, intent)\n  --full           Parsed full transcript (all prompts/responses from entire session)\n  --raw-transcript Raw transcript file (JSONL format)\n\nMachine-readable export modes (additive surface for external consumers):\n  --json           Metadata-only JSON. Lists checkpoints when no target is given;\n                   emits a single checkpoint envelope when a target is supplied,\n                   including its subagent task records under \"tasks\".\n                   Transcript bytes are NEVER embedded in the JSON envelope.\n  --transcript     Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes (JSONL) to stdout\n                   for the selected session. Same bytes as --raw-transcript\n                   while checkpoints v1 is the checkpoint store.\n  --session-index  Pick a session within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based).\n                   Defaults to the latest session. Only meaningful with\n                   --transcript or --raw-transcript.\n  --task           With --transcript, stream a subagent's stored transcript\n                   instead, selected by tool_use_id or agent_id (as listed\n                   under \"tasks\" in --json).\n  --limit          Cap the number of checkpoints returned by the list view.\n                   Defaults to 100. When the cap is hit, a stderr note\n                   says how many were skipped. Only meaningful with --json.\n\nSummary generation:\n  --generate    Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint. This is the only\n                part of this command that writes: it stores the summary on the\n                checkpoint and spends tokens with the configured summary\n                provider. Every other mode only reads.\n  --force       Regenerate even if a summary already exists (requires --generate)\n\nPerformance options:\n  --search-all  Remove branch/depth limits when searching for commits (may be slow)\n\nCheckpoint detail view shows:\n  - Author of the checkpoint\n  - Associated git commits that reference the checkpoint\n  - Prompts and responses from the session\n\nNote: --session filters the list view; the positional arg, --commit, and --checkpoint are mutually exclusive.\n\nUsage:\n  entire checkpoint explain [checkpoint-id | commit-sha] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -c, --checkpoint string             Explain a specific checkpoint (ID or prefix)\n      --commit string                 Explain a specific commit (SHA or ref, \"commit-ish\")\n      --force                         Regenerate summary even if one already exists (requires --generate)\n      --full                          Show full parsed transcript (all prompts/responses)\n      --generate                      Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint\n  -h, --help                          help for explain\n      --insecure-http-auth            Allow plain-HTTP auth for --repo (local dev only)\n      --json                          Output metadata as JSON (no transcript bytes)\n      --limit int                     Cap the list view at N checkpoints (default: 100). Only meaningful with --json.\n      --no-pager                      Disable pager output\n      --raw-transcript                Show raw transcript file (JSONL format)\n      --repo string                   Explain a checkpoint owned by another repo (gh/owner/name, et/project/repo, entire://<host>/gh/<owner>/<repo>, or entire://<host>/et/<project>/<repo>), read from that repo's Entire API\n      --search-all                    Search all commits (no branch/depth limit, may be slow)\n      --session string                Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n      --session-index int             Session index within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based, defaults to latest) (default -1)\n  -s, --short                         Show summary only (omit prompts and files)\n      --summary-timeout-seconds int   Hard deadline in seconds for --generate summary generation; overrides summary_timeout_seconds setting. 0 = use setting; if setting is also unset or 0, no automatic deadline applies.\n      --task string                   Subagent task (tool_use_id or agent_id) whose stored transcript --transcript streams\n      --transcript                    Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes to stdout (a session's, or a subagent's with --task)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"details_url\":\"https://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/26/changes/nexus-code/26\",\"external_id\":\"entire-gates:742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954\",\"id\":123215769507,\"name\":\"Entire Gates\",\"output\":{\"annotations_count\":0,\"annotations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/check-runs/123215769507/annotations\",\"summary\":\"- ❌ **Approvals**: failed — No reviewers have approved this trail\\n- ✅ **Checks**: passed — CI checks have passed\\n- ✅ **Findings**: passed — Agent review found no blocking issues\\n- ❌ **Up to date**: failed — 2 commits behind\\n\\n[Trail #26 on Entire](https://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/26/changes/nexus-code/26)\",\"text\":null,\"title\":\"2 blocking gates not passing\"},\"status\":\"completed\"}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a185b9-4677-7fa0-b830-2d9649c1019d","create_time":1793244898.4972012}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
