facts are waived for v1.0.0; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n21:**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not establish successor-RC qualification. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned (last updated 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC); no custodian acceptance or held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification is established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user waived screenshot artifacts, while terminal behavior checks remain unrun. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, required human terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\n37:Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its last update was 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC, with no custodian response observed. No held-out payload was accessed and no held-out qualification was run. The manual terminal matrix's last recorded result is 0/15; terminal setup exists on Ubuntu, but no operator screenshots or cell verdicts have been supplied. Held-out/T2/T3/T4, remaining provider and standalone coverage, successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n51:**Qualification, custody, and publication:** GitHub still lists [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) as the latest release; there is no `v1.0.0` tag or stable release. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, with the last metadata-only custodian request at 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC and no response observed. No protected payload was accessed or qualification run. The manual terminal matrix remains 0/15; the final installed RC does not exist. Exact-RC held-out/T2/T3/T4, provider and standalone coverage, cross-runner reproducibility, human terminal evidence, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. The chosen distribution target remains the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\n53:**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. PR integration is blocked by required Entire review findings/approvals; exact-RC qualification is additionally blocked by independent held-out custody and the required human terminal matrix. Existing publication authorization remains granted but gated. The checkpoint below is retained as the 13:34 UTC snapshot and is superseded for current CI, requirements, PR checks, local suite result, and release status.\n81:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Held-out T2/T3/T4, remaining live-provider and standalone gates, successor-RC artifact qualification, cross-runner evidence, the 15-cell human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on these mandatory checks.\n125:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the newest prerelease on source `16ee8ca`; stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Held-out custody acceptance and compatible frozen T2 data remain unresolved (issue #1 is open with no custodian response); T2/T3/T4, evaluator-host acceptance, the remaining live provider and standalone gates, and independent exact-RC acceptance are incomplete. The human five-environment by three-size terminal matrix remains **0/15**, pending the operator; no per-cell verdict or evidence is recorded. Keep stable publication gated on every required acceptance gate.\n137:**Qualification and publication:** RC10 remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed. Exact cross-runner reproducibility passed for immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca`; a successor candidate from current main still requires its own reproducibility run. Held-out custodian acceptance, T2/T3/T4, remaining live provider and standalone qualification, independent exact-RC acceptance, and human terminal evidence remain open. The five-environment by three-size operator terminal matrix remains **0/15**; no cell result or screenshot is recorded. Automated PTY evidence does not substitute for these human cells. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance criteria.\n178:**Release and acceptance gates:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains a prerelease; stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. The human real-terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user's report of rendering at 43×13 in tmux on GNOME Terminal is not the full matrix and had no captured screenshots. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN, last updated 2026-10-26 17:37:53 UTC, with no recorded custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, live provider/standalone, independent exact-RC, and human acceptance gates remain incomplete. Publication authorization remains gated on all required acceptance.\n194:**Candidate and gates:** The latest public release remains prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10), built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0` with archive SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. Stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. The required real-terminal matrix remains **0/15**; scripted terminal evidence does not replace operator evidence. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no recorded custodian acceptance; no private payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, exact-current-RC provider/standalone and cross-runner qualification, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization is granted but gated. The distribution target is the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\n230:**RC and remaining acceptance:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains an unaccepted prerelease from source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, not the current main source. PR #265's merged OpenRouter evidence covers one pinned-model verification and one synthetic small task. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without custodian acceptance; no held-out task payload was accessed or run. Installed exact-RC qualification, standalone/provider matrix coverage, T2/T3/T4, the complete terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release is published. Existing publication authorization remains gated on every mandatory acceptance gate.\n240:**Current convergence PRs:** PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264), head `73bdc7d91b1b8925b522b052d89228d99bad4893` on base `2622663313132864677cfdc93c94944d26a3ac06`, has independent ACCEPT; Node 22, Node 24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while its Linux package job remains in progress. It records scripted terminal evidence only and does not complete the manual terminal gate. PR [#266](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/266), head `11fc29ba39bc76624c55d34a1fc12b4d7544522a` on the same prior base, has Node 24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passing; its Node 22 TUI test failure is being rerun, currently in progress. PR [#267](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/267), head `d0cac8b959e3da8595a41651a60a2fcd3738d034` on current base `14a9c15`, carries the malformed credential-origin fix. Its exact two-file diff has independent ACCEPT (SHA-256 `2da500d09522bc059f63b07251953c552ac2270168c72d43920b181e44fd89d3`) and the focused provider connection suite passed 37/37 after rebase; its Node 22 and Node 24 jobs are running and CodeQL passed. None of these PRs is integrated yet. PR #265 merged at `14a9c152`; its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed. Its OpenRouter evidence covers one pinned-model verification and one synthetic small task, not full provider or standalone qualification.\n242:**RC10 artifact boundary:** The latest published prerelease is [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10), built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, not current main. Its Linux archive SHA-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. Previously completed RC10 artifact, installation, provenance and cross-runner checks apply only to that immutable artifact. Scripted terminal coverage remains partial; the required manual real-terminal matrix is 0/15. No exact-RC acceptance is established. Further source changes require constructing and qualifying a new candidate.\n244:**Held-out and human gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open with no custodian acceptance recorded; no held-out payload was accessed and T2/T3/T4 acceptance is not established. The manual terminal matrix still requires operator evidence across five environments and three sizes. At 2026-10-27 03:49 UTC, I verified over SSH to `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`) that `/home/mike/nexus-rc10-manual-evidence/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md` exists and contains an unfilled 15-cell template with directories for every environment/size pair. No cell evidence is present; the installed candidate identity is blank. Any matrix run must use the eventual installed RC. Scripted PTY output is not a substitute.\n263:**Custody and remaining acceptance:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN and its latest update is 17:37:53 UTC; no custodian response or assignee is recorded. No private held-out payload was accessed, and held-out qualification has not started. The repository's latest human terminal matrix status is 0/15; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute for those operator cells. Current-source provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC9 is unaccepted and stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; the existing publication authorization remains gated on every required release acceptance.\n280:**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN; its latest metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Independent private custody, evaluator-compatible corpus sealing, and held-out acceptance remain unestablished; no held-out payload was accessed or run. Current-candidate provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The human terminal matrix remains **0/15**. RC8 is a prior prerelease, not a qualified candidate for this source; stable v1.0.0 is unpublished. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authority remains granted but gated.\n291:**Accepta