reatedAt\": \"2026-10-29T01:10:57Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Custody identity clarification from the public historical records (metadata only; no private store access): `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md` names the `opencode` primary session as the T2 custodian/integrator and says it authored no tasks; §3 records that it validated all 40 tasks before sealing manifest `50895b84…`. The T3 custody report names the same historical session. This documents the prior role, but does not establish that this session is still active or that a current agent accepted the custodian role.\\n\\nCan the documented OpenCode primary session\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-29T03:35:28Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only custody reconciliation: the exact-main historical report `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md` names the `opencode` primary session as prior T2 custodian/integrator (not task author); the T3 report also names that session. The current local claim names `opencode` custodian and cites `CUSTODY_HANDOFF_ACCEPTED`, but that event is not present in the claim log I could verify. A validation process launched through the OpenCode server is currently live; I have not inspected its private log or contents. Please confirm, with public metadata only: whether\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":637644512}},"started_at_ms":1793245266353,"completed_at_ms":1793245266991}}
