{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:43:51.348Z","ordinal":488535,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a185b9-4677-7fa0-b830-2d9649c1019d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-360d9e43-d546-43ff-b08a-1577f4ff5549","process_id":"57771","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","set -e; CAND=/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9; case_home=$(mktemp -d /var/tmp/nexus-requirements-home.XXXXXX); mkdir -p \"$case_home/.config\"; git -C \"$CAND\" diff --check origin/main...HEAD; HOME=\"$case_home\" XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$case_home/.config\" node \"$CAND/scripts/check_requirements.mjs\" --enforce; printf 'HEAD '; git -C \"$CAND\" rev-parse HEAD; printf '\\nREADINESS current checkpoint:\\n'; sed -n '1,14p' \"$CAND/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\"; printf '\\nREADINESS qualification summary:\\n'; rg -n 'DEC-19|manual terminal|automated CI PTY|scripted installed-RC PTY|REQ-QUAL-108' \"$CAND/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\" | head -12"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"set -e; CAND=/home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9; case_home=$(mktemp -d /var/tmp/nexus-requirements-home.XXXXXX); mkdir -p \"$case_home/.config\"; git -C \"$CAND\" diff --check origin/main...HEAD; HOME=\"$case_home\" XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$case_home/.config\" node \"$CAND/scripts/check_requirements.mjs\" --enforce; printf 'HEAD '; git -C \"$CAND\" rev-parse HEAD; printf '\\nREADINESS current checkpoint:\\n'; sed -n '1,14p' \"$CAND/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\"; printf '\\nREADINESS qualification summary:\\n'; rg -n 'DEC-19|manual terminal|automated CI PTY|scripted installed-RC PTY|REQ-QUAL-108' \"$CAND/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\" | head -12"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"requirements: 123 rows; tested 108, partial 6, implemented 2, open 7 (enforce)\ndeferred to exact-RC qualification: REQ-AGT-002 (partial), REQ-AGT-010 (partial), REQ-PRV-003 (implemented), REQ-REL-003 (partial), REQ-REL-005 (partial), REQ-AGT-110 (open), REQ-PRV-111 (partial), REQ-REL-114 (open), REQ-QUAL-101 (open), REQ-QUAL-107 (open), REQ-QUAL-108 (partial), REQ-QUAL-109 (open)\nHEAD 9d6c8913cd384b66251bd939bffefdfa5d322ca5\n\nREADINESS current checkpoint:\n# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 22:00 UTC; custodian update 2026-10-29)\n\n**Custodian update (2026-10-29).** The release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0 ([DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)). The manual gate is **waived, not passed**: no cell verdicts were recorded. The automated CI PTY suites and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios remain required, and automated/scripted PTY qualification remains outstanding for the successor RC. The release notes must disclose the waiver. The manual terminal-matrix item is no longer an outstanding qualification gate; every other gate in this checkpoint is unchanged.\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496`, the PR #308 merge commit. Exact-main CI run [40770466028](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770466028) completed successfully at 2026-10-28 21:58:53 UTC on this SHA. Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices passed; Linux x86_64 passed Rust and CLI tests, requirements and security gates, reproducible package builds with matching output hashes, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. CodeQL run [40770465935](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770465935) completed successfully. On a clean detached worktree at this exact SHA, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n\n**Integrated changes:** PR #309 merged as `b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af` at 20:36 UTC with checksummed RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider evidence. PR #300 merged as `79cba842e86d64f895e1a269636776cdf1e7e6da` at 21:07:46 UTC after Node 22/24, Linux packaging/tests, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. PR #308 merged as `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496` at 21:15:37 UTC; exact PR head `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` passed Node 22/24 and Linux, with JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; its GitHub Entire Gates check was neutral. A post-merge source reviewer found no blocking defect in the reviewed restore path and reported a separate Entire trail 23 signal: approvals failed and one high-severity finding was unresolved. A later authenticated, read-only Entire query on `ubuntu-desktop` (2026-10-28 21:48 UTC) found trail 23 open but its Nexus Code change marked merged; the finding and approvals commands reported no open change, so the historical finding text and its disposition could not be retrieved. The earlier high-severity signal therefore remains unresolved/unverified and must be reconciled before successor-RC qualification; the later query does not establish that it was resolved. The current-main source CI passed as recorded above; this does not qualify an installed release candidate.\n\n**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. Per [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver), the five-environment, three-size manual terminal matrix is waived for v1.0.0, not PASS; no cell verdicts were recorded. Automated CI PTY suites and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios remain mandatory. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, scripted installed-RC PTY, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n\n\nREADINESS qualification summary:\n5:**Custodian update (2026-10-29).** The release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0 ([DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)). The manual gate is **waived, not passed**: no cell verdicts were recorded. The automated CI PTY suites and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios remain required, and automated/scripted PTY qualification remains outstanding for the successor RC. The release notes must disclose the waiver. The manual terminal-matrix item is no longer an outstanding qualification gate; every other gate in this checkpoint is unchanged.\n11:**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. Per [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver), the five-environment, three-size manual terminal matrix is waived for v1.0.0, not PASS; no cell verdicts were recorded. Automated CI PTY suites and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios remain mandatory. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, scripted installed-RC PTY, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n37:Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its last update was 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC, with no custodian response observed. No held-out payload was accessed and no held-out qualification was run. The manual terminal matrix's last recorded result is 0/15; terminal setup exists on Ubuntu, but no operator screenshots or cell verdicts have been supplied. Held-out/T2/T3/T4, remaining provider and standalone coverage, successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n51:**Qualification, custody, and publication:** GitHub still lists [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) as the latest release; there is no `v1.0.0` tag or stable release. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, with the last metadata-only custodian request at 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC and no response observed. No protected payload was accessed or qualification run. The manual terminal matrix remains 0/15; the final installed RC does not exist. Exact-RC held-out/T2/T3/T4, provider and standalone coverage, cross-runner reproducibility, human terminal evidence, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. The chosen distribution target remains the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\n240:**Current convergence PRs:** PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264), head `73bdc7d91b1b8925b522b052d89228d99bad4893` on base `2622663313132864677cfdc93c94944d26a3ac06`, has independent ACCEPT; Node 22, Node 24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while its Linux package job remains in progress. It records scripted terminal evidence only and does not complete the manual terminal gate. PR [#266](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/266), head `11fc29ba39bc76624c55d34a1fc12b4d7544522a` on the same prior base, has Node 24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passing; its Node 22 TUI test failure is being rerun, currently in progress. PR [#267](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/267), head `d0cac8b959e3da8595a41651a60a2fcd3738d034` on current base `14a9c15`, carries the malformed credential-origin fix. Its exact two-file diff has independent ACCEPT (SHA-256 `2da500d09522bc059f63b07251953c552ac2270168c72d43920b181e44fd89d3`) and the focused provider connection suite passed 37/37 after rebase; its Node 22 and Node 24 jobs are running and CodeQL passed. None of these PRs is integrated yet. PR #265 merged at `14a9c152`; its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed. Its OpenRouter evidence covers one pinned-model verification and one synthetic small task, not full provider or standalone qualification.\n244:**Held-out and human gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open with no custodian acceptance recorded; no held-out payload was accessed and T2/T3/T4 acceptance is not established. The manual terminal matrix still requires operator evidence across five environments and three sizes. At 2026-10-27 03:49 UTC, I verified over SSH to `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`) that `/home/mike/nexus-rc10-manual-evidence/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md` exists and contains an unfilled 15-cell template with directories for every environment/size pair. No cell evidence is present; the installed candidate identity is blank. Any matrix run must use the eventual installed RC. Scripted PTY output is not a substitute.\n302:**Terminal environment preparation:** A strict known-host SSH connection to the configured Ubuntu/GNOME desktop succeeded. Read-only inventory found xterm 407, kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, and VS Code 1.143.1; an active GNOME Wayland session is present. This is environment availability only. No manual terminal cell was run, no screenshot was captured, and the §5.3 matrix remains **0/15**. It still requires each of the five terminals at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with approval-panel and post-exit screenshots for every cell and genuine operator verdicts.\n304:**Acceptance and remaining gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest public metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Private custody acceptance and evaluator-compatible sealed corpus readiness remain unestablished; no held-out payload was accessed or run. PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) remains open at c3bb2235, based on b73b6ec; it needs refresh onto ff349383 after remediation. Exact-head CI run [40338957629](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957629) failed on both Node 22 and Node 24 at `npm --prefix cli test`; CodeQL [40338957381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957381) passed on the old candidate. This failure is on PR head c3bb2235 based on b73b6ec, not current main; refresh after remediation before using CI as evidence. A local, unpushed commit 8655ca87 fixes request-correlated local-setup cancellation (focused Node 34/34, Rust 4/4, build and diff checks passed), but the independent rereview recorded other unresolved credential/configuration findings; it is not integrated or accepted. T2/T3/T4, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, exact-candidate reproducibility, the manual terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; no stable v1.0.0 release exists. Publication authority remains granted and gated by acceptance.\n397:**Remaining qualification and disposition:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public update is the coordinator request from 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no custodian response or new custody acceptance. Held-out qualification has not started. Provider/standalone qualification remains incomplete, including OpenRouter; T2/T3/T4 qualification remains incomplete; the five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; RC7 is unaccepted and no stable `v1.0.0` release is published. Publication authorization remains granted and gated on all required acceptance evidence.\n407:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest comment is coordinator-authored at 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible held-out corpus disposition. Held-out T2 has not started, and no private payload was accessed. Provider/standalone qualification and T3/T4 evidence remain incomplete. The five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15, with no per-cell verdicts or required screenshots. The `cli/src/agent.ts` remediation handoff remains with KimiCode-defect-scan; implementation is still pending in that claimed lane.\n423:**Next evidence:** Finish the RC7 Release workflow and verify its exact artifact identity and provenance. Finish exact-head CI for PRs #243–245, integrate only after required review and checks, and requalify resulting main before constructing a subsequent candidate. The `cli/src/agent.ts` defect-remediation handoff is recorded for KimiCode-defect-scan; its implementation is not yet present in that branch. Resolve independent held-out custody and evaluator compatibility before beginning protected qualification; then qualify an eligible installed RC and complete the manual terminal matrix. Keep source gates, RC construction, installed-RC qualification, and stable-release checks distinct.\n539:- **Requirements gate:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was independently rerun with isolated HOME/XDG on exact `7d6673f` and passed: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. This source-stage gate pass does not satisfy those qualification requirements.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":119008418}},"started_at_ms":1793245431223,"completed_at_ms":179324