ts behind and had no trail approval. A local, not-yet-pushed candidate at `9d6c8913cd384b66251bd939bffefdfa5d322ca5` merges current main and includes the same reviewed source/test tree plus independently accepted readiness corrections. Cumulative independent source review is ACCEPT; requirements enforcement, version check, and diff check pass. Exact-head hosted checks have not run on this local candidate. A separate full-suite run on immutable snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c` was still running at the observation time; it is not exact-candidate evidence.\n+\n+PR [#315](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/315), documentation-only DEC-19 reconciliation, is based on `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`. Its Node 22/24, Linux x86_64, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks pass. Entire trail #30 remains open without an independent approval; the available authenticated identity is the release owner and cannot provide that approval.\n+\n+**Qualification and custody:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) is the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The GitHub installer is the selected distribution target; npm publication is inapplicable. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned. Its latest public metadata update (03:44 UTC) does not establish fresh private custody acceptance or held-out qualification; no protected payload was accessed and no held-out run is claimed. T2/T3/T4, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, fault injection, successor-RC reproducibility, scripted installed-RC PTY qualification, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC10-bound results do not qualify a successor candidate.\n+\n+**Terminal gate:** Under [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver), the manual real-terminal matrix is **waived, not passed**; no cell verdicts were recorded. Automated CI PTY suites and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios remain mandatory. `REQ-QUAL-108` remains partial; no terminal evidence status was promoted.\n+\n+**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted and gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. No RC is accepted and stable publication is not authorized by readiness alone.\n+\n+## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 22:00 UTC; custodian update 2026-10-29; superseded)\n \n **Custodian update (2026-10-29).** The release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0 ([DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)). The manual gate is **waived, not passed**: no cell verdicts were recorded. The automated CI PTY suites and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios remain required, and automated/scripted PTY qualification remains outstanding for the successor RC. The release notes must disclose the waiver. The manual terminal-matrix item is no longer an outstanding qualification gate; every other gate in this checkpoint is unchanged.\n \n9d6c8913 (HEAD -> v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9) Merge branch 'v1/dec19-consistency-20261029' into v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9\nafcc5247 docs(release): correct main CI completion time\nde9af530 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9\na6432889 (v1/dec19-consistency-20261029) docs(release): align readiness with DEC-19\n742d0087 (pr/311, origin/v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9) Merge pull request #313 from mikeholownych/v1/recovered-operation-verification-20261029\nb10a85ad (origin/main, v1/eval-agent-toolchain-binds) Merge pull request #312 from mikeholownych/v1/custodian-terminal-waiver-20261029\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a185b9-4677-7fa0-b830-2d9649c1019d","create_time":1793245647.122477}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
