{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:58:31.842Z","ordinal":489094,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a185cf-35a2-73f0-886a-f21c5c65e114","call_id":"call_ab7d717527ac4697afe12fa11337b336","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — exact head `fe28ec9e686b90e69e42a7a13d55f50264b3775f`.\\n\\nThe only change from `e12f81e` anchors the 03:44 UTC issue metadata to the checkpoint’s 03:45 UTC observation. That resolves the freshness concern; live metadata still shows issue #1 open and unassigned. The rest of the checkpoint is unchanged from my prior review, including the verified main checks, snapshot-suite distinction, manual waiver, and partial `REQ-QUAL-108`.\\n\\nRead-only review only; no tests or edits.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"PR #315 remains open at head `706c3b6` on base `b10a85a`. Entire trail #30 is open and current on branch `v1/dec19-terminal-waiver-reconcile`, with no recorded approvals. The branch points to the exact PR head, and its merge base is the exact PR base.\\n\\nI did not approve: the available Entire identity is Mike Holownych, the PR owner, and the trail’s author and assignee are the same account. An independent reviewer must authenticate with their own Entire account and approve trail #30 for that branch.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for PR #315’s documentation diff. Reviewed base `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` → head `706c3b6cda2577f1ee3ae3665c42859045a9dfa2`. Cumulative diff SHA-256: `7fe68b53f754a5a33b6edbac53d63562957e71e82eb5a1746321f90430628b44`.\\n\\nThe changed acceptance map, worksheet, PLAN-10, and SPEC-10 consistently treat DEC-19 as a v1.0.0 manual-matrix waiver, not a pass; they retain the CI and scripted PTY gates and the successor-release matrix procedure. DEC-18 remains the separate screenshot-artifact waiver. REQUIREMENTS.md is unchanged.\\n\\nREADINESS.md is outside this diff and remains separately owned; its current checkpoint still needs reconciliation of manual-matrix status. This PR’s body explicitly calls out that separate work.\\n\\nI could not record the disposition on **Entire trail 30**: the only configured Entire context reports “Not logged in,” and trail access failed because `org.freedesktop.secrets` has no service on this host. I did not use the repository owner’s GitHub identity. At review time, Node 22/24 and Entire Gates were still running. No tests were run.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a185cd-baa4-7fe1-bac6-635c68bc9b1f","create_time":1793246311.8420463}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
