{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:58:57.825Z","ordinal":489126,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a185cd-baa4-7fe1-bac6-635c68bc9b1f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3ba39a05-9f56-4505-8a4f-1adfb9d6bde3","process_id":"24904","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore status --short --branch && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore log -3 --oneline && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore diff --stat && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore diff --name-only && rg -n 'manual terminal|DEC-19|QUAL-108|15.cell|waiv' /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/REQUIREMENTS.md | head -n 70"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore status --short --branch && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore log -3 --oneline && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore diff --stat && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore diff --name-only && rg -n 'manual terminal|DEC-19|QUAL-108|15.cell|waiv' /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/REQUIREMENTS.md | head -n 70"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## codex/restore-terminal-human-matrix...origin/main\n M docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\nb10a85ad Merge pull request #312 from mikeholownych/v1/custodian-terminal-waiver-20261029\n9bec86be docs(release): record the owner waiver of the manual terminal matrix\ncbb3b653 Merge pull request #310 from mikeholownych/v1/readiness-post-308-merge-20261028\n docs/releases/v1.0.0.md                                      |  2 +-\n docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md                                    |  6 +++---\n docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md                                     | 10 +++++-----\n docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md                     |  2 +-\n docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md |  2 +-\n 5 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\nrg: /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/REQUIREMENTS.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_ASSESSMENT.md:82:Current evidence demonstrates role-based message separation, tool-schema separation, budgeting, output reserves, and guarded context assembly. It does not demonstrate provenance and classification metadata carried by every individual injected item. Role labels and structurally separated prompt sections do not supply all required source identities or classification metadata. Phase 4's budget-admission work-package mapping and the previous audit's “non-blocking” label do not weaken this explicit acceptance criterion. No accepted bounded operating envelope waives it. Final status: `PARTIALLY_DEMONSTRATED_BLOCKING`.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_ASSESSMENT.md:94:Accepted tests demonstrate preservation of decisions, findings, plan states, whitespace, and compaction provenance, and show that expired authority is not resurrected. They do not demonstrate preservation of every listed per-source property across every stage. In particular, per-item version, workspace applicability, and freshness are not evidenced, and the stale-knowledge acceptance criterion remains unproven. Compaction provenance is useful but is not equivalent to the full mandatory contract. No accepted bounded operating envelope waives it. Final status: `PARTIALLY_DEMONSTRATED_BLOCKING`.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_ASSESSMENT.md:110:Phase 2 does **not** require literal registration of every extension in the concrete `CapabilityRegistry` class or literal traversal through a class named `ExecutionSpine`. Those are Phase 3/4 architectural mechanisms. The normative obligation is semantic: declared extension authority and isolation must hold, core data protection must not be bypassed, and middleware changes must be recorded as specified. The missing middleware evidence remains material regardless of dispatch mechanism. No accepted bounded operating envelope waives it. Final status: `PARTIALLY_DEMONSTRATED_BLOCKING`.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_ASSESSMENT.md:138:No remaining requirement is classified `PARTIALLY_DEMONSTRATED_NON_BLOCKING`. The earlier non-blocking follow-up labels for CTX-001/002 and EXT-004 are retained as historical operator context, but they do not demonstrate or waive the explicit Phase 2 criteria. The current task specifically requires closure determination from the normative contract and permits a bounded interpretation only where an accepted operating envelope satisfies it; no such interpretation is established for these gaps.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md:157:## Release qualification and waivers\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md:159:- **Manual real-terminal matrix: required and not yet accepted.** The fifteen-cell manual E3 matrix (xterm, kitty, tmux in GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60) requires actual operator runs on the exact installed RC with a verdict and observed outcomes recorded for each cell. Automated CI and PTY scenarios do not substitute for this evidence. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18; DEC-19 withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md:160:- **Screenshot artifacts: waived** for v1.0.0 by [DEC-18](../v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver).\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md:162:Every other acceptance gate — installed-RC platform and lifecycle evidence, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger — is unaffected by these waivers and is governed by the release decision record.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/README.md:5:**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:241:| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | PTY CI plus a manual real-terminal matrix. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | TEST (PTY suites in CI); UNV (real terminals) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §5 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:276:| New v1 rows (§3) | 92 | **31 B**, 58 RR, 3 P. 79 open, 9 partial (REQ-SEC-118, REQ-PRV-101, REQ-PRV-103, REQ-PRV-105, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-PER-106, REQ-OPS-101, REQ-QUAL-108, REQ-QUAL-110), 1 implemented (REQ-OPS-103), 4 tested (REQ-SEC-103, REQ-SEC-119, REQ-PER-101, REQ-PER-102). |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:241:## DEC-18: v1.0.0 terminal screenshot-artifact waiver\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:243:**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:245:**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:247:**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:249:## DEC-19: withdrawn v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:251:**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:253:**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:255:**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:257:**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | All 15 cells have actual manual execution, recorded PASS/FAIL verdicts, observed outcomes, and evidence bound to the exact installed RC. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 do not substitute for these cells. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:159:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:192:**Required for v1.0.0.** Run every terminal × size combination below against the exact installed RC and record a verdict and observed outcomes for each cell. Automated suites in §5.1 and §5.2 remain required but do not replace operator execution. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. See [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-withdrawn-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:206:Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); this does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:336:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI and scripted gates PASS, and all 15 manual real-terminal cells have verified operator evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshots only.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:126:| HIST-01 | S2 | Extensions/MCP, release gating | docs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_ASSESSMENT.md:7,112-121; cli/src/plugins.ts:150-200 | DOC-CLAIM+SOURCE: Issue #12 remains OPEN; CTX-001, CTX-002, EXT-004 never closed in any later doc. EXT-004 still unmet at HEAD: `executeToolPipeline` pre/post middleware can rewrite args/results with no before/after audit record | Plugins can silently alter what tools did; prompt provenance not reconstructable | Either implement or record an explicit operator waiver/supersession before v1; do not ship v1 with silently-open normative blockers |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:190:| REQ-SEC-V1-01 | EXT-004 met or formally waived: middleware arg/result changes emit before/after audit | Normative MUST open since 10-01 | BLOCKER (or written waiver + plugins documented as fully trusted) | Plugin rewriting args → audit record with both states |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:202:## 8. Deferred, waived, or quietly dropped requirements (do not lose)\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:5:**Custodian update (2026-10-29).** The release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0 ([DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)). The gate is **waived, not passed**: no cell verdicts were recorded, the automated CI PTY suites and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios remain required and passing, and the release notes must disclose the waiver. The terminal-matrix item is no longer an outstanding qualification gate; every other gate in this checkpoint is unchanged.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:11:**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. Per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver), screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:21:**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not establish successor-RC qualification. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned (last updated 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC); no custodian acceptance or held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification is established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user waived screenshot artifacts, while terminal behavior checks remain unrun. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, required human terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:37:Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its last update was 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC, with no custodian response observed. No held-out payload was accessed and no held-out qualification was run. The manual terminal matrix's last recorded result is 0/15; terminal setup exists on Ubuntu, but no operator screenshots or cell verdicts have been supplied. Held-out/T2/T3/T4, remaining provider and standalone coverage, successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:51:**Qualification, custody, and publication:** GitHub still lists [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) as the latest release; there is no `v1.0.0` tag or stable release. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, with the last metadata-only custodian request at 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC and no response observed. No protected payload was accessed or qualification run. The manual terminal matrix remains 0/15; the final installed RC does not exist. Exact-RC held-out/T2/T3/T4, provider and standalone coverage, cross-runner reproducibility, human terminal evidence, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. The chosen distribution target remains the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:81:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Held-out T2/T3/T4, remaining live-provider and standalone gates, successor-RC artifact qualification, cross-runner evidence, the 15-cell human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on these mandatory checks.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:228:**Terminal observation and acceptance:** The user reports that the client rendered at the sizes they tried except in tmux inside GNOME Terminal; the smallest observed tmux window was 43×13. They said the remaining observations may take several days. No screenshots, exact installed-package identity, or cell-by-cell results were supplied. The 15-cell worksheet therefore remains 0/15 and unaccepted; the report is retained as provisional operator context only. Do not prompt while other gates can progress.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:240:**Current convergence PRs:** PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264), head `73bdc7d91b1b8925b522b052d89228d99bad4893` on base `2622663313132864677cfdc93c94944d26a3ac06`, has independent ACCEPT; Node 22, Node 24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while its Linux package job remains in progress. It records scripted terminal evidence only and does not complete the manual terminal gate. PR [#266](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/266), head `11fc29ba39bc76624c55d34a1fc12b4d7544522a` on the same prior base, has Node 24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passing; its Node 22 TUI test failure is being rerun, currently in progress. PR [#267](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/267), head `d0cac8b959e3da8595a41651a60a2fcd3738d034` on current base `14a9c15`, carries the malformed credential-origin fix. Its exact two-file diff has independent ACCEPT (SHA-256 `2da500d09522bc059f63b07251953c552ac2270168c72d43920b181e44fd89d3`) and the focused provider connection suite passed 37/37 after rebase; its Node 22 and Node 24 jobs are running and CodeQL passed. None of these PRs is integrated yet. PR #265 merged at `14a9c152`; its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed. Its OpenRouter evidence covers one pinned-model verification and one synthetic small task, not full provider or standalone qualification.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:244:**Held-out and human gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open with no custodian acceptance recorded; no held-out payload was accessed and T2/T3/T4 acceptance is not established. The manual terminal matrix still requires operator evidence across five environments and three sizes. At 2026-10-27 03:49 UTC, I verified over SSH to `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`) that `/home/mike/nexus-rc10-manual-evidence/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md` exists and contains an unfilled 15-cell template with directories for every environment/size pair. No cell evidence is present; the installed candidate identity is blank. Any matrix run must use the eventual installed RC. Scripted PTY output is not a substitute.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:302:**Terminal environment preparation:** A strict known-host SSH connection to the configured Ubuntu/GNOME desktop succeeded. Read-only inventory found xterm 407, kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, and VS Code 1.143.1; an active GNOME Wayland session is present. This is environment availability only. No manual terminal cell was run, no screenshot was captured, and the §5.3 matrix remains **0/15**. It still requires each of the five terminals at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with approval-panel and post-exit screenshots for every cell and genuine operator verdicts.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:304:**Acceptance and remaining gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest public metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Private custody acceptance and evaluator-compatible sealed corpus readiness remain unestablished; no held-out payload was accessed or run. PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) remains open at c3bb2235, based on b73b6ec; it needs refresh onto ff349383 after remediation. Exact-head CI run [40338957629](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957629) failed on both Node 22 and Node 24 at `npm --prefix cli test`; CodeQL [40338957381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957381) passed on the old candidate. This failure is on PR head c3bb2235 based on b73b6ec, not current main; refresh after remediation before using CI as evidence. A local, unpushed commit 8655ca87 fixes request-correlated local-setup cancellation (focused Node 34/34, Rust 4/4, build and diff checks passed), but the independent rereview recorded other unresolved credential/configuration findings; it is not integrated or accepted. T2/T3/T4, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, exact-candidate reproducibility, the manual terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; no stable v1.0.0 release exists. Publication authority remains granted and gated by acceptance.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:397:**Remaining qualification and disposition:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public update is the coordinator request from 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no custodian response or new custody acceptance. Held-out qualification has not started. Provider/standalone qualification remains incomplete, including OpenRouter; T2/T3/T4 qualification remains incomplete; the five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; RC7 is unaccepted and no stable `v1.0.0` release is published. Publication authorization remains granted and gated on all required acceptance evidence.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:407:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest comment is coordinator-authored at 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible held-out corpus disposition. Held-out T2 has not started, and no private payload was accessed. Provider/standalone qualification and T3/T4 evidence remain incomplete. The five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15, with no per-cell verdicts or required screenshots. The `cli/src/agent.ts` remediation handoff remains with KimiCode-defect-scan; implementation is still pending in that claimed lane.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:421:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest status has no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible corpus disposition. No held-out qualification is evidenced. The Ubuntu/GNOME terminal host is now connected and its five requested terminal applications were found in a setup-only preflight; the worksheet still has all 15 cells blank, no exact RC is installed there, and no screenshot evidence exists. The five-environment by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; independent exact-RC acceptance and stable-release gates are incomplete.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:423:**Next evidence:** Finish the RC7 Release workflow and verify its exact artifact identity and provenance. Finish exact-head CI for PRs #243–245, integrate only after required review and checks, and requalify resulting main before constructing a subsequent candidate. The `cli/src/agent.ts` defect-remediation handoff is recorded for KimiCode-defect-scan; its implementation is not yet present in that branch. Resolve independent held-out custody and evaluator compatibility before beginning protected qualification; then qualify an eligible installed RC and complete the manual terminal matrix. Keep source gates, RC construction, installed-RC qualification, and stable-release checks distinct.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:539:- **Requirements gate:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was independently rerun with isolated HOME/XDG on exact `7d6673f` and passed: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. This source-stage gate pass does not satisfy those qualification requirements.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:559:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed on exact source tree `8f4504e` (tree `2a0799c8a32e88e34322b712cf937d73cbe4d637`), with isolated `HOME`/XDG: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven rows remain below the ordinary tested threshold pending their approved exact-RC evidence: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The pre-RC checker pass does not imply those RC gates have passed or authorize an acceptance claim.\n/home/mike/nexu