ocs.md:49:3. **REQ-OPS-103.** Issue #12's open blockers (CTX-001, CTX-002, EXT-004) and the quietly superseded items (UI-006/007, DEDUP-003, \"no remote\", SUBP-004/005 deferrals) each have a written disposition in the ledger (implemented, waived with rationale, or superseded), per DEC-04.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/handoff-codex-t4-acceptance-2026-10-17.md:38:- **Line 17:** \"The T4 denominator conflict (eight stated classes versus nine enumerated cases) and CJK/Hangul tokenizer acceptance conflict remain unresolved owner/spec decisions.\" → both are now resolved: T4 denominator by the **DEC-05 amendment (2026-10-17, nine classes retained)** and the tokenizer conflict by **DEC-17**. Remaining pending items in that sentence (T3 authoring, manual terminal acceptance, M5 execution, independent acceptance, exact-RC package checks, cross-runner reproducibility, publication) are unchanged.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:40:This records artifact identity, published checksums, provenance verification results, and an installed-package version/self-test. It does not establish provider behavior, upgrade behavior from RC6, held-out results, standalone engineering correctness, T3/T4 results, cross-runner reproducibility, the manual terminal matrix, or independent RC acceptance. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/heldout-authorship-handoff-2026-10-17.md:8:| Authority | Owner, 2026-10-17: **no independence waiver granted.** |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":37041}},"started_at_ms":1793246337824,"completed_at_ms":1793246337824}}
