{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:59:04.805Z","ordinal":489133,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a185cd-baa4-7fe1-bac6-635c68bc9b1f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c47fee5e-e2cc-4c66-b7e5-2cc6224e4c42","process_id":"19450","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore diff -- docs/releases/v1.0.0.md docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore diff -- docs/releases/v1.0.0.md docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md b/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\nindex b12111ef..cbf2fa48 100644\n--- a/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\n+++ b/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\n@@ -156,7 +156,7 @@ nexus doctor\n \n ## Release qualification and waivers\n \n-- **Manual real-terminal matrix: waived.** The fifteen-cell manual E3 matrix (xterm, kitty, tmux in GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60) was waived for v1.0.0 by the release owner on 2026-10-29 ([DEC-19](../v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)). This is a waiver, not a pass: no per-cell verdict was recorded. Terminal evidence for this release is the automated CI PTY suites and the scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios defined by ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2; they remain required for the exact accepted candidate.\n+- **Manual real-terminal matrix: required and not yet accepted.** The fifteen-cell manual E3 matrix (xterm, kitty, tmux in GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60) requires actual operator runs on the exact installed RC with a verdict and observed outcomes recorded for each cell. Automated CI and PTY scenarios do not substitute for this evidence. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18; DEC-19 withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record.\n - **Screenshot artifacts: waived** for v1.0.0 by [DEC-18](../v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver).\n \n Every other acceptance gate — installed-RC platform and lifecycle evidence, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger — is unaffected by these waivers and is governed by the release decision record.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nindex 9f7180b9..8a0f266c 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n | ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n-| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | **Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** No per-cell verdicts are recorded; this is not a PASS. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 remain required. |\n+| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | All 15 cells have actual manual execution, recorded PASS/FAIL verdicts, observed outcomes, and evidence bound to the exact installed RC. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 do not substitute for these cells. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18. |\n \n ## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n \n@@ -189,7 +189,7 @@ These are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n \n ### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n \n-**Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** The procedure below is retained for a successor release; it is not required for v1.0.0 and no cell verdict is recorded. The automated suites in §5.1 and §5.2 remain mandatory.\n+**Required for v1.0.0.** Run every terminal × size combination below against the exact installed RC and record a verdict and observed outcomes for each cell. Automated suites in §5.1 and §5.2 remain required but do not replace operator execution. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. See [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-withdrawn-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\n \n Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n \n@@ -333,7 +333,7 @@ G6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable\n - [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n - [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n - [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n-- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI and scripted gates PASS; the manual real-terminal matrix is waived for v1.0.0 per DEC-19.\n+- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI and scripted gates PASS, and all 15 manual real-terminal cells have verified operator evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshots only.\n - [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n - [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n - [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\nindex db87654c..d4962156 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n@@ -246,15 +246,15 @@ This amendment is **narrow by design**. It applies only to corpora where the mea\n \n **Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\n \n-## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n+## DEC-19: withdrawn v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n \n-**Context.** [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waived screenshot artifacts only; the fifteen manual matrix cells (five terminals × three sizes, ACCEPTANCE §5.3) remained mandatory. On 2026-10-29 the release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0.\n+**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\n \n-**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-29).** The manual E3 matrix, its per-cell PASS/FAIL verdicts and its evidence records are not required for v1.0.0. ACC-TUI-MANUAL is **waived**, not PASS: no cell verdict is recorded and none may be inferred. The automated CI PTY suites and the scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2) remain mandatory and are the only terminal evidence for this release. This waiver changes no other acceptance criterion, safety gate, or verification rule, and it does not change any requirements-ledger status: REQ-QUAL-108 remains `partial` unless the ledger owner records a different disposition.\n+**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\n \n-**Disclosure.** The v1.0.0 release notes must state that the manual real-terminal matrix was waived by owner decision and that terminal evidence is automated (PTY/CI) only.\n+**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\n \n-**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS.\n+**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\n \n ## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md b/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\nindex a14e4c3e..186b674f 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n For `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3).\n \n-> **Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** This worksheet is retained for a successor release. It contains no results, no cell verdict is recorded for v1.0.0, and it does not qualify an RC.\n+> **Required for v1.0.0.** Complete all 15 cells against the exact installed RC. Blank cells are incomplete; no result is inferred. Automated PTY runs do not count as manual cell evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. The prior waiver record is withdrawn by [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-withdrawn-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\n \n ## Installed candidate identity\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\nindex 81046edf..82501ad1 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ Standalone live inference evidence is absent (HIST-08; SPEC-05). Real-terminal c\n    - The scorer logs every replacement.\n    - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\n 7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n-8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts) are mandatory. A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. **The manual matrix is waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)**; no per-cell verdicts are recorded and this is not a PASS. Screenshot artifacts were waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). Automated terminal evidence is the only terminal evidence for this release.\n+8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts) are mandatory. A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. All 15 cells require actual operator execution and per-cell verdict/evidence bound to the exact installed RC; automated terminal evidence does not replace this gate. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-withdrawn-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix waiver record.\n 9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0, false-presence = 0 (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-18), and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\n 10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\n \n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":29802}},"started_at_ms":1793246344804,"completed_at_ms":1793246344805}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:59:06.256Z","ordinal":489134,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a185cf-bc10-7b61-bfa1-d1f43a3b0741","call_id":"call_2d31dc0f48d14c50b268136b069124ec","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"diff --git a/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md b/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\nindex b12111ef..cbf2fa48 100644\n--- a/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\n+++ b/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\n@@ -156,7 +156,7 @@ nexus doctor\n \n ## Release qualification and waivers\n \n-- **Manual real-terminal matrix: waived.** The fifteen-cell manual E3 matrix (xterm, kitty, tmux in GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60) was waived for v1.0.0 by the release owner on 2026-10-29 ([DEC-19](../v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)). This is a waiver, not a pass: no per-cell verdict was recorded. Terminal evidence for this release is the automated CI PTY suites and the scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios defined by ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2; they remain required for the exact accepted candidate.\n+- **Manual real-terminal matrix: required and not yet accepted.** The fifteen-cell manual E3 matrix (xterm, kitty, tmux in GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60) requires actual operator runs on the exact installed RC with a verdict and observed outcomes recorded for each cell. Automated CI and PTY scenarios do not substitute for this evidence. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18; DEC-19 withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record.\n - **Screenshot artifacts: waived** for v1.0.0 by [DEC-18](../v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver).\n \n Every other acceptance gate — installed-RC platform and lifecycle evidence, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger — is unaffected by these waivers and is governed by the release decision record.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nindex 9f7180b9..8a0f266c 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n | ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n-| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | **Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** No per-cell verdicts are recorded; this is not a PASS. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 remain required. |\n+| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | All 15 cells have actual manual execution, recorded PASS/FAIL verdicts, observed outcomes, and evidence bound to the exact installed RC. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 do not substitute for these cells. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18. |\n \n ## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n \n@@ -189,7 +189,7 @@ These are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n \n ### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n \n-**Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** The procedure below is retained for a successor release; it is not required for v1.0.0 and no cell verdict is recorded. The automated suites in §5.1 and §5.2 remain mandatory.\n+**Required for v1.0.0.** Run every terminal × size combination below against the exact installed RC and record a verdict and observed outcomes for each cell. Automated suites in §5.1 and §5.2 remain required but do not replace operator execution. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. See [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-withdrawn-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\n \n Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n \n@@ -333,7 +333,7 @@ G6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable\n - [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n - [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n - [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n-- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI and scripted gates PASS; the manual real-terminal matrix is waived for v1.0.0 per DEC-19.\n+- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI and scripted gates PASS, and all 15 manual real-terminal cells have verified operator evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshots only.\n - [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n - [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n - [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\nindex db87654c..d4962156 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n@@ -246,15 +246,15 @@ This amendment is **narrow by design**. It applies only to corpora where the mea\n \n **Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\n \n-## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n+## DEC-19: withdrawn v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n \n-**Context.** [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waived screenshot artifacts only; the fifteen manual matrix cells (five terminals × three sizes, ACCEPTANCE §5.3) remained mandatory. On 2026-10-29 the release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0.\n+**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\n \n-**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-29).** The manual E3 matrix, its per-cell PASS/FAIL verdicts and its evidence records are not required for v1.0.0. ACC-TUI-MANUAL is **waived**, not PASS: no cell verdict is recorded and none may be inferred. The automated CI PTY suites and the scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2) remain mandatory and are the only terminal evidence for this release. This waiver changes no other acceptance criterion, safety gate, or verification rule, and it does not change any requirements-ledger status: REQ-QUAL-108 remains `partial` unless the ledger owner records a different disposition.\n+**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\n \n-**Disclosure.** The v1.0.0 release notes must state that the manual real-terminal matrix was waived by owner decision and that terminal evidence is automated (PTY/CI) only.\n+**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\n \n-**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS.\n+**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\n \n ## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md b/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\nindex a14e4c3e..186b674f 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n For `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3).\n \n-> **Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** This worksheet is retained for a successor release. It contains no results, no cell verdict is recorded for v1.0.0, and it does not qualify an RC.\n+> **Required for v1.0.0.** Complete all 15 cells against the exact installed RC. Blank cells are incomplete; no result is inferred. Automated PTY runs do not count as manual cell evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. The prior waiver record is withdrawn by [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-withdrawn-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\n \n ## Installed candidate identity\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\nindex 81046edf..82501ad1 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ Standalone live inference evidence is absent (HIST-08; SPEC-05). Real-terminal c\n    - The scorer logs every replacement.\n    - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\n 7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n-8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts) are mandatory. A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. **The manual matrix is waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)**; no per-cell verdicts are recorded and this is not a PASS. Screenshot artifacts were waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). Automated terminal evidence is the only terminal evidence for this release.\n+8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts) are mandatory. A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. All 15 cells require actual operator execution and per-cell verdict/evidence bound to the exact installed RC; automated terminal evidence does not replace this gate. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-withdrawn-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix waiver record.\n 9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0, false-presence = 0 (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-18), and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\n 10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\n \n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a185cd-baa4-7fe1-bac6-6