{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T04:02:40.845Z","ordinal":489232,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a185cd-baa4-7fe1-bac6-635c68bc9b1f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-94d33df1-f82e-4995-a0b0-51eb2aa26e9f","process_id":"9843","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore status --short --branch; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore diff --stat; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore diff -- docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | head -n 200; stat -c '%y %n' /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9 status --short --branch"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore status --short --branch; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore diff --stat; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore diff -- docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | head -n 200; stat -c '%y %n' /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v9 status --short --branch"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## codex/restore-terminal-human-matrix...origin/main\n M docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n docs/releases/v1.0.0.md                                    |  4 ++--\n docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md                                  |  6 +++---\n docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md                                   | 10 ++++++----\n docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md                                   | 14 +++++++++-----\n docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md                   |  2 +-\n .../specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md       |  2 +-\n 6 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\nindex db87654c..d081f852 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n@@ -248,13 +248,15 @@ This amendment is **narrow by design**. It applies only to corpora where the mea\n \n ## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n \n-**Context.** [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waived screenshot artifacts only; the fifteen manual matrix cells (five terminals × three sizes, ACCEPTANCE §5.3) remained mandatory. On 2026-10-29 the release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0.\n+**Status: withdrawn.** The waiver described in this decision is not in effect.\n \n-**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-29).** The manual E3 matrix, its per-cell PASS/FAIL verdicts and its evidence records are not required for v1.0.0. ACC-TUI-MANUAL is **waived**, not PASS: no cell verdict is recorded and none may be inferred. The automated CI PTY suites and the scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2) remain mandatory and are the only terminal evidence for this release. This waiver changes no other acceptance criterion, safety gate, or verification rule, and it does not change any requirements-ledger status: REQ-QUAL-108 remains `partial` unless the ledger owner records a different disposition.\n+**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\n \n-**Disclosure.** The v1.0.0 release notes must state that the manual real-terminal matrix was waived by owner decision and that terminal evidence is automated (PTY/CI) only.\n+**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\n \n-**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS.\n+**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\n+\n+**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\n \n ## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\nindex 70ade8f1..f770e49f 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n@@ -1,19 +1,23 @@\n # v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n \n-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 22:00 UTC; custodian update 2026-10-29)\n+## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 03:58 UTC)\n \n-**Custodian update (2026-10-29).** The release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0 ([DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)). The gate is **waived, not passed**: no cell verdicts were recorded, the automated CI PTY suites and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios remain required and passing, and the release notes must disclose the waiver. The terminal-matrix item is no longer an outstanding qualification gate; every other gate in this checkpoint is unchanged.\n+**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` (PR #312 merge). Exact-main CI run [40802654248](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654248) and CodeQL run [40802654255](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654255) passed on that SHA. The exact-source requirements gate passed with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open); 12 requirements remain mapped to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n \n-**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496`, the PR #308 merge commit. Exact-main CI run [40770466028](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770466028) completed successfully at 2026-10-28 21:58:49 UTC on this SHA. Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices passed; Linux x86_64 passed Rust and CLI tests, requirements and security gates, reproducible package builds with matching output hashes, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. CodeQL run [40770465935](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770465935) completed successfully. On a clean detached worktree at this exact SHA, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n+**Candidate convergence:** PR #311 remains open at `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954` on the older base `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`; its Node 22/24, Linux x86_64 and CodeQL checks passed, while its Entire gate failed because the branch was behind and lacked independent approval. A local candidate at `fe28ec9e686b90e69e42a7a13d55f50264b3775f` includes an accepted readiness refresh but has not run exact-head hosted checks. PR #315's required GitHub checks passed, but its waiver conclusion conflicts with this current release decision and must not be merged as-is. The current documentation correction has independent review pending after updating this checkpoint.\n \n-**Integrated changes:** PR #309 merged as `b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af` at 20:36 UTC with checksummed RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider evidence. PR #300 merged as `79cba842e86d64f895e1a269636776cdf1e7e6da` at 21:07:46 UTC after Node 22/24, Linux packaging/tests, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. PR #308 merged as `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496` at 21:15:37 UTC; exact PR head `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` passed Node 22/24 and Linux, with JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; its GitHub Entire Gates check was neutral. A post-merge source reviewer found no blocking defect in the reviewed restore path and reported a separate Entire trail 23 signal: approvals failed and one high-severity finding was unresolved. A later authenticated, read-only Entire query on `ubuntu-desktop` (2026-10-28 21:48 UTC) found trail 23 open but its Nexus Code change marked merged; the finding and approvals commands reported no open change, so the historical finding text and its disposition could not be retrieved. The earlier high-severity signal therefore remains unresolved/unverified and must be reconciled before successor-RC qualification; the later query does not establish that it was resolved. The current-main source CI passed as recorded above; this does not qualify an installed release candidate.\n+**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The prior held-out custodian is recorded as OpenCode; SageBridge accepted the handoff on 2026-10-29. The custodian status record reports a successor T2 store with 20 of 40 tasks converted; the remaining Go/Rust tasks are blocked by the current oracle toolchain boundary. Reported T3 digest/schema/isolation checks are 8/8, which is not full T3 task-quality qualification. A custodian validation invocation is still live, with no result accepted. T2 custody acceptance and qualification, T3/T4 qualification, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, fault injection, successor-RC reproducibility and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC10 evidence does not qualify a successor candidate.\n \n-**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. Per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver), screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n+**Terminal gate:** The release owner requires all 15 manual terminal cells (five environments × three sizes) on the exact installed RC. The current worksheet has no accepted cell evidence; blank cells remain incomplete. Actual operator execution and per-cell outcomes are mandatory; automated CI or PTY results do not substitute. [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waives screenshots only. [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal applications, but the manual matrix remains outstanding.\n+\n+**Active validation:** `make test` is running on immutable snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c`; the latest observed tests passed, and the overall result is pending. This run is not exact-current-main or RC qualification evidence.\n \n **Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n \n ## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 20:18 UTC; superseded)\n \n+This historical checkpoint includes a matrix-waiver conclusion that was later withdrawn by the current DEC-19 decision. It records the prior checkpoint only and is not the current acceptance disposition.\n+\n **Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`, the merge commit for PR #305. Exact-main CI run [40751988282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988282) and CodeQL run [40751988267](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988267) passed on that SHA. The source requirements check passed on this revision with 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, and 12 deferred to exact-RC qualification. These source-stage results do not qualify an installed release candidate.\n \n **Integrated changes and open PRs:** PR #299 merged as `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` (merge commit `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`). PR #307 merged as `90837aa5193d7c071066d27ccefd2b2ea2db0aff`. PR #305 merged at `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`; its GitHub Entire Gates check concluded **NEUTRAL** (“No trail tracks this branch”). PR #302 was closed unmerged. PR #308 supersedes it and is open at `2c1b2dfa6b10f736367020a86228ab64a4173500` on current base `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`. Exact-head CI run [40757432379](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757432379) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed. The PR head fixes the `globName` test by staging it with the literal `:(literal)` pathspec. A separate local follow-up commit `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` applies literal staging to the `magicName` fixture and asserts that it entered the index; this follow-up is not on the PR head. Its focused 77/77 result is owner-reported without a retained log, so that additional fixture change still needs exact-head checks before integration. PR #309 is open at `aace981bc3f46e10f1e57c5498825a76e9994ee5` on the current base. Run [40758300812](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40758300812) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed, and Linux packaging/tests are in progress. PR #300 is open at `f3957a67ac8f9b5ea1e60be2494b9402d943230f` on the current base. Run [40757603196](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757603196) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. A fresh checkpoint accuracy correction was posted on PR #300 (comment [6479279112](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300#issuecomment-6479279112)); this local update addresses the stale PR heads and main-CI status identified there. Source PR checks are distinct from release qualification.\n2026-10-29 04:01:24.133151868 +0000 /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n2026-10-29 04:01:23.825146552 +0000 /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n## v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9...origin/main [ahead 38]\n M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":13363716}},"started_at_ms":1793246560831,"completed_at_ms":1793246560845}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T04:02:42.258Z","ordinal":489233,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a185d3-07d2-7022-9380-0f6efa970712","call_id":"call_0b3efdd66cfd40b4842840b4a1990f7b","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3789)\nTotal output lines: 75\n\n## codex/restore-terminal-human-matrix...origin/main\n M docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n docs/releases/v1.0.0.md                                    |  4 ++--\n docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md                                  |  6 +++---\n docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md                                   | 10 ++++++----\n docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md                                   | 14 +++++++++-----\n docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md                   |  2 +-\n .../specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md       |  2 +-\n 6 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\nindex db87654c..d081f852 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n@@ -248,13 +248,15 @@ This amendment is **narrow by design**. It applies only to corpora where the mea\n \n ## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n \n-**Context.** [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waived screenshot artifacts only; the fifteen manual matrix cells (five terminals × three sizes, ACCEPTANCE §5.3) remained mandatory. On 2026-10-29 the release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0.\n+**Status: withdrawn.** The waiver described in this decision is not in effect.\n \n-**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-29).** The manual E3 matrix, its per-cell PASS/FAIL verdicts and its evidence records are not required for v1.0.0. ACC-TUI-MANUAL is **waived**, not PASS: no cell verdict is recorded and none may be inferred. The automated CI PTY suites and the scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2) remain mandatory and are the only terminal evidence for this release. This waiver changes no other acceptance criterion, safety gate, or verification rule, and it does not change any requirements-ledger status: REQ-QUAL-108 remains `partial` unless the ledger owner records a different disposition.\n+**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\n \n-**Disclosure.** The v1.0.0 release notes must state that the manual real-terminal matrix was waived by owner decision and that terminal evidence is automated (PTY/CI) only.\n+**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\n \n-**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS.\n+**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\n+\n+**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\n \n ## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\nindex 70ade8f1..f770e49f 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n@@ -1,19 +1,23 @@\n # v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n \n-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 22:00 UTC; custodian update 2026-10-29)\n+## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 03:58 UTC)\n \n-**Custodian update (2026-10-29).** The release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0 ([DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)). The gate is **waived, not passed**: no cell verdicts were recorded, the automated CI PTY suites and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios remain required and passing, and the release notes must disclose the waiver. The terminal-matrix item is no longer an outstanding qualification gate; every other gate in this checkpoint is unchanged.\n+**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` (PR #312 merge). Exact-main CI run [40802654248](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654248) and CodeQL run [40802654255](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654255) passed on that SHA. The exact-source requirements gate passed with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open); 12 requirements remain mapped to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n \n-**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496`, the PR #308 merge commit. Exact-main CI run [40770466028](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770466028) completed successfully at 2026-10-28 21:58:49 UTC on this SHA. Node 22 and Node 24 tes