{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T04:22:28.123Z","ordinal":490100,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a185e5-201b-78d0-ad96-3fb9db005380","call_id":"call_daed923447844ff3bfcfa683ca2c148d","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — exact head `fe28ec9e686b90e69e42a7a13d55f50264b3775f`.\\n\\nThe only change from `e12f81e` anchors the 03:44 UTC issue metadata to the checkpoint’s 03:45 UTC observation. That resolves the freshness concern; live metadata still shows issue #1 open and unassigned. The rest of the checkpoint is unchanged from my prior review, including the verified main checks, snapshot-suite distinction, manual waiver, and partial `REQ-QUAL-108`.\\n\\nRead-only review only; no tests or edits.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — commit `2e9ad10` correctly reports custodian revalidation as waiting on the active `SUITE` claim, with no result accepted.\\n\\nThe manual matrix remains mandatory across 15 cells in the acceptance docs, worksheet, specification, and release notes. DEC-19 is withdrawn; DEC-18 waives screenshots only. The readiness checkpoint’s main-CI, PR, issue, and ref-ancestry claims match the evidence checked. The `REQUIREMENTS.md` ledger is unchanged.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for PR #315’s documentation diff. Reviewed base `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` → head `706c3b6cda2577f1ee3ae3665c42859045a9dfa2`. Cumulative diff SHA-256: `7fe68b53f754a5a33b6edbac53d63562957e71e82eb5a1746321f90430628b44`.\\n\\nThe changed acceptance map, worksheet, PLAN-10, and SPEC-10 consistently treat DEC-19 as a v1.0.0 manual-matrix waiver, not a pass; they retain the CI and scripted PTY gates and the successor-release matrix procedure. DEC-18 remains the separate screenshot-artifact waiver. REQUIREMENTS.md is unchanged.\\n\\nREADINESS.md is outside this diff and remains separately owned; its current checkpoint still needs reconciliation of manual-matrix status. This PR’s body explicitly calls out that separate work.\\n\\nI could not record the disposition on **Entire trail 30**: the only configured Entire context reports “Not logged in,” and trail access failed because `org.freedesktop.secrets` has no service on this host. I did not use the repository owner’s GitHub identity. At review time, Node 22/24 and Entire Gates were still running. No tests were run.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a185e4-f059-7c83-884e-9306f1442d74","create_time":1793247748.1233726}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
