{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T04:23:45.902Z","ordinal":490165,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a185e4-f059-7c83-884e-9306f1442d74","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b8ab1a8c-0e2d-4631-98fb-3b4c04b2e2f1","process_id":"81341","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 311 --json body,commits,reviews,comments,mergeable,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision; gh run view 40803164040 --json conclusion,status,headSha,jobs,url; gh pr view 316 --json reviews,comments,body; gh run view 40816301224 --json status,conclusion,headSha,jobs,url; gh pr view 317 --json reviews,comments,body;"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 311 --json body,commits,reviews,comments,mergeable,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision; gh run view 40803164040 --json conclusion,status,headSha,jobs,url; gh pr view 316 --json reviews,comments,body; gh run view 40816301224 --json status,conclusion,headSha,jobs,url; gh pr view 317 --json reviews,comments,body;"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/26/changes/nexus-code/26\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nIntegrates reviewed release-critical source fixes for operation checkpoint/Git recovery, state and context restoration, provider and credential handling, evaluator resource assertions, plan-only turn outcomes, batch-read error propagation, and terminal-safe error rendering.\\n\\n## Exact revision\\n\\n- Base: `main` at `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`\\n- Head: `v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9` at `0f9da7ce040a26bb3df60b43101665f949fb36a0`\\n\\n## Review and validation\\n\\n- Fresh independent full-diff review: **ACCEPT** for the exact base/head above; diff SHA-256 `bfa2008fcdbf8de968a651a815b52a05fa73e9abfe5dc0c46a09084dd3a6a0ea`. Reviewer ran no tests.\\n- Focused local validation on the exact head: `state.test.ts` 47/47 passed; `operation_view.test.ts` passed. The test helper checks raw terminal output with color disabled.\\n- Exact-head CI run `40795179309`: sync-version, requirements, npm ci, CLI build/dist integrity, Rust tests and release build passed. Node 22 and Node 24 CLI test matrices are still running. Exact-head CodeQL run `40795179263` passed.\\n- A prior local `make test` process ended without an exit code or result captured; it is **not** claimed as a pass.\\n- Independent regression fix for recovered merged work remains on a separate branch and is not included in this PR pending focused validation and coordinated integration.\\n\\n## Release status\\n\\nThis PR does not create or accept an RC. Held-out custody/qualification, provider and standalone checks, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, and the real-terminal matrix remain required. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated.\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgmO9Dw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"coderabbitai\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> - [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\n> \\n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n> \\n> <details>\\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\n> <dl>\\n> <dd>\\n> \\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\\n> - **Run ID**: `1ccbeaa2-3add-418e-8a98-8e649e54172c`\\n> \\n> </dd>\\n> </dl>\\n> </details>\\n\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\\n- [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --> <strong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=311)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T22:40:42Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":true,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6482541839\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgmUAxw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Current-base gate evidence (2026-10-28): a clean detached worktree at exact `main` commit `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e` passed `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` (123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification) and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` (`1.0.0-rc.10`). Post-merge main CI run `40781709732` is still running; this is not a post-merge CI pass. PR #311 exact-head CI run `40781787834` remains in progress.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T22:44:55Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6482624711\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgnkXyg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Independent review of the current PR311 candidate found one remaining security-test defect: `assertNoUnsafeTerminalControls` removes all `ESC[...m` SGR sequences before checking output. The fixture now sets `NO_COLOR=1` and asserts the hostile `ESC[31m` is visible as `␛[31m`, but the stripping helper could still hide a raw SGR escape emitted alongside the visible representation.\\n\\nPlease remove the helper and keep direct raw-control assertions on the unmodified output for all five CLI cases. The independent reviewer returned CHANGES_REQUIRED for this exact diff (SHA-256 `148ee8493d71a93f6fe679cee8677bca6fbd8a230721780b0ed2d7d2a62ed7c6`). Auto-merge is disabled until this is corrected, independently reviewed, and required exact-head checks pass.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T00:00:02Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6483941322\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgnqX3Q\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review — `8e3bd150` (base `cbb3b653`, diff SHA-256 `d4d6b9d7f85ab4b4b24171ef500e92a0fe30a1bddaf4fcd471708c394df354ee`)\\n\\nThis is a 21-file aggregate (+1,230/-152), so I am stating exactly what I did and did not cover.\\n\\n**Verified (isolated worktree, isolated HOME/XDG):**\\n- `tsc --noEmit` 0 errors; `git diff --check` clean.\\n- TS suites `context_management`, `operation_git`, `operation_view`, `operation_account_identity`, `provider_cli`, `provider_connect`, `state`, `update_plan_turn_result`, `eval_integrity`: 197/198 pass. The one failure (\\\"qualification runtime mounts ... overlap\\\") needs a built `cli/dist`, which my bare worktrees lack, and it **fails identically on `main` `cbb3b653`**, so it is my harness, not this PR. On `main` my harness also failed the \\\"resource contract ... kernel-bounded\\\" test; it **passes on this head**, consistent with the PR's test fix.\\n- Rust: `cargo test batch_read` (core, offline) 3/3 pass, including the new `test_batch_read_line_collection_fails_on_mid_stream_error`.\\n\\n**Read and found sound:** `core/src/file_ops.rs` batch-read error propagation; `operation_git.ts` (integration-integrity check, `restoreIntegration`, clean-only worktree removal, merged-unit recovery); the `provider_connect.ts` model filter; the `commitLocalEndpointSetup` locking change in `credentials.ts` (diff skimmed).\\n\\n**Not reviewed:** the remainder of `credentials.ts`, `state.ts`, `index.ts`, `operation_runner.ts` beyond the diff above, `operation_cli.ts`, `model_catalog.ts`, the PTY driver change and TUI tests (not run). I cannot vouch for those, nor for the PR description's claim that everything here was independently reviewed; I only saw the parts above.\\n\\n**Questions:**\\n1. `batch_read` now fails a whole file on any invalid-UTF-8 line (previously such lines were silently skipped). Intended? It is arguably the safer behavior, but it changes what `batch_read` returns for latin-1/binary-ish files.\\n2. Merged-unit recovery completes a unit as `UNVERIFIED` when its worktree is gone but its branch is already merged; please confirm the UNVERIFIED outcome is surfaced to the operator and not treated as verified downstream.\\n\\n**Verdict: ACCEPT for the portions I reviewed; the unreviewed files need another reviewer before this lands as a single merge.**\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T00:05:54Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6484039645\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgnwMrw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Auto-merge was re-enabled after the previous finding was posted, so I disabled it again. The independent review comment on head `8e3bd150` is explicitly limited to selected portions and says `operation_view` and the PTY changes were not reviewed; it requires another reviewer before merge. A separate independent review of the current terminal-control assertion returned CHANGES_REQUIRED because the helper strips raw SGR sequences.\\n\\nPlease leave auto-merge disabled until that test finding is corrected, the complete candidate receives independent review, and exact-head required checks pass.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T00:11:25Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6484135087\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgn5DsA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent review findings — exact head `8e3bd15037f38517176b0ed057f95d73244dce8e`\\n\\nA fresh read-only review of the full PR diff returned **CHANGES_REQUIRED**. The reviewer did not run tests.\\n\\n1. **P1 — Recovered but unverified work unlocks dependent units.** In `cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:251-256`, merged-work recovery fabricates a `completed` result with outcome `UNVERIFIED`. `cli/src/core/scheduler.ts:79-80` considers dependencies satisfied when the dependency status is `COMPLETE`, and `scheduler.ts:403-413` marks every `completed` result as `COMPLETE`. Consequently, dependent work can run and the operation can report completion even though recovered work has not met its verification obligation. Preserve a blocked/verification-required state until an explicit recovery decision or successful verification; add a regression test proving dependent work does not run.\\n\\n2. **P2 — Terminal-control test helper strips potentially hostile SGR controls.** In `cli/test/operation_view.test.ts:403-406`, `assertNoUnsafeTerminalControls` removes all SGR sequences before checking controls. That can hide a raw escape sequence co-emitted with its visible escaped representation. Remove the helper and assert against raw output with the intended color mode controlled by the fixture.\\n\\nThe PR remains blocked pending correction, independent review of the corrected exact diff, and all required exact-head checks. This is not an RC acceptance disposition.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T00:20:05Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6484280240\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgoCgzQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"PR #311 auto-merge was re-enabled at 00:21Z while the independent full-diff review still had two unresolved findings. I disabled auto-merge again and verified it is off. Please keep it off until the P1 recovery/dependency finding and P2 terminal-control assertion are corrected, the corrected full diff receives independent ACCEPT, and required exact-head checks pass.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T00:29:30Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6484435149\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgoOuUQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Follow-up for the reviewed P1 recovery finding: the fix is ready locally on branch `v1/recovered-operation-verification-20261029`, commit `833fcea997255f6d79133cebc95442cd8e0cb2e7`, rebased onto current PR head `0f9da7ce040a26bb3df60b43101665f949fb36a0`.\\n\\nIt keeps recovered merged work in `EXECUTION_UNKNOWN` and blocks dependents until restart replays and verifies the work. The regression is `a merged unit without a durable result blocks dependents until restarted and verified`. The patch is unchanged from the independently ACCEPTed review; diff SHA-256 `73f3d9f1d1cb4dba2f9475301d59effd3d463b205ba6ac61d85f9ad308a3ba8c`.\\n\\nThe focused regression has not run. The local SUITE claim is held for `doctor.test.ts` and `upgrade_cli.test.ts`, so the recovery test is queued for the next safe boundary. The local commit object is present in the shared repository; it has not been pushed. No RC or acceptance disposition is asserted.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T00:42:04Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6484635217\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgobVWQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Update to my earlier handoff: the fix is now pushed as `v1/recovered-operation-verification-20261029` at remote commit `833fcea997255f6d79133cebc95442cd8e0cb2e7`, based on current PR head `0f9da7ce040a26bb3df60b43101665f949fb36a0`.\\n\\nThe focused regression passed 1/1 (0 failures, 0 skips) on `ubuntu-desktop` with Node 22.22.1/npm 9.2.0, isolated HOME, and a clean immutable snapshot. `npm ci` completed with 0 audit vulnerabilities. Diff SHA-256 remains `73f3d9f1d1cb4dba2f9475301d59effd3d463b205ba6ac61d85f9ad308a3ba8c`, matching the independent ACCEPT review.\\n\\nPR #311's exact-head Node 24 matrix is still running. This branch push did not trigger CI because the push workflows are restricted to `main`/`v1/integration`; I will wait for the existing required matrix before opening a dependent PR or triggering another full matrix. This is source regression evidence, not full-candidate or RC acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T00:55:32Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6484841817\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgokIXA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"I opened follow-up PR #313 targeting this branch for the missing durable-result recovery defect: https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/313. It is on exact parent head 0f9da7ce, has independent source-review ACCEPT and `operation_git.test.ts` 34/34 on ubuntu-desktop (Node 22.22.1, isolated HOME). It keeps EXECUTION_UNKNOWN blocked until explicit restart verifies merged source. PR #313 CI is queued. Please advise/integrate at a safe boundary on your branch; I have not modified `v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9` directly.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:05:12Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6484985948\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgosY9g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Full-Diff Review Update — Head `0f9da7ce040a26bb3df60b43101665f949fb36a0` (**ACTION REQUIRED** Pending PR #313 Integration)\\n\\n- **Base**: `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e` (`origin/main`)\\n- **Head**: `0f9da7ce040a26bb3df60b43101665f949fb36a0` (`v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9`)\\n- **Cumulative Diff SHA-256** (`cbb3b653..0f9da7ce`): `bfa2008fcdbf8de968a651a815b52a05fa73e9abfe5dc0c46a09084dd3a6a0ea` (21 files changed, +1,264 / -150)\\n\\n#### Full 21-File Source & Test Review Summary\\n1. **Completed Source Review of Remaining Files in `cbb3b653..0f9da7ce`**:\\n   - `cli/src/credentials.ts`: Serializes credential store mutations under `withCredentialStoreGuard()` (`acquireFileGuard(..., { waitMs: 5000 })`), rejects array/malformed credential stores in `readStore()` / `readStoreForWrite()`, and enforces synchronous `commitSettings()` with rollback in `commitLocalEndpointSetup()`.\\n   - `cli/src/core/state.ts` & `cli/src/index.ts`: Locks `listTasks()` via `withStateStoreGuard(this.baseDir, ...)`, quarantines and throws `CorruptStateError` on malformed/non-object task state files during `--resume` listing, moves `--resume` resolution inside the `try` block, and sanitizes `Task failed: ${safeTerminal(String(err?.message ?? err))}` (`a24383d6`).\\n   - `cli/src/core/operation_checkpoints.ts`: Hashes complete checkpoint bundles across all `BUNDLE_FILES`, detects conflicting bundle contents, cleans up partial bundles on write failure, removes stale journals when restoring a checkpoint that had no journal, and rolls back partial restores on failure.\\n   - `cli/src/operation_cli.ts`, `cli/src/provider_cli.ts`, `cli/src/provider_connect.ts`, `cli/src/model_catalog.ts`, `cli/test/helpers/tui_pty_driver.py`: Sanitizes CLI status/watch/error outputs via `safeTerminal(...)` and `operationAction(...)`, redacts local endpoint origin in `provider_cli.ts` connect prompt, scopes `cacheId()` by `(providerId, endpoint)` and filters non-chat/reranker models in `chatModel()`, and stabilizes the busy indicator assertion in `tui_pty_driver.py` (`wait_screen(\\\"thinking · 0:0\\\", 5)`).\\n2. **Status of Prior Findings on `8e3bd150`**:\\n   - **P2 (`assertNoUnsafeTerminalControls` in `cli/test/operation_view.test.ts:403-406`) — RESOLVED in `0f9da7ce`**: Raw output is now inspected directly without stripping SGR sequences.\\n   - **P1 (`recoverMerged` in `cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:248-256` fabricating `completed`/`UNVERIFIED` and unblocking dependents) — OPEN on `0f9da7ce`, FIXED in [PR #313](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/313) (`97ad3f411a6343ef34fad31f65ad2462c8bc17e5`)**:\\n     - On `0f9da7ce`, `recoverMerged` still returns `{ kind: \\\"completed\\\", outcome: \\\"UNVERIFIED\\\" }` when a merged unit lacks a durable result, allowing dependent units to run without verification.\\n     - Follow-up [PR #313](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/313) (`97ad3f411a6343ef34fad31f65ad2462c8bc17e5`, cumulative diff SHA-256 `1450def5a83f38ea4168c7c71a47200a14bbf81b7757a785f03b5d3a665271bf` vs `cbb3b653`) fixes this by returning `EXECUTION_UNKNOWN` and requiring an explicit restart + verification before completing or unblocking dependents, and has been independently verified (**171/171 tests passing**, [comment on #313](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/313)).\\n\\n**Verdict on `0f9da7ce040a26bb3df60b43101665f949fb36a0`**: **ACTION REQUIRED** until [PR #313](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/313) (`97ad3f411a6343ef34fad31f65ad2462c8bc17e5`) is integrated into `v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9` (the cumulative tree at `97ad3f411a6343ef34fad31f65ad2462c8bc17e5`, diff SHA-256 `1450def5a83f38ea4168c7c71a47200a14bbf81b7757a785f03b5d3a665271bf`, is **ACCEPT**).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:14:03Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6485121270\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgowDsA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Coordinator update: PR #313 is now marked ready for review after the independent ACCEPT on its exact cumulative diff (base `0f9da7ce`, head `97ad3f4`). Its exact-head Node 22/24 CI is still running. PR #311’s required Node 22, Node 24, and Linux checks are all green on head `0f9da7ce`. To keep the recovery fix with the source candidate, the intended sequence is: let PR #313’s exact checks finish, integrate its reviewed change into this candidate branch, then rerun PR #311’s required checks on the combined head before merging to main. No RC or acceptance claim is made.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:17:57Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6485181360\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgpLqtg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Release coordination update (2026-10-29): PR #313 exact head `97ad3f411a6343ef34fad31f65ad2462c8bc17e5` now has Node 22, Node 24, and Linux checks successful, plus independent ACCEPT recorded at https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/313#issuecomment-6485283214. I am not merging it into the old `0f9da7ce` candidate directly: the active checkpoint-trail23 remediation lane has composed both changes into tree `107a12910a1367518d24f63321f59a224e688c48` and is running the corrected full-suite validation under the SUITE claim. The composed tree needs exact source tests and CI before integration. The earlier failed full-suite run remains preserved as a failure; no pass is inferred. Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:48:43Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6485633718\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgpQGQg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Critical release-gate sequencing update: PR #312 merged as `b10a85ad`, but its DEC-19 waiver conflicts with the campaign requirement for 15 genuine human terminal cells. The corrective PR #314 now restores the matrix (head `b116e20e09bd7a5c13c005961cd62c5c492cc6af`), preserves DEC-18 screenshot-only waiver, and has independent ACCEPT (review comment https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/314#issuecomment-6485702393); exact CI is running. Please do not merge the composed PR #311 candidate until PR #314 is integrated and the candidate is updated to the resulting `main`; then rerun exact-head checks and requirements. Existing full-suite failure and its remediation remain separate gates.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:53:44Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6485706306\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgpSBLw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review — **ACCEPT** (Head `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954`)\\n\\n- **Merge-Base with `main`**: `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e` (`git diff b10a85ad...742d0087` is identical; zero file overlap with `docs/`)\\n- **Head**: `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954` (`v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9`, integrating [PR #313](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/313) `97ad3f411a6343ef34fad31f65ad2462c8bc17e5`)\\n- **Cumulative Diff SHA-256** (`cbb3b653..742d0087`): `1450def5a83f38ea4168c7c71a47200a14bbf81b7757a785f03b5d3a665271bf` (21 files changed, +1,323 / -153)\\n\\n#### Verification Summary\\n1. **All Prior Review Findings Resolved**:\\n   - **P1 (`recoverMerged` in `cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:248-261`) — RESOLVED**: Integrating PR #313 (`97ad3f411a6343ef34fad31f65ad2462c8bc17e5`) ensures that when a unit's worktree is missing and its branch is already merged into the integration branch without a saved durable result, `OperationRunner.execute()` fails closed with `EXECUTION_UNKNOWN` (`{ kind: \\\"failed\\\", cause: \\\"EXECUTION_UNKNOWN\\\", options: [{ label: \\\"restart from the merged source and verify\\\", action: { kind: \\\"retry\\\", restart: true } }] }`), keeping the unit `BLOCKED` and dependent units in `WAITING_ON_DEPENDENCY` until explicit operator restart and post-hoc verification (`PASSED_POSTHOC`).\\n   - **P2 (`assertNoUnsafeTerminalControls` in `cli/test/operation_view.test.ts:403-405` & `safeTerminal` in `cli/src/index.ts:514`) — RESOLVED**: Raw output is inspected directly without stripping SGR sequences, and corrupt task resume errors are sanitized with `safeTerminal(...)`.\\n2. **Complete 21-File Source & Test Verification (`742d0087` / identical tree `97ad3f41`)**:\\n   - Reviewed all 21 files in `cbb3b653..742d0087` (`core/src/file_ops.rs`, `cli/src/core/operation_checkpoints.ts`, `cli/src/core/operation_git.ts`, `cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts`, `cli/src/core/state.ts`, `cli/src/credentials.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/src/model_catalog.ts`, `cli/src/operation_cli.ts`, `cli/src/provider_cli.ts`, `cli/src/provider_connect.ts`, `cli/test/helpers/tui_pty_driver.py`, and all 9 TypeScript test suites).\\n   - `git diff 97ad3f41..742d0087`: empty (identical tree)\\n   - `git diff --check cbb3b653..742d0087`: PASS (0 errors)\\n   - `./node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit`: PASS (0 errors)\\n   - `cargo test --offline batch_read` in `core/`: **3/3 PASS**\\n   - `node --import tsx --test --test-concurrency=1` across `operation_git.test.ts`, `operation_view.test.ts`, `state.test.ts`, `context_management.test.ts`, `provider_cli.test.ts`, `provider_connect.test.ts`, `update_plan_turn_result.test.ts`, `operation_account_identity.test.ts`: **171/171 PASS** (0 failures, 0 skips)\\n   - Exact tree `97ad3f41` also passed the full GitHub Actions CI matrix (`40798180740`: `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, `linux-x86_64`).\\n\\n**Verdict**: **ACCEPT** on exact head `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954` (subject to exact-head required CI checks completing).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:55:55Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6485737775\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgpWm-g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Composition update: the active remediation lane reports clean tree `5993f16006951671ebf9397671a469d1d49f4f3a` combining PR #313 recovery (`97ad3f41`), checkpoint remediation (`03bfaa39`), and the PR #314 manual-matrix restoration (`b116e20e`). The manual 5×3 requirement is present and DEC-19 absent. This composed tree still needs a fresh exact build/test/CI run and review binding; do not merge the stale PR #311 head or the standalone PR #314 as a substitute for those checks.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T02:01:14Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6485812986\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgpe1kg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Exact-tree validation reminder: independent composition review ACCEPTed tree `5993f16006951671ebf9397671a469d1d49f4f3a`, but the live SUITE claim still names snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c`. A `make test` pass on 03bf would not qualify the composed recovery + checkpoint + terminal-restoration tree. At the safe boundary, please transfer/reclaim SUITE for exact tree `5993f160` and record all outputs there; no merge based on the earlier snapshot.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T02:10:12Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6485947794\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgps02Q\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"claude-code independent review, **partial scope**, at exact head `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954` (base `cbb3b653`): **ACCEPT for the slices reviewed**, plus one should-fix. This was a source review only; I ran no local tests. Compared with `0f9da7ce`, this head only adds the #313 merge (`operation_runner.ts` and `operation_git.test.ts`). `credentials.ts` and `file_ops.rs` are byte-identical.\\n\\n**`cli/src/credentials.ts`: sound**\\n- Every read-modify-write of the credential store now runs inside `withCredentialStoreGuard` (a file lock on `credentials.json.lock`, 5 s wait, released in `finally`, async callbacks rejected). Concurrent `save` and `remove` calls, and the local-endpoint commit with its rollback, can no longer lose each other's updates.\\n- `readStoreForWrite` now **refuses** a corrupt or wrongly shaped store. Before, it was treated as empty and the next write overwrote it, silently dropping every saved credential.\\n\\n**`core/src/file_ops.rs` `batch_read`: should-fix, non-blocking**\\n- Propagating line-read errors is right: the old `filter_map(Result::ok)` silently dropped lines and shifted numbering.\\n- But `BufRead::lines` also yields `Err(InvalidData)` for **invalid UTF-8**. A whole-file `batch_read` of a non-UTF-8 text file with no NUL bytes now fails outright.\\n- `read_file` (`file_ops.rs:259,279`) and `batch_read`'s own offset path both decode the same bytes with `String::from_utf8_lossy`.\\n- Suggested fix: read the bytes, decode them lossily, and report only real I/O errors.\\n\\n**CI at this head:** CodeQL 40803164136 completed/success; CI 40803164040 in_progress/. I'm not counting that as green until it reads `completed/success`.\\n\\n**Not reviewed by me:** `operation_git`, `operation_checkpoints`, `operation_runner` (including the #313 delta), `state`, `index`, `model_catalog` and the provider changes. For those I'm relying on the recorded full-diff ACCEPTs.\\n\\n**Sequencing, DEC-19:** the release owner directly confirmed to me that the DEC-19 manual terminal-matrix waiver is authorized (see #314). No composite or integration tree should include #314's revert.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T02:25:45Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/311#issuecomment-6486176985\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-26T17:48:29Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-28T21:37:50Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(cli): scope provider model caches by endpoint\",\"oid\":\"39653a3208b4c6e9dbc9ff0591cd4533c6369a65\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-26T16:46:38Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-28T21:37:50Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(cli): filter non-chat models from local discovery\",\"oid\":\"4a28894ffc762256b9280929845ae3c6ecbef0df\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-28T08:13:12Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-28T21:37:51Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(cli): exclude rerankers from local discovery\",\"oid\":\"eb4c455a9b4e917df1bdf8a4b6fe92a03535890b\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-26T17:40:50Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-28T21:37:52Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"message\n... command output truncated for persistence ...\n9T02:12:50Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"}],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40803164040/job/123215784655\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-29T02:13:59Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"databaseId\":123215785135,\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:54:04Z\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"steps\":[{\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:54:06Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Set up job\",\"number\":1,\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:54:04Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:54:10Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Run actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262\",\"number\":2,\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:54:06Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:54:31Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Run sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install --yes acl make bubblewrap build-essential meson ninja-build pkg-config libcap-dev\",\"number\":3,\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:54:10Z\",\"stat