oviders.md:18:- Config (config.ts:16-40): env load order = install `cli/.env` (no override) -> `~/.config/nexus/config.env` (override) -> **cwd `.env` (override:true, any key)**. Credential authority snapshot (operator env + config.env) taken before cwd `.env` (client.ts:77-101); provider selection, provider base URL, disclosure authorization and stored-token binding use that snapshot. Everything else (TLS/Node env, timeouts, recovery policy, LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT/FALLBACKS, provider key env vars) reads live `process.env`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:135:| R-SEC-4 | Read-only mode does not expose `$HOME` secrets (`~/.ssh`, `~/.config/nexus/config.env`). | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | `--read-only` run_command `cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa` (fixture HOME) fails. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:81:| DX-04 | S3 | doctor coverage | doctor.ts (no check on ~/.config/nexus/config.env mode) | RUNTIME. A `config.env` containing `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY` at mode 644 produced no warning. Only credentials.json is checked (line 644). Quickstart tells users to chmod 600. | A world-readable API key goes unflagged. | Add a `config.env` permission check with the same narrow chmod-600 repair. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:12:| agent-collab-worker/src/index.ts, src/work-state-contract.ts, cloudflare.config.ts, package.json, tsconfig.json, vite.config.ts | full read |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:13:| slice root: package.json, cloudflare.config.ts, tsconfig.json, vite.config.ts, .gitignore, src/index.ts | full read |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:78:| CON-001 | S1 (contest) | Judge deploy / CI | docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:48-49; .github/workflows/ci.yml:29-39; experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/package.json:5-9, cloudflare.config.ts:6-12, src/index.ts:3-4,66-95 | RUNTIME + SOURCE. The documented `npm run typecheck/deploy --prefix experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice` targets the **Experiment-1 Worker** `artifacts-first-repo`. That Worker has hard-coded namespace `nexus-exp1-oct02`, an **unauthenticated POST /create**, and an unauthenticated GET /readback that returns content. The built `worker.config.json` has name=artifacts-first-repo and namespace=nexus-exp1-oct02; the bundle has 0 occurrences of \"work-state\". The NEXUS_CF_* variables set in CI are inert. The contest Worker (agent-collab-worker/) has no npm scripts, no lockfile, and is never typechecked, built or deployed by any documented command. | A judge following the guide deploys the wrong service: unauthenticated, bound to the operator's namespace name, and lacking `/work-state`. The CI \"contest contract\" job is green without covering the submitted Worker. | Before submission: add build/typecheck/deploy scripts and a lockfile to agent-collab-worker (or point the root config at it); fix CONTEST.md; make CI build the contest Worker. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:87:| CON-010 | S3 | Typecheck gap | agent-collab-worker/cloudflare.config.ts:5; tsconfig.json:7 | RUNTIME. tsc on agent-collab-worker reports `TS2591 Cannot find name 'process'` (`types: []`). The Worker *builds* when invoked from its directory using the parent node_modules (worker.config.json name=nexus-contest-ci, bindings correct). | Once CON-001 is fixed, CI would fail until this is fixed too. | Add `@types/node` or a typed `process` declaration for the config file. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:108:cat experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/.cloudflare/output/v0/workers/default/worker.config.json\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:115:../node_modules/.bin/cf build   # ok; worker.config.json name=nexus-contest-ci, NEXUS_NAMESPACE/REPOSITORY text, EXPERIMENT_AUTH secret\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:164:| CON-R1 | The documented deploy and CI build/typecheck target agent-collab-worker, with a lockfile and scripts | workflow | BLOCKER (contest) | CI artifact `worker.config.json` has the configured name and contains a `/work-state` handler. The root Exp-1 Worker is moved to historical or deleted. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/manifest.json:14:      \"file\": \"~/.config/nexus/config.env\",\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/standalone-llamacpp.json:6:  \"apiKey\": { \"file\": \"~/.config/nexus/config.env\", \"var\": \"LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY\" },\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md:9:| C1 | Give `agent-collab-worker` scripts (`typecheck`, `build`, `deploy`) and a lockfile, and fix TS2591 (`@types/node`, or declare `process` in `cloudflare.config.ts`). Add ordinary build/typecheck coverage for the maintained worker and assert that `worker.config.json` has the configured name and that the bundle contains the `/work-state` handler; do not restore the retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` status check. Move the Experiment-1 Worker to `experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/historical/exp1/`, or delete it. | `experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/{package.json,cloudflare.config.ts,src/}`, `agent-collab-worker/`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml:29-39` | High. The current deployment documentation still directs operators to the legacy Worker; record any correction as post-submission maintenance. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md:11:| C3 | Broker config file `/etc/nexus-cloudflare-broker/config.json` (root-owned, 0400). `demo-transport.mjs` reads it and validates the host suffix and the credential path prefix. The launcher keeps `clearenv()` and passes only a validated `NEXUS_RUN_ID`. Add a negative test showing caller env is ignored. | `trusted-broker-bundle/broker/demo-transport.mjs:10-57,164-185,402-437`; `launcher.c:27-75` | High |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:61:operatorFile  = ~/.con