{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T04:37:31.986Z","ordinal":490786,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a185e4-f059-7c83-884e-9306f1442d74","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2cd8875dc819f98d9d4f0b6dd26b7","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Campaign remains active; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`.** No stable v1.0.0 release exists.\n\n- Remote refs are unchanged: `origin/main` is `b10a85ad`, and `origin/v1/integration` is `7d6673f1`. Main’s exact CI run 40802654248 passed.\n- I opened [PR #317](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/317) to add the `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` instruction to `AGENTS.md`. Independent review accepted exact head `ff7698d3`; CI is still running, so the instruction is **not yet integrated into main**.\n- [PR #316](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/316) is at `63485583`, independently accepted. Requirements enforcement, version sync, and diff checks pass on that head; Node 22/24 and Entire checks remain pending. The partial RC10 terminal report does not count as a matrix result: it remains **0/15**.\n- PR #311 still points to stale head `742d0087`. Its refreshed candidate `fe28ec9` has independent acceptance and source gates passing, but needs exact hosted checks after the overlapping documentation CI runs finish.\n- The OpenCode custodian has restarted revalidation of 20 converted tasks. A separate evaluator-toolchain takeover claim now preserves BlueFalcon’s diff; independent review accepted it, but validation is still pending.\n- `ubuntu-desktop` is reachable at `10.0.8.3` with all five terminal applications and an active GUI session. The required human matrix still must be run against the exact successor RC.\n\nThe readiness and claims records distinguish these results from qualification acceptance. [Readiness checkpoint](</home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md>) · [terminal worksheet](</home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md>)\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":777,"lineEnd":780,"note":"reconcile Nexus release state against current refs and exact evidence"},{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":802,"lineEnd":805,"note":"keep source checks distinct from RC qualification"}],"rolloutIds":["01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0"]}},"started_at_ms":1793248648510,"completed_at_ms":1793248651985}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T04:37:31.994Z","ordinal":490787,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2cd8875dc819f98d9d4f0b6dd26b7","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"**Campaign remains active; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`.** No stable v1.0.0 release exists.\n\n- Remote refs are unchanged: `origin/main` is `b10a85ad`, and `origin/v1/integration` is `7d6673f1`. Main’s exact CI run 40802654248 passed.\n- I opened [PR #317](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/317) to add the `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` instruction to `AGENTS.md`. Independent review accepted exact head `ff7698d3`; CI is still running, so the instruction is **not yet integrated into main**.\n- [PR #316](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/316) is at `63485583`, independently accepted. Requirements enforcement, version sync, and diff checks pass on that head; Node 22/24 and Entire checks remain pending. The partial RC10 terminal report does not count as a matrix result: it remains **0/15**.\n- PR #311 still points to stale head `742d0087`. Its refreshed candidate `fe28ec9` has independent acceptance and source gates passing, but needs exact hosted checks after the overlapping documentation CI runs finish.\n- The OpenCode custodian has restarted revalidation of 20 converted tasks. A separate evaluator-toolchain takeover claim now preserves BlueFalcon’s diff; independent review accepted it, but validation is still pending.\n- `ubuntu-desktop` is reachable at `10.0.8.3` with all five terminal applications and an active GUI session. The required human matrix still must be run against the exact successor RC.\n\nThe readiness and claims records distinguish these results from qualification acceptance. [Readiness checkpoint](</home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md>) · [terminal worksheet](</home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md>)\n\n