{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T04:42:22.403Z","ordinal":490977,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a185f3-6098-7a33-888a-92c4cb0fa9a1","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a185f3-6098-7a33-888a-92c4cb0fa9a1","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae2ceac47b0819f85693ed81a62d030","usage":{"input_tokens":74933,"cached_input_tokens":64512,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":136,"reasoning_output_tokens":119,"total_tokens":75069},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":4838993,"cached_input_tokens":4796160,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15584,"reasoning_output_tokens":10228,"total_tokens":4854577},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9170405523,"cached_input_tokens":9072705152,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":26423925,"reasoning_output_tokens":15452000,"total_tokens":9196829448}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T04:42:23.885Z","ordinal":490978,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a185f7-5f0d-77c3-bc28-f38dda69e7c3","call_id":"call_f0db38be30c04cfe9d48816a0381775a","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed the uncommitted diff against base `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`. Exact reviewed diff SHA-256: `8826ff77c28b00f640714fb6a6609bc08f2a5ab21773b71bc631c9a5f4a1fe60`.\\n\\n- Go and Rust mounts use fixed roots and `--ro-bind`; the agent PATH prepends their guest paths while retaining configured entries ([isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:28), [run.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/run.mjs:597)).\\n- Protected-corpus overlap checks include toolchain mount sources and refuse overlaps before launch ([isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:190), [run.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/run.mjs:586)). Python oracle execution is restricted to pinned roots, clears the environment, uses temporary caches, and sets offline Go/Rust modes ([isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:414), [oracle.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/oracle.mjs:105)).\\n- Regression coverage invokes the production candidate sandbox and checks Go/Rust commands run there; the Python oracle fixture builds a synthetic Go and Rust project through the production launch path and checks overlap refusal ([eval_integrity.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:479), [eval_integrity.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1255)).\\n\\nNo findings. Review only: I did not run tests or access held-out material.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — Reviewed commit `6348558315de7f52f23fd5a0c3dc317d676030dd` against `f76e5b706b576eaed0a4764cdeab6d65b511ca35`. The paragraph at `docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:45–47` labels the report partial, records that test time, installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell outcomes were not supplied, and says it establishes no installed-RC gate. All 15 verdicts remain blank (lines 55–69); none is counted as passed.\\n\\nDiff SHA-256: `96334ce56a78088bd245d31f10fd8c6b1c2ac82ecc3c5b4a06942f29b891af96`\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for PR #315’s documentation diff. Reviewed base `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` → head `706c3b6cda2577f1ee3ae3665c42859045a9dfa2`. Cumulative diff SHA-256: `7fe68b53f754a5a33b6edbac53d63562957e71e82eb5a1746321f90430628b44`.\\n\\nThe changed acceptance map, worksheet, PLAN-10, and SPEC-10 consistently treat DEC-19 as a v1.0.0 manual-matrix waiver, not a pass; they retain the CI and scripted PTY gates and the successor-release matrix procedure. DEC-18 remains the separate screenshot-artifact waiver. REQUIREMENTS.md is unchanged.\\n\\nREADINESS.md is outside this diff and remains separately owned; its current checkpoint still needs reconciliation of manual-matrix status. This PR’s body explicitly calls out that separate work.\\n\\nI could not record the disposition on **Entire trail 30**: the only configured Entire context reports “Not logged in,” and trail access failed because `org.freedesktop.secrets` has no service on this host. I did not use the repository owner’s GitHub identity. At review time, Node 22/24 and Entire Gates were still running. No tests were run.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a185f3-6098-7a33-888a-92c4cb0fa9a1","create_time":1793248943.8852038}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
