{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:07:31.882Z","ordinal":492115,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1860e-61aa-7d83-825a-bc485dc94546","call_id":"call_04973c0d120d46dcbbef90630548f6f7","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — confirmed and reviewed exact working-tree diff SHA-256 `a7294e84a885955c21e8c3394378f192edc791922d3416015f89917797169504` against base `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`.\\n\\nPinned Go and Rust roots are validated as canonical, root-owned, non-group-writable trees before they are exposed; candidate mounts use `--ro-bind` and reject corpus overlap ([isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:40), [isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:66), [isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:379)). Candidate PATH uses guest mount paths and retains configured entries ([isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:27)). Python oracle launches use pinned mounts, cleared environment, temporary offline caches, and corpus-overlap refusal ([isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:429), [isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:481), [oracle.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/oracle.mjs:105)).\\n\\nThe synthetic fixture checks unsafe-root rejection and compiles/runs Go and Rust through the oracle; the candidate sandbox regression exercises the production launch path and checks tool availability ([eval_integrity.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:479), [eval_integrity.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:572)).\\n\\nNo findings. Read-only review; no tests run or held-out data accessed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — Reviewed commit `6348558315de7f52f23fd5a0c3dc317d676030dd` against `f76e5b706b576eaed0a4764cdeab6d65b511ca35`. The paragraph at `docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:45–47` labels the report partial, records that test time, installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell outcomes were not supplied, and says it establishes no installed-RC gate. All 15 verdicts remain blank (lines 55–69); none is counted as passed.\\n\\nDiff SHA-256: `96334ce56a78088bd245d31f10fd8c6b1c2ac82ecc3c5b4a06942f29b891af96`\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for PR #315’s documentation diff. Reviewed base `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` → head `706c3b6cda2577f1ee3ae3665c42859045a9dfa2`. Cumulative diff SHA-256: `7fe68b53f754a5a33b6edbac53d63562957e71e82eb5a1746321f90430628b44`.\\n\\nThe changed acceptance map, worksheet, PLAN-10, and SPEC-10 consistently treat DEC-19 as a v1.0.0 manual-matrix waiver, not a pass; they retain the CI and scripted PTY gates and the successor-release matrix procedure. DEC-18 remains the separate screenshot-artifact waiver. REQUIREMENTS.md is unchanged.\\n\\nREADINESS.md is outside this diff and remains separately owned; its current checkpoint still needs reconciliation of manual-matrix status. This PR’s body explicitly calls out that separate work.\\n\\nI could not record the disposition on **Entire trail 30**: the only configured Entire context reports “Not logged in,” and trail access failed because `org.freedesktop.secrets` has no service on this host. I did not use the repository owner’s GitHub identity. At review time, Node 22/24 and Entire Gates were still running. No tests were run.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1860e-1ee0-7860-ad63-fe5f780b91f5","create_time":1793250451.8827174}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"f