{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:13:24.103Z","ordinal":492447,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1860e-1ee0-7860-ad63-fe5f780b91f5","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9fe2c3ca-5524-43b3-acb2-4a8d079fa267","process_id":"58365","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git diff origin/main...origin/v1/dec19-terminal-waiver-reconcile -- docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md; git diff origin/main...origin/codex/restore-terminal-human-matrix -- docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md docs/releases/v1.0.0.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git diff origin/main...origin/v1/dec19-terminal-waiver-reconcile -- docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md; git diff origin/main...origin/codex/restore-terminal-human-matrix -- docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md docs/releases/v1.0.0.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nindex 9f7180b9..ec97935b 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@ The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `\n | REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n | REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n | REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n-| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n+| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | CI PTY checks and installed-RC scripted PTY scenarios (§5.1–§5.2); the manual matrix is waived by DEC-19 |\n | REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n <!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n \n@@ -203,9 +203,9 @@ For each terminal × size, check:\n 6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n 7. NO_COLOR.\n \n-Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); this does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\n+For successor-release qualification, record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts were waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); that screenshot waiver did not waive checks for a release where the matrix applied. The v1.0.0 manual matrix itself is waived by DEC-19 above.\n \n-**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n+**Successor-release gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n \n ## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md b/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\nindex a14e4c3e..933107d0 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n@@ -28,9 +28,9 @@ Record the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have\n | VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code: ; integrated terminal profile: |\n | GNOME Terminal | |\n \n-## Procedure to perform in every matrix cell\n+## Successor-release procedure to perform in every matrix cell\n \n-Run each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by that row. Record the observations and evidence references for the cell.\n+For a successor release that requires this matrix, run each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by that row. Record the observations and evidence references for the cell.\n \n 1. Launch `nexus`; confirm the TUI appears.\n 2. At the approval panel, type continuously across it, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key.\n@@ -40,9 +40,9 @@ Run each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by\n 6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm clean terminal restoration (echo on, no stray escape codes).\n 7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\n \n-Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). This does not waive any live manual interaction, check, observation, per-cell verdict, or evidence record. Automated PTY runs do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\n+For a successor release, follow that release's screenshot and evidence decisions; the v1.0.0 screenshot waiver in [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) does not change this successor procedure. For v1.0.0, the entire manual matrix is waived by [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver), so no manual interaction, cell verdict, or cell evidence is required or claimed. Automated PTY runs remain mandatory for v1.0.0 but are not manual-matrix results.\n \n-## Terminal × size results\n+## Successor-release terminal × size results\n \n Select exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Record observed outcomes for every check and a per-cell evidence reference bound to the installed RC identity, terminal environment, and size. Record failures in the disposition/notes field.\n \n@@ -64,9 +64,9 @@ Select exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Record observed outcomes for ever\n | 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n | 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n \n-## Acceptance gate\n+## Successor-release acceptance gate\n \n-- Safety checks 2, 5, and 6: **zero failures across all 15 cells**. Any failure here blocks this gate.\n+- For a successor release that requires this matrix, safety checks 2, 5, and 6 must have **zero failures across all 15 cells**. Any failure here blocks that gate.\n - Any failure on another check requires a written disposition: fix, or a documented known limitation.\n - All 15 cells have exactly one verdict, check outcomes, and per-cell evidence references: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n - All non-safety failures have a written disposition: [ ] yes  [ ] no  [ ] no such failures\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\nindex 81046edf..3e64777b 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@\n | | |\n |---|---|\n | Status | Ready. Protocol and thresholds fixed by [DEC-05](../DECISIONS.md#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds); task authorship needs owner action X2. |\n-| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\n+| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, and the applicable automated PTY terminal gates. The v1.0.0 manual matrix is waived by DEC-19, not passed. |\n | Requirements | REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-102, REQ-QUAL-103, REQ-QUAL-104, REQ-QUAL-105, REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 |\n | Findings | EVL-001, EVL-002, EVL-003, EVL-004, EVL-005, HIST-08, PRV G1/G2, TUI gaps (kitty/real terminals), VER-07 |\n | Plan | [PLAN-10](../plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) |\ndiff --git a/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md b/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\nindex b12111ef..314465cd 100644\n--- a/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\n+++ b/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\n@@ -156,7 +156,7 @@ nexus doctor\n \n ## Release qualification and waivers\n \n-- **Manual real-terminal matrix: waived.** The fifteen-cell manual E3 matrix (xterm, kitty, tmux in GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60) was waived for v1.0.0 by the release owner on 2026-10-29 ([DEC-19](../v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)). This is a waiver, not a pass: no per-cell verdict was recorded. Terminal evidence for this release is the automated CI PTY suites and the scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios defined by ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2; they remain required for the exact accepted candidate.\n+- **Manual real-terminal matrix: required and not yet accepted.** The fifteen-cell manual E3 matrix (xterm, kitty, tmux in GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60) requires actual operator runs on the exact installed RC with a verdict and observed outcomes recorded for each cell. Automated CI and PTY scenarios do not substitute for this evidence. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18; DEC-19 withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record.\n - **Screenshot artifacts: waived** for v1.0.0 by [DEC-18](../v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver).\n \n-Every other acceptance gate — installed-RC platform and lifecycle evidence, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger — is unaffected by these waivers and is governed by the release decision record.\n+The screenshot-artifact waiver does not affect any other acceptance gate. Installed-RC platform and lifecycle evidence, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, the manual terminal matrix, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger remain governed by the release decision record.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nindex 9f7180b9..80f4647a 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n | ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n-| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | **Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** No per-cell verdicts are recorded; this is not a PASS. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 remain required. |\n+| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | All 15 cells have actual manual execution, recorded PASS/FAIL verdicts, observed outcomes, and evidence bound to the exact installed RC. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 do not substitute for these cells. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18. |\n \n ## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n \n@@ -189,7 +189,7 @@ These are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n \n ### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n \n-**Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** The procedure below is retained for a successor release; it is not required for v1.0.0 and no cell verdict is recorded. The automated suites in §5.1 and §5.2 remain mandatory.\n+**Required for v1.0.0.** Run every terminal × size combination below against the exact installed RC and record a verdict and observed outcomes for each cell. Automated suites in §5.1 and §5.2 remain required but do not replace operator execution. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. See [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\n \n Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n \n@@ -333,7 +333,7 @@ G6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable\n - [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n - [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n - [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n-- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI and scripted gates PASS; the manual real-terminal matrix is waived for v1.0.0 per DEC-19.\n+- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI and scripted gates PASS, and all 15 manual real-terminal cells have verified operator evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshots only.\n - [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n - [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n - [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\nindex db87654c..d081f852 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n@@ -248,13 +248,15 @@ This amendment is **narrow by design**. It applies only to corpora where the mea\n \n ## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n \n-**Context.** [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waived screenshot artifacts only; the fifteen manual matrix cells (five terminals × three sizes, ACCEPTANCE §5.3) remained mandatory. On 2026-10-29 the release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0.\n+**Status: withdrawn.** The waiver described in this decision is not in effect.\n \n-**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-29).** The manual E3 matrix, its per-cell PASS/FAIL verdicts and its evidence records are not required for v1.0.0. ACC-TUI-MANUAL is **waived**, not PASS: no cell verdict is recorded and none may be inferred. The automated CI PTY suites and the scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2) remain mandatory and are the only terminal evidence for this release. This waiver changes no other acceptance criterion, safety gate, or verification rule, and it does not change any requirements-ledger status: REQ-QUAL-108 remains `partial` unless the ledger owner records a different disposition.\n+**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\n \n-**Disclosure.** The v1.0.0 release notes must state that the manual real-terminal matrix was waived by owner decision and that terminal evidence is automated (PTY/CI) only.\n+**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\n \n-**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS.\n+**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\n+\n+**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\n \n ## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\nindex 70ade8f1..bd7cdaa6 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n@@ -1,19 +1,25 @@\n # v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n \n-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 22:00 UTC; custodian update 2026-10-29)\n+## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 04:23 UTC)\n \n-**Custodian update (2026-10-29).** The release owner waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0 ([DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)). The gate is **waived, not passed**: no cell verdicts were recorded, the automated CI PTY suites and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios remain required and passing, and the release notes must disclose the waiver. The terminal-matrix item is no longer an outstanding qualification gate; every other gate in this checkpoint is unchanged.\n+**Remote revision reconciliation:** `origin/main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`; `origin/v1/integration` is `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78`. The integration ref is an ancestor of main (875 commits behind), not a divergent head. Current release PRs target main; evidence from the two refs must remain distinct.\n \n-**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496`, the PR #308 merge commit. Exact-main CI run [40770466028](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770466028) completed successfully at 2026-10-28 21:58:49 UTC on this SHA. Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices passed; Linux x86_64 passed Rust and CLI tests, requirements and security gates, reproducible package builds with matching output hashes, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. CodeQL run [40770465935](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40770465935) completed successfully. On a clean detached worktree at this exact SHA, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n+**Source gates on main:** `origin/main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` (PR #312 merge). Exact-main CI run [40802654248](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654248) and CodeQL run [40802654255](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654255) passed on that SHA. The exact-source requirements gate passed with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open); 12 requirements remain mapped to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n \n-**Integrated changes:** PR #309 merged as `b3dea1a96fb204e5fa48becc90f12bf5042076af` at 20:36 UTC with checksummed RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider evidence. PR #300 merged as `79cba842e86d64f895e1a269636776cdf1e7e6da` at 21:07:46 UTC after Node 22/24, Linux packaging/tests, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. PR #308 merged as `10c84df89d391987454e4997aaa8f97529cc2496` at 21:15:37 UTC; exact PR head `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` passed Node 22/24 and Linux, with JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; its GitHub Entire Gates check was neutral. A post-merge source reviewer found no blocking defect in the reviewed restore path and reported a separate Entire trail 23 signal: approvals failed and one high-severity finding was unresolved. A later authenticated, read-only Entire query on `ubuntu-desktop` (2026-10-28 21:48 UTC) found trail 23 open but its Nexus Code change marked merged; the finding and approvals commands reported no open change, so the historical finding text and its disposition could not be retrieved. The earlier high-severity signal therefore remains unresolved/unverified and must be reconciled before successor-RC qualification; the later query does not establish that it was resolved. The current-main source CI passed as recorded above; this does not qualify an installed release candidate.\n+**Candidate convergence:** PR #311 remains open at `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954` on the older base `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`; its prior Node 22/24, Linux x86_64 and CodeQL checks passed, but they do not qualify the current base. A local candidate at `fe28ec9e686b90e69e42a7a13d55f50264b3775f` includes the reviewed source changes and readiness refresh; the completed full suite below ran on a different immutable snapshot and is not exact-candidate evidence. PR #316 carries the terminal-matrix correction at head `2e9ad10df4bab065bc9573680e3ed659709e4293` against main `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`; independent review accepted that exact head, CodeQL and JS/TS passed, Node 22/24 and Entire Gates remain in progress at 04:23 UTC, and GitHub reports the PR blocked. PR #315's waiver conclusion conflicts with the current release decision and must not be merged as-is.\n \n-**Qualification and release:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The user-reported RC8 host-identification defect is fixed in PR #273, merged as `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2` after RC10 was built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; RC10 therefore does not contain this fix. Current source explicitly identifies Nexus after dynamic skill instructions, and `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` covers a Claude model and Claude-specific skill. PR #273 exact Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. The regression still needs confirmation on an installed successor RC; the RC8 dogfood report is pre-fix evidence. RC10 cross-runner evidence and provider records remain bound to RC10 and do not qualify current main or a successor RC. The source requirements gate does not replace installed-RC gates. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, last updated at 20:25:33 UTC; no custodian handoff or fresh custody acceptance is recorded, so held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted. The five-environment, three-size terminal matrix remains 0/15. Per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver), screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0; terminal behavior checks remain required and have not been run. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable with an active Wayland session and all five terminal applications installed, but there is no successor RC to qualify there. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC reproducibility, manual terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n+**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The claims identify OpenCode as the prior/current custodian workflow, but do not verify the responsible human identity; SageBridge's 04:15 status says it is coordinating only. The successor T2 store remains 20/40 tasks; the remaining Go/Rust tasks need the reviewed, pinned-toolchain change integrated. Reported T3 digest/schema/isolation checks are 8/8, which is not full T3 task-quality qualification. At 04:23 UTC the OpenCode custodian holds SUITE for two-round setup/reference/oracle revalidation of the 20 converted tasks with isolated HOME; a live validator child process was observed. This is custody revalidation, not held-out qualification; no result or custody acceptance is recorded. Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; the latest metadata-only correction was posted at 04:18 UTC. T2 custody acceptance and qualification, full T3/T4 qualification, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, fault injection, successor-RC reproducibility and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC10 evidence does not qualify a successor candidate.\n+\n+**Terminal gate:** The release owner requires all 15 manual terminal cells (five environments × three sizes) on the exact installed RC. The latest verified worksheet status is 0/15 accepted cells; blank cells remain incomplete. Actual operator execution and per-cell outcomes are mandatory; automated CI or PTY results do not substitute. [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waives screenshots only. [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal applications, but the manual matrix remains outstanding.\n+\n+**Suite evidence:** `make test` completed on immutable snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c` with isolated HOME and the required evaluator workspace/runtime fixtures: 1,993 tests across 224 suites, 1,991 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped, 0 cancelled; Rust tests and post-test security lifecycle gates passed. The full run took 3,167,118 ms. This snapshot is not exact current main, PR #311 candidate `fe28ec9`, or an RC, so the result does not qualify those revisions. The SUITE claim transferred to the OpenCode custodian at 04:18 UTC for the 20-task custody revalidation above.\n \n **Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n \n ## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 20:18 UTC; superseded)\n \n+This historical checkpoint includes a matrix-waiver conclusion that was later withdrawn by the current DEC-19 decision. It records the prior checkpoint only and is not the current acceptance disposition.\n+\n **Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`, the merge commit for PR #305. Exact-main CI run [40751988282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988282) and CodeQL run [40751988267](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988267) passed on that SHA. The source requirements check passed on this revision with 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, and 12 deferred to exact-RC qualification. These source-stage results do not qualify an installed release candidate.\n \n **Integrated changes and open PRs:** PR #299 merged as `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` (merge commit `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`). PR #307 merged as `90837aa5193d7c071066d27ccefd2b2ea2db0aff`. PR #305 merged at `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`; its GitHub Entire Gates check concluded **NEUTRAL** (“No trail tracks this branch”). PR #302 was closed unmerged. PR #308 supersedes it and is open at `2c1b2dfa6b10f736367020a86228ab64a4173500` on current base `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`. Exact-head CI run [40757432379](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757432379) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed. The PR head fixes the `globName` test by staging it with the literal `:(literal)` pathspec. A separate local follow-up commit `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` applies literal staging to the `magicName` fixture and asserts that it entered the index; this follow-up is not on the PR head. Its focused 77/77 result is owner-reported without a retained log, so that additional fixture change still needs exact-head checks before integration. PR #309 is open at `aace981bc3f46e10f1e57c5498825a76e9994ee5` on the current base. Run [40758300812](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40758300812) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed, and Linux packaging/tests are in progress. PR #300 is open at `f3957a67ac8f9b5ea1e60be2494b9402d943230f` on the current base. Run [40757603196](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757603196) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. A fresh checkpoint accuracy correction was posted on PR #300 (comment [6479279112](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300#issuecomment-6479279112)); this local update addresses the stale PR heads and main-CI status identified there. Source PR checks are distinct from release qualification.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md b/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\nindex a14e4c3e..7d190a19 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n For `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3).\n \n-> **Waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (2026-10-29).** This worksheet is retained for a successor release. It contains no results, no cell verdict is recorded for v1.0.0, and it does not qualify an RC.\n+> **Required for v1.0.0.** Complete all 15 cells against the exact installed RC. Blank cells are incomplete; no result is inferred. Automated PTY runs do not count as manual cell evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. The prior waiver record is withdrawn by [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\n \n ## Installed candidate identity\n \n@@ -42,6 +42,10 @@ Run each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by\n \n Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). This does not waive any live manual interaction, check, observation, per-cell verdict, or evidence record. Automated PTY runs do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\n \n+## Partial operator report\n+\n+In response to the RC10 matrix request, the release owner reported that the client rendered at the tested sizes except in tmux inside GNOME Terminal; that setup could not be resized below 43×13, and the other results seemed okay. The report was received on 2026-10-29; test time, exact installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell check outcomes were not supplied. Treat this as useful partial operator information only: it does not fill any matrix cell or establish the installed-RC gate. No screenshot was supplied; DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts.\n+\n ## Terminal × size results\n \n Select exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Record observed outcomes for every check and a per-cell evidence reference bound to the installed RC identity, terminal environment, and size. Record failures in the disposition/notes field.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\nindex 81046edf..81822d95 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ Standalone live inference evidence is absent (HIST-08; SPEC-05). Real-terminal c\n    - The scorer logs every replacement.\n    - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\n 7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n-8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts) are mandatory. A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. **The manual matrix is waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver)**; no per-cell verdicts are recorded and this is not a PASS. Screenshot artifacts were waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). Automated terminal evidence is the only terminal evidence for this release.\n+8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts) are mandatory. A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. All 15 cells require actual operator execution and per-cell verdict/evidence bound to the exact installed RC; automated terminal evidence does not replace this gate. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix waiver record.\n 9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0, false-presence = 0 (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-18), and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\n 10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\n \n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":28986}},"started_at_ms":1793250804102,"completed_at_ms":1793250804103}}
