{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:18:24.478Z","ordinal":492687,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1860e-1ee0-7860-ad63-fe5f780b91f5","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a1860e-1ee0-7860-ad63-fe5f780b91f5","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae2d71e0240819f93598bd6848a64bf","usage":{"input_tokens":208013,"cached_input_tokens":200448,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":247,"reasoning_output_tokens":178,"total_tokens":208260},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":10404955,"cached_input_tokens":10278144,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":52829,"reasoning_output_tokens":39443,"total_tokens":10457784},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9205172837,"cached_input_tokens":9107136512,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":26549768,"reasoning_output_tokens":15540870,"total_tokens":9231722605}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:18:26.197Z","ordinal":492688,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1860e-1ee0-7860-ad63-fe5f780b91f5","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6a1de1bd-3286-410e-bff9-8516beda7dc6","process_id":"98756","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/311/comments --jq '.[-1].body'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/311/comments --jq '.[-1].body'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"claude-code independent review, **partial scope**, at exact head `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954` (base `cbb3b653`): **ACCEPT for the slices reviewed**, plus one should-fix. This was a source review only; I ran no local tests. Compared with `0f9da7ce`, this head only adds the #313 merge (`operation_runner.ts` and `operation_git.test.ts`). `credentials.ts` and `file_ops.rs` are byte-identical.\n\n**`cli/src/credentials.ts`: sound**\n- Every read-modify-write of the credential store now runs inside `withCredentialStoreGuard` (a file lock on `credentials.json.lock`, 5 s wait, released in `finally`, async callbacks rejected). Concurrent `save` and `remove` calls, and the local-endpoint commit with its rollback, can no longer lose each other's updates.\n- `readStoreForWrite` now **refuses** a corrupt or wrongly shaped store. Before, it was treated as empty and the next write overwrote it, silently dropping every saved credential.\n\n**`core/src/file_ops.rs` `batch_read`: should-fix, non-blocking**\n- Propagating line-read errors is right: the old `filter_map(Result::ok)` silently dropped lines and shifted numbering.\n- But `BufRead::lines` also yields `Err(InvalidData)` for **invalid UTF-8**. A whole-file `batch_read` of a non-UTF-8 text file with no NUL bytes now fails outright.\n- `read_file` (`file_ops.rs:259,279`) and `batch_read`'s own offset path both decode the same bytes with `String::from_utf8_lossy`.\n- Suggested fix: read the bytes, decode them lossily, and report only real I/O errors.\n\n**CI at this head:** CodeQL 40803164136 completed/success; CI 40803164040 in_progress/. I'm not counting that as green until it reads `completed/success`.\n\n**Not reviewed by me:** `operation_git`, `operation_checkpoints`, `operation_runner` (including the #313 delta), `state`, `index`, `model_catalog` and the provider changes. For those I'm relying on the recorded full-diff ACCEPTs.\n\n**Sequencing, DEC-19:** the release owner directly confirmed to me that the DEC-19 manual terminal-matrix waiver is authorized (see #314). No composite or integration tree should include #314's revert.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":352746667}},"started_at_ms":1793251105844,"completed_at_ms":1793251106197}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:18:27.984Z","ordinal":492689,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18618-6490-7dd3-bb44-8c669fe1eeee","call_id":"call_c27e06f971b74934876a39ccee5b0b12","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"claude-code independent review, **partial scope**, at exact head `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954` (base `cbb3b653`): **ACCEPT for the slices reviewed**, plus one should-fix. This was a source review only; I ran no local tests. Compared with `0f9da7ce`, this head only adds the #313 merge (`operation_runner.ts` and `operation_git.test.ts`). `credentials.ts` and `file_ops.rs` are byte-identical.\n\n**`cli/src/credentials.ts`: sound**\n- Every read-modify-write of the credential store now runs inside `withCredentialStoreGuard` (a file lock on `credentials.json.lock`, 5 s wait, released in `finally`, async callbacks rejected). Concurrent `save` and `remove` calls, and the local-endpoint commit with its rollback, can no longer lose each other's updates.\n- `readStoreForWrite` now **refuses** a corrupt or wrongly shaped store. Before, it was treated as empty and the next write overwrote it, silently dropping every saved credential.\n\n**`core/src/file_ops.rs` `batch_read`: should-fix, non-blocking**\n- Propagating line-read errors is right: the old `filter_map(Result::ok)` silently dropped lines and shifted numbering.\n- But `BufRead::lines` also yields `Err(InvalidData)` for **invalid UTF-8**. A whole-file `batch_read` of a non-UTF-8 text file with no NUL bytes now fails outright.\n- `read_file` (`file_ops.rs:259,279`) and `batch_read`'s own offset path both decode the same bytes with `String::from_utf8_lossy`.\n- Suggested fix: read the bytes, decode them lossily, and report only real I/O errors.\n\n**CI at this head:** CodeQL 40803164136 completed/success; CI 40803164040 in_progress/. I'm not counting that as green until it reads `completed/success`.\n\n**Not reviewed by me:** `operation_git`, `operation_checkpoints`, `operation_runner` (including the #313 delta), `state`, `index`, `model_catalog` and the provider changes. For those I'm relying on the recorded full-diff ACCEPTs.\n\n**Sequencing, DEC-19:** the release owner directly confirmed to me that the DEC-19 manual terminal-matrix waiver is authorized (see #314). No composite or integration tree should include #314's revert.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1860e-1ee0-7860-ad63-fe5f780b91f5","create_time":1793251107.9841232}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
