 on an immutable snapshot under the SUITE claim. Its focused Go/Rust oracle test passed after adding Cargo’s lockfile flag; the broader evaluator-integrity file is still executing. The earlier Rust toolchain permission issue is resolved, so that prerequisite can be handed back to the held-out custodian once the suite releases.","turn_id":"01a1860e-1ee0-7860-ad63-fe5f780b91f5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2d53f259c819f806808f38302f018","order":23118,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18611-0137-7a72-a377-6b3014066232","text":"The evaluator-integrity run completed with one fixture failure: the isolated snapshot had no generated `cli/dist`, which that test expects. The Go/Rust oracle and resource-boundary tests passed. I’m rerunning the same scoped suite after building the snapshot first; the missing artifact is a test prerequisite, not a product failure.","turn_id":"01a1860e-1ee0-7860-ad63-fe5f780b91f5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2d5c2f658819f99a36ddfb10690e2","order":23121,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18613-0444-78f0-a0fb-cad4783a573a","text":"The built-snapshot evaluator suite now passes, including the previously failing runtime-path assertion. The Cargo fixture correction has independent `ACCEPT` on exact diff `723a7d03…ba61ba05`; I’m committing that one-line test prerequisite, then I’ll hold off on opening a new PR until the active full-suite jobs finish.","turn_id":"01a1860e-1ee0-7860-ad63-fe5f780b91f5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2d67d09c8819fa39bd88d88601d0b","order":23124,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18615-dad0-7311-84bc-8189cc307a7d","text":"PR #316 has now merged after its exact-head Node 22, Node 24, and Linux checks passed; its review keeps the real-terminal matrix mandatory. I’m refreshing `main` and checking PR #315 immediately, since its proposed waiver overlaps and conflicts with the now-integrated requirement.","turn_id":"01a1860e-1ee0-7860-ad63-fe5f780b91f5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2d73754dc819f9807f1777a94c3ab","order":23125,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18618-b264-7c53-9bd1-d4b0cb6d4a32","text":"PR #311 has a concrete review finding that needs fixing before integration: its new `batch_read` error handling also rejects invalid UTF-8, although adjacent reads decode the same bytes lossily. I’m tracing that exact path and will add a regression before considering the source PR ready.","turn_id":"01a1860e-1ee0-7860-ad63-fe5f780b91f5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2d737f0cc819fbf3309de3bf2e376","order":23126,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18618-b412-7042-aae5-b5afb5c31dbd","text":"I’m applying the repository’s test-driven-development skill for this defect: first pin down the invalid-UTF-8 behavior with a focused regression, then make the narrow fix and run the relevant verification.","turn_id":"01a1860e-1ee0-7860-ad63-fe5f780b91f5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2d7e592ec819fa2e3027a0162f10b","order":23127,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1861b-5b14-76d2-98c1-0d4f0d589e4e","text":"The first targeted command completed with zero tests because Rust’s `--exact` filter needs the fully qualified test name; I’m treating that as no evidence, not a pass. The test-only build finished, and I’m rerunning with the correct filter before changing implementation.","turn_id":"01a1860e-1ee0-7860-ad63-fe5f780b91f5"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":23128,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, 