{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:25:17.416Z","ordinal":492937,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1861e-a3e8-71c1-9fdd-9d6268478eb2","call_id":"call_fcb0baa4a7974f3787c22f2936ab262e","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"mcp__mcp_search__get_observations\nStep 3: Fetch selected useful details for the IDs chosen after reviewing the index and timeline. Any shortening is marked. Params: ids (required), orderBy, limit, project (worker) or projectId (server). This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__get_observations(args: {\n  // Array of selected observation IDs to fetch (string IDs in server runtime)\n  ids: Array<number | string>;\n  // Server project ID; defaults to the configured server project\n  projectId?: string;\n  [key: string]: unknown;\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\n```\n---\nmcp__mcp_search__search\nSmart search (default), step 1: search memory for an index with IDs. Review it, use timeline for context, then get_observations only for selected IDs. Params: query, limit, project, platformSource, type, obs_type, dateStart, dateEnd, offset, orderBy. This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__search(args: {\n  // End date filter (ISO)\n  dateEnd?: string;\n  // Start date filter (ISO)\n  dateStart?: string;\n  // Max results (default 20)\n  limit?: number;\n  // Filter observations by their type (e.g. bugfix, feature). Comma-separated for multiple.\n  obs_type?: string;\n  // Pagination offset\n  offset?: number;\n  // Sort order: date_desc or date_asc\n  orderBy?: string;\n  // Filter by platform source (e.g. claude, codex, cursor) — restricts results to that agent's own memory\n  platformSource?: string;\n  // Worker project name\n  project?: string;\n  // Server project ID; defaults to the configured server project\n  projectId?: string;\n  // Search query\n  query?: string;\n  // Document category to search: 'observations', 'sessions', or 'prompts' (default: all). Any other value is treated as an observation-type filter (alias for obs_type).\n  type?: string;\n  [key: string]: unknown;\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\n```\n---\nmcp__mcp_search__timeline\nStep 2: Get context around results. Params: anchor (observation ID) OR query (finds anchor automatically), depth_before, depth_after, project. This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__timeline(args: {\n  // Observation ID to center the timeline around (string ID in server runtime)\n  anchor?: number | string;\n  // Items after anchor (default 3)\n  depth_after?: number;\n  // Items before anchor (default 3)\n  depth_before?: number;\n  // Worker project name\n  project?: string;\n  // Server project ID; defaults to the configured server project\n  projectId?: string;\n  // Query to find anchor automatically\n  query?: string;\n  [key: string]: unknown;\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\n```\n---\nmcp__mcp_search__work_state_read\nRead this project's to-do lists and working state written with work_state_write: every open item, or one list, with done and dropped items when includeClosed is true. Params: list, includeClosed. This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__work_state_read(args: {\n  // Also show done and dropped items and closed lists\n  includeClosed?: boolean;\n  // Read only this list\n  list?: string;\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\n```\n---\nmcp__mcp_search__work_state_write\nYour canonical to-do list and working state for this project, kept across sessions: whatever is still open is shown at the start of every session. Each call appends one entry to a list. To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...details}. State on the list itself: any other fields (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list). Returns what is still open in the list. Params: list (required), fields (required). This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__work_state_write(args: {\n  // Keys to set. Include \"task\" to update a to-do item. Values are strings, numbers, booleans, or null to clear a key.\n  fields: { [key: string]: string | number | boolean | null; };\n  // The to-do list or tracked thing this entry belongs to, e.g. \"release\" or \"auth-refactor\"\n  list: string;\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\n```"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5","create_time":1793251517.4161284}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
