{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:29:51.861Z","ordinal":493121,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae2d9c66ee8819f9ed5715499b74035","usage":{"input_tokens":118448,"cached_input_tokens":118144,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1067,"reasoning_output_tokens":989,"total_tokens":119515},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2891461,"cached_input_tokens":2846464,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":13215,"reasoning_output_tokens":8076,"total_tokens":2904676},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9213746510,"cached_input_tokens":9115609472,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":26582210,"reasoning_output_tokens":15561002,"total_tokens":9240328720}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:29:51.864Z","ordinal":493122,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18622-d3f8-7b20-9bc1-33bd7b657457","call_id":"call_1823a87e1d0742569e71467b514698a6","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"mcp__mcp_agent_mail__create_agent_identity\nYou are the MCP Agent Mail coordination server. Provide message routing, coordination tooling, and project context to cooperating agents. Outputs are JSON by default; pass format='toon' (or set MCP_AGENT_MAIL_OUTPUT_FORMAT=toon) to receive {format:'toon', data:'<TOON>'}.\n\nCreate a new, unique agent identity and persist its profile to Git.\n\nHow this differs from `register_agent`\n--------------------------------------\n- Always creates a new identity with a fresh unique name (never updates an existing one).\n- `name_hint`, if provided, MUST be a valid adjective+noun combination and must be available,\n  otherwise an error is raised. Without a hint, a random adjective+noun name is generated.\n\nCRITICAL: Agent Naming Rules\n-----------------------------\n- Agent names MUST be randomly generated adjective+noun combinations\n- Examples: \"GreenCastle\", \"BlueLake\", \"RedStone\", \"PurpleBear\"\n- Names should be unique, easy to remember, and NOT descriptive\n- INVALID examples: \"BackendHarmonizer\", \"DatabaseMigrator\", \"UIRefactorer\"\n- Best practice: Omit `name_hint` to auto-generate a valid name (RECOMMENDED)\n\nWhen to use\n-----------\n- Spawning a brand new worker agent that should not overwrite an exis\n---\nmcp__mcp_agent_mail__deregister_agent\nYou are the MCP Agent Mail coordination server. Provide message routing, coordination tooling, and project context to cooperating agents. Outputs are JSON by default; pass format='toon' (or set MCP_AGENT_MAIL_OUTPUT_FORMAT=toon) to receive {format:'toon', data:'<TOON>'}.\n\nRemove an agent from a project. Marks the agent as inactive and removes it from the active roster. Messages from/to the agent are preserved for audit but the agent can no longer send or receive new messages.\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_agent_mail__deregister_agent(args: { agent_name: string; project_key: string; registration_token?: string | null; }): Promise<CallToolResult<{ [key: string]: unknown; }>>; };\n```\n---\nmcp__mcp_agent_mail__fetch_inbox\nYou are the MCP Agent Mail coordination server. Provide message routing, coordination tooling, and project context to cooperating agents. Outputs are JSON by default; pass format='toon' (or set MCP_AGENT_MAIL_OUTPUT_FORMAT=toon) to receive {format:'toon', data:'<TOON>'}.\n\nRetrieve recent messages for an agent without mutating read/ack state.\n\nFilters\n-------\n- `urgent_only`: only messages with importance in {high, urgent}\n- `since_ts`: ISO-8601 timestamp string; messages strictly newer than this are returned\n- `limit`: max number of messages (default 20)\n- `include_bodies`: include full Markdown bodies in the payloads\n- `topic`: filter to messages with this topic tag\n- `unread_only`: when True, restrict to messages this recipient has not\n  yet explicitly marked read via `mark_message_read` or\n  `acknowledge_message`. Per-recipient: a message read by Agent A is\n  still unread for Agent B. A bare `fetch_inbox` call does NOT mark\n  messages read; this filter inspects existing read state without\n  mutating it.\n\nUsage patterns\n--------------\n- Poll after each editing step in an agent loop to pick up coordination messages.\n- Use `since_ts` with the timestamp from your last poll for effic\n---\nmcp__mcp_agent_mail__hard_delete_agent\nYou are the MCP Agent Mail coordination server. Provide message routing, coordination tooling, and project context to cooperating agents. Outputs are JSON by default; pass format='toon' (or set MCP_AGENT_MAIL_OUTPUT_FORMAT=toon) to receive {format:'toon', data:'<TOON>'}.\n\nIRREVERSIBLY delete an agent and ALL associated data: messages sent by the agent, message recipient records, file reservations, agent links, window identities, and on-disk archive files (inbox, outbox, attachments). This is NOT soft-delete — data is permanently destroyed and cannot be recovered. Requires the confirmation parameter to be exactly 'I UNDERSTAND'.\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_agent_mail__hard_delete_agent(args: { agent_name: string; confirmation: string; project_key: string; registration_token?: string | null; }): Promise<CallToolResult<{ [key: string]: unknown; }>>; };\n```\n---\nmcp__mcp_agent_mail__register_agent\nYou are the MCP Agent Mail coordination server. Provide message routing, coordination tooling, and project context to cooperating agents. Outputs are JSON by default; pass format='toon' (or set MCP_AGENT_MAIL_OUTPUT_FORMAT=toon) to receive {format:'toon', data:'<TOON>'}.\n\nCreate or update an agent identity within a project and persist its profile to Git.\n\nWhen to use\n-----------\n- At the start of a coding session by any automated agent.\n- To update an existing agent's program/model/task metadata and bump last_active.\n\nSemantics\n---------\n- If `name` is omitted, a random adjective+noun name is auto-generated.\n- Reusing the same `name` updates the profile (program/model/task) and\n  refreshes `last_active_ts`.\n- A `profile.json` file is written under `agents/<Name>/` in the project archive.\n\nAgent Identity\n---------------\nTwo naming modes are supported:\n1. **Explicit identity** — pass a stable ID like ``alpha-one``, ``cc-0``,\n   or ``worker_42``.  Must match ``[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,127}``.\n   Useful for swarm workflows where agents are relaunched onto the same\n   identity.\n2. **Auto-generated** — omit ``name`` to get a random adjective+noun\n   identity like ``GreenLake`` or ``Bl\n---\nmcp__mcp_agent_mail__retire_agent\nYou are the MCP Agent Mail coordination server. Provide message routing, coordination tooling, and project context to cooperating agents. Outputs are JSON by default; pass format='toon' (or set MCP_AGENT_MAIL_OUTPUT_FORMAT=toon) to receive {format:'toon', data:'<TOON>'}.\n\nSoft-delete an agent: mark it as retired so it stops accepting new messages while preserving message history. Retired agents are hidden from active agent lists but visible in 'all agents' views.\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_agent_mail__retire_agent(args: { agent_name: string; project_key: string; registration_token?: string | null; }): Promise<CallToolResult<{ [key: string]: unknown; }>>; };\n```\n---\nmcp__mcp_agent_mail__search_messages\nYou are the MCP Agent Mail coordination server. Provide message routing, coordination tooling, and project context to cooperating agents. Outputs are JSON by default; pass format='toon' (or set MCP_AGENT_MAIL_OUTPUT_FORMAT=toon) to receive {format:'toon', data:'<TOON>'}.\n\nFull-text search over subject and body for a project.\n\nTips\n----\n- SQLite FTS5 syntax supported: phrases (\"build plan\"), prefix (mig*), boolean (plan AND users)\n- Results are ordered by bm25 score (best matches first)\n- Limit defaults to 20; raise for broad queries\n\nQuery examples\n---------------\n- Phrase search: `\"build plan\"`\n- Prefix: `migrat*`\n- Boolean: `plan AND users`\n- Require urgent: `urgent AND deployment`\n\nParameters\n----------\nproject_key : str\n    Project identifier.\nquery : str\n    FTS5 query string.\nlimit : int\n    Max results to return.\n\nReturns\n-------\nlist[dict]\n    Each entry: { id, subject, importance, ack_required, created_ts, thread_id, from }\n\nExample\n-------\n```json\n{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":\"10\",\"method\":\"tools/call\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"search_messages\",\"arguments\":{\n  \"project_key\":\"/abs/path/backend\",\"query\":\"\"build plan\" AND users\", \"limit\": 50\n}}}\n```\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare co\n---\nmcp__mcp_agent_mail__sweep_stale_agents\nYou are the MCP Agent Mail coordination server. Provide message routing, coordination tooling, and project context to cooperating agents. Outputs are JSON by default; pass format='toon' (or set MCP_AGENT_MAIL_OUTPUT_FORMAT=toon) to receive {format:'toon', data:'<TOON>'}.\n\nRetire abandoned agents in the caller's project using the server's conservative inactivity heuristic. The caller is never retired, the threshold has a 60-second floor, and active file reservations block retirement by default.\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_agent_mail__sweep_stale_agents(args: { agent_name: string; project_key: string; registration_token?: string | null; require_no_active_reservations?: boolean; threshold_seconds?: number; }): Promise<CallToolResult<{ [key: string]: unknown; }>>; };\n```\n---\nmcp__mcp_agent_mail__unretire_agent\nYou are the MCP Agent Mail coordination server. Provide message routing, coordination tooling, and project context to cooperating agents. Outputs are JSON by default; pass format='toon' (or set MCP_AGENT_MAIL_OUTPUT_FORMAT=toon) to receive {format:'toon', data:'<TOON>'}.\n\nRestore a retired agent back to active status. The agent will resume accepting new messages.\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_agent_mail__unretire_agent(args: { agent_name: string; project_key: string; registration_token?: string | null; }): Promise<CallToolResult<{ [key: string]: unknown; }>>; };\n```"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5","create_time":1793251791.864691}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
