{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:30:04.055Z","ordinal":493135,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18623-0397-7f21-bd9a-d03b5170e55a","author":"/root/pr311_draft_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr311_draft_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — exact diff SHA-256: `61d3123133336b3588f84a7bdba264918c4b9c1e351de0dbf89ff292d368bdce`.\n\n`read_all_lines` now reads bytes through each newline, strips `\\n` and an optional preceding `\\r`, then decodes with `String::from_utf8_lossy`, preserving invalid-UTF-8 replacement behavior. The `?` on `read_until` propagates genuine mid-stream I/O errors; `batch_read` reports those as read failures instead of returning partial success ([file_ops.rs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/batch-read-utf8-main/core/src/file_ops.rs:984), [file_ops.rs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/batch-read-utf8-main/core/src/file_ops.rs:1135)). The added regression tests cover both lossy decoding and injected read failure.\n\nRead-only review; no tests run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5","create_time":1793251804.0557077,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23136}}
