-code/pull/287), and [#289](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/289) remain open on base `171fca4cfa61e695441e4be83e6ae30f19a8005c`, which predates this merge. Their owners must rebase and rerun exact-head checks before integration.\n\n**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest release and is still a prerelease; its immutable source is `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`. No stable `v1.0.0` exists. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without an independent custodian acceptance or a compatible sealed held-out corpus; no held-out payload has been accessed. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining live provider and standalone gates, qualification of a candidate built from current source, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The required five-terminal by three-size matrix has **0/15 formally recorded cell verdicts** and no screenshots. The operator reports that the client rendered at the sizes tried, but tmux inside GNOME Terminal could not be reduced below 43×13; this does not establish every prescribed interaction or matrix cell. Stable publication remains gated on all required acceptance gates.\n\nThe 2026-10-27 22:55 checkpoint below is retained as a historical snapshot; its archive-incomplete and pre-PR #288 statements are superseded by this update.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 22:55 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and checks:** `origin/main` is `7ddce16a900d2da9def27d53722243bf4df2de07`, merging PR #284 atop PR #283 and earlier RC10 fixes. Post-merge CI [40593091251](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40593091251) completed successfully on this exact SHA: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux packaging/reproducibility/smoke jobs passed. CodeQL [40593091302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40593091302) also passed. On the refreshed readiness worktree, requirements enforcement passed (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification), and version synchronization confirms every component remains `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source checks, not installed-RC acceptance.\n\n**RC10 reproducibility scope:** PR [#281](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/281) recorded the successful exact-tag run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805); PR [#282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/282) clarified that the comparison established byte identity for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against the published RC10. It does not claim byte identity for every build output. This evidence is bound to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; any successor source needs its own exact-tag reproducibility run.\n\n**RC10 E2 evidence:** PR [#283](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/283) reports 20/20 fresh-install, doctor and Node-preflight cells: eight positive cells across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12 and Fedora 40 with Node 22/24, plus twelve negative preflight cells for absent Node or Node 12/20. However, independent review of merged head `71a4218` returned CHANGES_REQUIRED, and I confirmed the evidence archive is incomplete: 21 of 34 `SHA256SUMS` entries are missing, including all listed per-cell logs; `prepared-images.json` contains cell/image/id but not the distro and Node metadata claimed by the README; and the positive-cell script sets `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` without documenting that limitation. Treat the matrix as a recorded result, not independently accepted E2 evidence, until the archive and claims are corrected and reviewed. The single Ubuntu 22.04/Node 22 lifecycle script re-runs the installer for alpha.2→RC10, rollback, reinstall and repair; it does not exercise `nexus upgrade` or the separate self-test-failure, crash-recovery and backup-restore acceptance rows. Other lifecycle cases and platforms remain open. All evidence applies only to installed RC10.\n\n**PR #284 lifecycle follow-up:** PR [#284](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/284) added RC10 checksum-tamper, failed-self-test, backup-restore and updater-process-crash scripts and logs, then merged at `7ddce16a` despite an independent CHANGES_REQUIRED review. Its exact-head CI run [40586513330](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40586513330) passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL. The independent review found the updated checksum index still has 21 missing files out of 45; the earlier lifecycle path still does not test successful `nexus upgrade`; the `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` bypass is not clearly disclosed; and the process-crash script does not verify the claimed staging cleanup. The merged code therefore does not close the E2 archive or lifecycle evidence gaps. Its process-death recovery result explicitly does not test power loss. The post-merge main CI and CodeQL runs subsequently passed on `7ddce16a`.\n\n**Readiness PR #268:** Its remote head remains `eac6cdb452726368d37a8ca373b56c688e0274da` on the older base `fc582c66`; its exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks all passed on that older candidate. The refreshed local readiness candidate `a3bb9e59e56e08de66ea5b7eaf682ce408b2e57f` includes current main `7ddce16a` and received independent ACCEPT from `rc5_candidate_review` against that exact base. Exact-main CI and CodeQL are green, but the refreshed candidate has not been pushed and therefore has no exact-head hosted checks. No merge is claimed.\n\n**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the newest prerelease on source `16ee8ca`; stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Held-out custody acceptance and compatible frozen T2 data remain unresolved (issue #1 is open with no custodian response); T2/T3/T4, evaluator-host acceptance, the remaining live provider and standalone gates, and independent exact-RC acceptance are incomplete. The human five-environment by three-size terminal matrix remains **0/15**, pending the operator; no per-cell verdict or evidence is recorded. Keep stable publication gated on every required acceptance gate.\n\nThe 19:22 and earlier checkpoints below remain historical snapshots and are superseded for current source, evidence, PR, CI and acceptance status by this checkpoint.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 19:22 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and checks:** `origin/main` is `fc582c66bf70e00938eedc0ce3cafc635f582540`, merging PR #279 after #278 and #277. Post-merge CI [40566591904](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566591904) is running Node 22 and Node 24 on that exact SHA; CodeQL [40566591883](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566591883) passed. Exact-main CI and CodeQL also passed on parent `cf05322` (runs [40561348972](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40561348972) and [40561348985](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40561348985)). Source requirements and RC10 version-sync checks passed on `cf05322` (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification). These are source-gate results, not installed-RC acceptance.\n\n**Readiness PR #268:** At 19:22 UTC, its remote head was `eac6cdb452726368d37a8ca373b56c688e0274da`, based on `main@fc582c66`. JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed on this exact head; Node 22 and Node 24 were still running. The preceding head `9c153d9` had not completed Node 22/24 at the last observation; its JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. No independent review is recorded on `eac6cdb`. This checkpoint update advances PR #268 again; its resulting head requires exact-head checks and independent review before merge.\n\n**Other source PRs:** PR [#279](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/279) corrected the configured-hook race and retention error-accounting findings left by #277. It merged at `fc582c6` after exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux packaging, JavaScript/TypeScript, CodeQL, and independent read-only review passed. PR [#278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/278) merged at `cf05322` as exact head `d617937`; its checks passed and independent evidence review accepted the sanitized ChatGPT receipts. That provider evidence covers the ChatGPT verify-on-RC row only. Open PR [#280](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/280) addresses configured state-directory recovery; Node 22/24 are running, while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL pass. Open PR [#281](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/281) records RC10 cross-runner reproducibility; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL pass, while Node 22/24 are running. These PRs do not establish the remaining provider/standalone matrix or release acceptance.\n\n**Qualification and publication:** RC10 remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed. Exact cross-runner reproducibility passed for immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca`; a successor candidate from current main still requires its own reproducibility run. Held-out custodian acceptance, T2/T3/T4, remaining live provider and standalone qualification, independent exact-RC acceptance, and human terminal evidence remain open. The five-environment by three-size operator terminal matrix remains **0/15**; no cell result or screenshot is recorded. Automated PTY evidence does not substitute for these human cells. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance criteria.\n\nThe 17:31 and earlier checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence and superseded for current source, PR, CI, and requirements status by this checkpoint.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 17:31 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and post-merge checks:** `origin/main` is `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`, integrating PR #275 after PR #273. Exact-main CI [40537474824](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40537474824) passed the Node 22, Node 24, and `linux-x86_64` jobs on `ceabfcc`; CodeQL [40537475057](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40537475057) also passed on that SHA. Earlier post-merge CI [40536704465](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40536704465) and CodeQL [40536704530](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40536704530) passed on `e94208d`. These establish source CI for those exact commits; they do not establish RC acceptance or release qualification.\n\n**Readiness PR #268:** GitHub reports PR [#268](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/268) open at exact remote head `d37746f20da27a8b11a9c25c14c08fe0db197add`, based on current `main` `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`. All exact-head checks passed: Node 22, Node 24, and `linux-x86_64` in CI run [40544627770](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40544627770), JavaScript/TypeScript in run `40544627915`, and CodeQL [122332399521](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/122332399521). The earlier independent review found stale attribution; the local follow-up corrects it and records the completed Linux result. This corrected follow-up is not yet pushed or independently reviewed. No merge is claimed.\n\n**Merged fixes:** PR #274 merged at `b17c64a2c84a6324fb78bc55d3a39a7c9cc4ed47`; its exact post-merge CI [40529300314](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40529300314) and CodeQL [40529300519](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40529300519) passed. PR #273 merged at `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2`; PR #275 merged at `ceabfcc`. Both merge commits have the passing exact post-merge checks listed above.\n\n**Other release-path PRs:** PR [#276](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/276) records a synthetic-only qualification-host preflight (10/10) bound to `ceabfcc`; its Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks pass, while Linux CI remains in progress. Its evidence does not establish custodian access, held-out qualification, or acceptance. PR [#277](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/277) addresses configured Git-hook execution during checkpoint and retention operations. Its exact diff received conflicting review dispositions: a GitHub review comment requested changes for a hook-discovery race and retention error accounting, while a separate read-only review returned ACCEPT. The findings remain unresolved pending the claimed implementation owner's response; no acceptance or merge is claimed. Node 22/24, CodeQL, and JavaScript/TypeScript checks pass; Linux CI remains in progress.\n\n**Requirements and qualification:** A clean disposable snapshot of `origin/main@ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227` passed `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals) and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10`. The first requirements invocation on the documentation-dirty readiness worktree was correctly refused by its clean-worktree preflight and is not treated as a gate result. The existing [RC10 OpenRouter evidence bundle](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md) establishes a pinned provider verification and one passing synthetic small task; this does not establish the broader provider/standalone matrix. Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains an unaccepted prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` is listed. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without independent custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining provider/standalone profiles, cross-runner exact-RC reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance, and scripted terminal gates remain incomplete.\n\n**Human terminal acceptance:** The five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15**. The operator cannot run the requested xterm 80×24 cell now; no cell result or screenshots are inferred. The prepared Ubuntu/GNOME host and worksheet remain available for a later genuine operator run. Scripted PTY evidence does not replace the human matrix. Publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance gates.\n\nThe 15:12 and earlier checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence and superseded for current source, PR, and CI status by this checkpoint.\n\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 15:12 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `3b7af5d3cd46ab1b83e9c8df9862e09cee22b1a7`, integrating PRs [#269](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/269) and [#270](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/270) after #271 and #272. Exact-main CI [40521505143](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40521505143) and CodeQL [40521505001](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40521505001) both passed on `3b7af5d`; CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux tests, security gates, packaging, reproducibility, package smoke, and installer smoke. PR #269 merge-commit CI [40519862728](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40519862728) passed on `f059770`. These runs establish CI for their exact commits, not the RC10 release gates.\n\n**Readiness PR #268:** The owner refreshed PR [#268](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/268) onto `main`; GitHub shows it open and mergeable at head `98f87bee6ca112e6d50f6fb2bc480fc47723c648`, based on `3b7af5d3cd46ab1b83e9c8df9862e09cee22b1a7`. Its Node 22, Node 24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks pass; Linux packaging/reproducibility run [40524245685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40524245685) is still pending. The 14:38 checkpoint update was independently accepted (diff SHA-256 `c8cf46163cd8be8666ea86e8a95a7483588e10aa3e8775fbfa213ce55895d41e`). The current local follow-up records terminal main and #269 CI plus the latest PR state; it has not been pushed, and no PR merge is claimed.\n\n**Merged hook remediations and residual:** PRs #269 (retention shell/hook execution) and #270 (checkpoint Git hooks) are merged at `f059770` and `3b7af5d`; both now have passing exact-merge CI. The merged implementation passes `core.hooksPath=/dev/null` to relevant Git commands. Configured `reference-transaction` hooks may remain callable despite that setting; this was independently reproduced and accepted on a local follow-up to #269 (`d349068`), whose focused tests passed 17/17 on Git 2.54.0 and Git 2.43.0 plus `tsc --noEmit`. That follow-up is not on current main or the merged #269 head and needs a separately refreshed fix and exact-head validation; its source and test files are currently claimed by another agent.\n\n**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` is listed. The human five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15** and pending. The user's informal observation is that rendering works at tested sizes except tmux in GNOME Terminal, where the smallest usable size is 43×13; there are no per-cell records or screenshots, so human acceptance is not established. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open, last updated 2026-10-26 17:37:53 UTC, with no custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody and host acceptance, live provider/standalone, independent exact-RC, scripted terminal, and human acceptance gates remain incomplete. Publication authorization remains gated on every required acceptance gate.\n\nThe 14:38, 13:56 and earlier checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence and superseded for current source, PR, and CI status by this checkpoint.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 12:46 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and post-merge CI:** `origin/main` is `1d9357ee63b1066a891584a898842814de614fbf`, integrating PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264). Its exact-head CI [40499840211](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40499840211) and CodeQL [40499839711](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40499839711) passed before merge. Post-merge CodeQL [40505388849](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40505388849) passed on `1d9357e`; post-merge CI [40505388775](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40505388775) is still running both Node 22 and Node 24 CLI suites. No result is inferred before they finish.\n\n**Readiness PR and local full-suite result:** PR [#268](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/268) remains remotely at `bda6714ff885f2fd4fef736b84ca7005a9cddbdf`, based on `303ea322a7148b4a9d1a8231d7ce1c8f824bbae4`; it is conflicting with current `main` and its old successful checks are stale. The claimed local branch had been refreshed through `bff9f13085368e6cc269b1bb294db5b3b810bd7a`; the updated branch now incorporates `1d9357e` and is awaiting final independent review. No push or merge is claimed.\n\nENHANCEMENT SCOPE REFERENCES\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:136:| Agent loop and core (`cli/src/agent.ts`, `core/{turn,app,execution_tracking,objective,provider_recovery,operation_runner}.ts`, `team.ts`) | 9 | Full read | A_core_agent | — |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:254:| AGT-11 | S3 | RR | Team outcome | `operation_runner.ts:651-663` | SRC | COMPLETE without a change | REQ-AGT-107 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:255:| AGT-12 | S4 | RR | Operation bound | `operation_runner.ts:95-137` | SRC | Dead-end decision | REQ-AGT-107 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:67:**Requested codebase-review findings:** The prior checkpoint's implementation and evidence summary remains applicable; the current main includes the capability-category split, scheduler extraction, operation-runner decomposition, bounded diagnostics, `DecisionRejected` guidance, lifecycle tests, and 100 fixed-seed scheduler invariants. The operator config remains intentionally limited to `operationPolicy`; general runtime-default customization is not claimed.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:81:**Requested codebase-review findings are part of the v1.0.0 scope:** The large capability registry is split into category modules (`cli/src/core/capabilities.ts`, 10,046 bytes, plus `capability_definitions/`); scheduler logic is in `cli/src/core/scheduler.ts` (23,696 bytes), with `operation.ts` reduced to 12,818 bytes; runner revalidation, execution, and persistence are separated from `operation_runner.ts` (14,931 bytes). Runner decomposition and bounded revalidation/runner diagnostics were integrated through PR [#287](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/287); TDD evidence diagnostics landed through PR [#295](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/295), and scheduler observer diagnostics through PR [#296](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/296). PR [#297](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/297), now merged, adds regression coverage for the TDD diagnostic paths. The capability split and scheduler extraction were integrated through PRs [#286](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/286) and [#285](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/285), respectively. PR [#293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/293) added operator guidance for `DecisionRejected` and is merged with its Node 22/24, Linux, and CodeQL checks successful. These source changes are implemented on current `main`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:95:**Integration queue:** PR #285 merged to `d3b7af3`; its exact diff hash and independent ACCEPT were preserved, and the initial state-store lock timeout did not reproduce in its full Linux retry. PR [#289](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/289) is refreshed onto `d3b7af3` at `3f66ee138b1d8aeded2902851f659873d887f307`; its seven-file patch SHA-256 remains `3e13bdaa…`. Fresh Node 22/24/JavaScript checks and Entire Gates are in progress. The first fresh reviewer response described only the docs file, but the GitHub and local diff both contain six implementation/test files plus docs; a complete read-only source review has been requested, so the rebase is not independently accepted yet. PR [#293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/293), DecisionRejected operator documentation, is refreshed onto `d3b7af3` at `d0e1fbfb10463948b640361bb123177e9490ee1b`; its exact docs diff SHA-256 remains `83de84d7…`. Independent review ACCEPT was reconfirmed at this exact head. Fresh CI is running. Entire's refreshed trail currently reports Approvals failed (no reviewers approved), Findings passed, Up to date passed, and CI pending. The reviewer confirmed no Entire approval integration or distinct identity is available in their session, so the required trail approval remains outstanding. PR [#292](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/292) remains on base `8b24d8e1`, is reported conflicting against current main, and its Entire Gates check failed for missing reviewer approval and staleness. Its remote checks do not establish current-base readiness. No merge is inferred from stale checks.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:684:| `REQ-AGT-004` | tested (depth 0; work-unit mechanism landed in PR-4b) | `AGT-02a` archive→task→session commit ordering is applied to durable work units by PR-4b (`agent.ts:3339-3402`, `operation_runner.ts:566`, `durable_continuity.test.ts:359`, `dispositions.md` M2); work-unit pressure-forced compaction + SIGKILL crash-boundary test is in flight under `PLAN-04 PR-4g`, and live long-task `ACC-CONT-10` remains pending RC qualification. | `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (`ACC-CONT-03` SIGKILL), `ACC-CONT-10` on installed RC | Continuity implementer, independent reviewer, and qualification operator | Land and independently review `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (M1/M3/L5), then execute `ACC-CONT-10` on the installed RC during M5. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:161:| REQ-AGT-107 | Audit | Implementer and tester units cannot be COMPLETE with no change. | honesty | `operation_runner.ts:651-663` | SRC (AGT-11; test:cli/test/team_convergence.test.ts) | tested | ACC-CONT-07 | RR | AGT-11, AGT-12 | SPEC-04 / PLAN-04 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:18:| src/core/operation_runner.ts | full read |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:45:| AGT-02 | S2 | `/team`, `nexus operation run/resume` (work units) | agent.ts:3081 (`durableUnit = this.depth === 0`), 3127, 1136-1139, 4389, 1489-1501; operation_runner.ts:559 | SOURCE + DOC-CLAIM. Work units run as `new AutonomousAgent(config, 1)` and ARE durable (resumed via `recoverFromTaskState`), but every depth-gated rule treats depth 1 as a non-durable in-turn subagent: (a) compaction is applied in memory only — no archive append, no checkpoint, never `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; the next `persistProgress` then writes the compacted conversation and a `committedCompactions` id that has no archive lines, so originals are lost and `read_archive` cannot return them after resume (contradicts COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:145-160 \"Every compaction ... is committed in a fixed order\"); (b) no objective ledger: no requirement gating, no steering, `update_requirements`/`read_objective` not offered; (c) `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` per turn, so loop/stagnation history and cumulative steps reset at every resume/retry; (d) no change baseline / independence judgement (`captureChangeBaseline` depth 0 only, 4034) so discovered-verifier passes are at best REGRESSION_FREE. `runningAsSubagent` already distinguishes the two cases (5003). | Long team/operation units lose compaction originals and convergence history across resume; doc claims overstate durability. | Gate on `runningAsSubagent` (non-durable) instead of `depth`; add a work-unit compaction+resume test asserting archive lines exist. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:54:| AGT-11 | S3 | Team/unit outcome semantics | operation_runner.ts:651-663; turn.ts:358-370 | SOURCE. `classify` marks a unit COMPLETE on `turnSucceeded`, which includes `NOT_REQUIRED` (no changes, FINAL_TEXT). An `implementer`/`tester` unit that answers in prose without changing or verifying anything is COMPLETE and its dependents run. | Team \"COMPLETE\" can mean nothing was implemented. | Role-aware success (implementation units require a change + non-UNVERIFIED outcome) or decision. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:55:| AGT-12 | S4 | Operation runner safety bound | operation_runner.ts:95-137 | SOURCE. 10 000 scheduler transitions → BLOCKED with a decision whose `options: []`; `nexus operation decide` has nothing to apply. Bound itself is a resource-safety valve, not a work ceiling. | Rare dead-end state. | Offer resume/stop options. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:183:| EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE I3/I4/stale-lock status | grep operation_runner for 502/504 park + lock CAS; add tests |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:15:- `cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:95-137,559,651-663`\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:34:| 10 | Role-aware unit classification: a NOT_REQUIRED result from an implementer or tester unit becomes BLOCKED(no_change); give the 10k-transition stop real options. | `operation_runner.ts:95-137,651-663` | — |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:36:Work units (`/team`, `nexus operation`) run as `new AutonomousAgent(config, 1)` and *are* durable: they are resumed from task state (`operation_runner.ts:559`). But every durability rule is gated on `this.depth === 0` (`agent.ts:3081,3127,1136-1139,4389,1489-1501,4034`). The consequences:\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:55:| AGT-11 | Implementer/tester units become COMPLETE with NOT_REQUIRED, which means no change was made (`operation_runner.ts:651-663`). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:119:In `operation_runner.ts classify`, `turnSucceeded && outcome === NOT_REQUIRED && role ∈ {implementer, tester}` gives `BLOCKED(decision: no_change)` with options `[\"retry\", \"accept_no_change\", \"stop\"]`. Also give the 10,000-transition stop the options `[\"resume\", \"stop\"]` (AGT-12).\n\nPR319 CHECKS\nCodeQL\tSUCCESS\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/123282292531\ntest-matrix (22)\tIN_PROGRESS\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40823779576/job/123282034289\ntest-matrix (24)\tIN_PROGRESS\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40823779576/job/123282034065\njavascript-typescript\tSUCCESS\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40823779581/job/123282033838\nEntire Gates\tIN_PROGRESS\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/668721d8135d3a3332bca27b820caa5a4a76c7af\nCodeRabbit\tSUCCESS\t\n\nPR318 CHECKS\nCodeQL\tSUCCESS\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/123282336618\ntest-matrix (22)\tIN_PROGRESS\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40823786380/job/123282053206\njavascript-typescript\tSUCCESS\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40823786346/job/123282052751\ntest-matrix (24)\tIN_PROGRESS\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40823786380/job/123282052876\nEntire Gates\tIN_PROGRESS\thttps://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/33/changes/nexus-code/33\nCodeRabbit\tSUCCESS\t\n\nMAIN CI JOB STATES\ntest-matrix (24)\tin_progress\t\tRun npm --prefix cli test\ntest-matrix (22)\tin_progress\t\tRun npm --prefix cli test\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":253294631}},"started_at_ms":1793251952060,"completed_at_ms":1793251954314}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:32:35.582Z","ordinal":493261,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18625-537e-7222-abe8-fab57d2af38c","call_id":"call_acda8912960748ac8a1d4d68eac21566","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 16676)\nTotal output lines: 221\n\nREADINESS\n# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 04:23 UTC)\n\n**Remote revision reconciliation:** `origin/main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`; `origin/v1/integration` is `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78`. The integration ref is an ancestor of main (875 commits behind), not a divergent head. Current release PRs target main; evidence from the two refs must remain distinct.\n\n**Source gates on main:** `origin/main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` (PR #312 merge). Exact-main CI run [40802654248](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654248) and CodeQL run [40802654255](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654255) passed on that SHA. The exact-source requirements gate passed with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open); 12 requirements remain mapped to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n\n**Candidate convergence:** PR #311 remains open at `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954` on the older base `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`; its prior Node 22/24, Linux x86_64 and CodeQL checks passed, but they do not qualify the current base. A local candidate at `fe28ec9e686b90e69e42a7a13d55f50264b3775f` includes the reviewed source changes and readiness refresh; the completed full suite below ran on a different immutable snapshot and is not exact-candidate evidence. PR #316 carries the terminal-matrix correction at head `2e9ad10df4bab065bc9573680e3ed659709e4293` against main `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`; independent review accepted that exact head, CodeQL and JS/TS passed, Node 22/24 and Entire Gates remain in progress at 04:23 UTC, and GitHub reports the PR blocked. PR #315's waiver conclusion conflicts with the current release decision and must not be merged as-is.\n\n**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The claims identify OpenCode as the prior/current custodian workflow, but do not verify the responsible human identity; SageBridge's 04:15 status says it is coordinating only. The successor T2 store remains 20/40 tasks; the remaining Go/Rust tasks need the reviewed, pinned-toolchain change integrated. Reported T3 digest/schema/isolation checks are 8/8, which is not full T3 task-quality qualification. At 04:23 UTC the OpenCode custodian holds SUITE for two-round setup/reference/oracle revalidation of the 20 converted tasks with isolated HOME; a live validator child process was observed. This is custody revalidation, not held-out qualification; no result or custody acceptance is recorded. Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; the latest metadata-only correction was posted at 04:18 UTC. T2 custody acceptance and qualification, full T3/T4 qualification, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, fault injection, successor-RC reproducibility and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC10 evidence does not qualify a successor candidate.\n\n**Terminal gate:** The release owner requires all 15 manual terminal cells (five environments × three sizes) on the exact installed RC. The latest verified worksheet status is 0/15 accepted cells; blank cells remain incomplete. Actual operator execution and per-cell outcomes are mandatory; automated CI or PTY results do not substitute. [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waives screenshots only. [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal applications, but the manual matrix remains outstanding.\n\n**Suite evidence:** `make test` completed on immutable snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c` with isolated HOME and the required evaluator workspace/runtime fixtures: 1,993 tests across 224 suites, 1,991 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped, 0 cancelled; Rust tests and post-test security lifecycle gates passed. The full run took 3,167,118 ms. This snapshot is not exact current main, PR #311 candidate `fe28ec9`, or an RC, so the result does not qualify those revisions. The SUITE claim transferred to the OpenCode custodian at 04:18 UTC for the 20-task custody revalidation above.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 20:18 UTC; superseded)\n\nThis historical checkpoint includes a matrix-waiver conclusion that was later withdrawn by the current DEC-19 decision. It records the prior checkpoint only and is not the current acceptance disposition.\n\n**A…14176 tokens truncated…M. Work units run as `new AutonomousAgent(config, 1)` and ARE durable (resumed via `recoverFromTaskState`), but every depth-gated rule treats depth 1 as a non-durable in-turn subagent: (a) compaction is applied in memory only — no archive append, no checkpoint, never `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; the next `persistProgress` then writes the compacted conversation and a `committedCompactions` id that has no archive lines, so originals are lost and `read_archive` cannot return them after resume (contradicts COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:145-160 \"Every compaction ... is committed in a fixed order\"); (b) no objective ledger: no requirement gating, no steering, `update_requirements`/`read_objective` not offered; (c) `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` per turn, so loop/stagnation history and cumulative steps reset at every resume/retry; (d) no change baseline / independence judgement (`captureChangeBaseline` depth 0 only, 4034) so discovered-verifier passes are at best REGRESSION_FREE. `runningAsSubagent` already distinguishes the two cases (5003). | Long team/operation units lose compaction originals and convergence history across resume; doc claims overstate durability. | Gate on `runningAsSubagent` (non-durable) instead of `depth`; add a work-unit compaction+resume test asserting archive lines exist. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:54:| AGT-11 | S3 | Team/unit outcome semantics | operation_runner.ts:651-663; turn.ts:358-370 | SOURCE. `classify` marks a unit COMPLETE on `turnSucceeded`, which includes `NOT_REQUIRED` (no changes, FINAL_TEXT). An `implementer`/`tester` unit that answers in prose without changing or verifying anything is COMPLETE and its dependents run. | Team \"COMPLETE\" can mean nothing was implemented. | Role-aware success (implementation units require a change + non-UNVERIFIED outcome) or decision. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:55:| AGT-12 | S4 | Operation runner safety bound | operation_runner.ts:95-137 | SOURCE. 10 000 scheduler transitions → BLOCKED with a decision whose `options: []`; `nexus operation decide` has nothing to apply. Bound itself is a resource-safety valve, not a work ceiling. | Rare dead-end state. | Offer resume/stop options. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:183:| EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE I3/I4/stale-lock status | grep operation_runner for 502/504 park + lock CAS; add tests |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:15:- `cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:95-137,559,651