{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:34:44.370Z","ordinal":493360,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ad261ad9-8f39-41e0-9994-21e3d4c93b29","process_id":"64086","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr checks 319 --json name,state --jq '.[] | [.name,.state] | @tsv'; gh pr checks 318 --json name,state --jq '.[] | [.name,.state] | @tsv'; gh run view 40822684551 --json status,conclusion,jobs --jq '{status,conclusion,jobs:[.jobs[]|{name,status,conclusion,step:([.steps[]?|select(.status==\"in_progress\")|.name]|first)}]}'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md | sed -n '1,120p'; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md | sed -n '1,140p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr checks 319 --json name,state --jq '.[] | [.name,.state] | @tsv'; gh pr checks 318 --json name,state --jq '.[] | [.name,.state] | @tsv'; gh run view 40822684551 --json status,conclusion,jobs --jq '{status,conclusion,jobs:[.jobs[]|{name,status,conclusion,step:([.steps[]?|select(.status==\"in_progress\")|.name]|first)}]}'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md | sed -n '1,120p'; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md | sed -n '1,140p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"CodeQL\tSUCCESS\ntest-matrix (22)\tIN_PROGRESS\ntest-matrix (24)\tIN_PROGRESS\njavascript-typescript\tSUCCESS\nEntire Gates\tIN_PROGRESS\nCodeRabbit\tSUCCESS\nCodeQL\tSUCCESS\ntest-matrix (22)\tIN_PROGRESS\njavascript-typescript\tSUCCESS\ntest-matrix (24)\tIN_PROGRESS\nEntire Gates\tIN_PROGRESS\nCodeRabbit\tSUCCESS\n{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"jobs\":[{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"step\":\"Run npm --prefix cli test\"},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"step\":\"Run npm --prefix cli test\"}],\"status\":\"in_progress\"}\n# Manual real-terminal acceptance worksheet\n\nFor `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3).\n\n> **Required for v1.0.0.** Complete all 15 cells against the exact installed RC. Blank cells are incomplete; no result is inferred. Automated PTY runs do not count as manual cell evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. The prior waiver record is withdrawn by [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\n\n## Installed candidate identity\n\nFill these fields from the installed candidate before the first cell. Do not copy identity from a source branch or local build.\n\n- RC tag: ______________________________________________\n- Full RC source commit: ________________________________\n- Installed package/archive name and location: ____________\n- Installed artifact SHA256: ____________________________\n- Installation procedure/run reference: __________________\n- `nexus --version` output reference: ____________________\n- Operator and UTC date/time: ____________________________\n- Host OS and version: __________________________________\n- Per-cell evidence record directory or reference: ________\n\nRecord the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\n\n| Environment | Version / protocol details |\n|---|---|\n| xterm | |\n| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | |\n| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux: ; GNOME Terminal: |\n| VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code: ; integrated terminal profile: |\n| GNOME Terminal | |\n\n## Procedure to perform in every matrix cell\n\nRun each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by that row. Record the observations and evidence references for the cell.\n\n1. Launch `nexus`; confirm the TUI appears.\n2. At the approval panel, type continuously across it, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Exercise multiline input with Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Press Esc during `sleep 30`; confirm no child processes survive.\n6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm clean terminal restoration (echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\n\nScreenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). This does not waive any live manual interaction, check, observation, per-cell verdict, or evidence record. Automated PTY runs do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\n\n## Partial operator report\n\nIn response to the RC10 matrix request, the release owner reported that the client rendered at the tested sizes except in tmux inside GNOME Terminal; that setup could not be resized below 43×13, and the other results seemed okay. The report was received on 2026-10-29; test time, exact installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell check outcomes were not supplied. Treat this as useful partial operator information only: it does not fill any matrix cell or establish the installed-RC gate. No screenshot was supplied; DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts.\n\n## Terminal × size results\n\nSelect exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Record observed outcomes for every check and a per-cell evidence reference bound to the installed RC identity, terminal environment, and size. Record failures in the disposition/notes field.\n\n| # | Terminal environment | Size | Verdict (select one) | Per-cell evidence / result reference | Failure disposition / notes |\n|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|\n| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n\n## Acceptance gate\n\n- Safety checks 2, 5, and 6: **zero failures across all 15 cells**. Any failure here blocks this gate.\n- Any failure on another check requires a written disposition: fix, or a documented known limitation.\n- All 15 cells have exactly one verdict, check outcomes, and per-cell evidence references: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n- All non-safety failures have a written disposition: [ ] yes  [ ] no  [ ] no such failures\n- Safety gate has zero failures: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n\n§5.3 matrix gate: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\n\nMark the §5.3 matrix gate PASS when all 15 verdicts, check outcomes, and per-cell evidence\nreferences are complete, checks 2, 5, and 6 have zero failures, and every\nfailure on another check has a written disposition. Mark it FAIL if any safety\ncheck (2, 5, or 6) failed. Mark it INCOMPLETE when required evidence is missing\nor a non-safety failure has no written disposition.\n\nACC-TUI-MANUAL: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\n\nMark ACC-TUI-MANUAL PASS only when all 15 cell verdicts are PASS and the\nper-cell outcomes and evidence records are complete. Screenshots are waived per DEC-18. Mark it FAIL if any\ncell is FAIL. Mark it INCOMPLETE when evidence is missing and no cell has\nfailed. A documented known limitation for a non-safety failure may satisfy the\n§5.3 disposition requirement, but the cell remains FAIL and ACC-TUI-MANUAL\nremains unmet until every cell passes.\n\nOperator summary / evidence index: ______________________________________________\n\nThis worksheet records manual terminal evidence only. It does not replace the separate CI PTY, installed-RC, or independent acceptance gates in `ACCEPTANCE.md`.\n# Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n\nA human runs this procedure against the **installed RC**. Automated PTY suites (§5.1, §5.2) do not replace it.\n\n**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\n- xterm\n- kitty, with the kitty keyboard protocol on\n- tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal\n- the VS Code integrated terminal\n- GNOME Terminal\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition.\n\n## Before you start\n\n1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\n   not resolve into a checkout.\n2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n\n## Each cell\n\nOpen the terminal and resize it to the cell's size. For tmux, start tmux inside GNOME Terminal. For kitty, enable the\nkeyboard protocol. Then run:\n\n```sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc <rc> --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> --size <WxH> --out \"$OUT\"\n```\n\nThe script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\n`tmux-gnome`, or a cell already recorded. It creates an isolated HOME and workspace and starts the mock. Then it opens\nthe TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\n\n| # | You do | You judge |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\n| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\n| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n\nThe script also **measures** two things:\n- whether `stty` state after each exit equals the state before it;\n- any process started from the cell's HOME that is still running after exit.\n\nA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nresults and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\nattempt and use a new evidence directory.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\npopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\nto an unavailable measurement.\n\n```sh\n# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\nnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n```\n\nThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n  `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n\nThe record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Commit the evidence directory\nto the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":113084957}},"started_at_ms":1793252082256,"completed_at_ms":1793252084370}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:34:45.847Z","ordinal":493361,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18627-5057-7992-898c-64185f02e1d1","call_id":"call_2ec4807cb4254d3c8270c89603b4f3f3","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2843)\nTotal output lines: 186\n\nCodeQL\tSUCCESS\ntest-matrix (22)\tIN_PROGRESS\ntest-matrix (24)\tIN_PROGRESS\njavascript-typescript\tSUCCESS\nEntire Gates\tIN_PROGRESS\nCodeRabbit\tSUCCESS\nCodeQL\tSUCCESS\ntest-matrix (22)\tIN_PROGRESS\njavascript-typescript\tSUCCESS\ntest-matrix (24)\tIN_PROGRESS\nEntire Gates\tIN_PROGRESS\nCodeRabbit\tSUCCESS\n{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"jobs\":[{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"step\":\"Run npm --prefix cli test\"},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"step\":\"Run npm --prefix cli test\"}],\"status\":\"in_progress\"}\n# Manual real-terminal acceptance worksheet\n\nFor `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3).\n\n> **Required for v1.0.0.** Complete all 15 cells against the exact installed RC. Blank cells are incomplete; no result is inferred. Automated PTY runs do not count as manual cell evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. The prior waiver record is withdrawn by [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\n\n## Installed candidate identity\n\nFill these fields from the installed candidate before the first cell. Do not copy identity from a source branch or local build.\n\n- RC tag: ______________________________________________\n- Full RC source commit: ________________________________\n- Installed package/archive name and location: ____________\n- Installed artifact SHA256: ____________________________\n- Installation procedure/run reference: __________________\n- `nexus --version` output reference: ____________________\n- Operator and UTC date/time: ____________________________\n- Host OS and version: __________________________________\n- Per-cell evidence record directory or reference: ________\n\nRecord the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\n\n| Environment | Version / protocol details |\n|---|---|\n| xterm | |\n| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | |\n| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux: ; GNOME Terminal: |\n| VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code: ; integrated terminal profile: |\n| GNOME Terminal | |\n\n## Procedure to perform in every matrix cell\n\nRun each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by that row. Record the observations and evidence references for the cell.\n\n1. Launch `nexus`; confirm the TUI appears.\n2. At the approval panel, type continuously across it, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Exercise multiline input with Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Press Esc during `sleep 30`; confirm no child processes survive.\n6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm clean terminal restoration (echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\n\nScreenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). This does not waive any live manual interaction, check, observation, per-cell verdict, or evidence record. Automated PTY runs do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\n\n## Partial operator report\n\nIn response to the RC10 matrix request, the release owner reported that the client rendered at the tested sizes except in tmux inside GNOME Terminal; that setup could not be resized below 43×13, and the other results seemed okay. The report was received on 2026-10-29; test time, exact installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell check outcomes were not supplied. Treat this as useful partial operator information only: it does not fill any matrix cell or establish the installed-RC gate. No screenshot was supplied; DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts.\n\n## Terminal × size results\n\nSelect exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Record observed outcomes for every check and a per-cell evidence reference bound to the installed RC identity, terminal environment, and size. Record failures in the disposition/notes field.\n\n| # | Terminal environment | Size | Verdict (select one) | Per-cell evidence / result reference | Failure disposition / notes |\n|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|\n| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ …343 tokens truncated…limitation for a non-safety failure may satisfy the\n§5.3 disposition requirement, but the cell remains FAIL and ACC-TUI-MANUAL\nremains unmet until every cell passes.\n\nOperator summary / evidence index: ______________________________________________\n\nThis worksheet records manual terminal evidence only. It does not replace the separate CI PTY, installed-RC, or independent acceptance gates in `ACCEPTANCE.md`.\n# Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n\nA human runs this procedure against the **installed RC**. Automated PTY suites (§5.1, §5.2) do not replace it.\n\n**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\n- xterm\n- kitty, with the kitty keyboard protocol on\n- tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal\n- the VS Code integrated terminal\n- GNOME Terminal\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition.\n\n## Before you start\n\n1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\n   not resolve into a checkout.\n2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n\n## Each cell\n\nOpen the terminal and resize it to the cell's size. For tmux, start tmux inside GNOME Terminal. For kitty, enable the\nkeyboard protocol. Then run:\n\n```sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc <rc> --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> --size <WxH> --out \"$OUT\"\n```\n\nThe script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\n`tmux-gnome`, or a cell already recorded. It creates an isolated HOME and workspace and starts the mock. Then it opens\nthe TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\n\n| # | You do | You judge |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\n| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\n| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n\nThe script also **measures** two things:\n- whether `stty` state after each exit equals the state before it;\n- any process started from the cell's HOME that is still running after exit.\n\nA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nresults and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\nattempt and use a new evidence directory.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\npopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\nto an unavailable measurement.\n\n```sh\n# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\nnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n```\n\nThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n  `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n\nThe record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Commit the evidence directory\nto the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5","create_time":1793252085.8471935}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
