EPTANCE.md' | while read f; do echo \"---$f\"; cat \"$f\"; done"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"DEC18\n241:## DEC-18: v1.0.0 terminal screenshot-artifact waiver\n242-\n243-**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\n244-\n245-**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\n246-\n247-**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\n248-\n249-## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n250-\n251-**Status: withdrawn.** The waiver described in this decision is not in effect.\n252-\n253-**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\n254-\n255-**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\n\nACCEPTANCE 5.3 SCREENSHOT REFERENCES\n49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n50-| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n52-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n53-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n--\n79-| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82-| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83-| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n--\n119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | All 15 cells have actual manual execution, recorded PASS/FAIL verdicts, observed outcomes, and evidence bound to the exact installed RC. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 do not substitute for these cells. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n--\n188-| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n189-\n190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n191-\n192:**Required for v1.0.0.** Run every terminal × size combination below against the exact installed RC and record a verdict and observed outcomes for each cell. Automated suites in §5.1 and §5.2 remain required but do not replace operator execution. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. See [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\n193-\n194-Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n--\n204-7. NO_COLOR.\n205-\n206:Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); this does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\n207-\n208-**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n--\n334-- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n335-- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n336:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI and scripted gates PASS, and all 15 manual real-terminal cells have verified operator evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshots only.\n337-- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n338-- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n\nTERMINAL SCRIPT README REFERENCES\n17-   not resolve into a checkout.\n18-2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n19:3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n20-   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n21-\n--\n36-|---|---|---|\n37-| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n38:| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\n39-| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n40-| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n41-| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n42:| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\n43-| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n44-\n--\n48-\n49-A measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n50:`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\n51:results and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\n52-attempt and use a new evidence directory.\n53-\n--\n64-```\n65-\n66:The summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n67-- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n68-- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n\nSCRIPT SCREENSHOT ENFORCEMENT\norigin/main:cli/sr