ots/).\"\norigin/main:cli/src/core/tool_groups.ts:21:    tools: [\"browser_navigate\", \"browser_click\", \"browser_type\", \"browser_screenshot\", \"browser_console_logs\"],\norigin/main:cli/src/core/tool_groups.ts:22:    summary: \"drive a headless browser: open a page, click, type, screenshot, read console logs\",\norigin/main:cli/src/core/tool_groups.ts:23:    trigger: /\\b(browser|web ?page|screenshots?|localhost|front-?end|playwright)\\b/i,\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:1086:  .option(\"--screenshot\", \"Capture page screenshot\")\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:1094:    if (options.screenshot) {\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:1095:      const shot = await driver.screenshot();\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:1096:      console.log(pc.green(`✔ Screenshot saved: ${shot.path}\\n`));\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:19:3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:38:| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:42:| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:51:results and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:8:# The human records PASS/FAIL per check and two screenshots. Every attempt is kept. Usage:\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:146:     approve with a deliberate key. Screenshot an approval panel.\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:150:  6  Quit with Ctrl-C twice. Screenshot the terminal after exit.\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:163:# Answers are saved before anything else can fail, so a typo in a screenshot path does not lose them.\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:178:  read -r -p \"approval-panel screenshot path: \" shot_approval\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:179:  read -r -p \"post-exit screenshot path: \" shot_exit\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:183:  echo \"both screenshots must be .png/.jpg files taken during this attempt, and differ; try again\"\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:224:              [(\"approvalScreenshot\", e[\"APPROVAL_SHOT\"]), (\"postExitScreenshot\", e[\"EXIT_SHOT\"]), (\"mockLog\", f\"{stem}.mock.log\"),\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs:45:  if (record.files.approvalScreenshot.sha256 === record.files.postExitScreenshot.sha256) return \"the two screenshots are the same file\";\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:86:  \"approval.png\": \"approval screenshot\",\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:87:  \"post-exit.png\": \"post exit screenshot\",\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:93:  approvalScreenshot: \"approval.png\",\norigin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:94:  postExitScreenshot: \"post-exit.png\",\n\nTERMINAL DOCUMENT CLAIMS\n---.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md/owner.json\n{\n  \"agent\": \"codex-root\",\n  \"branch\": \"codex/restore-terminal-human-matrix\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-restore\",\n  \"base\": \"b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-29T03:51:00Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Restore the required 15-cell human terminal matrix in acceptance documents; DEC-19 owner waiver conflicts with direct user instruction; preserve truthful historical record and do not claim cells passed\",\n  \"handoff_from\": \"BlueFalcon\",\n  \"recovery_evidence\": \