{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:35:28.128Z","ordinal":493403,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-629e07c8-bedc-4868-838f-55f7806d058a","process_id":"88431","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main scripts/terminal-acceptance cli/test | rg -i 'terminal|screenshot'; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh | nl -ba | sed -n '155,250p'; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs | nl -ba | sed -n '1,140p'; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md | nl -ba | sed -n '1,100p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main scripts/terminal-acceptance cli/test | rg -i 'terminal|screenshot'; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh | nl -ba | sed -n '155,250p'; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs | nl -ba | sed -n '1,140p'; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md | nl -ba | sed -n '1,100p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"cli/test/agent_terminal_controls.test.ts\ncli/test/ui_terminal_safety.test.ts\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/mockgw.py\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/scope-procs.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh\n   155\tcat <<EOF\n   156\t\n   157\t7  NO_COLOR: the TUI opens again with NO_COLOR=1. Check that it is readable without colour, then quit with Ctrl-C twice.\n   158\tPress Enter to launch.\n   159\tEOF\n   160\tread -r _\n   161\tlaunch no_color NO_COLOR=1\n   162\t\n   163\t# Answers are saved before anything else can fail, so a typo in a screenshot path does not lose them.\n   164\t: > \"$cell_home/checks.tsv\"\n   165\tfor check in 1 2 3 4 5 6 7; do\n   166\t  while true; do\n   167\t    read -r -p \"check $check PASS or FAIL? \" answer\n   168\t    answer=\"${answer^^}\"; [[ \"$answer\" == PASS || \"$answer\" == FAIL ]] && break\n   169\t  done\n   170\t  read -r -p \"check $check note (optional): \" note\n   171\t  printf '%s\\t%s\\t%s\\n' \"$check\" \"$answer\" \"${note//$'\\t'/ }\" >> \"$cell_home/checks.tsv\"\n   172\tdone\n   173\tcp \"$cell_home/checks.tsv\" \"$stem.answers.tsv\"\n   174\tcp \"$cell_home/exits.tsv\" \"$stem.exits.tsv\"\n   175\tcp \"$mock_log\" \"$stem.mock.log\"\n   176\tread -r -p \"operator name: \" operator\n   177\twhile true; do\n   178\t  read -r -p \"approval-panel screenshot path: \" shot_approval\n   179\t  read -r -p \"post-exit screenshot path: \" shot_exit\n   180\t  if [[ \"$shot_approval\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && \"$shot_exit\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && -f \"$shot_approval\" && -f \"$shot_exit\" ]] \\\n   181\t     && ! cmp -s \"$shot_approval\" \"$shot_exit\" \\\n   182\t     && (( $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_approval\") >= attempt_start && $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_exit\") >= attempt_start )); then break; fi\n   183\t  echo \"both screenshots must be .png/.jpg files taken during this attempt, and differ; try again\"\n   184\tdone\n   185\tapproval_copy=\"$stem.approval.${shot_approval##*.}\"\n   186\texit_copy=\"$stem.post-exit.${shot_exit##*.}\"\n   187\tcp \"$shot_approval\" \"$approval_copy\"\n   188\tcp \"$shot_exit\" \"$exit_copy\"\n   189\t\n   190\t# Values reach Python only through the environment, never through generated source.\n   191\tCELL=\"$cell\" ATTEMPT=\"$attempt\" TERMINAL_NAME=\"$terminal\" CELL_SIZE=\"$size\" RC=\"$rc\" NEXUS_VERSION_LINE=\"$version_line\" \\\n   192\tNEXUS_PATH=\"$nexus_real\" PACKAGE_DIR=\"$package\" MANIFEST_SHA=\"$manifest_sha\" TMUX_VERSION=\"$tmux_version\" \\\n   193\tKITTY_PROTOCOL=\"$kitty_protocol\" OPERATOR_NAME=\"$operator\" STEM=\"$stem\" APPROVAL_SHOT=\"$approval_copy\" EXIT_SHOT=\"$exit_copy\" \\\n   194\tpython3 - <<'PY'\n   195\timport hashlib, json, os\n   196\te = os.environ\n   197\tstem = e[\"STEM\"]\n   198\tsha = lambda p: hashlib.sha256(open(p, \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()\n   199\texits = []\n   200\tfor line in open(f\"{stem}.exits.tsv\"):\n   201\t    label, status, restored, survivors, scope_measurement, at = line.rstrip(\"\\n\").split(\"\\t\")\n   202\t    exits.append({\"launch\": label, \"exitStatus\": int(status), \"sttyRestored\": restored == \"true\", \"survivors\": int(survivors), \"scopeMeasurement\": scope_measurement, \"at\": at})\n   203\tchecks = {}\n   204\tfor line in open(f\"{stem}.answers.tsv\"):\n   205\t    check, result, note = (line.rstrip(\"\\n\").split(\"\\t\") + [\"\"])[:3]\n   206\t    checks[check] = {\"result\": result, \"note\": note}\n   207\t# Scenario proof from the mock log: which prompts and tool rounds actually reached the gateway.\n   208\tscenarios = {\"approveToolRounds\": set(), \"stream\": 0, \"sleepTool\": 0}\n   209\tfor line in open(f\"{stem}.mock.log\"):\n   210\t    entry = json.loads(line)\n   211\t    prompt, tools = entry[\"turn\"]\n   212\t    if prompt == \"approve\" and entry[\"kind\"] == \"tools\": scenarios[\"approveToolRounds\"].add(tools)\n   213\t    if prompt == \"stream\" and entry[\"kind\"] == \"stream\": scenarios[\"stream\"] += 1\n   214\t    if prompt == \"sleep\" and entry[\"kind\"] == \"tools\": scenarios[\"sleepTool\"] += 1\n   215\tscenarios[\"approveToolRounds\"] = sorted(scenarios[\"approveToolRounds\"])\n   216\trecord = {\n   217\t    \"acceptance\": \"ACCEPTANCE §5.3\", \"cell\": e[\"CELL\"], \"attempt\": int(e[\"ATTEMPT\"]), \"terminal\": e[\"TERMINAL_NAME\"], \"size\": e[\"CELL_SIZE\"],\n   218\t    \"rc\": e[\"RC\"], \"nexusVersion\": e[\"NEXUS_VERSION_LINE\"], \"nexusPath\": e[\"NEXUS_PATH\"], \"packageDir\": e[\"PACKAGE_DIR\"],\n   219\t    \"packageManifestSha256\": e[\"MANIFEST_SHA\"],\n   220\t    \"env\": {k: e.get(k) for k in [\"TERM\", \"TERM_PROGRAM\", \"TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION\", \"COLORTERM\", \"VTE_VERSION\", \"KITTY_WINDOW_ID\", \"TMUX\", \"XTERM_VERSION\"]},\n   221\t    \"tmux\": e[\"TMUX_VERSION\"] or None, \"kittyKeyboardProtocol\": e[\"KITTY_PROTOCOL\"] or None,\n   222\t    \"measured\": exits, \"scenarios\": scenarios, \"checks\": checks,\n   223\t    \"files\": {name: {\"path\": os.path.basename(path), \"sha256\": sha(path)} for name, path in\n   224\t              [(\"approvalScreenshot\", e[\"APPROVAL_SHOT\"]), (\"postExitScreenshot\", e[\"EXIT_SHOT\"]), (\"mockLog\", f\"{stem}.mock.log\"),\n   225\t               (\"answers\", f\"{stem}.answers.tsv\"), (\"exits\", f\"{stem}.exits.tsv\")]},\n   226\t    \"operator\": e[\"OPERATOR_NAME\"],\n   227\t}\n   228\twith open(f\"{stem}.json\", \"x\") as f:\n   229\t    json.dump(record, f, indent=2)\n   230\tPY\n   231\tsha256sum \"$stem.json\" > \"$stem.json.sha256\"\n   232\trm -f \"$stem.partial\"\n   233\techo \"recorded $stem.json\"\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env node\n     2\t// Gate for the manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3) over the attempt records written by run-cell.sh.\n     3\t//   node scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs <evidence dir> --rc vX.Y.Z-rc.N --manifest-sha256 <hex> \\\n     4\t//     [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n     5\t// --manifest-sha256 is the SHA-256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC release archive, so every cell must have run the\n     6\t// published RC package. The gate fails closed:\n     7\t//   - every terminal × size cell needs a complete, verified attempt (otherwise NOT RUN: ACCEPTANCE §1 rule 5);\n     8\t//   - an attempt is complete only when its self-hash, file hashes, both launch measurements and the mock log's\n     9\t//     scenario proof (approve x2 tool rounds, stream, sleep tool call) all verify;\n    10\t//   - checks 2, 5 and 6 have zero FAIL in ANY attempt; a measured survivor or unrestored terminal turns PASS into FAIL;\n    11\t//   - every other FAIL, in any attempt, needs a written disposition keyed \"<cell>:<check>\";\n    12\t//   - an aborted attempt (a .partial file) needs a written disposition keyed \"<cell>:partial-<n>\".\n    13\t// Hashes prove the files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them: commit the evidence directory.\n    14\timport { createHash } from \"node:crypto\";\n    15\timport fs from \"node:fs\";\n    16\timport path from \"node:path\";\n    17\t\n    18\tconst TERMINALS = [\"xterm\", \"kitty\", \"tmux-gnome\", \"vscode\", \"gnome\"];\n    19\tconst SIZES = [\"80x24\", \"40x14\", \"200x60\"];\n    20\tconst CHECKS = [\"1\", \"2\", \"3\", \"4\", \"5\", \"6\", \"7\"];\n    21\tconst SAFETY = new Set([\"2\", \"5\", \"6\"]);\n    22\tconst arg = (name) => (process.argv.includes(name) ? process.argv[process.argv.indexOf(name) + 1] : null);\n    23\tconst dir = process.argv[2];\n    24\tconst rc = arg(\"--rc\");\n    25\tconst manifestSha = arg(\"--manifest-sha256\");\n    26\tif (!dir || !/^v\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+-rc\\.\\d+$/.test(rc ?? \"\") || !/^[0-9a-f]{64}$/.test(manifestSha ?? \"\")) {\n    27\t  console.error(\"usage: summarize.mjs <evidence dir> --rc vX.Y.Z-rc.N --manifest-sha256 <hex> [--dispositions file]\");\n    28\t  process.exit(2);\n    29\t}\n    30\tconst dispositions = arg(\"--dispositions\") ? JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(arg(\"--dispositions\"), \"utf8\")) : {};\n    31\tconst sha = (file) => createHash(\"sha256\").update(fs.readFileSync(file)).digest(\"hex\");\n    32\t\n    33\t/** Why an attempt record cannot be used, or null. */\n    34\tfunction attemptProblem(file, record, cell) {\n    35\t  const sidecar = `${file}.sha256`;\n    36\t  if (!fs.existsSync(sidecar) || fs.readFileSync(sidecar, \"utf8\").split(/\\s+/)[0] !== sha(file)) return \"record self-hash missing or wrong\";\n    37\t  if (record.cell !== cell) return `record names cell ${record.cell}`;\n    38\t  if (record.rc !== rc) return `record is for ${record.rc}, not ${rc}`;\n    39\t  if (record.packageManifestSha256 !== manifestSha) return \"installed package manifest differs from the RC archive\";\n    40\t  for (const [name, entry] of Object.entries(record.files ?? {})) {\n    41\t    const target = path.join(dir, entry.path);\n    42\t    if (!fs.existsSync(target) || sha(target) !== entry.sha256) return `${name} file missing or changed`;\n    43\t  }\n    44\t  if (Object.keys(record.files ?? {}).length !== 5) return \"record does not list its five evidence files\";\n    45\t  if (record.files.approvalScreenshot.sha256 === record.files.postExitScreenshot.sha256) return \"the two screenshots are the same file\";\n    46\t  const launches = (record.measured ?? []).map((m) => m.launch).sort().join(\",\");\n    47\t  if (launches !== \"main,no_color\") return `measured launches are [${launches}], not main and no_color`;\n    48\t  if (record.measured.some((m) => !Number.isInteger(m.survivors) || m.survivors < 0 || ![\"verified\", \"unavailable\"].includes(m.scopeMeasurement) || typeof m.sttyRestored !== \"boolean\")) return \"measurements are malformed\";\n    49\t  const s = record.scenarios ?? {};\n    50\t  if (!(s.approveToolRounds?.includes(0) && s.approveToolRounds?.includes(1)) || !(s.stream >= 1) || !(s.sleepTool >= 1)) return \"the mock log does not show the approve, stream and sleep scenarios\";\n    51\t  if (CHECKS.some((check) => ![\"PASS\", \"FAIL\"].includes(record.checks?.[check]?.result))) return \"a check has no PASS/FAIL\";\n    52\t  return null;\n    53\t}\n    54\t\n    55\tconst problems = [];\n    56\tconst rows = [];\n    57\tfor (const terminal of TERMINALS) {\n    58\t  for (const size of SIZES) {\n    59\t    const cell = `${terminal}-${size}`;\n    60\t    const attemptPrefix = `cell-${cell}.attempt-`;\n    61\t    const files = fs.readdirSync(dir).filter((name) => {\n    62\t      if (!name.startsWith(attemptPrefix) || !name.endsWith(\".json\")) return false;\n    63\t      return /^\\d+$/.test(name.slice(attemptPrefix.length, -\".json\".length));\n    64\t    }).sort();\n    65\t    const partials = fs.readdirSync(dir).filter((f) => f.startsWith(`cell-${cell}.attempt-`) && f.endsWith(\".partial\"));\n    66\t    const aborted = partials.length;\n    67\t    for (const partial of partials) {\n    68\t      const n = /attempt-(\\d+)\\.partial$/.exec(partial)?.[1];\n    69\t      if (!dispositions[`${cell}:partial-${n}`]) problems.push(`${cell}: aborted attempt ${n} without a written disposition`);\n    70\t    }\n    71\t    const attempts = [];\n    72\t    for (const name of files) {\n    73\t      const file = path.join(dir, name);\n    74\t      const record = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\n    75\t      const problem = attemptProblem(file, record, cell);\n    76\t      if (problem) { problems.push(`${cell} ${name}: unusable (${problem})`); continue; }\n    77\t      const results = {};\n    78\t      for (const check of CHECKS) {\n    79\t        let result = record.checks[check].result;\n    80\t        if (check === \"5\" && record.measured.some((m) => m.scopeMeasurement !== \"verified\")) result = \"FAIL (scope measurement unavailable)\";\n    81\t        if (check === \"5\" && record.measured.some((m) => m.survivors > 0)) result = \"FAIL (measured survivors)\";\n    82\t        if (check === \"6\" && record.measured.some((m) => !m.sttyRestored)) result = \"FAIL (terminal not restored)\";\n    83\t        results[check] = result;\n    84\t        if (!result.startsWith(\"FAIL\")) continue;\n    85\t        if (SAFETY.has(check)) problems.push(`${cell} attempt ${record.attempt}: safety check ${check} ${result}`);\n    86\t        else if (!dispositions[`${cell}:${check}`]) problems.push(`${cell} attempt ${record.attempt}: check ${check} FAIL without a written disposition`);\n    87\t      }\n    88\t      attempts.push({ attempt: record.attempt, results });\n    89\t    }\n    90\t    if (!attempts.length) { problems.push(`${cell}: NOT RUN`); rows.push({ cell, status: \"NOT RUN\", attempts: 0, aborted }); continue; }\n    91\t    rows.push({ cell, status: \"RECORDED\", attempts: attempts.length, aborted, latest: attempts[attempts.length - 1] });\n    92\t  }\n    93\t}\n    94\t\n    95\tconsole.log(`| cell | attempts | ${CHECKS.join(\" | \")} |\\n|---|---|${\"---|\".repeat(CHECKS.length)}`);\n    96\tfor (const row of rows) {\n    97\t  const cells = row.status === \"NOT RUN\" ? CHECKS.map(() => \"NOT RUN\") : CHECKS.map((c) => row.latest.results[c]);\n    98\t  console.log(`| ${row.cell} | ${row.attempts}${row.aborted ? ` (+${row.aborted} aborted)` : \"\"} | ${cells.join(\" | \")} |`);\n    99\t}\n   100\tconst verdict = problems.length ? \"FAIL\" : \"PASS\";\n   101\tconsole.log(`\\nREQ-QUAL-108 manual matrix gate for ${rc} (package manifest ${manifestSha.slice(0, 12)}): ${verdict}`);\n   102\tfor (const problem of problems) console.log(`- ${problem}`);\n   103\tfs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"matrix-summary.json\"), `${JSON.stringify({ verdict, rc, packageManifestSha256: manifestSha, rows, problems, dispositions }, null, 2)}\\n`);\n   104\tprocess.exit(problems.length ? 1 : 0);\n     1\t# Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n     2\t\n     3\tA human runs this procedure against the **installed RC**. Automated PTY suites (§5.1, §5.2) do not replace it.\n     4\t\n     5\t**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\n     6\t- xterm\n     7\t- kitty, with the kitty keyboard protocol on\n     8\t- tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal\n     9\t- the VS Code integrated terminal\n    10\t- GNOME Terminal\n    11\t\n    12\t**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition.\n    13\t\n    14\t## Before you start\n    15\t\n    16\t1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\n    17\t   not resolve into a checkout.\n    18\t2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n    19\t3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n    20\t   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n    21\t\n    22\t## Each cell\n    23\t\n    24\tOpen the terminal and resize it to the cell's size. For tmux, start tmux inside GNOME Terminal. For kitty, enable the\n    25\tkeyboard protocol. Then run:\n    26\t\n    27\t```sh\n    28\tscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc <rc> --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> --size <WxH> --out \"$OUT\"\n    29\t```\n    30\t\n    31\tThe script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\n    32\t`tmux-gnome`, or a cell already recorded. It creates an isolated HOME and workspace and starts the mock. Then it opens\n    33\tthe TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\n    34\t\n    35\t| # | You do | You judge |\n    36\t|---|---|---|\n    37\t| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n    38\t| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\n    39\t| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n    40\t| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n    41\t| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n    42\t| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\n    43\t| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n    44\t\n    45\tThe script also **measures** two things:\n    46\t- whether `stty` state after each exit equals the state before it;\n    47\t- any process started from the cell's HOME that is still running after exit.\n    48\t\n    49\tA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n    50\t`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\n    51\tresults and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\n    52\tattempt and use a new evidence directory.\n    53\t\n    54\t## Gate\n    55\t\n    56\tThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\n    57\tpopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\n    58\tto an unavailable measurement.\n    59\t\n    60\t```sh\n    61\t# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n    62\t#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\n    63\tnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n    64\t```\n    65\t\n    66\tThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n    67\t- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n    68\t- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n    69\t- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n    70\t- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n    71\t- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n    72\t  `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n    73\t\n    74\tThe record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Commit the evidence directory\n    75\tto the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27069}},"started_at_ms":1793252128127,"completed_at_ms":1793252128127}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:35:29.595Z","ordinal":493404,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18627-fb3b-7f73-be4b-080b4be4dc63","call_id":"call_50727acb48954d82851a2a2d35d3ef20","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 4530)\nTotal output lines: 266\n\ncli/test/agent_terminal_controls.test.ts\ncli/test/ui_terminal_safety.test.ts\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/mockgw.py\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/scope-procs.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh\n   155\tcat <<EOF\n   156\t\n   157\t7  NO_COLOR: the TUI opens again with NO_COLOR=1. Check that it is readable without colour, then quit with Ctrl-C twice.\n   158\tPress Enter to launch.\n   159\tEOF\n   160\tread -r _\n   161\tlaunch no_color NO_COLOR=1\n   162\t\n   163\t# Answers are saved before anything else can fail, so a typo in a screenshot path does not lose them.\n   164\t: > \"$cell_home/checks.tsv\"\n   165\tfor check in 1 2 3 4 5 6 7; do\n   166\t  while true; do\n   167\t    read -r -p \"check $check PASS or FAIL? \" answer\n   168\t    answer=\"${answer^^}\"; [[ \"$answer\" == PASS || \"$answer\" == FAIL ]] && break\n   169\t  done\n   170\t  read -r -p \"check $check note (optional): \" note\n   171\t  printf '%s\\t%s\\t%s\\n' \"$check\" \"$answer\" \"${note//$'\\t'/ }\" >> \"$cell_home/checks.tsv\"\n   172\tdone\n   173\tcp \"$cell_home/checks.tsv\" \"$stem.answers.tsv\"\n   174\tcp \"$cell_home/exits.tsv\" \"$stem.exits.tsv\"\n   175\tcp \"$mock_log\" \"$stem.mock.log\"\n   176\tread -r -p \"operator name: \" operator\n   177\twhile true; do\n   178\t  read -r -p \"approval-panel screenshot path: \" shot_approval\n   179\t  read -r -p \"post-exit screenshot path: \" shot_exit\n   180\t  if [[ \"$shot_approval\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && \"$shot_exit\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && -f \"$shot_approval\" && -f \"$shot_exit\" ]] \\\n   181\t     && ! cmp -s \"$shot_approval\" \"$shot_exit\" \\\n   182\t     && (( $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_approval\") >= attempt_start && $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_exit\") >= attempt_start )); then break; fi\n   183\t  echo \"both screenshots must be .png/.jpg files taken during this attempt, and differ; try again\"\n   184\tdone\n   185\tapproval_copy=\"$stem.approval.${shot_approval##*.}\"\n   186\texit_copy=\"$stem.post-exit.${shot_exit##*.}\"\n   187\tcp \"$shot_approval\" \"$approval_copy\"\n   188\tcp \"$shot_exit\" \"$exit_copy\"\n   189\t\n   190\t# Values reach Python only through the environment, never through generated source.\n   191\tCELL=\"$cell\" ATTEMPT=\"$attempt\" TERMINAL_NAME=\"$terminal\" CELL_SIZE=\"$size\" RC=\"$rc\" NEXUS_VERSION_LINE=\"$version_line\" \\\n   192\tNEXUS_PATH=\"$nexus_real\" PACKAGE_DIR=\"$package\" MANIFEST_SHA=\"$manifest_sha\" TMUX_VERSION=\"$tmux_version\" \\\n   193\tKITTY_PROTOCOL=\"$kitty_protocol\" OPERATOR_NAME=\"$operator\" STEM=\"$stem\" APPROVAL_SHOT=\"$approval_copy\" EXIT_SHOT=\"$exit_copy\" \\\n   194\tpython3 - <<'PY'\n   195\timport hashlib, json, os\n   196\te = os.environ\n   197\tstem = e[\"STEM\"]\n   198\tsha = lambda p: hashlib.sha256(open(p, \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()\n   199\texits = []\n   200\tfor line in open(f\"{stem}.exits.tsv\"):\n   201\t    label, status, restored, survivors, scope_measurement, at = line.rstrip(\"\\n\").split(\"\\t\")\n   202\t    exits.append({\"launch\": label, \"exitStatus\": int(status), \"sttyRestored\": restored == \"true\", \"survivors\": int(survivors), \"scopeMeasurement\": scope_measurement, \"at\": at})\n   203\tchecks = {}\n   204\tfor line in open(f\"{stem}.answers.tsv\"):\n   205\t    check, result, note = (line.rstrip(\"\\n\").split(\"\\t\") + [\"\"])[:3]\n   206\t    checks[check] = {\"result\": result, \"note\": note}\n   207\t# Scenario proof from the mock log: which prompts and tool rounds actually reached the gateway.\n   208\tscenarios = {\"approveToolRounds\": set(), \"stream\": 0, \"sleepTool\": 0}\n   209\tfor line in open(f\"{stem}.mock.log\"):\n   210\t    entry = json.loads(line)\n   211\t    prompt, tools = entry[\"turn\"]\n   212\t    if prompt == \"approve\" and entry[\"kind\"] == \"tools\": scenarios[\"approveToolRounds\"].add(tools)\n   213\t    if prompt == \"stream\" and entry[\"kind\"] == \"stream\": scenarios[\"stream\"] += 1\n   214\t    if prompt == \"sleep\" and entry[\"kind\"] == \"tools\": scenarios[\"sleepTool\"] += 1\n   215\tscenarios[\"approveToolRounds\"] = sorted(scenarios[\"approveToolRounds\"])\n   216\trecord = {\n   217\t    \"acceptance\": \"ACCEPTANCE §5.3\", \"cell\": e[\"CELL\"], \"attempt\": int(e[\"ATTEMPT\"]), \"terminal\": e[\"TERMINAL_NAME\"], \"size\": e[\"CELL_SIZE\"],\n   218\t    \"rc\": e[\"RC\"], \"nexusVersion\": e[\"NEXUS_VERSION_LINE\"], \"nexusPath\": e[\"NEXUS_PATH\"], \"packageDir\": e[\"PACKAGE_DIR\"],\n   219\t    \"packageManifestSha256\": e[\"MANIFEST_SHA\"],\n   220\t    \"env\": {k: e.get(k) for k in [\"TERM\", \"TERM_PROGRAM\", \"TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION\", \"COLORTERM\", \"VTE_VERSION\", \"KITTY_WINDOW_ID\", \"TMUX\", \"XTERM_VERSION\"]},\n   221\t    \"tmux\": e[\"TMUX_VERSION\"] or None, \"kittyKeyboardProtocol\": e[\"KITTY_PROTOCOL\"] or None,\n   222\t    \"measured\": exits, \"scenarios\": scenarios, \"checks\": checks,\n   223\t    \"files\": {name: {\"path\": os.path.basename(path), \"sha256\": sha(path)} for name, path in\n   224\t              [(\"approvalScreenshot\", e[\"APPROVAL_SHOT\"]), (\"postExitScreenshot\", e[\"EXIT_SHOT\"]), (\"mockLog\", f\"{stem}.mock.log\"),\n   225\t               (\"answers\", f\"{stem}.answers.tsv\"), (\"exits\", f\"{stem}.exits.tsv\")]},\n   226\t    \"operator\": e[\"OPERATOR_NAME\"],\n   227\t}\n   228\twith open(f\"{stem}.json\", \"x\") as f:\n   229\t    json.dump(record, f, indent=2)\n   230\tPY\n   231\tsha256sum \"$stem.json\" > \"$stem.json.sha256\"\n   232\trm -f \"$stem.partial\"\n   233\techo \"recorded $stem.json\"\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env node\n     2\t// Gate for the manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3) over the attempt records written by run-cell.sh.\n     3\t//   node scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs <evidence dir> --rc vX.Y.Z-rc.N --manifest-sha256 <hex> \\\n     4\t//     [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n     5\t// --manifest-sha256 is the SHA-256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC release archive, so every cell must have run the\n     6\t// published RC package. The gate fails closed:\n     7\t//   - every terminal × size cell needs a complete, verified attempt (otherwise NOT RUN: ACCEPTANCE §1 rule 5);\n     8\t//   - an attempt is complete only when its self-hash, file hashes, both launch measurements and the mock log's\n     9\t//     scenario proof (approve x2 tool rounds, stream, sleep tool call) all verify;\n    10\t//   - checks 2, 5 and 6 have zero FAIL in ANY attempt; a measured survivor or unrestored terminal turns PASS into FAIL;\n    11\t//   - every other FAIL, in any attempt, needs a written disposition keyed \"<cell>:<check>\";\n    12\t//   - an aborted attempt (a .partial file) needs a written disposition keyed \"<cell>:partial-<n>\".\n    13\t// Hashes prove the files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them: commit the evidence directory.\n    14\timport { createHash } from \"node:crypto\";\n    15\timport fs from \"node:fs\";\n    16\timport path from \"node:path\";\n    17\t\n    18\tconst TERMINALS = [\"xterm\", \"kitty\", \"tmux-gnome\", \"vscode\", \"gnome\"];\n    19\tconst SIZES = [\"80x24\", \"40x14\", \"200x60\"];\n    20\tconst CHECKS = [\"1\", \"2\", \"3\", \"4\", \"5\", \"6\", \"7\"];\n    21\tconst SAFETY = new Set([\"2\", \"5\", \"6\"]);\n    22\tconst arg = (name) => (process.argv.includes(name) ? process.argv[process.argv.indexOf(name) + 1] : null);\n    23\tconst dir = process.argv[2];\n    24\tconst rc = arg(\"--rc\");\n    25\tconst manifestSha = arg(\"--manifest-sha256\");\n    26\tif (!dir || !/^v\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+-rc\\.\\d+$/.test(rc ?? \"\") || !/^[0-9a-f]{64}$/.test(manifestSha ?? \"\")) {\n    27\t  console.error(\"usage: summarize.mjs <evidence dir> --rc vX.Y.Z-rc.N --manifest-sha256 <hex> [--dispositions file]\");\n    28\t  process.exit(2);\n    29\t}\n    30\tconst dispositions = arg(\"--dispositions\") ? JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(arg(\"--dispositions\"), \"utf8\")) : {};\n    31\tconst sha = (file) => createHash(\"sha256\").update(fs.readFileSync(file)).digest(\"hex\");\n    32\t\n    33\t/** Why an attempt record cannot be used, or null. */\n    34\tfunction attemptProblem(file, record, cell) {\n    35\t  const sidecar = `${file}.sha256`;\n    36\t  if (!fs.existsSync(sidecar) || fs.readFileSync(sidecar, \"utf8\").split(/\\s+/)[0] !== sha(file)) return \"record self-hash missing or wrong\";\n    37\t  if (record.cell !== cell) return `record names cell ${record.cell}`;\n    38\t  if (record.rc !…530 tokens truncated…-${cell}.attempt-`) && f.endsWith(\".partial\"));\n    66\t    const aborted = partials.length;\n    67\t    for (const partial of partials) {\n    68\t      const n = /attempt-(\\d+)\\.partial$/.exec(partial)?.[1];\n    69\t      if (!dispositions[`${cell}:partial-${n}`]) problems.push(`${cell}: aborted attempt ${n} without a written disposition`);\n    70\t    }\n    71\t    const attempts = [];\n    72\t    for (const name of files) {\n    73\t      const file = path.join(dir, name);\n    74\t      const record = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\n    75\t      const problem = attemptProblem(file, record, cell);\n    76\t      if (problem) { problems.push(`${cell} ${name}: unusable (${problem})`); continue; }\n    77\t      const results = {};\n    78\t      for (const check of CHECKS) {\n    79\t        let result = record.checks[check].result;\n    80\t        if (check === \"5\" && record.measured.some((m) => m.scopeMeasurement !== \"verified\")) result = \"FAIL (scope measurement unavailable)\";\n    81\t        if (check === \"5\" && record.measured.some((m) => m.survivors > 0)) result = \"FAIL (measured survivors)\";\n    82\t        if (check === \"6\" && record.measured.some((m) => !m.sttyRestored)) result = \"FAIL (terminal not restored)\";\n    83\t        results[check] = result;\n    84\t        if (!result.startsWith(\"FAIL\")) continue;\n    85\t        if (SAFETY.has(check)) problems.push(`${cell} attempt ${record.attempt}: safety check ${check} ${result}`);\n    86\t        else if (!dispositions[`${cell}:${check}`]) problems.push(`${cell} attempt ${record.attempt}: check ${check} FAIL without a written disposition`);\n    87\t      }\n    88\t      attempts.push({ attempt: record.attempt, results });\n    89\t    }\n    90\t    if (!attempts.length) { problems.push(`${cell}: NOT RUN`); rows.push({ cell, status: \"NOT RUN\", attempts: 0, aborted }); continue; }\n    91\t    rows.push({ cell, status: \"RECORDED\", attempts: attempts.length, aborted, latest: attempts[attempts.length - 1] });\n    92\t  }\n    93\t}\n    94\t\n    95\tconsole.log(`| cell | attempts | ${CHECKS.join(\" | \")} |\\n|---|---|${\"---|\".repeat(CHECKS.length)}`);\n    96\tfor (const row of rows) {\n    97\t  const cells = row.status === \"NOT RUN\" ? CHECKS.map(() => \"NOT RUN\") : CHECKS.map((c) => row.latest.results[c]);\n    98\t  console.log(`| ${row.cell} | ${row.attempts}${row.aborted ? ` (+${row.aborted} aborted)` : \"\"} | ${cells.join(\" | \")} |`);\n    99\t}\n   100\tconst verdict = problems.length ? \"FAIL\" : \"PASS\";\n   101\tconsole.log(`\\nREQ-QUAL-108 manual matrix gate for ${rc} (package manifest ${manifestSha.slice(0, 12)}): ${verdict}`);\n   102\tfor (const problem of problems) console.log(`- ${problem}`);\n   103\tfs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"matrix-summary.json\"), `${JSON.stringify({ verdict, rc, packageManifestSha256: manifestSha, rows, problems, dispositions }, null, 2)}\\n`);\n   104\tprocess.exit(problems.length ? 1 : 0);\n     1\t# Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n     2\t\n     3\tA human runs this procedure against the **installed RC**. Automated PTY suites (§5.1, §5.2) do not replace it.\n     4\t\n     5\t**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\n     6\t- xterm\n     7\t- kitty, with the kitty keyboard protocol on\n     8\t- tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal\n     9\t- the VS Code integrated terminal\n    10\t- GNOME Terminal\n    11\t\n    12\t**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition.\n    13\t\n    14\t## Before you start\n    15\t\n    16\t1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\n    17\t   not resolve into a checkout.\n    18\t2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n    19\t3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n    20\t   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n    21\t\n    22\t## Each cell\n    23\t\n    24\tOpen the terminal and resize it to the cell's size. For tmux, start tmux inside GNOME Terminal. For kitty, enable the\n    25\tkeyboard protocol. Then run:\n    26\t\n    27\t```sh\n    28\tscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc <rc> --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> --size <WxH> --out \"$OUT\"\n    29\t```\n    30\t\n    31\tThe script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\n    32\t`tmux-gnome`, or a cell already recorded. It creates an isolated HOME and workspace and starts the mock. Then it opens\n    33\tthe TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\n    34\t\n    35\t| # | You do | You judge |\n    36\t|---|---|---|\n    37\t| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n    38\t| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\n    39\t| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n    40\t| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n    41\t| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n    42\t| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\n    43\t| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n    44\t\n    45\tThe script also **measures** two things:\n    46\t- whether `stty` state after each exit equals the state before it;\n    47\t- any process started from the cell's HOME that is still running after exit.\n    48\t\n    49\tA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n    50\t`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\n    51\tresults and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\n    52\tattempt and use a new evidence directory.\n    53\t\n    54\t## Gate\n    55\t\n    56\tThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\n    57\tpopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\n    58\tto an unavailable measurement.\n    59\t\n    60\t```sh\n    61\t# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n    62\t#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\n    63\tnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n    64\t```\n    65\t\n    66\tThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n    67\t- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n    68\t- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n    69\t- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n    70\t- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n    71\t- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n    72\t  `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n    73\t\n    74\tThe record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Commit the evidence directory\n    75\tto the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5","create_time":1793252129.5952377}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
