{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:36:44.532Z","ordinal":493437,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0db389702a7164cc016ae2db654858819fa794ce19f96ed126","status":"completed","call_id":"call_8d6f9a5b7b024400a6a09dde8a5d98ce","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-screenshot-optional/scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh\\n@@\\n-# The human records PASS/FAIL per check and two screenshots. Every attempt is kept. Usage:\\n+# The human records PASS/FAIL per check. Screenshots are optional under DEC-18; every attempt is kept. Usage:\\n@@\\n-     approve with a deliberate key. Screenshot an approval panel.\\n+     approve with a deliberate key.\\n@@\\n-  6  Quit with Ctrl-C twice. Screenshot the terminal after exit.\\n+  6  Quit with Ctrl-C twice. Confirm the terminal is restored (echo on, no stray escape codes).\\n@@\\n read -r -p \\\"operator name: \\\" operator\\n-while true; do\\n-  read -r -p \\\"approval-panel screenshot path: \\\" shot_approval\\n-  read -r -p \\\"post-exit screenshot path: \\\" shot_exit\\n-  if [[ \\\"$shot_approval\\\" =~ \\\\.(png|jpe?g)$ && \\\"$shot_exit\\\" =~ \\\\.(png|jpe?g)$ && -f \\\"$shot_approval\\\" && -f \\\"$shot_exit\\\" ]] \\\\\\n-     && ! cmp -s \\\"$shot_approval\\\" \\\"$shot_exit\\\" \\\\\\n-     && (( $(stat -c %Y \\\"$shot_approval\\\") >= attempt_start && $(stat -c %Y \\\"$shot_exit\\\") >= attempt_start )); then break; fi\\n-  echo \\\"both screenshots must be .png/.jpg files taken during this attempt, and differ; try again\\\"\\n-done\\n-approval_copy=\\\"$stem.approval.${shot_approval##*.}\\\"\\n-exit_copy=\\\"$stem.post-exit.${shot_exit##*.}\\\"\\n-cp \\\"$shot_approval\\\" \\\"$approval_copy\\\"\\n-cp \\\"$shot_exit\\\" \\\"$exit_copy\\\"\\n+shot_approval=\\\"\\\" shot_exit=\\\"\\\" approval_copy=\\\"\\\" exit_copy=\\\"\\\"\\n+read -r -p \\\"Attach optional approval and post-exit screenshots? (y/N): \\\" screenshot_choice\\n+if [[ \\\"${screenshot_choice,,}\\\" == y || \\\"${screenshot_choice,,}\\\" == yes ]]; then\\n+  while true; do\\n+    read -r -p \\\"approval-panel screenshot path: \\\" shot_approval\\n+    read -r -p \\\"post-exit screenshot path: \\\" shot_exit\\n+    if [[ \\\"$shot_approval\\\" =~ \\\\.(png|jpe?g)$ && \\\"$shot_exit\\\" =~ \\\\.(png|jpe?g)$ && -f \\\"$shot_approval\\\" && -f \\\"$shot_exit\\\" ]] \\\\\\n+       && ! cmp -s \\\"$shot_approval\\\" \\\"$shot_exit\\\" \\\\\\n+       && (( $(stat -c %Y \\\"$shot_approval\\\") >= attempt_start && $(stat -c %Y \\\"$shot_exit\\\") >= attempt_start )); then break; fi\\n+    echo \\\"both optional screenshots must be distinct .png/.jpg files taken during this attempt; try again\\\"\\n+  done\\n+  approval_copy=\\\"$stem.approval.${shot_approval##*.}\\\"\\n+  exit_copy=\\\"$stem.post-exit.${shot_exit##*.}\\\"\\n+  cp \\\"$shot_approval\\\" \\\"$approval_copy\\\"\\n+  cp \\\"$shot_exit\\\" \\\"$exit_copy\\\"\\n+fi\\n@@\\n-KITTY_PROTOCOL=\\\"$kitty_protocol\\\" OPERATOR_NAME=\\\"$operator\\\" STEM=\\\"$stem\\\" APPROVAL_SHOT=\\\"$approval_copy\\\" EXIT_SHOT=\\\"$exit_copy\\\" \\\\\\n+KITTY_PROTOCOL=\\\"$kitty_protocol\\\" OPERATOR_NAME=\\\"$operator\\\" STEM=\\\"$stem\\\" APPROVAL_SHOT=\\\"$approval_copy\\\" EXIT_SHOT=\\\"$exit_copy\\\" \\\\\\n python3 - <<'PY'\\n import hashlib, json, os\\n e = os.environ\\n stem = e[\\\"STEM\\\"]\\n sha = lambda p: hashlib.sha256(open(p, \\\"rb\\\").read()).hexdigest()\\n@@\\n scenarios[\\\"approveToolRounds\\\"] = sorted(scenarios[\\\"approveToolRounds\\\"])\\n+files = {name: {\\\"path\\\": os.path.basename(path), \\\"sha256\\\": sha(path)} for name, path in\\n+         [(\\\"mockLog\\\", f\\\"{stem}.mock.log\\\"), (\\\"answers\\\", f\\\"{stem}.answers.tsv\\\"), (\\\"exits\\\", f\\\"{stem}.exits.tsv\\\")]}\\n+for name, env_name in [(\\\"approvalScreenshot\\\", \\\"APPROVAL_SHOT\\\"), (\\\"postExitScreenshot\\\", \\\"EXIT_SHOT\\\")]:\\n+    if e[env_name]:\\n+        files[name] = {\\\"path\\\": os.path.basename(e[env_name]), \\\"sha256\\\": sha(e[env_name])}\\n record = {\\n@@\\n-    \\\"files\\\": {name: {\\\"path\\\": os.path.basename(path), \\\"sha256\\\": sha(path)} for name, path in\\n-              [(\\\"approvalScreenshot\\\", e[\\\"APPROVAL_SHOT\\\"]), (\\\"postExitScreenshot\\\", e[\\\"EXIT_SHOT\\\"]), (\\\"mockLog\\\", f\\\"{stem}.mock.log\\\"),\\n-               (\\\"answers\\\", f\\\"{stem}.answers.tsv\\\"), (\\\"exits\\\", f\\\"{stem}.exits.tsv\\\")]},\\n+    \\\"files\\\": files,\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5","create_time":1793252197.2838023}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:36:44.570Z","ordinal":493438,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-87619701-308b-4de4-874d-4f9be2a14626","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-screenshot-optional/scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -7,3 +7,3 @@\n #   - the mock's request log, which proves which scenarios ran.\n-# The human records PASS/FAIL per check and two screenshots. Every attempt is kept. Usage:\n+# The human records PASS/FAIL per check. Screenshots are optional under DEC-18; every attempt is kept. Usage:\n #   scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc v1.0.0-rc.N --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> \\\n@@ -145,3 +145,3 @@\n   2  Prompt \"approve\". While each of the two approval panels is open, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then\n-     approve with a deliberate key. Screenshot an approval panel.\n+     approve with a deliberate key.\n   3  Enter a multiline prompt with Shift+Enter (or Alt+Enter).\n@@ -149,3 +149,3 @@\n   5  Prompt \"sleep\" and press Esc while \"sleep 30\" runs.\n-  6  Quit with Ctrl-C twice. Screenshot the terminal after exit.\n+  6  Quit with Ctrl-C twice. Confirm the terminal is restored (echo on, no stray escape codes).\n Press Enter to launch.\n@@ -176,14 +176,18 @@\n read -r -p \"operator name: \" operator\n-while true; do\n-  read -r -p \"approval-panel screenshot path: \" shot_approval\n-  read -r -p \"post-exit screenshot path: \" shot_exit\n-  if [[ \"$shot_approval\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && \"$shot_exit\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && -f \"$shot_approval\" && -f \"$shot_exit\" ]] \\\n-     && ! cmp -s \"$shot_approval\" \"$shot_exit\" \\\n-     && (( $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_approval\") >= attempt_start && $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_exit\") >= attempt_start )); then break; fi\n-  echo \"both screenshots must be .png/.jpg files taken during this attempt, and differ; try again\"\n-done\n-approval_copy=\"$stem.approval.${shot_approval##*.}\"\n-exit_copy=\"$stem.post-exit.${shot_exit##*.}\"\n-cp \"$shot_approval\" \"$approval_copy\"\n-cp \"$shot_exit\" \"$exit_copy\"\n+shot_approval=\"\" shot_exit=\"\" approval_copy=\"\" exit_copy=\"\"\n+read -r -p \"Attach optional approval and post-exit screenshots? (y/N): \" screenshot_choice\n+if [[ \"${screenshot_choice,,}\" == y || \"${screenshot_choice,,}\" == yes ]]; then\n+  while true; do\n+    read -r -p \"approval-panel screenshot path: \" shot_approval\n+    read -r -p \"post-exit screenshot path: \" shot_exit\n+    if [[ \"$shot_approval\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && \"$shot_exit\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && -f \"$shot_approval\" && -f \"$shot_exit\" ]] \\\n+       && ! cmp -s \"$shot_approval\" \"$shot_exit\" \\\n+       && (( $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_approval\") >= attempt_start && $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_exit\") >= attempt_start )); then break; fi\n+    echo \"both optional screenshots must be distinct .png/.jpg files taken during this attempt; try again\"\n+  done\n+  approval_copy=\"$stem.approval.${shot_approval##*.}\"\n+  exit_copy=\"$stem.post-exit.${shot_exit##*.}\"\n+  cp \"$shot_approval\" \"$approval_copy\"\n+  cp \"$shot_exit\" \"$exit_copy\"\n+fi\n \n@@ -215,2 +219,7 @@\n scenarios[\"approveToolRounds\"] = sorted(scenarios[\"approveToolRounds\"])\n+files = {name: {\"path\": os.path.basename(path), \"sha256\": sha(path)} for name, path in\n+         [(\"mockLog\", f\"{stem}.mock.log\"), (\"answers\", f\"{stem}.answers.tsv\"), (\"exits\", f\"{stem}.exits.tsv\")]}\n+for name, env_name in [(\"approvalScreenshot\", \"APPROVAL_SHOT\"), (\"postExitScreenshot\", \"EXIT_SHOT\")]:\n+    if e[env_name]:\n+        files[name] = {\"path\": os.path.basename(e[env_name]), \"sha256\": sha(e[env_name])}\n record = {\n@@ -222,5 +231,3 @@\n     \"measured\": exits, \"scenarios\": scenarios, \"checks\": checks,\n-    \"files\": {name: {\"path\": os.path.basename(path), \"sha256\": sha(path)} for name, path in\n-              [(\"approvalScreenshot\", e[\"APPROVAL_SHOT\"]), (\"postExitScreenshot\", e[\"EXIT_SHOT\"]), (\"mockLog\", f\"{stem}.mock.log\"),\n-               (\"answers\", f\"{stem}.answers.tsv\"), (\"exits\", f\"{stem}.exits.tsv\")]},\n+    \"files\": files,\n     \"operator\": e[\"OPERATOR_NAME\"],\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-screenshot-optional/scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793252204568,"completed_at_ms":1793252204570}}
