,"tool_name":"github.search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.list_pr_changed_filenames"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_pr_diff"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_file"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.rerun_failed_workflow_run_jobs"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch"},{"first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"fetch_topic"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15e3e-2987-7e62-9699-29ab11a9d023","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_issues"},{"first_turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"observation_search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a17ded-e7ae-7300-8479-0fca92a43367","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_user_login"},{"first_turn_id":"01a18105-4b30-7810-8340-21a990975e0a","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"get_observations"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_search"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_field_report"},{"first_turn_id":"01a18508-75af-7cb3-abdc-d10cbdc7b2fb","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"summarize_recent"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5","turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2d8986ee4819fba137441573c5994","order":23130,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a1861e-15e9-76f3-9028-773252d9ea6c","text":"`origin/main` at `6b786d54dd5bf60234c67fec6ef070c62af9b141` already has the requirement in `AGENTS.md`: set `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` before running any `entire` command, with `export ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` as the example.\n\nThe shared checkout’s dirty `AGENTS.md` lacks that section and is 1,548 commits behind. I left it untouched to preserve its existing changes. No repository edit was needed on the authoritative branch.","turn_id":"01a1860e-1ee0-7860-ad63-fe5f780b91f5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2d8ba0414819fa52a0be9b5593e85","order":23131,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1861e-983b-7052-96a0-b4b561144734","text":"I’m resuming the release convergence from current evidence. I’ll refresh the authoritative `origin/main`, open PRs and required checks, then pick the highest-priority unblocked lane without touching the dirty shared checkout.","turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2d8db061c819faed214265e24b9e1","order":23132,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1861f-1a37-7b61-bdd5-8548845f396c","text":"The UTF‑8 regression test is still failing on the expected invalid-input case, and the focused test process has exited. PR #311 is now integrated; I’m carrying the reported decoding regression forward as a separate fix against current `main`, then I’ll verify it alongside the existing I/O-error test.","turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2d96d4118819f8189c7ad82e56b9c","order":23134,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18621-54ce-7bb1-994c-01524e5b34e6","text":"The targeted Rust run now passes both the lossy UTF‑8 regression and the mid-stream I/O-error test (2/2) on current `main`. The suite claim is released; I’m checking the surrounding code contract and then I’ll get an independent review before updating the PR path.","turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2da02b528819fbbb6f3403cb4e4dd","order":23137,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18623-9c93-7b50-8ae8-22ce209cf9c2","text":"The fix is committed on current `main`, independently reviewed `ACCEPT`, and pushed. A PR already exists for that branch (#319), so I’m checking its exact-head CI and using the wait time to refresh the protected-corpus handoff status.","turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2db06a15c819fa8e9d2f4178b1fbf","order":23138,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18627-94ac-7f01-a49f-d87175f08d42","text":"I found a qualification blocker: DEC‑18 waives screenshot artifacts, but the installed terminal-matrix runner still requires two screenshots per cell and its summarizer rejects missing screenshots. That makes the required 15-cell manual gate impossible under the accepted decision. I’m reconciling the runner and its tests to make screenshots optional while keeping every interaction, measurement, verdict, and safety gate mandatory.","turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2dbe92684819faeb56c769255c6d6","order":23139,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1862b-08d9-7143-bd9d-b335fc5caad5","text":"The runner now records the required interaction evidence without screenshots, and the summarizer accepts screenshot-free records while still verifying any optional pair that is supplied. I added a PTY regression fixture that drives the real runner with a synthetic package, plus summary cases for no screenshots and an incomplete optional pair. I’m running that focused fixture now.","turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2dc7d458c819fa184d81d48a54d27","order":23144,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1862d-4b7b-79b1-ac00-e378dc110153","text":"Independent review caught a scope issue: I had applied DEC‑18 to every RC. I’m narrowing the waiver strictly to `v1.0.0-rc.N`; other version series will continue requiring both screenshots. I’m adding regression coverage for both sides of that boundary.","turn_id":"01a1861e-8c1c-7f72-bf3a-94d3dd58f8c5"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":23145,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280