{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:45:52.392Z","ordinal":493873,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18631-7c07-7570-ac29-e70b3cf1a14a","call_id":"call_adae7d43f6bf4dc09ce6cdebf7d89231","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"SUITE claim released\n1119aa8df5b656d3964f7f014118917648ede96516dd208a64da5ebd7e886074  -\n## v1/term-screenshot-optional...origin/main\n M scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\n M scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh\n M scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs\n M scripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 6042)\nTotal output lines: 397\n\ndiff --git a/scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md b/scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\nindex adbfa350..3f66cc7d 100644\n--- a/scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\n+++ b/scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\n@@ -11,12 +11,17 @@ A human runs this procedure against the **installed RC**. Automated PTY suites (\n \n **Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition.\n \n+**Screenshots:** DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only for `v1.0.0-rc.N`. For those candidates, screenshots are\n+optional; every interactive check, measurement, per-cell verdict, observed outcome, exact installed-RC identity, and\n+written disposition remains required. Other release series retain the approval-panel and post-exit screenshot\n+requirement. Automated PTY runs do not replace these manual cells.\n+\n ## Before you start\n \n 1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\n    not resolve into a checkout.\n 2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n-3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n+3. You need `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n    (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n \n ## Each cell\n@@ -35,11 +40,11 @@ the TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through\n | # | You do | You judge |\n |---|---|---|\n | 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n-| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\n+| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides |\n | 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n | 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n | 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n-| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\n+| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes |\n | 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n \n The script also **measures** two things:\n@@ -48,8 +53,8 @@ The script also **measures** two things:\n \n A measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n `cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\n-results and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\n-attempt and use a new evidence directory.\n+results and notes, and the mock request log. If you provide both optional screenshots, their hashes are also recorded.\n+A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed attempt and use a new evidence directory.\n \n ## Gate\n \n@@ -71,5 +76,5 @@ The summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS\n - every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n   `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n \n-The record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Commit the evidence directory\n-to the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\n+The record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Screenshot presence does not\n+change the gate. Commit the evidence directory to the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\ndiff --git a/scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh b/scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh\nindex 361cc785..e4a5f9c2 100755\n--- a/scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh\n+++ b/scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh\n@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@\n #   - terminal state (stty) before and after each exit;\n #   - processes from the cell (by HOME or workspace cwd) that survive an exit, with a planted positive control;\n #   - the mock's request log, which proves which scenarios ran.\n-# The human records PASS/FAIL per check and two screenshots. Every attempt is kept. Usage:\n+# The human records PASS/FAIL per check. Screenshots are optional under DEC-18; every attempt is kept. Usage:\n #   scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc v1.0.0-rc.N --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> \\\n #     --size <80x24|40x14|200x60> --out <evidence dir>\n set -euo pipefail\n@@ -143,11 +143,11 @@ cat <<EOF\n In the TUI that opens next (the first word of each prompt selects the mock scenario):\n   1  It launches and shows the TUI.\n   2  Prompt \"approve\". While each of the two approval panels is open, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then\n-     approve with a deliberate key. Screenshot an approval panel.\n+     approve with a deliberate key.\n   3  Enter a multiline prompt with Shift+Enter (or Alt+Enter).\n   4  Prompt \"stream\" and resize the window while it streams; restore $size afterwards.\n   5  Prompt \"sleep\" and press Esc while \"sleep 30\" runs.\n-  6  Quit with Ctrl-C twice. Screenshot the terminal after exit.\n+  6  Quit with Ctrl-C twice. Confirm the terminal is restored (echo on, no stray escape codes).\n Press Enter to launch.\n EOF\n read -r _\n@@ -174,18 +174,28 @@ cp \"$cell_home/checks.tsv\" \"$stem.answers.tsv\"\n cp \"$cell_home/exits.tsv\" \"$stem.exits.tsv\"\n cp \"$mock_log\" \"$stem.mock.log\"\n read -r -p \"operator name: \" operator\n-while true; do\n-  read -r -p \"approval-panel screenshot path: \" shot_approval\n-  read -r -p \"post-exit screenshot path: \" shot_exit\n-  if [[ \"$shot_approval\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && \"$shot_exit\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && -f \"$shot_approval\" && -f \"$shot_exit\" ]] \\\n-     && ! cmp -s \"$shot_approval\" \"$shot_exit\" \\\n-     && (( $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_approval\") >= attempt_start && $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_exit\") >= attempt_start )); then break; fi\n-  echo \"both screenshots must be .png/.jpg files taken during this attempt, and differ; try again\"\n-done\n-approval_copy=\"$stem.approval.${shot_approval##*.}\"\n-exit_copy=\"$stem.post-exit.${shot_exit##*.}\"\n-cp \"$shot_approval\" \"$approval_copy\"\n-cp \"$shot_exit\" \"$exit_copy\"\n+shot_approval=\"\" shot_exit=\"\" approval_copy=\"\" exit_copy=\"\"\n+if [[ \"$rc\" =~ ^v1\\.0\\.0-rc\\.[0-9]+$ ]]; then\n+  read -r -p \"Attach optional approval and post-exit screenshots? (y/N): \" screenshot_choice\n+  screenshots_requested=\"${screenshot_choice,,}\"\n+else\n+  echo \"Screenshots are required for $rc; DEC-18 applies only to v1.0.0-rc.N.\"\n+  screenshots_requested=\"yes\"\n+fi\n+if [[ \"$screenshots_requested\" == y || \"$screenshots_requested\" == yes ]]; then\n+  while true; do\n+    read -r -p \"approval-panel screenshot path: \" shot_approval\n+    read -r -p \"post-exit screenshot path: \" shot_exit\n+    if [[ \"$shot_approval\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && \"$shot_exit\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && -f \"$shot_approval\" && -f \"$shot_exit\" ]] \\\n+       && ! cmp -s \"$shot_approval\" \"$shot_exit\" \\\n+       && (( $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_approval\") >= attempt_start && $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_exit\") >= attempt_start )); then break; fi\n+    echo \"both optional screenshots must be distinct .png/.jpg files taken during this attempt; try again\"\n+  done\n+  approval_copy=\"$stem.approval.${shot_approval##*.}\"\n+  exit_copy=\"$stem.post-exit.${shot_exit##*.}\"\n+  cp \"$shot_approval\" \"$approval_copy\"\n+  cp…2042 tokens truncated…ames = {\n   mockLog: \"mock.log\",\n   answers: \"answers.tsv\",\n   exits: \"exits.tsv\",\n-}).map(([key, name]) => [key, { path: name, sha256: sha(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dir, name))) }]));\n+};\n+if (contents[\"approval.png\"]) fileNames.approvalScreenshot = \"approval.png\";\n+if (contents[\"post-exit.png\"]) fileNames.postExitScreenshot = \"post-exit.png\";\n+const files = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(fileNames).map(([key, name]) => [key, { path: name, sha256: sha(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dir, name))) }]));\n for (const terminal of [\"xterm\", \"kitty\", \"tmux-gnome\", \"vscode\", \"gnome\"]) {\n   for (const size of [\"80x24\", \"40x14\", \"200x60\"]) {\n     const cell = `${terminal}-${size}`;\n@@ -110,7 +112,7 @@ for (const terminal of [\"xterm\", \"kitty\", \"tmux-gnome\", \"vscode\", \"gnome\"]) {\n     const record = {\n       cell,\n       attempt: 1,\n-      rc: \"v1.0.0-rc.1\",\n+      rc: process.env.RC,\n       packageManifestSha256: \"a\".repeat(64),\n       measured: [measurement(\"main\"), measurement(\"no_color\")],\n       scenarios: { approveToolRounds: [0, 1], stream: 1, sleepTool: 1 },\n@@ -139,4 +141,141 @@ node \"$HERE/summarize.mjs\" \"$tmp/evidence\" --rc v1.0.0-rc.1 --manifest-sha256 \"$\n grep -q 'manual matrix gate for v1.0.0-rc.1 .*: PASS' \"$tmp/verified-summary.log\"\n grep -q '^| xterm-80x24 | 1 | PASS | PASS' \"$tmp/verified-summary.log\"\n \n+# DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts, but a supplied screenshot pair remains hash-checked.\n+write_evidence_fixture no_screenshots\n+node \"$HERE/summarize.mjs\" \"$tmp/evidence\" --rc v1.0.0-rc.1 --manifest-sha256 \"$(printf 'a%.0s' {1..64})\" > \"$tmp/no-screenshots-summary.log\"\n+grep -q 'manual matrix gate for v1.0.0-rc.1 .*: PASS' \"$tmp/no-screenshots-summary.log\"\n+write_evidence_fixture one_screenshot\n+if node \"$HERE/summarize.mjs\" \"$tmp/evidence\" --rc v1.0.0-rc.1 --manifest-sha256 \"$(printf 'a%.0s' {1..64})\" > \"$tmp/one-screenshot-summary.log\" 2>&1; then\n+  echo \"summary gate accepted an incomplete optional screenshot pair\" >&2\n+  exit 1\n+fi\n+grep -q 'optional screenshots must be supplied as a pair' \"$tmp/one-screenshot-summary.log\"\n+write_evidence_fixture no_screenshots v1.0.1-rc.1\n+if node \"$HERE/summarize.mjs\" \"$tmp/evidence\" --rc v1.0.1-rc.1 --manifest-sha256 \"$(printf 'a%.0s' {1..64})\" > \"$tmp/non-v100-no-screenshots.log\" 2>&1; then\n+  echo \"summary gate applied the v1.0.0 screenshot waiver to another release series\" >&2\n+  exit 1\n+fi\n+grep -q 'required screenshots are missing for this release series' \"$tmp/non-v100-no-screenshots.log\"\n+\n+# Drive the actual manual runner in a PTY with a synthetic installed package to prove that\n+# the interactive run can be recorded without prompting for screenshot paths. This is a\n+# tooling regression fixture only and never counts as a manual qualification cell.\n+runner=\"$tmp/runner\"\n+mkdir -p \"$runner/package/bin\" \"$runner/bin\" \"$runner/out\"\n+cat > \"$runner/package/VERSION\" <<'EOF'\n+v1.0.0-rc.1\n+EOF\n+cat > \"$runner/package/bin/nexus\" <<'EOF'\n+#!/usr/bin/env bash\n+package=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\"\n+version=\"$(cat \"$package/VERSION\")\"\n+if [[ \"${1:-}\" == --version ]]; then echo \"Nexus $version\"; exit 0; fi\n+: > \"$HOME/mock.log\"\n+echo 'synthetic terminal runner fixture'\n+EOF\n+chmod +x \"$runner/package/bin/nexus\"\n+(cd \"$runner/package\" && sha256sum VERSION bin/nexus > MANIFEST.sha256)\n+cat > \"$runner/bin/systemd-run\" <<'EOF'\n+#!/usr/bin/env bash\n+set -euo pipefail\n+while [[ $# -gt 0 && \"$1\" != -- ]]; do shift; done\n+[[ $# -gt 0 ]] || exit 2\n+shift\n+exec \"$@\"\n+EOF\n+cat > \"$runner/bin/systemctl\" <<'EOF'\n+#!/usr/bin/env bash\n+set -euo pipefail\n+property=\"\"\n+for arg in \"$@\"; do [[ \"$arg\" == --property=* ]] && property=\"${arg#--property=}\"; done\n+case \"$property\" in\n+  LoadState) echo not-found ;;\n+  ActiveState|ControlGroup) echo \"\" ;;\n+  *) exit 2 ;;\n+esac\n+EOF\n+chmod +x \"$runner/bin/systemd-run\" \"$runner/bin/systemctl\"\n+RUNNER=\"$HERE/run-cell.sh\" FIXTURE=\"$runner\" python3 - <<'PY'\n+import fcntl, glob, hashlib, json, os, pty, select, struct, termios, time, sys\n+fixture = os.environ[\"FIXTURE\"]\n+out = os.path.join(fixture, \"out\")\n+env = os.environ.copy()\n+env.update({\n+    \"HOME\": os.path.join(fixture, \"home\"),\n+    \"TMPDIR\": fixture,\n+    \"PATH\": os.path.join(fixture, \"package\", \"bin\") + os.pathsep + os.path.join(fixture, \"bin\") + os.pathsep + env[\"PATH\"],\n+    \"TERM\": \"xterm\", \"XTERM_VERSION\": \"XTerm fixture\", \"COLUMNS\": \"80\", \"LINES\": \"24\",\n+})\n+os.makedirs(env[\"HOME\"], exist_ok=True)\n+\n+def update_package_version(version):\n+    package = os.path.join(fixture, \"package\")\n+    with open(os.path.join(package, \"VERSION\"), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: f.write(version + \"\\n\")\n+    paths = [\"VERSION\", \"bin/nexus\"]\n+    with open(os.path.join(package, \"MANIFEST.sha256\"), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n+        for relative in paths:\n+            with open(os.path.join(package, relative), \"rb\") as source:\n+                digest = hashlib.sha256(source.read()).hexdigest()\n+            f.write(f\"{digest}  {relative}\\n\")\n+\n+def run_cell(version, screenshot_inputs):\n+    update_package_version(version)\n+    pid, fd = pty.fork()\n+    if pid == 0:\n+        time.sleep(0.1)\n+        os.execve(os.environ[\"RUNNER\"], [os.environ[\"RUNNER\"], \"--rc\", version, \"--terminal\", \"xterm\", \"--size\", \"80x24\", \"--out\", out], env)\n+    fcntl.ioctl(fd, termios.TIOCSWINSZ, struct.pack(\"HHHH\", 24, 80, 0, 0))\n+    payload = \"\\n\\n\" + \"PASS\\n\\n\" * 7 + \"test-operator\\n\" + screenshot_inputs\n+    os.write(fd, payload.encode())\n+    captured = bytearray()\n+    deadline = time.monotonic() + 45\n+    status = None\n+    while time.monotonic() < deadline:\n+        ready, _, _ = select.select([fd], [], [], 0.2)\n+        if ready:\n+            try: captured.extend(os.read(fd, 65536))\n+            except OSError: pass\n+        done, status = os.waitpid(pid, os.WNOHANG)\n+        if done:\n+            while True:\n+                ready, _, _ = select.select([fd], [], [], 0)\n+                if not ready: break\n+                try: captured.extend(os.read(fd, 65536))\n+                except OSError: break\n+            break\n+    if status is None:\n+        os.kill(pid, 9)\n+        os.waitpid(pid, 0)\n+        raise SystemExit(f\"run-cell fixture timed out for {version}\")\n+    text = captured.decode(errors=\"replace\")\n+    if status != 0:\n+        print(text[-6000:], file=sys.stderr)\n+        raise SystemExit(f\"run-cell fixture exited with wait status {status} for {version}\")\n+    return text\n+\n+v100 = run_cell(\"v1.0.0-rc.1\", \"n\\n\")\n+if \"Attach optional approval and post-exit screenshots?\" not in v100:\n+    raise SystemExit(\"v1.0.0 runner did not expose the optional screenshot choice\")\n+if \"approval-panel screenshot path:\" in v100 or \"post-exit screenshot path:\" in v100:\n+    raise SystemExit(\"v1.0.0 runner still required screenshot paths\")\n+for name, body in ((\"approval.png\", b\"approval\"), (\"post-exit.png\", b\"post-exit\")):\n+    path = os.path.join(fixture, name)\n+    with open(path, \"wb\") as f: f.write(body)\n+    future = time.time() + 120\n+    os.utime(path, (future, future))\n+non_v100 = run_cell(\"v1.0.1-rc.1\", os.path.join(fixture, \"approval.png\") + \"\\n\" + os.path.join(fixture, \"post-exit.png\") + \"\\n\")\n+if \"Screenshots are required for v1.0.1-rc.1\" not in non_v100:\n+    raise SystemExit(\"non-v1.0.0 runner did not retain required screenshot behavior\")\n+records = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(out, \"cell-xterm-80x24.attempt-*.json\")))\n+if len(records) != 2:\n+    raise SystemExit(f\"expected two synthetic runner records, found {len(records)}\")\n+v100_record = json.load(open(records[0], encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n+if set(v100_record[\"files\"]) != {\"mockLog\", \"answers\", \"exits\"}:\n+    raise SystemExit(f\"v1.0.0 record unexpectedly requires screenshots: {sorted(v100_record['files'])}\")\n+non_v100_record = json.load(open(records[1], encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n+if not {\"approvalScreenshot\", \"postExitScreenshot\"}.issubset(non_v100_record[\"files\"]):\n+    raise SystemExit(\"non-v1.0.0 record did not retain both required screenshot artifacts\")\n+PY\n+\n echo \"scope measurement fixtures passed\"\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18630-61f0-70c3-bfde-82b542f705db","create_time":1793252752.3919253}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
