stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n498-\n499-## Historical integration update (2026-10-22 21:14 UTC; superseded by the current status above)\n--\n505-PR #149 is open at `1972adb8a6d4b9bacf9974f33974b61d751de8ab` on base `269d611`; Node 20/22/24 matrix checks and CodeQL pass, while its exact-head Linux packaging job is still running. Its independent source review accepted the T3 symlink hardening, but it is not integrated until the required job concludes.\n506-\n507:The public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release remains the only published v1 candidate. `v1.0.0-rc.2` points to older source and is nonqualifying under the Node 22 decision. There is no accepted RC or stable release. Held-out custody, provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC packaging and qualification, five-terminal by three-size human evidence, and independent acceptance remain incomplete. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated.\n508-\n509-## Integration update (2026-10-22 11:50 UTC)\n--\n517-**Requirements and acceptance:** I reran `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` at 09:34 UTC from a clean detached worktree at exact source `44ca13d58a262b5f89be459b47aefa50c2d61683`, with isolated HOME/XDG; it exited 0 and reported 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 11 requirements explicitly mapped to exact-RC qualification in `ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1. The checker output is reproducible from that source revision. This is a source-stage gate only; it does not establish RC qualification or acceptance. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`.\n518-\n519:**Evaluator containment and Git isolation:** Source tests cover CPU, memory, process-count, storage limits, process cleanup, solution-bearing Git refs/reflogs/dangling objects, and external canary stores in `cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts`. PR #140 records a separate exact-source synthetic host preflight with 10/10 checks; its merge and CI do not establish held-out qualification. The public held-out manifest records 40 T2 tasks, ten each across four task classes and four languages; this metadata does not prove private digest re-derivation, author-session independence, effective access controls, custody acceptance, or qualification readiness. No private payloads or validators were accessed for this checkpoint.\n520-\n521:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\n522-\n523-**Runtime floor:** The merged DEC-12 and current `main` specify Node `>=20`; the upstream release schedule lists Node 20 end of life as 2026-04-30. Open PR #143 proposes to correct that date in the RC1 release note; its exact checks passed on the prior base, and it still needs a refresh against current `main`. README, quickstart, and the development guide still contain the old date on `main`; edits to those files are part of the separate Node 22 lane. PR #137 is open and ready for review, implementing its stated owner-directed `>=22` target. It remains based on old base `8935918` and needs a current-main refresh. Its Node 22/24, Linux packaging, and CodeQL checks pass on that prior base, but the required `test-matrix (20)` context is absent and it has no independent review. The proposed source change is not integrated and conflicts with accepted DEC-12 and REQ-REL-111, which still specify `>=20` and a Node 20/22/24 matrix. The active ruleset requires `test-matrix (20)`, which this candidate omits; its checks are on the prior base and no independent review is recorded. Do not treat `>=22` as v1 policy until the policy records and required checks are formally reconciled. No runtime-floor change is made by this checkpoint.\n--\n543-\n544-- **Exact-head CI:** PR #8 targets `main@db1ca55` from `v1/integration@7d6673f`. On current head, `javascript-typescript` runs [39624982585](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39624982585) and [39624995598](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39624995598) passed, as did CodeQL [119308898279](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/119308898279). The required `test-matrix (20)`, `(22)`, and `(24)` jobs in run [39624995762](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39624995762) were still pending at 15:26 UTC. The successful source workflow [39615105190] ran on parent `8f4504e`, so its results are not represented as exact-`7d6673f` results.\n545:- **Requirements gate:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was independently rerun with isolated HOME/XDG on exact `7d6673f` and passed: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. This source-stage gate pass does not satisfy those qualification requirements.\n546-- **Contest:** the contest is over; no contest freeze applies. The contest-contract check has been retired and is not a release gate. Historical contest artifacts remain evidence of past activity only.\n547:- **Qualification and release:** PR #102 contributes synthetic host-preflight evidence only. Private held-out custody/schema compatibility, T2/T3/T4 qualification, live provider and standalone checks, exact-RC reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding. No RC has been constructed, installed, or accepted.\n548-\n549-This update supersedes the 14:56 UTC `8f4504e` checkpoint below for current state. Earlier evidence remains bound to its recorded revisions.\n--\n555-**Acceptance status:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n556-\n557:Exact-source CI and requirements enforcement pass on `8f4504e`, but held-out custody and corpus compatibility, installed-RC qualification, independent RC acceptance, and final publication remain incomplete. No v1.0.0 RC or stable release exists. Publication authorization is granted and remains gated on acceptance.\n558-\n559-This checkpoint reconciles the candidate ledger and acceptance procedure against recorded source and test evidence. It is not a release approval. Historical inspection sections below are preserved as audit evidence and do not represent current branch state where superseded by the 2026-10-21 update.\n--\n562-\n563-- **Authoritative integration and source CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is `8f4504ebd3484149bde39b78934c193752a95bfd`, including the PR #101 restore-safety follow-up. PR #101 exact-head CI run [39604909967](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39604909967) passed Node 20/22/24 and Linux packaging; CodeQL [39604909977](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39604909977) passed. Post-merge PR CI [39610114264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39610114264) passed, but checked out synthetic merge commit `5955b5e` (`8f4504e` merged with `db1ca55`). The separately dispatched source workflow [39615105190](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39615105190) passed all jobs on exact `v1/integration` SHA `8f4504e`; post-merge CodeQL runs [39610114305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39610114305) and [39610102703](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39610102703) passed on that SHA.\n564:- **PR and contest state:** PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-`main` candidate. Its CI and CodeQL checks are green, but it is not a release acceptance or publication. PR #102 is open at `3756afe05dbd75c4e6929d87cd50facbb8ab1748`, based on `8f4504e`, to record a synthetic qualification-host preflight; its CodeQL and TypeScript checks passed and its Node matrix was still running at this checkpoint. The preflight report records 10/10 checks using only an empty synthetic marker store; it does not establish private corpus custody or qualification acceptance. The contest has concluded; no contest freeze applies. Historical contest artifacts remain historical evidence only.\n565:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed on exact source tree `8f4504e` (tree `2a0799c8a32e88e34322b712cf937d73cbe4d637`), with isolated `HOME`/XDG: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven rows remain below the ordinary tested threshold pending their approved exact-RC evidence: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The pre-RC checker pass does not imply those RC gates have passed or authorize an acceptance claim.\n566:- **Evaluator and qualification-host boundary:** Source fixtures for cgroup resource limits, process-tree cleanup, workspace storage, and staged Git-history isolation are in the integration source suite and passed its exact-source CI. A synthetic host preflight at source `8f4504e` recorded 10/10 checks and is being documented in PR #102. Neither source fixtures nor the synthetic-host report establish access separation against the custodian's real store or permit held-out execution before custody acceptance.\n567:- **Held-out corpus and custody:** Public T2 manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` remains the 40-task identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`; T3 public manifest identity remains `85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4bfa0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383`. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no custodian response since 2026-10-21 12:21 UTC. Current evaluator qualification rejects the sealed T2 corpus's legacy `hidden.command` format; the documented path requires a custodian-owned compatible immutable successor and repeated custody checks. Private digest re-derivation, exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective access separation, and current custody acceptance remain unverified here. No payload, validator, reference solution, or hidden answer was accessed, and no held-out run has started.\n568-- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\n569-- **Version, RC, and publication:** Root and CLI package versions remain `0.1.0-alpha.2`. GitHub currently lists only alpha pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`; no `v1.0.0-rc.N` artifact/tag or stable v1.0.0 tag, npm package, or GitHub release exists. Follow the staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md`: pre-RC source gates, RC construction, artifact-bound RC gates, installed-RC qualification and independent G6 acceptance, then stable promotion/publication and post-publication verification.\n--\n579-- **Authoritative integration and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0`, merge commit for PR #45, whose only changed file was `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md`. PR #45 exact-head CI run `39144798481` and CodeQL run `39144798415` passed; independent read-only review accepted exact head `8041c0dbe1a982b2a9e275083f336eb4c5b768b3`. Post-merge CodeQL run `39146982807` passed. Post-merge CI run `39146982849` is in progress on exact `6a16cb6`: Cloudflare and Node 20/22/24 passed; Linux `linux-x86_64` is still executing the CLI suite. This checkpoint does not combine its status with results from another revision.\n580-- **PR and evaluator state:** PRs #9, #13, #15, #16, #44, and #45 are integrated. PR #33 remains open at `0ca77e5ee64f80db02e2b16178c5be551ce5de0c` on stale base `faf95803714a3c543f5c59bc0610ca6291a6184d`. Its exact CI run `39141771002` passed on that old head, but independent review found qualification preflight does not account for host-source mounts created unconditionally by `agentSandboxArgv`. The finding is recorded in comment `6252102243`; a read-only source inventory and shared-mount-plan remediation target are in comment `6252621855`. Owner handoff request `6252543078` has no response as of this checkpoint. The evaluator claim remains protected. Do not execute held-out tasks until this boundary is fixed, exact-head validated, and independently accepted.\n581:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` ran in a detached worktree at exact `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0` with isolated `HOME` and failed as required. It reports 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below threshold: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The exact result is recorded in the claims log and was sent to the ledger owner in PR #17 comment `6252582027`; no ledger status changed.\n582:- **Held-out custody and qualification:** The custodian previously accepted the sealed 40-task manifest identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b` and its private digest/reference validation. This does not establish evaluator acceptance or T2 qualification. The implementing agent has not accessed private payloads. No held-out run has started because evaluator confidentiality preflight remains unaccepted and corpus/evaluator schema compatibility is unresolved.\n583:- **Other qualification and release gates:** Provider/standalone, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, qualification-host validation, and human five-environment × three-size terminal acceptance remain incomplete. Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; no RC artifact/tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on accepted exact-RC evidence.\n584-\n585-The 16:19 UTC `4bce876` checkpoint below remains as historical evidence for that revision.\n--\n589-- **Authoritative integration and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is `4bce8760893b222789b76011a477dd61988ecba6`, merge commit for PR #44. PR #44 was merged from exact head `86b30f54b0fe087befbce8be258ae3bd3ff7cfa2` on base `faf95803714a3c543f5c59bc0610ca6291a6184d`; exact PR CI run `39141379739`, CodeQL run `39141379747`, and the `javascript-typescript` check passed. Independent read-only review accepted the only post-review delta. Post-merge CodeQL run `39144374432` passed on `4bce876`. Post-merge CI run `39144374445` is still running Node 20/22/24; its Cloudflare contract job passed. Exact integration CI on the parent `faf9580` passed as run `39139084949`, but it does not replace checks on `4bce876`.\n590-- **PR state:** PRs #9, #13, #15, #16, and #44 are integrated. PR #9's stale readiness changes were merged earlier and are retained in history. PR #33 remains open at `0ca77e5ee64f80db02e2b16178c5be551ce5de0c`, based on now-stale `faf9580`; its exact CI run `39141771002` passed all five jobs, including 1,243 CLI tests with zero failures, resource enforcement fixtures, staged Git-history/external-store canaries, security gates, deterministic package/SBOM comparison, and installer/package smoke. Independent review found a release-critical gap: preflight does not compare protected corpus paths with the evaluator's unconditional system mounts such as `/usr/local/lib`. The reviewer requested refusal of protected paths beneath every mounted host path and regression coverage. The evaluator claim remains active; no transfer or remediation checkpoint has been reported. Do not run held-out qualification. PR #33 must incorporate `4bce876`, fix this finding, pass exact-head checks, and receive independent re-review.\n591:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` ran from a detached worktree at exact revision `4bce8760893b222789b76011a477dd61988ecba6` with isolated `HOME`; it failed as required. Ledger result: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 11 below threshold: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` remains tested. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its existing ACC-TRUST-04 source evidence is pinned to `2c70d39`, and the current row still needs exact-revision evidence and a DEC-04-aligned disposition before promotion. The ledger owner was given this exact checker output; no ledger status was changed.\n592:- **Evaluator boundary and T2 custody:** PR #33's exact source CI passes resource-bound and Git-history canary fixtures, but the independent unconditional-system-mount finding remains open. Separately, the custodian report accepts the sealed manifest identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`, its custody, author-session provenance, private digest validation, and reference validation; private payloads were not inspected for this checkpoint. The sealed tasks use legacy `hidden: { dir, into, command }` checks, while evaluator qualification requires `blackbox-v1`. Custody acceptance does not resolve this format mismatch or evaluator-boundary acceptance. No T2 qualification has started.\n593-- **Qualification host and terminal:** Qualification-host tooling is integrated through PR #31 (`8c0ab7b`), but this checkpoint has no evidence that the qualification host was provisioned and validated at `4bce876`. Terminal acceptance procedure is integrated; the required human matrix remains unexecuted. It requires five environments × three sizes on the exact installed RC, with per-cell PASS/FAIL and screenshots of the approval panel and post-exit state.\n594-- **Version, RC, and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`. PR #44's deterministic package checks are source CI evidence for that alpha package; they do not establish cross-runner RC reproducibility or installed-RC acceptance. No RC artifact, installed-RC provider/standalone, held-out, T3/T4, cross-runner, human-terminal, or independent acceptance evidence exists. The staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md` remains authoritative. Publication authorization remains granted and gated; no RC tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists.\n--\n598-## Current state update (2026-10-18 10:44 UTC, `5193984`)\n599-\n600:- **Authoritative integration and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is `519398495b7c3a2e5915ed76eee0bb731feb0bcf`. The earlier reported `2c70d39` and `d2c4bfc` are ancestors of this revision; they are not competing integration heads. PR #9 and PR #23 are integrated as `64ee88b` and `886766b`; PR #24's terminal acceptance kit is integrated at `5193984`. Exact-head integration CI run [39120013759](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39120013759) is in progress, so there is no current-head green claim yet. PR #24's checks passed on its exact head `91eaee9` in run [39117464186](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39117464186); its accepted procedure does not replace the human terminal matrix.\n601:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was run from a clean archive of exact `519398495b7c3a2e5915ed76eee0bb731feb0bcf`; it exited 1 as required. The ledger has 121 rows (107 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below-threshold rows: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` is now `tested` with the DEC-17 accuracy exceptions preserved. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its `CTX-001` blocking marker/mapping is under owner reconciliation against DEC-04. No requirement was promoted by this checkpoint.\n602-- **PR #26 evaluator boundary:** PR #26 head `c019575` contains the independently reviewed dedicated-tmpfs preflight and adversarial staged-Git/external-store canary; it is rebased on `886766b`, while integration has since advanced to `5193984`. Exact-head CI run [39119705161](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119705161) is still running its Node 20/22/24 CLI suites at this checkpoint. It must be rebased and requalified on `5193984` before merge. A local synthetic permission probe passed (0711 accepted; 0755 and 0721 rejected); the targeted TypeScript test could not run on this host because no dedicated tmpfs was mounted, and the shared `/dev/shm` correctly failed preflight. That failed local attempt is not counted as a pass.\n603-- **Qualification host:** PR #22 is still based on `a7126aa` (head `7d30494`); its historical exact-head CI passed, but it is not current-base evidence. The owner confirmed the file split with PR #26 and requested owner approval before running `eval/host/provision.sh`. No host account, sudoers, mount unit, or runtime directory has been provisioned. Resource-limit qualification and held-out execution remain blocked until this host boundary is installed and validated.\n604:- **Held-out T2 custody:** The custodian reported re-derived manifest, 40 task, and 40 private-payload digest matches; isolated author-session audits; and 40/40 reference validation. The public manifest identity is `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`. At 10:38:44 UTC the custodian recorded moving the store and quarantine to `root:root` mode `0700` (task/reference subdirectories `0500`) without changing contents or manifest identity, and explicitly accepted sealed-manifest custody under this boundary. Coordinator verification was limited to metadata (`stat`, `namei`, and a denied `ls` as uid `mike`); private payloads were not inspected. This is custody evidence, not T2 qualification: held-out execution remains blocked on host provisioning, frozen resources, and an installed RC.\n605-- **Continuity PR #25:** Latest head is `db44e0b`; exact CI run [39119984308](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119984308) is running. Previous exact head `8907703` failed Node 20/22/24 matrices (run `39118809319`); Node 24 reported 9 behavioral failures among 1,157 tests, including convergence recovery and tester-verifier completion cases. The owner has been given the exact failures; no merge is authorized until the latest head is green and independently reviewed.\n606-- **T3 and terminal lanes:** PR #27 T3 harness head `12edf74` has independent code review ACCEPT. Its CI run [39119197191](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119197191) has the contest-contract and Node 20/22/24 jobs successful; `linux-x86_64` remains in progress. The custodian recorded an 8/8-task T3 corpus seal at 10:43:02 UTC, with corrected private manifest digest `dcbd794ed2998423787fdead4957b38b0c4a8a641855d87304d065d01c3fae37` at 10:43:22 UTC, and released both authoring claims. This is sealed, custodian-validated corpus evidence; no T3 qualification run has occurred. PR