{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:50:47.648Z","ordinal":494128,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18635-fd60-7863-a28a-433ce64f7a9b","call_id":"call_5e37950769194b3993f143adde3f3fba","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 10551)\nTotal output lines: 120\n\n495-**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags are `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor. GitHub currently publishes RC1 as a prerelease; RC2 has a tag but no published release. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. The next candidate needs a fresh RC3 identity after its source/version checks; it must be installed and qualified before acceptance.\n496-\n497:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n498-\n499-## Historical integration update (2026-10-22 21:14 UTC; superseded by the current status above)\n--\n505-PR #149 is open at `1972adb8a6d4b9bacf9974f33974b61d751de8ab` on base `269d611`; Node 20/22/24 matrix checks and CodeQL pass, while its exact-head Linux packaging job is still running. Its independent source review accepted the T3 symlink hardening, but it is not integrated until the required job concludes.\n506-\n507:The public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release remains the only published v1 candidate. `v1.0.0-rc.2` points to older source and is nonqualifying under the Node 22 decision. There is no accepted RC or stable release. Held-out custody, provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC packaging and qualification, five-terminal by three-size human evidence, and independent acceptance remain incomplete. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated.\n508-\n509-## Integration update (2026-10-22 11:50 UTC)\n--\n517-**Requirements and acceptance:** I reran `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` at 09:34 UTC from a clean detached worktree at exact source `44ca13d58a262b5f89be459b47aefa50c2d61683`, with isolated HOME/XDG; it exited 0 and reported 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 11 requirements explicitly mapped to exact-RC qualification in `ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1. The checker output is reproducible from that source revision. This is a source-stage gate only; it does not establish RC qualification or acceptance. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`.\n518-\n519:**Evaluator containment and Git isolation:** Source tests cover CPU, memory, process-count, storage limits, process cleanup, solution-bearing Git refs/reflogs/dangling objects, and external canary stores in `cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts`. PR #140 records a separate exact-source synthetic host preflight with 10/10 checks; its merge and CI do not establish held-out qualification. The public held-out manifest records 40 T2 tasks, ten each across four task classes and four languages; this metadata does not prove private digest re-derivation, author-session independence, effective access controls, custody acceptance, or qualification readiness. No private payloads or validators were accessed for this checkpoint.\n520-\n521:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\n522-\n523-**Runtime floor:** The merged DEC-12 and current `main` specify Node `>=20`; the upstream release schedule lists Node 20 end of life as 2026-04-30. Open PR #143 proposes to correct that date in the RC1 release note; its exact checks passed on the prior base, and it still needs a refresh against current `main`. README, quickstart, and the development guide still contain the old date on `main`; edits to those files are part of the separate Node 22 lane. PR #137 is open and ready for review, implementing its stated owner-directed `>=22` target. It remains based on old base `8935918` and needs a current-main refresh. Its Node 22/24, Linux packaging, and CodeQL checks pass on that prior base, but the required `test-matrix (20)` context is absent and it has no independent review. The proposed source change is not integrated and conflicts with accepted DEC-12 and REQ-REL-111, which still specify `>=20` and a Node 20/22/24 matrix. The active ruleset requires `test-matrix (20)`, which this candidate omits; its checks are on the prior base and no independent review is recorded. Do not treat `>=22` as v1 policy until the policy records and required checks are formally reconciled. No runtime-floor change is made by this checkpoint.\n--\n543-\n544-- **Exact-head CI:** PR #8 targets `main@db1ca55` from `v1/integration@7d6673f`. On current head, `javascript-typescript` runs [39624982585](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39624982585) and [39624995598](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39624995598) passed, as did CodeQL [119308898279](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/119308898279). The required `test-matrix (20)`, `(22)`, and `(24)` jobs in run [39624995762](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39624995762) were still pending at 15:26 UTC. The successful source workflow [39615105190] ran on parent `8f4504e`, so its results are not represented as exact-`7d6673f` results.\n545:- **Requiremen…7351 tokens truncated…all. The remaining lifecycle cases are not complete. Current-source evaluator host preflight passed 10/10 using synthetic markers only; this is not held-out custody or qualification evidence.\n740:- Ubuntu/GNOME is reachable and has all five required terminal applications, but `gh auth status` there reports no GitHub login. The RC5 installer stopped before creating files; the version-scoped desktop install prefix is absent. The manual terminal matrix is **0/15**.\n741-\n742:### Provider, PTY and reproducibility evidence\n743-\n744:- On the exact installed RC5 package, OpenRouter pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` and ChatGPT sign-in model `gpt-6-luna` each passed streamed completion and tool-call/result verification. No workspace content was involved. OpenRouter's required live small engineering task remains pending; the disposable synthetic task has a failing baseline and waits for the operator's folder-trust choice. Nexus remains in its default `review` approval mode; folder trust does not change approvals.\n745-- The installed-package startup PTY smoke reached the Nexus prompt under isolated HOME. This does not satisfy the §5.2 scripted PTY set or the §5.3 human matrix. An attempted legacy §5.2 driver was invalid: its checkout-layout paths and wait condition do not match the current RC startup/trust prompt; its mock gateway recorded zero requests. No product pass/fail was inferred.\n746-- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag, but its official `compare` job **failed**. The comparator's earlier archive and compatibility checks passed; it then found that `metadata.tools` records npm `10.9.9` in the published RC SBOM versus npm `10.9.4` in both rebuild SBOMs. Because it stopped at that mismatch, the later `install.sh` comparison was not reached. A local comparison of only the runner identity artifacts passed but did not establish `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08`; the official result is authoritative. `REQ-REL-114` remains open until the toolchain is aligned, the release/rebuild evidence is regenerated as needed, and a new exact-RC comparison passes.\n--\n750-| Gate | State at RC5 | Next executable step / completion condition |\n751-|---|---|---|\n752:| T2/T3 held-out custody | Blocked. Issue #1 has no custodian reply; the public 40-task manifest does not establish private custody acceptance, and the legacy validator contract is incompatible with the current evaluator. No private payload was accessed or run. | Independent custodian confirms author/handoff, compatible immutable corpus or successor, validation, access separation, digests and custody acceptance; only then prepare and execute the approved runs. |\n753:| Evaluator resource/secret boundary | Synthetic current-source host preflight 10/10; no accepted qualification-host/custody result. | Complete independent host and custody acceptance before any held-out execution. |\n754:| Standalone profiles | Not run on the installed RC; T2 subset dependency remains unmet. | After custody and frozen configuration, execute §4.2 profiles and archive exact-artifact receipts. |\n755-| T4 and long-task T3 | Not run. T4 remains nine fault classes × five runs; T3 remains eight tasks × five runs. | Freeze approved workload/configurations and prerequisites, then run exact RC serially with independent scoring. |\n756-| Scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) | Not established; legacy driver invocation was invalid. | Use an RC-compatible driver or otherwise execute all listed scenarios against the installed package and mock gateway, with measured outcomes. |\n757:| Human terminal matrix (§5.3) | 0/15. No screenshots or per-cell operator verdicts. | Install exact RC on the desktop after GitHub CLI authentication; complete all five terminals × three sizes with two distinct screenshots per cell. |\n758-| Cross-runner `REQ-REL-114` | **Failed** on RC5: run 40195749685 `compare` reports npm-version metadata mismatch (published 10.9.9; both rebuilds 10.9.4). Builder archives match, but the SBOM does not. | Align and pin release/rebuild toolchains; independently review and integrate the fix; create the next correctly versioned RC only after pre-RC gates; rerun exact-artifact cross-runner comparison and retain its generated evidence. |\n759-| Independent RC acceptance | Not performed. | Independent reviewer evaluates the exact candidate and all mandatory evidence after qualification gates pass. |\n--\n769-- **Checkpoint restore PR #302:** The remote PR head remains `934ed912b8e187c5c418709e472a6313bb4169a8`; its exact run [40729450236](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40729450236) failed the Node 22 and Node 24 suites on the tracked-deletion/symlink-parent checkpoint creation case, with Linux skipped. A separate local candidate has been rebased onto `8580c82` at `87b560c7e581fa71cce270474ba40766f372fb04`; the cumulative change is limited to `checkpoint.ts` and its two restore tests. Independent full-diff review and the authorized full-suite owner’s safe-boundary release are pending. The candidate has not been pushed, and no test result is claimed for it.\n770-- **Readiness change review:** PR #300 remains remotely at head `d38341f` against base `145d464`; it has not been refreshed on GitHub. Its previous exact-head checks passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL; its Entire status failed because no separate reviewer approved that trail. The local readiness branch at `51409f5` has merged current `origin/main` `8580c82` and contains the checkpoint update now under review. It requires exact-head required checks before integration. Earlier contents remain historical evidence and must not be read as current source status.\n771:- **Qualification and release:** Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. The installed-RC evidence remains tied to RC10, not this source revision. Held-out custody and evaluator compatibility are unresolved; no protected payload was accessed or run. The manual real-terminal matrix remains 0/15, with two screenshots and human verdicts required per cell. Current exact-RC provider, standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent acceptance are not established. Stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Existing publication authorization remains granted but gated by acceptance.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18630-61f0-70c3-bfde-82b542f705db","create_time":1793253047.6484332}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
