{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T05:52:34.137Z","ordinal":494216,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18630-61f0-70c3-bfde-82b542f705db","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-41ed1107-662a-4899-8320-b58f3fb154d1","process_id":"41433","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git grep -n -i 'connect a provider\\|local endpoint\\|local appliance\\|provider connect' origin/main -- core/src/bin/nexus_tui core/src | head -140; git show --stat --oneline c3d50a1b; git show --format=fuller --no-ext-diff c3d50a1b -- core/src/bin/nexus_tui cli/test/tui_model_picker_e2e.test.ts | head -180;"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-screenshot-optional","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git grep -n -i 'connect a provider\\|local endpoint\\|local appliance\\|provider connect' origin/main -- core/src/bin/nexus_tui core/src | head -140; git show --stat --oneline c3d50a1b; git show --format=fuller --no-ext-diff c3d50a1b -- core/src/bin/nexus_tui cli/test/tui_model_picker_e2e.test.ts | head -180;"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"origin/main:core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs:385:    /// ctrl+p in the picker (or `/connect`): connect a provider.\norigin/main:core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs:4046:        state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Down)); // local endpoint -> ChatGPT\norigin/main:core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs:4062:        assert_eq!(state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Enter)), None, \"appliance opens local endpoint setup\");\norigin/main:core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs:4072:        state.apply(ev(&format!(r#\"{{\"v\":1,\"type\":\"provider.result\",\"id\":\"{request}\",\"provider\":\"appliance\",\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Local endpoint ready (127.0.0.1; 2 models found). Choose a model to finish setup.\"}}\"#)));\norigin/main:core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs:4101:        state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Enter)); // local appliance option\norigin/main:core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs:505:    (\"ctrl+p\", \"in /model: connect a provider (API key or sign-in); /connect opens it directly\"),\norigin/main:core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs:3121:        assert!(screen.contains(\"Connect a provider\"), \"{screen}\");\norigin/main:core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs:3143:// ---------------------------------------------------------------- model picker and provider connection\norigin/main:core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs:3197:        Paragraph::new(key_hints(&[(\"enter\", \"use\"), (\"ctrl+p\", \"connect a provider\"), (\"↑↓\", \"move\"), (\"esc\", \"close\")])),\norigin/main:core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs:3256:    let block = titled_block(\" Connect a provider \".into());\norigin/main:core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs:3367:                None if method == \"local-endpoint\" => lines.push(Line::from(Span::styled(\"Checking the local endpoint and discovering models…\", white))),\norigin/main:core/src/bin/nexus_tui/models.rs:1://! Model picker (`/model`) and provider connection (ctrl+p in the picker). Pure: keys in, intents out; the live\norigin/main:core/src/bin/nexus_tui/models.rs:300:/// Connectable cloud providers and the local appliance endpoint setup entry.\norigin/main:core/src/bin/nexus_tui/protocol.rs:37:/// A way to connect a provider: an API key, a browser sign-in, or a device-code sign-in.\nc3d50a1b feat: configure local endpoint from connect flow\n cli/src/client.ts                    |  10 ++-\n cli/src/config.ts                    |  70 +++++++++++++++++++-\n cli/src/credentials.ts               |  41 ++++++++++++\n cli/src/protocol.ts                  |  11 +++-\n cli/src/provider_cli.ts              |  63 ++++++++++++++++--\n cli/src/provider_connect.ts          | 123 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n cli/src/sidecar.ts                   |  19 +++++-\n cli/test/provider_cli.test.ts        |  50 ++++++++++++++\n cli/test/provider_connect.test.ts    | 101 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs |  47 ++++++++++++-\n core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs  |  40 +++++++++++-\n core/src/bin/nexus_tui/models.rs     |  95 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--\n core/src/bin/nexus_tui/protocol.rs   |   2 +\n 13 files changed, 644 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)\ncommit c3d50a1b12de75f619ea4eae403461e5d7db2c64\nAuthor:     Mike Holownych <mike@holownych.com>\nAuthorDate: Mon Oct 26 13:50:50 2026 +0000\nCommit:     Mike Holownych <mike@holownych.com>\nCommitDate: Mon Oct 26 13:50:50 2026 +0000\n\n    feat: configure local endpoint from connect flow\n\ndiff --git a/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs b/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs\nindex 7354182d..9ae9a354 100644\n--- a/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs\n+++ b/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs\n@@ -611,6 +611,25 @@ impl LiveState {\n                     provider,\n                     method,\n                     key: key.map(Secret),\n+                    endpoint: None,\n+                }))\n+            }\n+            ConnectIntent::LocalEndpoint { endpoint, key } => {\n+                let id = self.next_id('c');\n+                if let Some(Overlay::Connect(flow)) = &mut self.overlay {\n+                    flow.step = Step::Waiting {\n+                        request: id.clone(),\n+                        provider: \"appliance\".into(),\n+                        method: \"local-endpoint\".into(),\n+                        auth: None,\n+                    };\n+                }\n+                Some(Action::Send(Command::ProviderConnect {\n+                    id,\n+                    provider: \"appliance\".into(),\n+                    method: \"local-endpoint\".into(),\n+                    key,\n+                    endpoint: Some(endpoint),\n                 }))\n             }\n             ConnectIntent::Cancel { request } => Some(Action::Send(Command::ProviderCancel { id: request })),\n@@ -3986,14 +4005,15 @@ mod tests {\n         state.apply(catalog(&id));\n         assert_eq!(state.on_key(ctrl('p')), None);\n         assert!(matches!(state.overlay, Some(Overlay::Connect(_))));\n+        state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Down)); // appliance -> chatgpt\n         state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Down)); // chatgpt -> anthropic\n         assert_eq!(state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Enter)), None, \"a single key method opens the key field\");\n         state.on_paste(\"sk-ant-SECRET-1\\n\");\n-        let Some(Action::Send(Command::ProviderConnect { id: request, provider, method, key: Some(secret) })) = state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Enter)) else {\n+        let Some(Action::Send(Command::ProviderConnect { id: request, provider, method, key: Some(secret), .. })) = state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Enter)) else {\n             panic!(\"expected provider.connect\");\n         };\n         assert_eq!((provider.as_str(), method.as_str(), secret.0.as_str()), (\"anthropic\", \"api-key\", \"sk-ant-SECRET-1\"));\n-        assert!(!format!(\"{:?}\", Command::ProviderConnect { id: request.clone(), provider: \"a\".into(), method: \"m\".into(), key: Some(secret) }).contains(\"SECRET\"));\n+        assert!(!format!(\"{:?}\", Command::ProviderConnect { id: request.clone(), provider: \"a\".into(), method: \"m\".into(), key: Some(secret), endpoint: None }).contains(\"SECRET\"));\n         state.apply(ev(&format!(r#\"{{\"v\":1,\"type\":\"provider.result\",\"id\":\"{request}\",\"provider\":\"anthropic\",\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Anthropic connected (3 models available).\"}}\"#)));\n         let outbox = state.take_outbox();\n         assert!(matches!(outbox.as_slice(), [Action::Send(Command::ModelsList { .. })]), \"reopens the picker for the provider\");\n@@ -4007,6 +4027,7 @@ mod tests {\n         let Some(Action::Send(Command::ModelsList { id })) = state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Enter)) else { panic!() };\n         state.apply(catalog(&id));\n         assert!(matches!(state.overlay, Some(Overlay::Connect(_))), \"/connect opens the connect panel once providers are known\");\n+        state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Down)); // local endpoint -> ChatGPT\n         let Some(Action::Send(Command::ProviderConnect { id: request, key: None, .. })) = state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Enter)) else {\n             panic!(\"chatgpt's only method is a sign-in\");\n         };\n@@ -4015,4 +4036,26 @@ mod tests {\n         assert_eq!(state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Esc)), Some(Action::Send(Command::ProviderCancel { id: request })));\n     }\n \n+    #[test]\n+    fn connect_panel_configures_local_endpoint_then_opens_its_model_picker() {\n+        let mut state = ready();\n+        type_text(&mut state, \"/connect\");\n+        let Some(Action::Send(Command::ModelsList { id })) = state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Enter)) else { panic!() };\n+        state.apply(catalog(&id));\n+        assert!(matches!(state.overlay, Some(Overlay::Connect(_))));\n+        assert_eq!(state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Enter)), None, \"appliance opens local endpoint setup\");\n+        state.on_paste(\"http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1\");\n+        state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Enter));\n+        state.on_paste(\"local-secret\");\n+        assert!(!format!(\"{:?}\", state.overlay).contains(\"local-secret\"));\n+        let Some(Action::Send(Command::ProviderConnect { id: request, provider, method, key: Some(secret), endpoint: Some(endpoint) })) = state.on_key(key(KeyCode::Enter)) else {\n+            panic!(\"expected local provider.connect with endpoint and protected key\");\n+        };\n+        assert_eq!((provider.as_str(), method.as_str(), endpoint.as_str(), secret.0.as_str()), (\"appliance\", \"local-endpoint\", \"http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1\", \"local-secret\"));\n+        assert!(!format!(\"{:?}\", Command::ProviderConnect { id: request.clone(), provider, method, key: Some(secret), endpoint: Some(endpoint) }).contains(\"local-secret\"));\n+        state.apply(ev(&format!(r#\"{{\"v\":1,\"type\":\"provider.result\",\"id\":\"{request}\",\"provider\":\"appliance\",\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Local endpoint ready (127.0.0.1; 2 models found). Choose a model to finish setup.\"}}\"#)));\n+        assert!(matches!(&state.overlay, Some(Overlay::Models(p)) if p.only.as_deref() == Some(\"appliance\")));\n+        assert!(matches!(state.take_outbox().as_slice(), [Action::Send(Command::ModelsList { .. })]));\n+    }\n+\n }\ndiff --git a/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs b/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs\nindex 1d1b203a..d150dc38 100644\n--- a/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs\n+++ b/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs\n@@ -3119,9 +3119,16 @@ mod tests {\n         state.on_key(KeyEvent::new(KeyCode::Char('p'), KeyModifiers::CONTROL));\n         let screen = draw(&state, 100, 24);\n         assert!(screen.contains(\"Connect a provider\"), \"{screen}\");\n+        assert!(screen.contains(\"Appliance\"), \"the connect menu exposes local setup: {screen}\");\n         assert!(screen.contains(\"connected via Codex CLI\"), \"{screen}\");\n         assert!(screen.contains(\"unofficial sign-in\"), \"{screen}\");\n-        state.on_key(KeyEvent::new(KeyCode::Down, KeyModifiers::NONE));\n+        state.on_key(KeyEvent::new(KeyCode::Enter, KeyModifiers::NONE));\n+        let screen = draw(&state, 100, 24);\n+        assert!(screen.contains(\"Local OpenAI-compatible endpoint\"), \"{screen}\");\n+        assert!(screen.contains(\"http://localhost:1234/v1\"), \"{screen}\");\n+        state.on_key(KeyEvent::new(KeyCode::Esc, KeyModifiers::NONE));\n+        state.on_key(KeyEvent::new(KeyCode::Down, KeyModifiers::NONE)); // appliance -> ChatGPT\n+        state.on_key(KeyEvent::new(KeyCode::Down, KeyModifiers::NONE)); // ChatGPT -> Anthropic\n         state.on_key(KeyEvent::new(KeyCode::Enter, KeyModifiers::NONE));\n         state.on_paste(\"sk-ant-VISIBLE-NEVER\");\n         let screen = draw(&state, 100, 24);\n@@ -3325,8 +3332,39 @@ fn render_connect(frame: &mut Frame, area: Rect, flow: &Connect) {\n             )));\n             &[(\"enter\", \"verify and save\"), (\"ctrl+u\", \"clear\"), (\"esc\", \"back\")]\n         }\n+        Step::LocalEndpoint { input, error } => {\n+            lines.push(Line::from(Span::styled(\"Local OpenAI-compatible endpoint\", white.add_modifier(Modifier::BOLD))));\n+            lines.push(Line::default());\n+            lines.push(Line::from(Span::styled(\"Enter the base URL, including its API path when required.\", muted)));\n+            lines.push(Line::default());\n+            lines.push(Line::from(vec![\n+                Span::styled(\"› \", Style::default().fg(ACCENT).add_modifier(Modifier::BOLD)),\n+                Span::styled(format!(\"{}▏\", input), white),\n+            ]));\n+            focus = lines.len() - 1;\n+            if let Some(error) = error { lines.push(Line::from(Span::styled(error.clone(), Style::default().fg(Color::Red)))); }\n+            lines.push(Line::default());\n+            lines.push(Line::from(Span::styled(\"Example: http://localhost:1234/v1\", muted)));\n+            &[(\"enter\", \"continue\"), (\"paste\", \"endpoint URL\"), (\"esc\", \"back\")]\n+        }\n+        Step::LocalKey { input, error, .. } => {\n+            lines.push(Line::from(Span::styled(\"Optional endpoint API key\", white.add_modifier(Modifier::BOLD))));\n+            lines.push(Line::default());\n+            let dots = \"•\".repeat(input.0.chars().count().min(48));\n+            lines.push(Line::from(vec![\n+                Span::styled(\"› \", Style::default().fg(ACCENT).add_modifier(Modifier::BOLD)),\n+                Span::styled(format!(\"{dots}▏\"), white),\n+                Span::styled(if input.0.is_empty() { String::new() } else { format!(\"  {} characters\", input.0.chars().count()) }, muted),\n+            ]));\n+            focus = lines.len() - 1;\n+            if let Some(error) = error { lines.push(Line::from(Span::styled(error.clone(), Style::default().fg(Color::Red)))); }\n+            lines.push(Line::default());\n+            lines.push(Line::from(Span::styled(\"Nexus checks the endpoint, stores the 