ate.mjs` cannot detect distro backports, so it also rejects older vendor-patched builds. Ubuntu 24.04 `0.9.0-1ubuntu0.3` removed the fix. Install a release with the fix before qualification; `scripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh` shows the pinned source build that CI uses. `provision.sh` does not replace the binary.\neval/host/README.md-20-- `provision.sh` applies these changes and is idempotent. It never remounts an active tmpfs.\neval/host/README.md:21:- `rollback.sh` removes them. It keeps `/opt/nexus-qual` unless you pass `--purge-runtime`, and it leaves `acl` installed.\neval/host/README.md-22-- `validate.mjs`, run as the operator, proves the result using infrastructure fixtures only.\neval/host/README.md-23-\neval/host/README.md-24-```sh\n--\neval/host/rollback.sh-3-# Removes only resources that the ledger names AND that still verifiably belong to this procedure: the account only if\neval/host/rollback.sh-4-# its uid and home match what was recorded, files only if they carry the procedure's marker, and only the exact paths\neval/host/rollback.sh-5-# provision.sh computes. Anything else (pre-existing, re-created by someone else, or a tampered ledger entry) is left.\neval/host/rollback.sh:6:# /opt/nexus-qual (installed RC and peer agents) is kept unless --purge-runtime is given. A package provision installed\neval/host/rollback.sh-7-# (acl) is left installed. Run outputs elsewhere are kept.\neval/host/rollback.sh-8-set -euo pipefail\neval/host/rollback.sh-9-\n--\neval/host/rollback.sh-12-readonly ACCOUNT=nexus-eval\neval/host/rollback.sh-13-readonly ACCOUNT_HOME=/var/lib/nexus-eval\neval/host/rollback.sh-14-readonly SUDOERS=/etc/sudoers.d/99-nexus-eval\neval/host/rollback.sh:15:readonly RUNTIME=/opt/nexus-qual\neval/host/rollback.sh-16-readonly LEDGER_DIR=/var/lib/nexus-qual-host\neval/host/rollback.sh-17-readonly LEDGER=\"$LEDGER_DIR/ledger\"\neval/host/rollback.sh-18-readonly MARKER=\"# Managed by nexus-code eval/host/provision.sh\"\n--\neval/host/provision.sh-2-# Provision the qualification host (eval/host/README.md). Run as root on the qualification host only:\neval/host/provision.sh-3-#   sudo OPERATOR=<harness user> bash eval/host/provision.sh\neval/host/provision.sh-4-# Idempotent. Touches only: the acl package, the nexus-eval system account and its home, one sudoers drop-in, one\neval/host/provision.sh:5:# systemd mount unit for the tmpfs workspace root (and the root's parent directory if absent), and /opt/nexus-qual.\neval/host/provision.sh-6-# Fail-closed on collisions: a pre-existing account, sudoers file, unit, runtime directory or mount that this procedure\neval/host/provision.sh-7-# did not create stops the run unchanged. Every creation is first recorded as `pending <kind> <value>` in a root-only\neval/host/provision.sh-8-# ledger and then confirmed, so an interrupted run can be resumed or rolled back; rollback.sh removes only resources the\n--\neval/host/provision.sh-16-readonly ACCOUNT_HOME=/var/lib/nexus-eval\neval/host/provision.sh-17-readonly SUDOERS=/etc/sudoers.d/99-nexus-eval\neval/host/provision.sh-18-readonly LEGACY_SUDOERS=/etc/sudoers.d/90-nexus-eval\neval/host/provision.sh:19:readonly RUNTIME=/opt/nexus-qual\neval/host/provision.sh-20-readonly LEDGER_DIR=/var/lib/nexus-qual-host\neval/host/provision.sh-21-readonly LEDGER=\"$LEDGER_DIR/ledger\"\neval/host/provision.sh-22-readonly MARKER=\"# Managed by nexus-code eval/host/provision.sh\"\n--\neval/host/container-test/run.sh-20-# 2 rollback\neval/host/container-test/run.sh-21-$R >/tmp/o 2>&1 && ok \"2a rollback\" || { bad \"2a\"; cat /tmp/o; }\neval/host/container-test/run.sh-22-[[ ! -e /etc/sudoers.d/99-nexus-eval && -z \"$(ls /etc/systemd/system/*.mount 2>/dev/null)\" ]] && ! id nexus-eval >/dev/null 2>&1 && ! findmnt --mountpoint /srv/nexus-qual/ws >/dev/null && ok \"2b all removed\" || { bad \"2b\"; state; }\neval/host/container-test/run.sh:23:[[ -d /opt/nexus-qual ]] && ok \"2c runtime kept without --purge-runtime\" || bad \"2c\"\neval/host/containe