tests, Linux tests, packaging, reproducibility, SBOM, and installer checks. The requirements gate also passed on exact current main `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4` in an isolated worktree (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 applicable release-qualification rows remain deferred to their documented exact-RC stages). PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) is being updated to this exact main revision. Source checks do not establish installed-RC acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:83:**Lifecycle, scheduler, and evaluation evidence:** `cli/test/convergence_integration.test.ts` covers end-to-end scheduling and execution scenarios. `cli/test/convergence_scheduler_properties.test.ts` runs generated DAG invariants over 100 fixed seeds; this is reproducible generated coverage, not a claim that every scheduler property or arbitrary graph has been proven. PR #297’s regression tests for the TDD diagnostic paths are merged and its required CI passed. The `eval/` pilot suite does not satisfy held-out acceptance: the independent 40-task corpus, custody acceptance, and exact-RC qualification remain required and open.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:87:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Held-out T2/T3/T4, remaining live-provider and standalone gates, successor-RC artifact qualification, cross-runner evidence, the 15-cell human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on these mandatory checks.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:93:**Authoritative source and source checks:** `main` is now `d3b7af3ca3d216841f8ff8a0e7b4cefbd637ef9f`, the merge commit for PR [#285](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/285) (merged 2026-10-28 03:38:26 UTC). The exact PR-head Linux retry and required CI passed before merge. Post-merge CI [40627840511](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40627840511) is running the Node 22/24 matrix; CodeQL [40627840517](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40627840517) passed. This is source validation, not installed-RC acceptance. The prior main CI [40621815585](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40621815585) passed on `59f07c4` and does not establish post-merge `d3b7af3` status.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:97:**RC10 E2 archive repair:** PR #288 restored the 21 retained log files whose entries were already present in the archive manifest, corrected the evidence README's attestation and lifecycle disclosures, and updated `SHA256SUMS`. On the merged candidate, all 45 manifest entries passed `sha256sum -c`; Gitleaks found no leaks; the exact diff received independent ACCEPT. This review accepted the archive repair and factual README corrections only. It did not accept the RC10 E2 product qualification or turn the historical logs into new test results.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:99:**RC10 E2 limits:** The archive still does not demonstrate a successful ordinary `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 to RC10, successful provenance-attestation verification, power-loss recovery, or an explicit staging-directory-cleanup assertion. The recorded updater process-death recovery is not a power-loss test. E2 acceptance remains open.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:101:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease, built from immutable source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and was last updated 2026-10-27 18:47 UTC; no custodian acceptance or compatible sealed held-out corpus is recorded, and no held-out payload has been accessed. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining live provider and standalone gates, qualification of a candidate built from current source, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15 formally recorded cell verdicts**, with no screenshots. The operator reports successful rendering at tested sizes but a 43×13 lower limit for tmux inside GNOME Terminal; this is partial observation, not completion of the prescribed matrix. The available `mike-dev` shell is headless, and its configured `ubuntu-desktop` host name does not resolve, so I could not produce real-terminal screenshots or verdicts from this session. Stable publication remains gated on every required acceptance gate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:107:**Authoritative source and source checks:** `main` is `1bc63ef471e0fedb3ad4e980cc12e9c303382c69`, the merge commit for PR [#288](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/288). PR #288's exact-head CI [40604512023](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40604512023) passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux packaging/reproducibility/smoke; CodeQL [40604512234](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40604512234) and JavaScript/TypeScript also passed. The exact PR jobs passed `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs`. Post-merge CI [40608989828](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40608989828) is still running Node 22 and Node 24 on `1bc63ef`; post-merge CodeQL [40608989717](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40608989717) passed. The earlier run on base `171fca4` had one Node 22 failure in `tui_diff_e2e` (review navigation expected edit 1, observed edit 3); Node 24 passed there, and the exact PR #288 candidate passed all three test matrices. The exact post-merge CI run is the next source-level confirmation. These source checks are not installed-RC acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:109:**RC10 E2 archive repair:** PR #288 restored the 21 retained log files whose entries were already present in the archive manifest, corrected the evidence README's attestation and lifecycle disclosures, and updated `SHA256SUMS`. On the merged candidate, all 45 manifest entries passed `sha256sum -c`; Gitleaks found no leaks; the exact diff received independent ACCEPT. This review accepted the archive repair and factual README corrections only. It did not accept the RC10 E2 product qualification or turn the historical logs into new test results.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:111:**RC10 E2 limits:** The archive still does not demonstrate a successful ordinary `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 to RC10, successful provenance-attestation verification, power-loss recovery, or an explicit staging-directory-cleanup assertion. The recorded updater process-death recovery is not a power-loss test. E2 acceptance remains open.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:115:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest release and is still a prerelease; its immutable source is `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`. No stable `v1.0.0` exists. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without an independent custodian acceptance or a compatible sealed held-out corpus; no held-out payload has been accessed. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining live provider and standalone gates, qualification of a candidate built from current source, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The required five-terminal by three-size matrix has **0/15 formally recorded cell verdicts** and no screenshots. The operator reports that the client rendered at the sizes tried, but tmux inside GNOME Terminal could not be reduced below 43×13; this does not establish every prescribed interaction or matrix cell. Stable publication remains gated on all required acceptance gates.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:121:**Authoritative source and checks:** `origin/main` is `7ddce16a900d2da9def27d53722243bf4df2de07`, merging PR #284 atop PR #283 and earlier RC10 fixes. Post-merge CI [40593091251](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40593091251) completed successfully on this exact SHA: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux packaging/reproducibility/smoke jobs passed. CodeQL [40593091302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40593091302) also passed. On the refreshed readiness worktree, requirements enforcement passed (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification), and version synchronization confirms every component remains `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source checks, not installed-RC acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:123:**RC10 reproducibility scope:** PR [#281](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/281) recorded the successful exact-tag run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805); PR [#282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/282) clarified that the comparison established byte identity for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against the published RC10. It does not claim byte identity for every build output. This evidence is bound to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; any successor source needs its own exact-tag reproducibility run.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:125:**RC10 E2 evidence:** PR [#283](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/283) reports 20/20 fresh-install, doctor and Node-preflight cells: eight positive cells across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12 and Fedora 40 with Node 22/24, plus twelve negative preflight cells for absent Node or Node 12/20. However, independent review of merged head `71a4218` returned CHANGES_REQUIRED, and I confirmed the evidence archive is incomplete: 21 of 34 `SHA256SUMS` entries are missing, including all listed per-cell logs; `prepared-images.json` contains cell/image/id but not the distro and Node metadata claimed by the README; and the positive-cell script sets `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` without documenting that limitation