ng reproduction; they are not verified defects or RC acceptance evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:254:**Disposition:** Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; RC10 is unaccepted and stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Existing publication authorization remains granted but gated on all mandatory qualification and independent acceptance. The user-selected distribution target is the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:256:The earlier checkpoint immediately below is retained as historical evidence and is superseded by this current source, PR, RC and acceptance status.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:265:**RC9 installed accessibility result and source fix:** Published tag `v1.0.0-rc.9` still points to source `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`; its archive SHA-256 is `35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb`. PR [#260](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/260) merged the exact installed-RC PTY evidence as `9def2658e9269f6468ff7c5562839999cc7352a8`; captures and verifier are in [the RC9 accessibility evidence](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/accessibility/README.md). On installed RC9, `NO_COLOR=1` under xterm at 40x14 and 100x30 emitted no color SGR codes (2/2 subcases passed); `TERM=dumb` with `NO_COLOR` unset emitted reset SGR `39m`, `49m`, and `59m` at both sizes (2/2 subcases failed). The complete all-state accessibility gate remains partial. PR [#261](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/261) now disables Crossterm color output when the TUI resolves `Depth::Mono` and adds a real-backend regression test. This fix is on `main`, not in the immutable RC9 artifact; RC9 remains failed for the `TERM=dumb` subcase. A new immutable RC and affected-gate requalification are required before any stable release.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:267:**RC9 artifact and installation record:** Tag object `d211d1c7545d2dd629531e4f712e98a240a782c6` targets the source above. Local `git