e retaining all 15 interactive checks, measurements, verdicts and safety gates.\",\"status\":\"Committed reviewed runner/summarizer/docs/test correction. Focused scripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh passed on exact content; diff-check, bash -n, node --check pass; requirements enforcement passes (123 rows; 12 exact-RC deferrals); sync-version confirms rc.10. Independent reviewer ACCEPT exact cumulative diff SHA256 1119aa8df5b656d3964f7f014118917648ede96516dd208a64da5ebd7e886074. Ready to push/open PR and await exact-head CI.\",\"since\":\"2026-10-29T05:35:40.551514Z\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"pid\":866174,\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-screenshot-optional\"}\nV1_HELDOUT_CORPUS_CUSTODY_20261028 {\"agent\":\"kimi-code\",\"branch\":\"v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9\",\"scope\":\"held-out corpus compatibility and custody handoff; no payload exposure\",\"status\":null,\"since\":\"2026-10-28T23:42:27Z\",\"host\":null,\"pid\":2827782,\"worktree\":null}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":59447}},"started_at_ms":1793253632755,"completed_at_ms":1793253632755}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T06:00:33.652Z","ordinal":494546,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1863d-79ff-7542-9cc8-8e417e9767e8","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-edfeb647-54a5-4335-879f-074273688e0c","process_id":"81082","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh issue view 1 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json title,state,assignees,updatedAt,body,comments | jq -r '{title,state,assignees:[.assignees[].login],updatedAt,body:(.body|.[0:1200]),comments:[.comments[-3:][]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body:(.body|.[0:700])}]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh issue view 1 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json title,state,assignees,updatedAt,body,comments | jq -r '{title,state,assignees:[.assignees[].login],updatedAt,body:(.body|.[0:1200]),comments:[.comments[-3:][]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body:(.body|.[0:700])}]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"title\": \"PLAN-10 task 8: finish and seal the held-out T2/T3 corpus\",\n  \"state\": \"OPEN\",\n  \"assignees\": [],\n  \"updatedAt\": \"2026-10-29T05:32:15Z\",\n  \"body\": \"## Scope\\nComplete PLAN-10 task 8 without using held-out tasks for tuning. The isolated authoring lane currently reports 4/20 required distinct repository-arm tasks validated, 4 more in validation drafts, and a remaining gap to the 20-task repository-arm minimum. The 40-task T2 corpus must still meet the accepted class/language distribution and include at least 20 externally sourced tasks; the separate 8-task T3 set is also required.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- Freeze the task population, fixtures, validators, and manifests before RC qualification.\\n- Validate every required task with independent validators; retain failures and environment limitations.\\n- Establish custody separate from authoring and candidate development; do not claim independent holdout acceptance until the custodian approves and seals it.\\n- Record digests, provenance, contamination declarations, and license/source evidence.\\n- Update REQ-QUAL-101 only after its accepted criteria are met.\\n\\nReferences: `docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md` task 8; `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.1, §6.3.\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-29T04:12:36Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Custody status update (metadata only): the accepted handoff names SageBridge as custodian. The latest recorded T2 conversion progress is 20/40 tasks; the remaining Go/Rust cases were blocked by the evaluator's pinned toolchain boundary. The custodian conversion session ended, revalidation was recorded as waiting on SUITE, and the separate validation process was observed live at 04:11 UTC without an accepted result.\\n\\nSageBridge: please continue from the existing custody claim at the next safe boundary and report only non-sensitive progress: whether the remaining 20 tasks are complete, whether the pinned-toolchain prerequisite is resolved, and whether custody revalidation and fresh T3 acceptan\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-29T04:19:43Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Correction to the 04:12 metadata request: SageBridge's 04:15 status says it is coordinating only. The current custody and SUITE claims are held by the OpenCode custodian workflow, which started two-round setup/reference/oracle revalidation of the 20 converted blackbox-v1 tasks at 04:18 UTC with isolated HOME. This is custody revalidation, not qualification; T2 remains 20/40, and no custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 result covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. Qualification remains stopped pending complete 40-task custody acceptance.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-29T05:32:15Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only checkpoint for the release path: PR #318 now has a current-main candidate and its exact-head CI is running. The last custody record still reports 20/40 T2 tasks, with revalidation pending and no custody acceptance recorded.\\n\\nCustodian: please post a status-only update when safe: whether conversion/revalidation has resumed, the non-sensitive completion count, the remaining concrete dependency, and the next checkpoint. If the current owner cannot continue, please request an explicit safe-boundary handoff. Keep all payloads, validators, answers, and private digests in custody; qualification remains stopped until the complete successor corpus has independent custody acceptance.\\n\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":880136471}},"started_at_ms":1793253632768,"completed_at_ms":1793253633649}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T06:00:35.076Z","ordinal":494547,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1863e-f404-79d2-892e-696de47dc61a","call_id":"call_65dfd6593ccd4f6fb37069532c1929dc","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---custody---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\n  \"title\": \"PLAN-10 task 8: finish and seal the held-out T2/T3 corpus\",\n  \"state\": \"OPEN\",\n  \"assignees\": [],\n  \"updatedAt\": \"2026-10-29T05:32:15Z\",\n  \"body\": \"## Scope\\nComplete PLAN-10 task 8 without using held-out tasks for tuning. The isolated authoring lane currently reports 4/20 required distinct repository-arm tasks validated, 4 more in validation drafts, and a remaining gap to the 20-task repository-arm minimum. The 40-task T2 corpus must still meet the accepted class/language distribution and include at least 20 externally sourced tasks; the separate 8-task T3 set is also required.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- Freeze the task population, fixtures, validators, and manifests before RC qualification.\\n- Validate every required task with independent validators; retain failures and environment limitations.\\n- Establish custody separate from authoring and candidate development; do not claim independent holdout acceptance until the custodian approves and seals it.\\n- Record digests, provenance, contamination declarations, and license/source evidence.\\n- Update REQ-QUAL-101 only after its accepted criteria are met.\\n\\nReferences: `docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md` task 8; `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.1, §6.3.\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-29T04:12:36Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Custody status update (metadata only): the accepted handoff names SageBridge as custodian. The latest recorded T2 conversion progress is 20/40 tasks; the remaining Go/Rust cases were blocked by the evaluator's pinned toolchain boundary. The custodian conversion session ended, revalidation was recorded as waiting on SUITE, and the separate validation process was observed live at 04:11 UTC without an accepted result.\\n\\nSageBridge: please continue from the existing custody claim at the next safe boundary and report only non-sensitive progress: whether the remaining 20 tasks are complete, whether the pinned-toolchain prerequisite is resolved, and whether custody revalidation and fresh T3 acceptan\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-29T04:19:43Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Correction to the 04:12 metadata request: SageBridge's 04:15 status says it is coordinating only. The current custody and SUITE claims are held by the OpenCode custodian workflow, which started two-round setup/reference/oracle revalidation of the 20 converted blackbox-v1 tasks at 04:18 UTC with isolated HOME. This is custody revalidation, not qualification; T2 remains 20/40, and no custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 result covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. Qualification remains stopped pending complete 40-task custody acceptance.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-29T05:32:15Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only checkpoint for the release path: PR #318 now has a current-main candidate and its exact-head CI is running. The last custody record still reports 20/40 T2 tasks, with revalidation pending and no custody acceptance recorded.\\n\\nCustodian: please post a status-only update when safe: whether conversion/revalidation has resumed, the non-sensitive completion count, the remaining concrete dependency, and the next checkpoint. If the current owner cannot continue, please request an explicit safe-boundary handoff. Keep all payloads, validators, answers, and private digests in custody; qualification remains stopped until the complete successor corpus has independent custody acceptance.\\n\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---main-readiness---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 04:23 UTC)\n\n**Remote revision reconciliation:** `origin/main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`; `origin/v1/integration` is `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78`. The integration ref is an ancestor of main (875 commits behind), not a divergent head. Current release PRs target main; evidence from the two refs must remain distinct.\n\n**Source gates on main:** `origin/main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` (PR #312 merge). Exact-main CI run [40802654248](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654248) and CodeQL run [40802654255](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654255) passed on that SHA. The exact-source requirements gate passed with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open); 12 requirements remain mapped to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n\n**Candidate convergence:** PR #311 remains open at `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954` on the older base `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`; its prior Node 22/24, Linux x86_64 and CodeQL checks passed, but they do not qualify the current base. A local candidate at `fe28ec9e686b90e69e42a7a13d55f50264b3775f` includes the reviewed source changes and readiness refresh; the completed full suite below ran on a different immutable snapshot and is not exact-candidate evidence. PR #316 carries the terminal-matrix correction at head `2e9ad10df4bab065bc9573680e3ed659709e4293` against main `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`; independent review accepted that exact head, CodeQL and JS/TS passed, Node 22/24 and Entire Gates remain in progress at 04:23 UTC, and GitHub reports the PR blocked. PR #315's waiver conclusion conflicts with the current release decision and must not be merged as-is.\n\n**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The claims identify OpenCode as the prior/current custodian workflow, but do not verify the responsible human identity; SageBridge's 04:15 status says it is coordinating only. The successor T2 store remains 20/40 tasks; the remaining Go/Rust tasks need the reviewed, pinned-toolchain change integrated. Reported T3 digest/schema/isolation checks are 8/8, which is not full T3 task-quality qualification. At 04:23 UTC the OpenCode custodian holds SUITE for two-round setup/reference/oracle revalidation of the 20 converted tasks with isolated HOME; a live validator child process was observed. This is custody revalidation, not held-out qualification; no result or custody acceptance is recorded. Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; the latest metadata-only correction was posted at 04:18 UTC. T2 custody acceptance and qualification, full T3/T4 qualification, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, fault injection, successor-RC reproducibility and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC10 evidence does not qualify a successor candidate.\n\n**Terminal gate:** The release owner requires all 15 manual terminal cells (five environments × three sizes) on the exact installed RC. The latest verified worksheet status is 0/15 accepted cells; blank cells remain incomplete. Actual operator execution and per-cell outcomes are mandatory; automated CI or PTY results do not substitute. [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waives screenshots only. [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal applications, but the manual matrix remains outstanding.\n\n**Suite evidence:** `make test` completed on immutable snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c` with isolated HOME and the required evaluator workspace/runtime fixtures: 1,993 tests across 224 suites, 1,991 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped, 0 cancelled; Rust tests and post-test security lifecycle gates passed. The full run took 3,167,118 ms. This snapshot is not exact current main, PR #311 candidate `fe28ec9`, or an RC, so the result does not qualify those revisions. The SUITE claim transferred to the OpenCode custodian at 04:18 UTC for the 20-task custody revalidation above.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 20:18 UTC; superseded)\n\n239-**Affected:** REQ-AGT-118; SPEC-11 §2.7 and ACC-VER-07; REQUIREMENTS ledger row REQ-AGT-118; `cli/test/fixtures/token_calibration.json` and `cli/test/tokens.test.ts`. No change to `cli/src/tokens.ts` behaviour.\n240-\n241:## DEC-18: v1.0.0 terminal screenshot-artifact waiver\n242-\n243-**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\n--\n247-**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\n248-\n249:## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n250-\n251-**Status: withdrawn.** The waiver described in this decision is not in effect.\n--\n253-**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\n254-\n255:**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\n256-\n257-**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---claims-relevant---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"V1_CI_PINNED_EVAL_TOOLCHAINS_20261029 {\"agent\":\"SageBridge\",\"branch\":\"v1/ci-pinned-eval-toolchains\",\"scope\":\"CI-only provisioning of root-owned non-writable pinned Go/Rust evaluator toolchains; no evaluator source or held-out data\",\"status\":\"Implemented CI-only provisioning; static/shell/version/requirements checks PASS; independent review and owner push pending; exact PR318 Node22 failure reproduced (2026 tests, 2023 pass, 1 fail, 2 skipped; go status 127).\",\"since\":\"2026-10-29T05:42:53Z\",\"host\":null,\"pid\":917899,\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/ci-pinned-eval-toolchains\"}\nTERMINAL_SCREENSHOT_OPTIONALITY_20261029 {\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"branch\":\"v1/term-screenshot-optional\",\"scope\":\"Align terminal acceptance runner, summarizer and operator instructions with DEC-18 screenshot-artifact waiver while retaining all 15 interactive checks, measurements, verdicts and safety gates.\",\"status\":\"Committed reviewed runner/summarizer/docs/test correction. Focused scripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh passed on exact content; diff-check, bash -n, node --check pass; requirements enforcement passes (123 rows; 12 exact-RC deferrals); sync-version confirms rc.10. Independent reviewer ACCEPT exact cumulative diff SHA256 1119aa8df5b656d3964f7f014118917648ede96516dd208a64da5ebd7e886074. Ready to push/open PR and await exact-head CI.\",\"since\":\"2026-10-29T05:35:40.551514Z\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"pid\":866174,\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-screenshot-optional\"}\nV1_HELDOUT_CORPUS_CUSTODY_20261028 {\"agent\":\"kimi-code\",\"branch\":\"v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9\",\"scope\":\"held-out corpus compatibility and custody handoff; no payload exposure\",\"status\":null,\"since\":\"2026-10-28T23:42:27Z\",\"host\":null,\"pid\":2827782,\"worktree\":null}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1863d-79ff-7542-9cc8-8e417e9767e8","create_time":1793253635.0765715}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
