{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T06:00:59.397Z","ordinal":494579,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1863f-5305-7272-ac9d-7955d36840be","call_id":"call_f0d0198d1f8b44a1a34f04e0ed1cfbd9","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed commit `d53caea7c480c5e88dff43c6e5d4cb8a16868400`; exact patch SHA-256: `b42067a589cd9bda7802cf1550a2a7741d99cb3e34b44827eee58b1d66d4c85f`.\\n\\nBoth `test-matrix` and `linux-x86_64` copy the active Go root and Rust sysroot to the fixed locations, set root ownership and remove group/other write permission, then compare the copied Go, Rust, and Cargo versions with their source tools. The filesystem changes are confined to the ephemeral CI runner; I found no source-path overlap or cross-job persistence issue in the workflow.\\n\\nRead-only source review; no tests run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Unable to record a valid independent approval. Entire trail #32 is open for `v1/docs-entire-token-store`; PR #317 is open at exact head `ff7698d3a8fccedf6fbbc0a514b74acbfa613589`, based on `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`, and changes only `AGENTS.md`. The trail has no approvals.\\n\\nThe active Entire identity is Mike Holownych, the PR author, so approving would not be independent. I did not approve. A different authorized reviewer must approve trail #32.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Trail 30 is the matching open change for PR #315’s exact branch and head. Its approval list is empty.\\n\\nI did **not** approve: `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file entire auth status` identifies the active account as **Mike Holownych**, the PR author and trail author/assignee. Only that one Entire context is configured, so I have no independent non-owner authenticated identity to submit the approval